hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2872","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar Al-Zahid told us, Ahmad bin Mahdi bin Rustum Al-Asbahani told us, Abu Amer Al-Aqdi told us, Qurra bin Khaled, on the authority of Abu Raja al-Atardi, on the authority of Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with him, said: “We learned the Qur’an in this mosque - Meaning the Basra Mosque - and we were sitting one by one, and it was as if I was looking at it between two white dresses, and it is from him that I took this Surah: {Read in the name of your Lord who created} [Al-Alaq: 1] He said: It was the first surah that was revealed to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This is an authentic hadith based on The condition of the two sheikhs, and he did not narrate it, and he has evidence with a valid chain of transmission according to the condition of Muslim.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2872 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2873","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us, Bishr ibn Musa informed us, al-Humaydi informed us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The first surah to be revealed was: {Read in the name of your Lord who created} [Al-Alaq: 1].”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2873 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2874","Ali bin Issa told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her. On her authority - Sufyan said: Ibn Ishaq preserved it for us - she said: “Indeed, the first thing that was revealed from the Qur’an was: {Read in the name of your Lord who created} [Al-Alq: 1].”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2874 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2875","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Fadl told us, Hawdha bin Khalifa told us, Awf bin Abi Jamila told us, Yazid told us Al-Farisi, he said: Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said to us: I said to Uthman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him: What made you decide to Al-Anfal, which is from Al-Mathani and Al-Baraa, which is from Al-Ma’in, so you combined them, and did not write a line between them. In the name of God, the Most Gracious. The Most Merciful, and you placed it in the seven long ones. What motivated you to do that? Othman, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to come to a time when numerous surahs would descend upon him, and when Something was revealed to him. He called someone who was writing it down and said: “Put this in the surah in which such-and-such is mentioned,” and it was revealed to him. The verse, and he says: “Put this in the surah in which such-and-such is mentioned.” Al-Anfal was one of the first to be revealed in Medina, and Bara’ah From the end of the Qur’an, her story was similar to hers, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested and he did not explain to us that it was from her. Hence I compared them, and did not write a line between them. In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2876","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i informed us in Baghdad, and Abu Mansour Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Farisi informed us, saying: Abu Bakr told us Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Mu’alla bin Mansour told us, Hushaym told us, Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of Badr: “Whoever kills a dead person will get such-and-such.” As for the sheikhdom, they remained firm under banners, and as for the young men, they hastened to kill and take the spoils. The sheikhdom said to the young men: Join us with you, for we were a response to you. If there had been anything among you, you would have come to us, but they refused, so they disputed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So it was revealed: “They ask you about Al-Anfal} [Al-Anfal: 1] So the spoils were divided equally among them. “This is an authentic hadith, and they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2876 - True"
"2877","Ali bin Issa told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Abdul-A’la bin Abdul-A’la told us, Dawud bin Abi told us Hind, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “God sent down the Qur’an to the lowest heaven on the Night of Decree, and it was If God wanted to inspire something from it, He inspired it, or to create something from it on earth, He caused it. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. “He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2877 - True"
"2878","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq al-Faqih told us, Musa bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Abu Bakr and Uthman, Ibn Abi Shaybah told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, in the Almighty’s saying: {Indeed, We sent it down in the Night of Decree} [Al-Qadr: 1] He said: “The Qur’an was sent down in one sentence on the Night of Decree to the lowest heaven, and it was in the position of the stars, and God used to send it down to the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, one after the other. He said: And they said: “If the Qur’an had not been revealed to him in one sentence, it is thus that We might thereby strengthen your heart.” And We recited it with a chant.” [Al-Furqan: 32] “This is an authentic hadith according to their condition, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2878 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2879","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “The Qur’an was revealed in one sentence to the lowest heaven on the Night of Decree, then it was revealed Twenty years after that: {And they bring you no example except that We have brought you the truth and the best explanation} [Al-Furqan: 33] {And a Qur’an which We have divided so that you may recite it in people for a period of time, and We sent it down with a final revelation} [Al-Isra: 106] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2879 - True"
"2880","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, Sulayman bin Al-Mugheerah Al-Basri, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah Al-Ansari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “It was When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was inspired, none of us would be able to raise our eyes to him, until the revelation ended. This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2880 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2881","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Taher Al-Zubayri told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Hafs, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Hassan bin Harith, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “Chapter The Qur’an is from the remembrance, so it was placed in the House of Glory in the lowest heaven, and Gabriel, peace be upon him, revealed it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and recited it. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2881 - True"
"2882","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Amr Ibn Alqamah, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: «There is hypocrisy in the Qur’an “Disbelief” followed by Omar bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of his father\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2882 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2883","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, Abd al-Malik bin Muhammad al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, On the authority of Omar bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Arguing about the Qur’an “Disbelief.” The hadith of Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. As for Omar bin Abi Salamah, they did not use it as evidence. \"with it\""
"2884","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab and Abd al-Samad bin Ali bin Makram informed us, saying: Ja`far bin Abi Uthman al-Tayalisi told us, Affan told us. Ibn Muslim, Hammad Ibn Salama told us, Qatada told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “It was revealed “The Qur’an is in three letters.” Al-Bukhari used as evidence the narration of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, and Muslim used the hadiths of Hammad bin Salamah as evidence, and this “The hadith is authentic and has no defect.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2884 - It is authentic and has no defect"
"2885","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, about Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited to me Surah Ham, and I went to the mosque in the evening. A group of people sat next to me, and I said to a man from the group: “Recite to me,” and lo and behold, he was reciting letters that I could not recite. So I said to him: Who recited them to you? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed me. So we went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and suddenly there was a man with him, and I said to him: They differed in our reading, and then the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, changed, and he found it within himself, when I mentioned the difference to him, and he said: “Indeed, those before you were destroyed by disagreement.” Then Ali confided in me, and Ali said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commands you to read every verse. A man among you, as he knew, so we set off, and each man among us recited letters that his companion did not read."
"2886","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Muhammad bin Abi Al-Shawareb told us, Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, Abu Awanah told us, On the authority of Asim, he mentioned the hadith with a similar chain of transmission, in which he said: So we went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and behold, with him was a man who said: Button: They designate him as Ali, meaning “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2885 - True"
"2887","Abu Jafar Omar bin Muhammad bin Safwan Al-Jumahi told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz bin Yahya told us, Sulayman bin Daoud Al-Hashimi told us, Abdullah bin Abi Al-Zinad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Kharijah bin Zaid, on the authority of his father Zaid bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Reciting is seven.” Suleiman said: “It means that people do not differ from your opinion by following.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2887 - True"
"2888","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Bakhtari Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “We recited al-Mufassal in Mecca as proofs that did not contain: Oh O you who have believed, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2888 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2889","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan bin Ahmad al-Asadi told me, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein bin Diezel told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu`bah told us, On the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me: “God has commanded me to recite upon you is the Qur’an.” He recited: “Those who disbelieve are not from among the People of the Book and the polytheists.” [Al-Bayyinah: 1] And its description is: If the son of Adam asked a valley who Money, so I gave him, he asked a second time, and if I gave him a second time, he asked a third time, and nothing fills the stomach of the son of Adam except dust, and God turns to whoever repents, and indeed The religion in the sight of God is Hanifism other than Judaism or Christianity, and whoever does good will not be declared an unbeliever by him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2889 - True"
"2890","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, and Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, they said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais, on the authority of Nabih Al-Anazi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: While I was reading a verse from the Book of God Almighty, As I was walking on one of the roads of Medina, I saw a man calling me after me. Follow Ibn Abbas. Then he was the Commander of the Faithful, Omar. So I said: I follow you on Ubayy bin Ka’b. He said: Did he recite it to you as I heard you reciting? I said: Yes. He said: Then send a messenger with me. He said: Go with him to Ubayy ibn Ka’b and see if Ubayy will recite like that? He said: So I and his messenger went to Ubayy ibn Ka’b. He said: So I said: O my father, I read a verse from the Book of God, and then Umar ibn Ka’b called me after me. Al-Khattab: Follow Ibn Abbas, so I said: I follow you on Ubayy bin Ka’b, so he sent his messenger with me. Did you read it to me as you read it? My father said: Yes, he said: So the messenger returned to him, and I went to my needs. He said: So Omar went to my father, and I found that he had finished washing. His head, and his daughter was moving his beard to its length, so my father said: Welcome, O Commander of the Faithful. Have you come as a visitor or seeking something? Omar said: Rather, he asked for a need. He said: So he sat with his two servants of his until he finished trimming his beard, and I turned his right side from his head, then He placed it on his left side until when he was finished, he turned to Omar with his face and said: What is the need of the Commander of the Faithful? Omar said: O my father, why do you deceive people? My father said: O Commander of the Faithful, I received the Qur’an when I met Gabriel while he was fresh. Omar: By God, you are not destined, and I am not patient, three times, then he got up and started, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2890 - True"
"2891","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazyid told us, Muhammad bin Shuaib bin Shabur told us, Abdullah bin Al-Alaa bin Zubr, on the authority of Busr bin Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Abu Idris, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, that he used to recite: {When He made Those who disbelieve have in their hearts fervor, the fervor of ignorance.} [Al-Fath: 26] And if you had protected, as they did, the Sacred Mosque would have been corrupted. {So God sent down His tranquility upon His Messenger} [Al-Fath: 26]. This reached Umar and it became difficult for him, so he sent for her while he was enjoying a she-camel of his, so he entered upon him and called some of his companions. Among them was Zaid bin Thabit, and he said: Who among you recites Surat Al-Fath? So Zaid recited as we recited today, and Omar spoke harshly to him, and my father said to him: Shall I speak? He said: Speak, I knew that I used to go to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he would make me meet, while you were at the door, so if you would like to I read to the people for what he read to me. I read, otherwise I will never read a word as long as I live.” He said: Rather, I read to the people. “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2891 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2892","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim Al-Adl told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Raqqashi told us, Ja’far bin Suleiman told us, Abu Imran Al-Juni, on the authority of Jundub, said: “I came to Medina to learn knowledge, and when I entered the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I suddenly People were talking in a circle.” He said: “So I started to move on until I came to a circle in which there was a pale man wearing two clothes, as if he had come from a journey. So I heard him say: The Companions of the Aqad and the Lord of the Kaaba have perished, and I do not feel sorry for them. He says it three times. The Companions of the Aqad and the Lord of the Kaaba have perished. He has perished. The owners of the contract and the Lord of the Kaaba, the owners of the contract and the Lord of the Kaaba have perished.” He said: “So I sat with him and he spoke what was decided for him and then he got up. So I asked about him, and they said: This is the master of the people, Ubayy bin Ka’b. He said: “So I followed him until he came to his house, and behold, he was in a shabby house. The clothing was shabby, and some of it looked similar to the other. So I greeted him, and he returned my greetings. He said: Then he asked me, “Who are you from?” He said: I said: From the people of Iraq. He said: He asked the most questions, and he became angry. He said: “So I faced the Qiblah, then I knelt down and raised My hands are like this, and he extended his arms, and I said: Oh God, we complain to You, we will spend our expenses, we will erect our bodies, and we will raise our mounts. Seeking knowledge, and when we met them, they frowned at us and said to us. He said: Then my father cried and began to console me and say: Woe to you, I did not go. “There,” then my father said: I promise you that if you keep me until Friday to speak about what I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, no. I feared the blame of the wrongdoer. He said: “Then I left him and waited for Friday. When it was Thursday, I went out to fulfill some needs. Then, behold, the roads were full of people. I would not take a street without people greeting me.” He said: “So I said: What is the matter with the people? They said: We consider you a stranger. He said: I said: Yes. They said: The master of the Muslims, Ubayy bin Ka’b, died. He said: I met Abu Musa in Iraq. So I spoke to him,” and he said: “Would he not have stayed until his statement reached us?” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2892 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2893","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, He said: A man came to Omar while he was at Arafat, and he said: O Commander of the Faithful, I came from Kufa and left there someone who dictates the Qur’an from the back of the book. His heart. He said: Omar became angry, and swelled until it almost filled the space between the man’s forelocks, then he said: Woe to you, who is he? He said: Abdullah bin Masoud, and he continued to extinguish and spread his anger, until he returned to the state he was in. Then he said: Woe to you, by God! I know that there is one among the Muslims who is more deserving of this than him. I will tell you about that. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was still He spent the night in a Muslim affair with Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, and he spent the night with him one night, and I was with him, then he went out. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we went out walking with him, when a man was standing and praying in the mosque. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up. He listens to his reading, and when we were unable to know who the man was, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is pleased to recite the Qur’an, as It was revealed, so let him recite it to Ibn Umm Abd.” Then the man sat down to make supplication, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, began to say to him: “Ask and it will be given to you.” Umar said. So I said: “By God, I will go to him in the morning to give him the good news.” He said: “So I went to him to give him the good news, and I found Abu Bakr who had preceded me and gave him the good news. By God, I have never preceded him in doing good unless he preceded me in it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2893 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2894","Abu Bakr bin Adam, the Hafiz in Kufa, told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Al-Qasim bin Bishr bin Marouf told us, Musab told us. Ibn Al-Miqdam Al-Khathami, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever likes to read the Qur’an in its pure form, as it was revealed, let him read it as Ibn Umm Abd read.” The hadith of Alqamah, on the authority of Omar, The chain of narration is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it, and they believed that it was not authentic in their opinion that Alqamah bin Qays heard from Omar, and God knows best.” There is an explanatory witness to it from the hadith of Ammar bin Yasser."
"2895","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Jaafar Al-Farisi told us, Yaqoub bin Sufyan Al-Farisi told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Uwaisi told us, Muhammad bin Ja`far bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ismail bin Sakhr al-Ayli, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Muhammad bin Ammar bin Yasser, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Ammar bin Yasser, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by Abdullah bin Masoud while he was reciting letter by letter. He said: “Whoever is pleased to read the Qur’an as it was revealed, let him read it as Ibn Masoud reads.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2895 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2896","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Muthanna bin Muadh told us, my father told us, Abdullah bin Awf told me, Omar bin Qais told me, On the authority of Abu Maysarah Amr bin Shurahbil, he said: A man came to me while I was praying, and said: May your mother be bereaved of you. Shall I not see you praying? He ordered that a letter be written. By God, may all that is torn be torn apart. He said: So I passed my prayer, and I was sitting, so I entered the house, and did not sit, and I rose and did not sit, and behold, I With Al-Ash'ari, Hudhayfah, and Ibn Masoud were negotiating, and Hudhayfah said to Ibn Masoud: Give them this Qur’an. He said: “By God, I will not hand it over to them. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught me seventy-four surahs, and then I will hand it over to them. By God, I will not give it to them.” “I gave it to them.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not take it out.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2896 - True"
"2897","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Qubaisah bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hamza Ibn Malik, he said: Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: “I have read from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, seventy surahs.” And Zaid Ibn Thabit with two wolves playing with the boys “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.” There is evidence of this addition on the authority of Abdullah\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2897 - True"
"2898","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Handali told us in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba told us, Yahya bin Hammad told us, Abu Awanah told us, he told me Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Asadi, said: I heard Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught me “On him and grant him peace, seventy surahs, which I composed correctly, before Zayd ibn Thabit converted to Islam.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2898 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2899","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us that he was dictating in his mosque in Baghdad, Ibrahim bin Haitham Al-Baladi told us, Muhammad bin Many, Abu Salamah told me, Abdullah bin Salam, may God be pleased with him, told me, he said: A group of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat down. So we said: “If we knew which deeds are most beloved to God, we would do them.” Then God Almighty revealed: {Glory be to God whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on earth, and He The Mighty, the Wise, O you who have believed, why do you say what you do not do? It is most abhorrent to God to say what you do not do. Indeed, God loves Those who fight in His cause in array as if they were a solid building} until the end of the surah, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it to us. “Muhammad added. Ibn Kathir in his hadith: Al-Awza’i said to us: “Yahya bin Abi Kathir recited it to us like this.” Muhammad bin Kathir said: “And he recited it to us.” Al-Awza’i recited it to us like this.” Ibrahim said: “And Muhammad bin Kathir recited it to us like this until the end of the surah.” Abu Amr bin Al-Sammak said: “And Ibrahim bin Al-Haytham recited it to us until the end of the surah like this.” Al-Hakim said: “And Abu Amr bin Al-Sammak recited it to us from the beginning of the surah.” To the end like this.” Al-Hakim read it to us from the beginning of the surah to the end. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2899 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2900","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Bishr bin Musa Al-Asadi, and Al-Harith bin Abi Usama al-Tamimi, they said: Yahya bin Ishaq al-Silahini told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, Yazid bin Abi Habib told me that Abd al-Rahman bin Shamasa told him on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him, who said: We were around the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, compiling the Qur’an, when he said: “Blessed are “For the Levant.” It was said to him: Why? He said: “Indeed, the angels of the Most Gracious spread their wings over them.” Narrated by Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Yahya bin Ayyub.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2900 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2901","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Ubayy told us, I heard Yahya Ibn Ayyub, narrating on the authority of Yazid Ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Shamasa, on the authority of Zayd Ibn Thabit, may God be pleased with him, he said: We were at The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, We compose the Qur’an from pieces of paper, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Blessed is the Levant,” so we said: For anything. That? He said: “Because the angels of the Most Gracious spread their wings over them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and it contains the explanation. What is clear is that the compilation of the Qur’an was not just one time. Some of it was collected in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then some of it was collected. In the presence of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, and the third plural is in the order of the surah. It was during the caliphate of the Commander of the Faithful, Othman bin Affan, may God be pleased with them. \"all of them\""
"2902","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghdadi informed us, Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Alaf informed us, Sa`id ibn Abi Maryam informed us, Muhammad ibn Ja`far informed us Ibn Abi Kathir, Sharik Ibn Abdullah Ibn Abi Nimr told us, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, that he said: I entered The mosque was on Friday, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was delivering a sermon, so I sat close to Ubayy bin Ka’b. “Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited Surat Bara’a.” So I said to my father: When was this Surah revealed? He said: He frowned at me and did not speak to me. He said: “And he mentioned the hadith like this. I found it in my book, and I looked for it in the Musnads, but I did not find it as long as the hadith.” With its chain of transmission, it is authentic.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2902 - True"
"2903","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abraham Ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: Which of the two recitations do you think was the last recitation? They said: Zayd’s recitation. He said: No, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to present the Qur’an every year to Gabriel, peace be upon him. In the year in which he was arrested, he presented it to him two times, and the recitation of Ibn Masoud was the last of them. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. In this context, and the benefit of the hadith, Abdullah bin Masoud mentioned “\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2903 - True"
"2904","Jafar bin Muhammad bin Nusayr Al-Khalidi told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz Al-Baghawi told us, in Mecca, Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal told us, he said: Hammad told us Ibn Salama, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Qur’an was presented to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, several times.” So they say: Our reading of this is the final incident. “This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Bukhari, some of it, and some of it according to the condition of Muslim. And they did not bring it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2904 - True\n From the book of recitations of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, from what they did not narrate, and its chain of transmission is authentic."
"2905","I heard Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub say: Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam bin Ayan Al-Misri told us: Abu Abdullah told us Muhammad bin Idris Al-Shafi’i, Ismail bin Abdullah bin Constantine told us, he said: I read to Shibl, and Shibl told us that he read to Shibl. Ubayd Allah bin Kathir, and Abdullah told that he read to Mujahid, and Mujahid told that he read to Ibn Abbas, and Ibn Abbas told Abbas, that he recited to Ubayy ibn Ka’b, and Ibn Abbas said: “My father recited to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Al-Shafi’i said: And I read to Ismail ibn Constantine, and he used to say: “The Qur’an is a noun, not a vocab, and it was not taken from what I recited, and if it was taken from what I recited, everything that was recited would be.” Qur’an, but it is a name for the Qur’an, like the Torah and the Gospel. It is pronounced “I read,” and the Qur’an is not accented."
"2906","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Abbas ibn Imam al-Muqri told me, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdul Aziz al-Baghawi told me, Khalaf ibn Hisham Al-Muqri, Ali bin Hamza Al-Kisa’i narrated to me, Husayn bin Ali Al-Jafi narrated to me, on the authority of Hamran bin Ayan, on the authority of my father Al-Aswad Al-Daili, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Prophet of God. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am not a prophet of God, but I am a prophet of God.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and he has An interpreting witness with a chain of transmission is not a requirement of this book.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2906 - Rather, it is objectionable and not valid"
"2907","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yaqoub, the Hafiz and reciter, told me. Abu Al-Qasim Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl bin Shazan, the reciter, told me. Ibrahim bin Mihran Al-Ayli, Mihran bin Dawud bin Mihran Al-Muqri, narrated to us, Abdullah bin Udhaynah Al-Tai, narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, said: “Neither the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, nor Abu Bakr, nor Omar, nor the caliphs swayed, but rather Hamza is an innovation, they invented it after them.” I heard Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani, the memorizer, saying: I heard Abu Zakariya Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya, saying: I heard Ahmad bin Hanbal, saying: “I do not write the hadith of Musa bin Ubaidah al-Rabdi, nor the hadith of Abd Al-Rahman bin Ziyad Al-Afriqi»"
"2908","Abu Ali Al-Hasan bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Makram told us, Nasr bin Ali Al-Jahdami told us, Bakkar bin Abdullah, Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz bin Omar bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf told us, Abu Al-Zannad told me, on the authority of Kharijah bin Zaid, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Thabit, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The Qur’an was sent down with exaggeration {like the appearance of a bird} [Al Imran: 49] as an excuse and a warning. And the two shells, and {Indeed, to Him belongs the creation and the command} [Al-A’raf: 54], and something similar to this in the Qur’an: “Its chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2908 - No, by God, Al-Awfi is weak, and Bakkar is not a pillar, and the hadith is weak and objectionable."
"2909","Al-Hussein bin Ayyub and Muhammad bin Al-Hasan told us, saying: Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abu Ubaid Al-Qasim bin Salam told us, Yahya told me Ibn Saeed Al-Umayyad, Abdul-Malik Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to interrupt his recitation {In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful. Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds, Most Gracious, Most Merciful, Master of the Day of Religion} »"
"2910","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih, Abu Bakr bin Quraysh, and Abu Amr bin Abdoos Al-Muqri told us, they said: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Ali told us. Bin Hajr bin Iyas Al-Saadi, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qurashi told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with On her authority, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would interrupt his recitation verse by verse: {Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds} [Al-Fatihah: 2] and then he would stop {The Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} [Al-Fatihah: 1] Then he stands. “Ibn Abi Mulaika said: “And Umm Salamah used to recite it (The Angel of the Day of Judgment).” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. And they did not narrate it.” “And he has evidence with an authentic chain of transmission to their condition, on the authority of Abu Hurairah\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2910 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2911","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih and Ali ibn Hamshadh al-Adl informed us. Abu Bakr said: He informed, and Ali said: Muhammad ibn Ghalib informed us. Yahya bin Ismail Al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that “the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he used to recite: (The King of the Day of Judgment)"
"2912","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi told us about Marw, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi told us, Ibrahim bin Suleiman Al-Kateb told us, Ibrahim bin Tahman, on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he recited: “Guide us to the straight path” [Al-Fatihah: 6] with the word “Saad”: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2912 - Rather, it is not authentic"
"2913","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih, Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar Al-Zahid, and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, they said: Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi, Suleiman bin Harb and Abu Al-Walid told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhail, he said: I heard Hujr Aba Al-Anbas, He narrates on the authority of Alqamah bin Wa’il, on the authority of his father, that he prayed with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when he said: “Not those with anger nor those who go astray” [Al-Fatihah: 7] He said: “Ameen,” lowering his voice with it. “The judge said: {other} [Al-Fatihah: 7] by lowering the rā’, for in the recitation of the people of Mecca {other than the one upon whom is angered} [Al-Fatihah: 7] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2913 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2914","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told me about Al-Ray, Muhammad bin Al-Faraj Al-Azraq told me, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told me, Ibn Jurayj told me, On the authority of Ismail ibn Kathir, on the authority of Asim ibn Laqit ibn Sabrah, on the authority of his father Laqit ibn Sabrah, a delegate of Banu al-Muntafiq, he said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. A friend of mine and I did not find him, so Aisha fed us dates and porridge, and he said: It was not long before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came. He said, “Have you two been fed anything?” We said: Yes. He said: While we were doing that, the shepherd came with a lamb in his hand, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Have you given birth?” He said: Yes. He said: “What?” He said: eagerly. He said: “Slay a sheep in its place.” Then he came to me and said: “Do not think that we slaughtered it for your sake. We have a hundred sheep. We do not like To increase, then when the shepherd carries a lamb, we slaughter a sheep in its place. Ibn Jurayj said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not think so.” He did not say: They do not think. It was narrated by Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Asim bin Laqit with this narration [p. 254].\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2914 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2915","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Abu Ahmad Al-Zubairi told us, Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Asim bin Laqit, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not think so,” and he did not say: No. They think, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2915 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2916","Bukayr bin Muhammad bin Sahl Al-Sufi told us, in Mecca, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Ahmad bin Al-Qasim bin Abi Bazza told us, Dawud bin Shibl bin Abbad Al-Makki, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Kathir Al-Qari, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him On their authority, he said: I read to Ubayy ibn Ka’b: “And fear a Day when no soul will avail another soul in the slightest” [Al-Baqarah: 48] with the letter “And no intercession will be accepted from it.” And no justice will be taken from it.) My father said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, taught me: {Not one soul is of benefit to another at all} [Al-Baqarah: 48] with the letter T. (And no intercession will be accepted from her) with the T, {And no justice is taken from her} [Al-Baqarah: 48] with the Ya “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2916 - True"
"2917","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sirafi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Al-Hakam bin Abdul-Malik told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may God be pleased with him, said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on a journey, and some of the His companions were on their way, so he raised his voice with these two verses: {O people, fear your Lord. Indeed, the earthquake of the Hour is a great thing, the day you see it. Every nursing woman will be amazed at what she has suckled, and every pregnant female will give birth to her child, and you will see people drunk, but they are not drunk, but the punishment of God is severe.} [Al-Hajj: 2] When his companions heard that, they urged Al-Muti, and they knew that he had something to say, so he said: “Do you know what day that is?” They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “The day Adam will call upon his Lord and say: O Adam, send forth the source of the Fire.” He will say: O Lord, and what is the source of the Fire? He said: “Out of every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine will be in Hell, and one will be in Paradise.” Then his companions became foolish, and they did not explain it with a smile, so when The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw those with his companions and said: “Know and give good tidings, for by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are a merging of two creatures. They were never with anything unless they multiplied it, Gog and Magog, and whoever of the sons of Adam perished, and the sons of Satan.” So some of those who find Then he said: “Know and give good news, for by the One in Whose Hand is Muhammad’s soul, you are only like a mole on the side of a camel, or like a spot on the arm of people. “The Beast” The hadith of Hisham al-Dastawai is an authentic hadith, as most of our imams among the predecessors are of the opinion that Al-Hasan heard from Imran bin Husayn. But if Hisham and Al-Hakam bin Abdul-Malik disagree, then the opinion is Hisham’s opinion.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2917 - Al-Hakam bin Abdul Malik Wah"
"2918","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Ibrahim bin Yusuf Al-Hasanjani told us, Hisham bin Khaled Al-Azraq told us, Ismail bin Qays, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Abi Nu’aym al-Qaari, Ismail ibn Abi Hakim narrated to me, Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to us, on the authority of his father Zayd ibn Thabit, may God be pleased with him, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: {How can we raise it?} [Al-Baqarah: 259] in the same way: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not take it out, because they did not use Ismail bin Qays bin Thabit as evidence.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2918 - Ismail bin Qays, from the descendants of Zaid bin Thabit, they weakened him."
"2919","Abu Abdullah al-Saffar informed us, Ahmad ibn Mihran informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me: ‘I am “The Sustainer, the One who is Powerful.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2919 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2920","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Mahran told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, On the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: A man from Banu Sulaym passed by a group of the Companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted them, and he had some of his sheep with him. He greeted them, and they said: He only greeted you to seek refuge from you. So they went to him, killed him, and took his sheep. So they brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “So God Almighty revealed {O you who have believed, when you strike in the way of God, then investigate and do not say You are not a believer in anyone who extends greetings to you.} [An-Nisa: 94] to his saying: “Thus you were before, so God has bestowed upon you so understand” [An-Nisa: 94] “This is A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2920 - True"
"2921","Muhammad ibn Mu’mal ibn al-Hasan ibn Issa told me, Al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn al-Musayyab told me, Issa ibn Mina Qalun told me, Abu Ghaziyah told me Muhammad bin Musa bin Al-Qadi, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Ashhali, on the authority of Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him On their authority: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: {And it is not for a prophet to deceive} [Al Imran: 161] with the opening of the yā’. This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2921 - Indeed, it is false"
"2922","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Ibrahim bin Yusuf Al-Hasanjani told us, Hisham bin Khalid told us, Ismail bin Qais told us, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Abi Nu’aym: “Collected mortgage.” Then Nafi’ said: Ibn Zayd ibn Thabit informed me of Kharijah and said: Zayd ibn Thabit informed me. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, read to me: ‘A mortgage taken, not for a thousand.’ This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2922 - Ismail is weak"
"2923","Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Adl told me, Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib told me, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta’i told me, Yahya ibn Rashid told me, Khalid told us The Shoe, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of his father, who said: I said to Aisha, may God be pleased with her: O Mother of the Believers, how was the Messenger of God? God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recites this letter: {And those who give what they give} [Al-Mu’minun: 60] She said: Which of the two is more beloved to you? I said: One of them is more beloved to me than red camels. She said: Which one? I said: {Those who give what they give}. She said: “This is how I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2923 - Yahya bin Rashid is weak"
"2924","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Salman al-Faqih in Baghdad informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Issa al-Qadi informed us, Abu al-Nu`man Muhammad ibn al-Fadl informed us, Harun bin Musa Al-Nahwi, Budayl bin Maysarah Al-Uqaili narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she heard The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recites: {Faruh and Basil} [Al-Waqi’ah: 89] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2924 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2925","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told us in Mecca, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah bin Yazid told us The reciter, Harmala bin Imran told us, Abu Yunus told me, I heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, “reciting this verse: {Indeed, God He commands you to return trusts to their rightful owners, and when you judge between people, to judge with justice. Indeed, God is a blessing that He encourages you with. Indeed, God is All-Hearing and All-Seeing} [An-Nisa: 58] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2925 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2926","Muhammad bin Saleh and Ibrahim bin Asma told us, saying: Abu Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told us, Abu Saleh Abdullah bin Saleh told us, Musa bin Ali bin Rabah told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent to me: “Take your clothes and your weapons on you and then come to me.” So I took my clothes and weapons and then came to him and found him sitting and performing ablution, so he climbed into me. He looked, then bowed his head, then said: “O Amr, I want to send you to an army so that God will give you spoils and grant you peace, and I would like for you some wealth.” Righteous.” So I said: O Messenger of God, I did not embrace Islam out of money, but rather I embraced Islam out of a desire to become a Muslim and to be with you. He said: “O Amr, we have been blessed with good money for a good man,” meaning the opening of the noun and the kasra of the ayn. “An authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim according to the narration of Musa bin Ali bin Rabah, and according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari according to Abu Salih.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2926 - True"
"2927","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Hasan bin Abdul-Samad told us, Abdan bin Uthman told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Yazid, Abu Ali bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite: {And We prescribed for them In it is that a soul for a soul} [Al-Ma’idah: 45] in the accusative {and an eye for an eye} [Al-Ma’idah: 45] in the nominative case: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.” It was narrated by Muhammad bin Muawiyah Al-Naysaburi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, with wording additions.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2927 - True"
"2928","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya the martyr told us, Abu Ali Muhammad bin Muawiyah told us. Al-Naysaburi in Mecca, Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Ali bin Yazid, brother of Yunus bin Yazid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas.” The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: “A life for a life, an eye for an eye, a nose for a nose, an ear for an ear, and a tooth for a tooth. And wounds are retaliation.” [Al-Ma’idah: 45] “Muhammad bin Muawiyah is not a condition of this book.”"
"2929","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i informed us in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Wasiti informed us, Yazid bin Harun informed us, he informed us Asbagh bin Zayd Al-Juhani Al-Warraq, Al-Qasim bin Abi Ayyub narrated to me, Saeed bin Jubayr narrated to me, he said: I asked Abdullah bin Abbas, may God bless him and grant him peace. God on their authority, on the authority of God Almighty’s saying: “And We tried you with trials” [Taha: 40] in a hadith in which the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, reported: “Two men from among those who They fear} [Al-Ma’idah: 23] with the yā’ raised, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2929 - True"
"2930","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi narrated to us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Al-Nadr Al-Jaudi narrated to us, Abdul-A’la bin Hammad Al-Narsi narrated to us, and Nasr bin Ali narrated to us. Al-Jahdhami, they said: Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, He said: When “Glorify the Name of your Lord Most High” was revealed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “All of them are in the scriptures of Abraham and Moses.” So when they were revealed: “By the Star” When he inclines, then he reaches: {And Abraham is the one who fulfilled} [An-Najm: 37] He burdened him and said: And he fulfilled: {Should not one bearer of burden bear the burden of another} [An-Najm: 38] until his saying: {This A warner from the first wars} [An-Najm: 56] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2930 - True"
"2931","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Ishaq bin Ahmad bin Mahran al-Jazzar told us, Ishaq bin Sulayman al-Razi told us, Abu Jafar Issa bin Mahan, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, she said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. “He recites: {Yes, My signs have come to you, but you denied them and were arrogant, and you were of the disbelievers} [Az-Zumar: 59] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2931 - True"
"2932","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi told me about Marw, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told me, Ishaq bin Muhammad Al-Farwi, Suleiman bin Bilal told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: {Among those to whom the saints are worthy} [Al-Ma’idah: 107] “This is an authentic hadith according to Muslim’s conditions. And they did not bring it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2932 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2933","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani and Muhammad bin Al-Qasim Al-Ataki told us, saying: Abu Sahl Bishr bin Sahl Al-Labad told us, Abdullah bin Sahl told us Saleh Al-Masry, Hammad told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khuthaym, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr - Hammad said, and I heard it from Saeed bin Jubayr - on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite: {In a swampy spring} [Al-Kahf: 86] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2933 - True"
"2934","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Hakim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, said: He was with Ibn Ziyad Abu Al-Aswad Al-Dili and Jubayr bin Hayya Al-Thaqafi. He said: So mention this letter: {Indeed, it was cut off between you} [Al-An'am: 94] until they imposed dangers. Aslam bin Zur'ah said: I heard Abu Musa. It reads: {Indeed there has been a division between you} [Al-An’am: 94] “Then one of them said: Between me and you is the first to enter upon us. Then Yahya bin Yamar came to us and they asked him, and Yahya said: Relations between you have been broken off. Yahya said: Abu Musa is not one of the people of deception, and I do not accuse him. “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2934 - True"
"2935","Imam Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih and Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Qari told me, saying: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Suwayd bin Saeed told us, Al-Walid told us. Ibn Jundub, Bakr Ibn Khunais told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Ubadah Ibn Nasi, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Ghanam al-Ash’ari, he said: I asked Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the disciples, {Can your Lord be able} [Al-Maeda: 112] or Can you be able to your Lord? He said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told me, ‘Can you read it with the ta’? This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2935 - True"
"2936","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, my brother Abu Bakr told me, on the authority of Ibn Abu Dhib, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Abraham will meet his father Azar. On the Day of Resurrection, there will be dirt and dust on Azar’s face, and Abraham will say to him: Did I not tell you not to disobey me? So his father says: Today I will not disobey you. So Abraham says: O Lord, you promised me that you would not disgrace me on the day they were resurrected, so what disgrace would I be? Who is Abi Al-Abaad? Then God says: Indeed, I have forbidden Paradise to the unbelievers. Then he says: O Abraham, what is under your feet? Then he looks, and behold, it is a slaughtered animal stained. It is taken by its sides and thrown into the Fire. An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2936 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2937","Abu Sa`id Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Muqri informed me, Ahmad ibn Zayd ibn Harun al-Qazzaz told us, in Mecca, Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Abu Bazza, Wahb bin Zamaa reported, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Humaid bin Qais al-Araj, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, he said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, taught me: {And they would say, ‘I have studied.’” [Al-An’am: 105] - meaning - With the juzm as-sīn and the accusative case of the ta’, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2937 - True"
"2938","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote a line, and he wrote to the right of that line, and on the A line to his left, then he said: “This is the straight path of your Lord, and on each of these paths is a devil calling to it.” Then he recited: {And this My path is straight, so follow it, and do not follow other paths, lest He separate you from His path.} [Al-An’am: 153] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2938 - True"
"2939","Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told me, Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmed Al-Sijzi told me, Harun bin Hatim Al-Muqri told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, And Muhammad bin Fudayl, and Abdullah bin Numayr, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Al-Baraa, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting: {The gates of heaven shall not be opened to them} [Al-A`raf: 40] abbreviated: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2939 - Harun was left by Abu Zar’ah"
"2940","Ahmad bin Othman Al-Ahwazi told us, Ruh bin Abdul-Mu’min told us, Ubaid bin Aqeel told me, Hammad bin Salamah told me, on the authority of Thabit, On the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: ‘Dakka’ [Al-A’raf: 143] in a calm manner, and he did not extend it.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that Muslim, and they did not produce it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2940 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2941","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris Al-Razi told us, Salam bin Sulayman Al-Madani told us, Abu Amr bin Al-Ala’, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: {Now God has lightened it for you and knows that in you Double} [Al-Anfal: 66] “This is an authentic hadith, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2941 - Salam bin Suleiman went to Damascus, lost"
"2942","Mahboub bin Al-Hassan told us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: {That he may have captives} is true\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2942 - True"
"2943","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam Al-Misri told us, my father informed us, And Shuaib bin Al-Layth, they said: Al-Layth bin Saad narrated, Khaled bin Yazid narrated, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Nu`aym bin Abdullah al-Mujmar said: Suhaib told me that he heard Abu Hurairah and Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with them, say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us while he was on the pulpit, and he said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul,” three times, then he remained silent, and each man fell down. Who among us cries sadly at the right hand of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he said: “There is no servant who performs the five daily prayers and fasts during Ramadan. And he avoids the seven great sins, except that the gates of Paradise will be opened for him on the Day of Resurrection, to the point that they will clap together.” Then he recited: {If you avoid “As for the great sins which you are forbidden, We will expiate from you your evil deeds” [An-Nisa: 31] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2943 - True"
"2944","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Abu Saad Yahya bin Mansour Al-Harawi told us, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Amr Ibn Uthman, on the authority of Usama Ibn Zayd, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “People of two religions do not inherit, and no Muslim inherits.” An unbeliever, and no unbeliever is a Muslim.” Then he recited: “And those who disbelieve are allies of one another. Unless you do it, there will be strife on earth and great corruption.” [Al-Anfal: 73] With the letter “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2945","This is what Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me. Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Muqri informed us, Ibrahim bin Mihran Al-Aili told us, we told him Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Abdul Rahman Al-Dimashqi, Muslim bin Khaled Al-Zanji told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas May God be pleased with them both. He raises it to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He read: {Indeed there has come to you a messenger from among yourselves} [At-Tawbah: 128] “meaning from the greatest of you.” Destiny\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2945 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2946","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Musa bin Harun bin Abdullah told us, Nasr bin Ali Al-Jahdhami told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abdul-Rahman Ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Ubayy Ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting: {Say, “By the grace of God and His mercy,” so let them rejoice, for it is better than They gather} [Yunus: 58] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2946 - True"
"2947","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told me, in Kufa, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Zabarqan Al-Taymi told us, Abu Ruq, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Juhadah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to recite: (It is an unrighteous deed)\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2947 - Its chain of transmission is dark"
"2948","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told me, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told me, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Omar, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: {So ask him what happened to the women who cut off their hands} [Joseph: 50] He said: “If he had sent me a message, I would have responded quickly and not sought an excuse.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2948 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2949","Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi informed me, Abu Al-Abbas Ahmad bin Muhammad told me, Harun bin Hatim informed us, Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Hammad informed me, Ishaq bin Yusuf told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said to Ali: “O Ali, people are from different trees, and you and I are from one tree.” Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited. And he said: (Gardens of grapes, crops, and palm trees, both tree-shaped and non-tree-tree, watered with a single water) “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2949 - No, by God, Aaron is perished"
"2950","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih in Baghdad informed us, Hilal bin Al-Ala’ Al-Raqi told us, Ubayd Allah bin Amr Al-Raqi told us, on the authority of Zaid bin Abu Unaysa, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him “And We prefer some of them over others in eating.} [Al-Ra’ad: 4] In the letter “Nun,” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2950 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2951","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Abu Saleh Abdullah bin Saleh told us, Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Ziyad bin Muhammad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Ansari, on the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid Al-Ansari, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’ On his authority, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “{Allah erases whatever He wills and confirms” [Al-Ra’ad: 39] abbreviated “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2951 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2952","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail al-Faqih told us about Rayy, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, He said: I heard him saying: I heard Al-Qasim bin Rabi’ah saying: I heard Sa’d, “reciting: ‘We do not abrogate a verse or forget it.’ He said: So I said: Indeed He was happy to recite it: {Or he forgot it} [Al-Baqarah: 106] He said: Then he said: “Indeed, the Qur’an was not revealed to Al-Musayyab nor to his son. He said: And remember that he recited: {We will make you read, so you do not forget} {And remember your Lord when you forget} [Al-Kahf: 24] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2952 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2953","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrafi told me about Marw, Abdul Malik bin Muhammad al-Raqqashi told us, Bakkar bin Muhammad bin Abdullah told us, we told him Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz, Abu Al-Zinad told us, on the authority of Kharijah bin Zaid bin Thabit, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The Qur’an was sent down with exaggeration: {like the appearance of a bird} [Al Imran: 49], {as an excuse or a warning} [Al-Mursalat: 6] and with two shells {except His is the creation. And the matter” [Al-A’raf: 54] and the like: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2954","Sheikh Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Al-Junaid told us, Abu Al-Sha’a’a told us, Khaled told us Ibn Nafi’ al-Ash’ari, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Burdah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “ When the people of Hell gather in Hell, and with them from the people of the qiblah whoever God wills, they will say: What is of no use to you is your Islam, when you have joined us in Fire? They said: We had sins, so we were caught for them, so God heard what they said. He said: So he commanded that those of the people of the qiblah who were in Hell be taken out. Then the infidels say: I wish we were Muslims, then we were expelled as they were expelled. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: {These are the verses of the Book. And a clear Qur’an. Perhaps those who disbelieve would wish they were Muslims.} [Al-Hijr: 2] burdened with “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2954 - True"
"2955","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Al-Sadi, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in the Almighty’s saying: “On the Day when We will call every people with their Imam” [Al-Isra: 71] He said: “He will be called One of them will be given his letter in his right hand, and sixty cubits will be extended to him around his body.” He said: “And his face will be whitened, and a crown of Sparkling pearls.” He said: “Then he goes to his companions.” He said: “And they see him from afar and say: O God, bring him and bless us in This is until he comes to them and says: Rejoice, for every man among you is like this. As for the disbeliever, his face will be darkened, and his face will be extended. His body is sixty cubits, in the image of Adam, and his companions see him and say: We seek refuge in God from this. Oh God, do not bring him. He said: Then it comes to them and they say: Oh God, delay it. He said: Then he says: May God keep you away, for each of you has something like this: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2955 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2956","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin al-Nadr al-Jarudi told us, Ismail bin Zakaria told us Al-Asbahani in Al-Ray, Mahran bin Abi Amr told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Qaboos bin Abi Dhabyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him About them, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stayed in Mecca for thirteen years as a prophet. “So the following verse was revealed to him: ‘Enter me into an entrance of truth and bring me out. A source of truth} [Al-Isra: 80] with the opening of the meem, so he migrated, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2956 - True"
"2957","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Ali bin Duhaym Al-Shaybani told us in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Abu Gharza, Ali bin Hakim told us Al-Awdi, Ishaq bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Hamza bin Habib, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of them, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: {If I ask you about anything after that} [Al-Kahf: 76] Mahmoozatin “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. Rather, they agreed on the hadith of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, the story of Moses and Al-Khidr in its entirety, and it does not contain any mention of the two hamzas.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2957 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2958","Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr al-Khawas told us, Abu Imran Musa bin Ibrahim told us, Amr bin Muhammad al-Naqid told me, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told me, On the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he recited: {If you wish, you could have taken a reward for him} [Al-Kahf: 77] with the abbreviation: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in The long hadith\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2958 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2959","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Hafs Al-Khathami told us in Kufa, Harun bin Hatem, Sulaym bin Issa told us, on the authority of Hamza al-Zayat, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “The Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he used to recite: “And there was a king before them, who seized every good ship by force.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it was not He takes him out\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2959 - It includes Harun bin Hatim, and it is weak"
"2960","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Sharik Al-Bazzaz told us, Abu Saleh Abdul Ghaffar bin Daoud Al-Harrani told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, On the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite: {In the eye of Ham’ah} [Al-Kahf: 86] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2960 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2961","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Wasiti told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, who said: I was the buttocks of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him while he was riding a donkey, and he saw the sun when it was setting, so he said: “O Abu Dharr, where does this one set?” So I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “For it sets in a hot eye,” not quenched. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2961 - True"
"2962","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told us, Jeddi told us, Khalaf bin Hisham told us, Khalid bin Abdullah Al-Wasiti told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “I do not know how the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited ‘Ati’ or ‘Jathiya’, for they were “All together with dhamma.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2962 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2963","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih informed us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad informed us, Ibrahim bin Musa told us, Issa bin Yunus informed us, about Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Rahman bin Muhib, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu Al-Rijal, that Aisha used to send something as charity to the people of Suffah, And you say: Do not give any of them to a barbarian or a barbarian, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “They are the successors whom God Almighty said: {Then there were successors after them who neglected the prayer} [Maryam: 59] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2963 - Ubaidullah differed in his documentation, and Malik I do not know him, then it is interrupted."
"2964","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Abdi told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad al-Nufaili told us, Muhammad bin Salama al-Harrani told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Harrani told us, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, “that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He recited: (The heavens almost burst from it) with the Ya’ and the Nun {And the mountains fall down} [Maryam: 90] with the Ta {that they called for the Most Merciful a son And it is not befitting for the Most Merciful to take a son} [Maryam: 92] open after open “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2964 - True"
"2965","Abu Bakr bin Abi Dharm told me, in Kufa, Ubaid bin Ghannam bin Hafs bin Ghayath told us, Ubaid bin Yaish told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, On the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, he said: A man recited to Abdullah: {Taha} [Taha: 1] open, so Abdullah took it to him {Taha} [Taha: 1] broken, The man said to him: He means put your leg open. Abdullah said: “This is how the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, read it, and this is how Gabriel, peace be upon him, sent it down.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission, and he did not narrate it. “And Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah bin Asim narrated it with his chain of transmission, and he said about it: Then Abdullah said: By God, this is how The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught me it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2965 - True"
"2966","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Asim bin Omar Ibn Qatada, on the authority of Mahmoud Ibn Labid, on the authority of Abu Saeed, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “It should be opened. Gog and Magog, as God Almighty said: {From every mountain they descend} [Al-Anbiya’: 96] Ibn Ishaq said: In Abdullah’s recitation: “From every They descend, with a ji and tha’, like his saying: {From the graves they descend to their Lord} [Yasin: 51] which are the graves. “This is an authentic hadith. On the condition of a Muslim, and they did not produce it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2966 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2967","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Al-Hasan bin Bishr Al-Bajli told us, Al-Hakam bin Abdul-Malik told us, about Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may God be pleased with him, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: {And you see the people drunk, and they are not Biskara [Al-Hajj: 2] “Al-Bukhari narrated this hadith on the authority of Omar ibn Hafs ibn Ghayath, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, On the authority of Abu Saeed, may God be pleased with him, God says: “O Adam, bring out the fire.” The hadith is in its length and at its end: {And you will see the people drunk, but they are not drunk} [Al-Hajj: 2], and the more correct of the two hadiths is the hadith narrated by the Imam. Al-Bukhari"
"2968","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim Al-Bateen, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was expelled from Mecca, Abu Bakr: They expelled their Prophet, “Indeed, to Allah we belong, and to Him we shall return,” to destroy them. Then God Almighty revealed: {Permission has been given to those who fight, because they have been wronged, and indeed God is Powerful to grant them victory} [Al-Hajj: 39] “He said: “And it is the first verse. “It was revealed about fighting.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. No one other than Abu Hudhayfah narrated it, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2968 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2969","Muhammad bin Yazid al-Adl told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Yahya al-Qutayi told us, Yahya bin Rashid told us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hudha’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair Al-Laythi, on the authority of his father, who said: I said to Aisha, may God be pleased with her: O Mother of the Believers, how was he? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recites this letter: {And those who give what they give} [Al-Mu’minun: 60]. She said: I bear witness that I have heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him."
"2970","Muhammad bin Ali bin Duhaym Al-Shaybani informed me, in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza Abu Ghassan told us, Yahya bin Salamah told us. Ibn Kuhayl, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite: “You were arrogant and deserted about it.” [Al-Mu’minun: 67] He said: The polytheists used to desert the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2971","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil ibn al-Hasan ibn Issa told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, Nu’aym ibn Hammad told me, and Ahmad ibn Jamil told me Al-Marwazi and Abdah bin Sulaiman Al-Tarsusi said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, Saeed bin Yazid informed Abu Shuja’, on the authority of Abu Al-Samh Darraj bin Samaan, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham Suleiman bin Amr bin Abd Al-Awari, on the authority of Abu Saeed, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him: {And therein they will grieve} [Al-Mu’minun: 104] He said: “The fire distorts, so his upper lip shrinks, until it reaches the middle of his head, and relaxes.” His lower lip until it reaches his navel.” This is an authentic hadith from the chain of transmission of the Egyptians, and they did not narrate it. “I heard Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub He says: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri say: I asked Yahya bin Ma’in about the hadiths of Darraj, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, and he said: “This Authentic chain of transmission"
"2972","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Daoud bin Sulaiman Al-Zahid told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid Al-Maliki told us in Al-Ray, Suwayd bin Saeed told us Al-Anbari, Al-Walid bin Jundub told us, Bakr bin Khunnis told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubadah bin Nasi, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ghanam, He said: I asked Muadh about the words of God Almighty: “It is not appropriate for us to take” [Al-Furqan: 18] or to take a decision. He said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “It is recited: {that we may take action other than you} [Al-Furqan: 18] with the accusative case of nūn.”"
"2973","Abu Bakr bin Dawud narrated to us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Junaid narrated to us, Suwayd bin Saeed narrated to us, Al-Walid bin Jundub narrated to us, Bakr bin Khunnis narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubadah bin Nasi, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ghanam, he said: I asked Muadh bin Jabal about the saying of God Almighty: Did it defeat the Romans?} [Al-Rum: 2] or did it defeat? He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, read to me: {Have you not defeated the Romans?} [Al-Rum: 1] We did not write down the two hadiths except with this chain of transmission, except that Muhammad bin Saeed al-Shami is not a condition of the Book.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2973 - Muhammad bin Saeed is crucified and perished, and Bakr bin Khanis is abandoned."
"2974","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Fudayl bin Marzuq, on the authority of Attiya Al-Awfi, he said: I read to Ibn Umar: {It is Allah who created you from weakness, then made after weakness strength, then after strength He made weakness And Shaybah} [Al-Rum: 54] Then Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, said: {It is God who created you from weakness, then made after weakness strength, then made after Strength, weakness, and gray hair.} [Al-Rum: 54] Then Ibn Umar said: “I recited to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as it was recited to me, and he took action against me, as “I took it against you.” Atiyya al-Awfi was the only one to use it and did not use it as evidence, and Muslim used al-Fudayl ibn Marzuq as evidence.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2974 - Attiya was not used as evidence"
"2975","Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told me, Ali bin Saeed bin Abdullah Al-Askari told me, Al-Hassan bin Arafa Al-Abdi told us, Ammar bin Muhammad told us, On the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: {So no soul knows what has been hidden.” “For them is the comfort of eyes.” [Al-Sajdah: 17] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2975 - True"
"2976","Abu al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Muzaki told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Muhammad bin Musaffa al-Homsi told us, Baqiya told us, Abbad bin Ishaq told me, Abdullah bin Waqid told me, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that “ He recited: {And the sea supplies it} [Luqman: 27] Raised: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2976 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2977","Abu Al-Hussein Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Quta’i informed us of Baghdad from the origin of his book. Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Abd told us Al-Aziz bin Abdullah bin Abi Farwa, Suleiman bin Bilal told us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala bin Abdullah bin Abi Farwa, on the authority of Qatun bin Wahb, On the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left Uhud, he passed by Musab bin Umair. He was killed on his way, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood over him and prayed for him, then he recited this verse: {Among the believers are men who are truthful. Whatever they covenanted with God, some of them have fulfilled their promise, and some of them are waiting, but they have not changed it with the slightest change.} [Al-Ahzab: 23] Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “I bear witness that these are martyrs with God on the Day of Resurrection, so go to them and visit them, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, he will not greet them.” “No one until the Day of Resurrection unless they respond to him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2977 - I consider it fabricated"
"2978","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Al-Harith, the client of Banu Hashim, told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn al-Bilamani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: There were captives in their dwellings.” “This is a version that we did not write, except on the authority of Abu al-Abbas, and the two sheikhs did not use Ibn al-Bilamani as evidence.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2978 - It is not authentic"
"2979","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to me, Bishr bin Musa Al-Asadi narrated to me, Al-Humaidi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, “ The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: “Their hearts were dismayed. They said: What has your Lord said?” [Saba: 23] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim. And they did not bring it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2979 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2980","Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Saleh ibn Muhammad ibn Habib al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Dawud ibn al-Musayyab narrated to us. Al-Dhabi, Abu Asim narrated to us, Ismail bin Nafi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, “ The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: “And indeed He has led astray many mountains among you” [Yasin: 62] abbreviated: “His narrators are all trustworthy, except for Ismail bin Rafi’. They did not use it as evidence.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2980 - In its chain of transmission, Ismail bin Rafi’ is perished"
"2981","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Hashim, Al-Hafiz, told us dictation, Tamim bin Muhammad bin Tamghaj told us, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah, and Abu Usama, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdul Rahman bin Hatib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubair May God be pleased with them both. He said: Al-Zubair said: When it was revealed: “Indeed, you are dead and they will be dead, then on the Day of Resurrection you will be with your Lord.” You will dispute} [Az-Zumar: 31] Al-Zubair said: O Messenger of God, will what happened between us in this world be repeated to us along with the specific sins? He said: “Yes, that will be repeated to them until they pay each person his due.” Al-Zubayr said: “By God, the matter is severe.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2981 - True"
"2982","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told me, Yazid bin Harun told me, Hammad bin Salamah told me, about... Thabit, about a month ago, on the authority of Asmaa bint Yazid, may God be pleased with her, who said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting: (O My servants who They have been extravagant over themselves, do not despair of God’s mercy, for God forgives all sins, and does not care.) “This is a strange and loud hadith, and I was not mentioned in This book of mine is about a month other than this one hadith.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2982 - Strange"
"2983","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me: (Indeed, I am the Provider of Power, the Most Powerful) “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2983 - True"
"2984","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya the Martyr told us, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl bin Ghazwan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: {Those who believe and I follow them.” Their descendants in faith, We will join with them their descendants} [At-Tur: 21] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2984 - True"
"2985","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Shadhan al-Jawhari told us, Zakaria bin Adi told us, Waki` told us, Israel told us, On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: “I read to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him: “Is there anyone who will remind” of the “dhal”? Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Is there anyone who will remember” [Al-Qamar: 15] with the “dāl” “This is a hadith that they have agreed to narrate.” From the hadith of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, briefly.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2985 - They reported it briefly"
"2986","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq al-Saghani told us, Husayn bin Muhammad al-Marwudi told us, Abu Abd al-Rahman told us. Al-Artabani, cousin of Abdullah bin Aoun, on the authority of Asim Al-Jahdari, on the authority of Abu Bakra, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He recited: {Reclining on a green and beautiful place of honor} [Al-Rahman: 76] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2986 - Interrupted and Asim did not reach Abu Bakra"
"2987","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Salam bin Sulayman Al-Madani told us, Abu Amr bin Al-Ala’, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: {So they drink the drink of heme} [Al-Waqi’ah: 55] “This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2987 - A weak peace"
"2988","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sirafi told us, Abdullah bin Raja told us, Saeed bin Salamah told us, Saleh told me Ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Issa Ibn Masoud Ibn Al-Hakam Al-Zarqi, on the authority of his grandmother Habiba bint Shariq, that she was with her daughter, the daughter of Al-Ajama in During the days of Hajj in Mina, he said: Then Budail ibn Warqa’ came to them on the camel of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he called out that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, God, peace and blessings be upon him, says: “Whoever is fasting, let him break his fast, for these are the days of eating and drinking.” This hadith is not part of the entirety of this book."
"2989","Omar bin Muhammad bin Safwan Al-Jumahi told us, in Mecca, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abu Ubaid Marwan bin Muawiya told us, on the authority of Hammad, On the authority of Budail bin Maysarah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He reads: “Faruh and fragrance” [Al-Waqi’ah: 89] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2990","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrafi told me, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin al-Faraj al-Azraq told me, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj: On the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: So divorce them before their waiting period.” “Muslim narrated this hadith in its length, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, that he heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayman being asked about Abd “By Allah, Ibn Umar, about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating, and I think he mentioned this word.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2990 - Muslim reported a longer hadith"
"2991","Ahmad bin Mansour Al-Hafiz told me about Al-Tabaran, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Nasr told me, Abu Hatim Sahl bin Muhammad told us, Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Al-Hawajib Al-Kufi said: I was holding Al-Amash by the hand and Yusuf Al-Samti on the other side, so he asked him about the Almighty’s saying: {By Al-Rajaz} [Al-Muddaththir: 5] He said: I took up that, then he said: I recited the Qur’an to Yahya bin Wathhab thirty times, and Yahya recited it to Alqamah. Alqamah recited to Abdullah, “And Abdullah recited to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, (and the rajaz, so abandon) with a kasra on the r.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2991 - True"
"2992","Mukarram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told us, Abu Al-Ahwas Muhammad bin Al-Haytham told us, Muhammad bin Katheer Al-Maisi told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting: {And the rajaz, so abandon it} [Al-Muddaththir: 5] by raising the rā’, and he said: “They are the idols.”"
"2993","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Dawood al-Zahid and Abu Sa`id Ahmad bin Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told us, saying: Ali bin al-Hussein bin al-Junaid told us, they told us: Ahmad bin Salih, Abdul Razzaq told us, and Muammar told us, Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was speaking about the period of revelation, said: “So I said: ‘Gather me together, and gather me together.’ Then God Almighty revealed: {O you! Al-Muddaththir} [Al-Muddaththir: 2], Arise and warn, and your Lord, so exalt Him, and purify your clothes, and abandon filth. He said: “They are the idols.” This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, they did not narrate it with this wording."
"2994","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told me, Affan bin Muslim Al-Saffar told me, Sufyan bin Uyaynah Al-Hilali told me, On the authority of Asim ibn Abi al-Najjoud, on the authority of Zirr ibn Hubaysh, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: “We were with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in Ghar, so it was revealed: {And the Mursalat by custom} [Al-Mursalat: 1] So I took it from his mouth, and indeed his mouth was moist with it, so I do not know with which one it was. He concluded: {So with what hadith? After Him they will believe” [Al-Mursalat: 50] or “And when it is said to them, “Bow,” they do not bow” [Al-Mursalat: 48] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2994 - True"
"2995","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Thabit bin Yazid Abu Zaid told us, Hilal bin Khabbab, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “You will be gathered barefoot and naked.” Uncircumcised.” Then his wife said: Do we look at each other’s private parts? He said: “O so-and-so. {For every one of them on that day will have an affair that will enrich him} [Abs: 37] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2995 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2996","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ahmad bin Ali Al-Khazzaz told us, Saeed bin Suleiman told us, Al-Mu’affa bin Imran told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Farwa, on the authority of Yahya bin Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He used to recite: ‘And what is in the unseen, with two suspicions,’ with the word ‘This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration,’ and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2996 - Ishaq is abandoned"
"2997","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Jarrahhi told me about Marwa, Yahya bin Masawayh Al-Dhuli told us, Suwayd bin Nasr told us, Hatim bin Ismail, and Kharijah bin Musab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was reciting,” so he sew you, so he modified you, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2997 - True"
"2998","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us, dictating, in the month of Rabi’ al-Awwal in the year three hundred and ninety-nine, Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Ishaq bin Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Ishaq bin Suleiman al-Razi told us, Abu Jafar Al-Razi, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliya, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said, “He recites: {Yes, My signs have come to you, but you denied them and were arrogant, and you were of the disbelievers} [Az-Zumar: 59] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”"
"2999","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Yahya bin Al-Mughirah Al-Saadi told me, Harun bin Al-Mughirah told us, Anbasa narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amra, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he said: “Do you know what the capacity of Hell? He said: I said: I do not know. He said: “Yes, by God, you do not know. Indeed, between the width of the lobe of their ear and the head of his neck, there is a journey of seventy autumns taking place in it.” “Valleys of pus and blood,” so I said: “Rivers?” He said: “No, but valleys.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2999 - True\n Then Ibn Abbas said: Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, may God be pleased with her, told me that she asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about these things. The verse: {And they have not estimated God as He deserves, while the earth as a whole is His grip on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens are rolled up in His right hand} He said: He says: “I “The mighty one, I am, and the Lord will glorify himself.” He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, shook his pulpit until we said, “Let them fall down.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”"
"3000","Ali bin Isa bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told us, Abu Bakr and Uthman, the sons of Abi Shaybah, told us, they said: Abu Osama, on the authority of Omar bin Muhammad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He asked Gabriel, peace be upon him, about this verse: {And the trumpet was blown, and it struck whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on earth, except whom God wills} who Those whom God did not want to stun? He said: They are the martyrs of God Almighty. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3000 - Sahih according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3001","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Daoud Al-Zahid told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Zayd bin Akhzam Al-Tai told us, Aamir bin Mudrak told us. Al-Harithi, told us by Utba bin Yaqzan, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “No Muslim does good, nor does any infidel, but God rewards him.” He said: So we said: O Messenger of God, what is God’s reward to the infidel? He said: “If he was a relative, or gave charity or did a good deed, God will reward him with wealth, children, health, and the like.” He said: So we said: What is his reward in the Hereafter? He said: “A punishment other than the punishment.” He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: “Enter Pharaoh’s family to the severest punishment” [Ghafir: 46]. This is how the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, read the verse “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3001 - Utbah bin Yaqzan is weak"
"3002","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Bakhtari Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, Al-Ajlah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Dhiyāl ibn Harmala, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: One day Quraysh gathered, and Utbah ibn Rabia bin Abdul Shams and said: O Muhammad, are you better or Abdullah? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Have you finished?” He said: Yes, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “In the Name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful {Ham, a revelation from the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} [Fussilat: 2] until it reached {then if Turn away, and say, “I warn you of a thunderbolt like the thunderbolt of Ad and Thamud.” [Fussilat: 13] “And Utbah said to him: It is enough for you. You do not have anything other than this?”"
"3003","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazyid told us, Muhammad bin Shuaib told us, Shayban bin Abd told us The Most Gracious, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Razin, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: {And indeed For knowledge of the Hour} [Al-Zukhruf: 61] He said: “The emergence of Jesus before the Day of Resurrection.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3003 - True"
"3004","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ali bin Abdullah Al-Barqi, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, “When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would ride His mount said, “Allahu Akbar” three times, then said: “Glory be to Him who has subjugated this to us, and we would not have been near to it, and indeed to our Lord we are returning.” [Al-Zukhruf: 14] “This is A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3004 - True"
"3005","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali Al-Maamari told us, Abu Musab Al-Zuhri told us, and Hisham bin Ammar Al-Sulami told us, they said: Hatem bin Ismail told us, Muawiyah bin Abi Muzard told us, a client of Banu Hashim, my uncle Abu Al-Hubab Saeed bin Yassar told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. May God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Indeed, God created creation, so that when He had finished with them, the womb would stand up and say: This The position of the one who seeks refuge with you from estrangement. He said: Yes, are you not satisfied that I should keep in touch with him who has joined you, and cut off whoever has cut off ties with you? She said: Yes, he said: Then that is for you.” He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Recite, if you wish: {So would it be possible, if you were given authority, to Make corruption on earth and sever your ties of kinship} [Muhammad: 22] to the Almighty’s saying: {Or upon the hearts of which are locks?} [Muhammad: 24] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3005 - True"
"3006","Abu Amr bin Abi Ja`far Al-Hairi narrated to me, Hamid bin Muhammad bin Shuaib narrated to me, Hafs bin Omar Al-Duri narrated to us, Hamza bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, on the authority of my father Al-Haytham Saeed bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Nufay’ Abi Dawud, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, may God be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. It reads: {Is it possible that you would, if you were given power, do corruption on earth?} [Muhammad: 22]\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3006 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3007","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Dawud al-Zahid told me, Abu al-Qasim al-Abbas bin al-Fadl bin Shazan al-Muqri told me, my father told us, Muhammad bin Issa told us The reciter, Abu Nu’aym and Qabisa told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them, he said: “He recited The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: {So remember, for you are only a reminder. You have no control over them} [Al-Ghashiya: 22] with Al-Saad {except those who turn away and disbelieve} [Al-Ghashiya: 23] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3007 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3008","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Yusuf bin Musa Al-Marwudi told us, Ahmad bin Salih told us, Abu Mutarrif told us, on the authority of Sufyan Bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to recite: No, rather they do not honor the orphan, nor encourage the needy to feed the needy, and they eat and love, all of which are marked with a yā’. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3008 - True"
"3009","Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marw, Abdullah bin Ali Al-Ghazal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of “the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, read it to him: {On that day no one will be punished with his punishment, nor It is authenticated} [Al-Fajr: 26] It was authenticated by Uhud, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and the companion who did not name him in his chain of transmission was named by someone else, Malik ibn Al-Huwairit »\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3009 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3010","Abu Al-Abbas Ahmad bin Harun Al-Faqih told us, Abdullah bin Mahmoud told us, Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, Humaid bin Hammad Abu Al-Jahm told us, Aidh bin Shurayh narrated to us, I heard Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a terrier around him, and he said: “If only Hardship came and he entered this hole. Then ease came and entered upon it and took it out. He said: Then God Almighty revealed: {For indeed, with hardship comes ease. Hardship brings ease} [Explanation: 6] “This is a strange hadith, except that the two sheikhs did not use Aidh bin Shurayh as evidence.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3010 - Humaid bin Hammad was the only one to narrate it on the authority of A’idh, and Humaid is a denier of hadith like A’idh."
"3011","Abu Abdul Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Al-Wazir Al-Tajer told us, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris Al-Razi told us, Muhammad bin Yazid bin Sinan al-Rahwi reported from Maqil bin Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas Radi May God bless them both, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Ubayy: “I will recite to you a surah,” so he said to him My father: You ordered that to my father? He said: “Yes,” and he recited: “Those who disbelieved from among the People of the Book and the polytheists were not to separate themselves until clear proof came to them, a messenger from God reciting Purified pages} [Al-Bayyinah: 2] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3011 - Muhammad’s weakness al-Daraqutni"
"3012","Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Saeed bin Abi Ayyub informed, then Yahya bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, read this Verse: {On that day its tidings will be told} [Al-Zalzalah: 4] He said: “Do you know what its tidings are?” They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “For its news is that it will bear witness against every male and female slave of what he has done on its back, that it will say: He has done deeds.” Such-and-such on such-and-such a day. This is her news: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3012 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3013","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Hatim Al-Ijli told us, and Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, they said: Nuh bin Abi Habib told us, Abd told us Al-Malik bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Dhimari, Sufyan Al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, “that The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: He thought that his wealth had left him eternally, by breaking the sin. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3013 - Abd al-Malik is weak"
"3014","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Ali Al-Hanafi told us, Abd Al-Hamid bin Bahram told us, about the month Ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma’ bint Yazid, may God be pleased with her, who said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting: “To confuse the Quraysh, to confuse them.” The journey of winter and summer} [Quraysh: 2] “This is a strange and loud hadith on this subject, and the two sheikhs do not use Shahr ibn Hawshab as evidence.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3014 - Strange"
"3015","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Ya’la Al-Mawsili told us, Azhar bin Marwan told us, Abd Al-Warith bin Saeed told us, On the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hussein, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: {Indeed, We have given you Al-Kawthar} [Al-Kawthar: 1] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3015 - Rather, Amr is Ibn Ubaid and he is weak"
"3016","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ibrahim bin Musa told us, Abu Anas Muhammad bin Anas, narrated by Al-A’mash, on the authority of Talha, and Zubaid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the string of praising the name of your Lord Most High, and say, ‘O disbelievers, and say, ‘He is God, One.’” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3016 - Muhammad Razi is unique in his hadiths"
"3017","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Abu Dawud told us, Shu’bah told us, Amr bin Murrah told me, I heard Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, said: When this surah was revealed: When victory and conquest came, he recited it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until he concluded it, then he said: “I and my companions will remain on a separate stage, and the people will remain on a separate stage. There will be no migration after the conquest.” This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3017 - True\n Interpretation of Surat Al-Fatihah: “The news about the obligation of reciting it in every rak’ah, and pronouncing “In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful” aloud. I presented these narrations in the Book of Prayer.”"
"3018","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar Al-Atardi told us, Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “And We have given you seven of the repeated verses” [Al-Hijr: 87] He said: The Opener of the Book, then He said: {In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds} [Al-Fatihah: 2] So I said to my father: Sa`id told you that Ibn Abbas said: {In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} [Al-Fatihah: 1] verse. He said: “Yes.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. This chapter is complete in the Book of Prayer.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3018 - True"
"3019","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abu Usama told us, Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told me, On the authority of Al-Alaa bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Shall I not teach you a surah that has not been revealed in the Torah, nor in the Gospel, nor in the Psalms, nor in the Criterion like it?” So I said: Yes. He said: “I hope that you will not leave that door until you know it.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and I stood with him. So he started talking to me while my hand was in his hand, and I started to slow down for fear that he would leave before he could tell me about it, so when I approached the door, I said: Oh Messenger of God, the surah that you promised me. He said: “How do you recite when you stand up for prayer?” So I recited: the opening of the Book, and he said: “This is it, and it is the seven times repeated. “And the Great Qur’an which I have been given.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and no one has narrated it. It was narrated by Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Abd The Most Gracious, with another chain of transmission,"
"3020","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Maslamah told us, regarding what was read to Malik, on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, the client of Aamir bin Kuraiz, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him And he greeted him like that\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3019 - According to Muslim’s condition\n . . . . . . . ."
"3021","Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty saying: {Praise To God belongs, Lord of the worlds.} [Al-Fatihah: 2] He said: “The jinn and mankind.” Al-Hakim said: “Let the seeker of this knowledge know that the interpretation of the companion who witnessed According to the two sheikhs, revelation and revelation are a chain of transmission hadith."
"3022","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saffar al-Adl told me, Ahmad ibn Nasr told me, Amr ibn Talha al-Qannad told me, Asbat ibn Nasr told me, On the authority of Ismail bin Abdul Rahman Al-Suddi, on the authority of Murrah Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, and on the authority of people among the companions of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: (The King of the Day of Judgment) said: “It is the Day of Judgment.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3022 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3023","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Omar bin Saad Abu Dawud told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, in His Almighty’s saying: {The straight path} [Al-Fatihah: 6] He said: “It is the Book of God.” This is a hadith It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3023 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3024","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told me, in Kufa, Al-Haytham bin Khalid told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Al-Hasan bin Saleh told us, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, said: {The straight path} [Al-Fatihah: 6] “It is Islam, and it is “It is wider than what is between the heaven and the earth.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3024 - True"
"3025","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told me, Abu Al-Nadr told us, Hamza bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying {The Straight Path} [Al-Fatihah: 6] He said: “He is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And his two companions.” He said: So we mentioned that to Al-Hasan, and he said: “By God, he spoke the truth and was sincere. By God, he is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr and Omar.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3025 - True"
"3026","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Hakim bin Jubayr Al-Asadi told me, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Surat Al-Baqarah contains a dominant verse, that is, the Qur’an. It should not be read in a home.” And there is a devil in him, but the verse of the Throne will come out of him.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3026 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3027","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaydah told us, on the authority of Hakim Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, everything has a hump, and “The pillar of the Qur’an is Surah Al-Baqarah” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3027 - True"
"3028","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, Ubaid Allah bin Abi Humaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih Al-Hudhaili, on the authority of Maqil bin Yasar, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was given Surat Al-Baqarah from the remembrance The first: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3028 - Ubaidullah said that Ahmad abandoned his hadith"
"3029","Abu Al-Qasim Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us in Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, Adam bin Abi told us Iyas, Shu`bah reported, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: “Recite Surat Al-Baqarah in your homes, for “Satan does not enter a house in which Surat Al-Baqarah is recited.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3029 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3030","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaydah told us, on the authority of Hakim bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The mistress of the verse of the Qur’an is the verse of the Throne.” This hadith The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”"
"3031","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Affan told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Al-Ash’ath bin Abdul Rahman told us, On the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abu al-Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Nu’man ibn Bashir, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Indeed, God has written a book Two thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth, and He sent down from Him two verses with which He concluded Surah Al-Baqarah, which must not be recited in a house for three nights. Then Satan brings it near.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3031 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3032","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saffar told me, Ahmad ibn Nasr told me, Amr ibn Talha al-Qannad told me, Asbat ibn Nasr told me, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Murrah Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him: {The sign of that book} [Al-Baqarah: 2] He said: “{The sign} [Al-Baqarah: 1]: The letter of the name of God, and {the Book} [Al-Baqarah: 2]: the Qur’an, {about which there is no doubt} [Al-Baqarah: 2]: there is no doubt about it. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3032 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3033","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, about Al-A'mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, said: They mentioned to Abdullah the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, And their faith, he said: Then Abdullah said: “Indeed, the matter of Muhammad was clear to whoever saw it, and by Him there is no god other than Him. No believer has believed better than belief in the unseen. Then he recited: {This is the Book about which there is no doubt} [Al-Baqarah: 2] up to the Almighty’s saying: {They believe in the unseen} [Al-Baqarah: 3] “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3033 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3034","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, Mas’ar told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Maysara, On the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Sabit, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: “The stones that he named In the Qur’an, “God’s fuel is people and stones, stones of sulphur. God Almighty created them with Him as He willed or as He willed.” This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3034 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3035","Abdullah bin Musa Al-Saydalani told me, Ismail bin Qutaybah told me, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, On the authority of Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “God cast Adam out of Paradise before he Anyone enters it. God Almighty said: {Indeed, I will place a caliph on earth. They said: Will You place therein someone who will spread corruption therein and shed blood?} [Al-Baqarah: 30] And He Therein existed two thousand years before creation the jinn, the sons of jinn, and they spread corruption on earth and shed blood. Then when God Almighty said: {Indeed, I will put The earth as a successor. They said, “Will You place therein someone who will spread corruption therein and shed blood?” [Al-Baqarah: 30] meaning the jinn, the descendants of the jinn. So when they spread corruption in the earth, He was sent There were soldiers of angels against them, and they struck them until they chased them into the islands of the seas. He said: Then the angels said: {Will You place therein someone who will cause corruption therein} [Al-Baqarah: 30] as those jinn, the sons of the jinn, did? He said: Then God said: {Indeed, I know what you do not know} [Al-Baqarah: 30] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3035 - True"
"3036","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told me, al-Hasan ibn Issa told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, al-Nufaili told us, Muhammad ibn Salamah told us, on the authority of Khaseef Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “When God had finished creating Adam and put the spirit into him, he sneezed. He said: Praise be to God. Then his Lord said to him: May your Lord have mercy on you. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. Attab narrated it, on the authority of Khusaif, and there is no condition. This book\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3036 - True"
"3037","Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-San’ani informed us of Mecca, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, Awf Al-Abdi, on the authority of Qasamah bin Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God created Adam From the depths of the entire earth, and his descendants came forth according to that, among them the white and the black, the brown and the red, and among them the In between, and among them are the easy, the bad, and the good.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3037 - True"
"3038","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abd Al-Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, about Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Yahya ibn Damrah, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Indeed, Adam was A tall man, like a tall palm tree, with a lot of hair on his head. When he rode the sinner, his private parts appeared to him, and he had not seen it before that. So he ran away into Paradise, and a tree clung to him, and he said to it: Send me. She said: I did not send you. He said: And his Lord called to him: O Adam, will you flee? He said: O Lord, I have made You feel ashamed. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3038 - True"
"3039","Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Qaari told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Abu Tawbah Al-Rabi’ bin Nafi’ Al-Halabi told me, Muawiyah bin Salam told us, Zaid bin Salam told me that he heard Abu Salam say: Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, told me that a man said: O Messenger of God, a prophet Was it Adam? He said: “Yes, a teacher who speaks.” He said: How much distance was there between him and Noah? He said: “Ten centuries.” He said: How much time was there between Noah and Abraham? He said: “Ten centuries.” They said: O Messenger of God, how many were the apostles? He said: “Three hundred and fifteen large numbers of people.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3039 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3040","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both: {Enter the gate prostrating} [An-Nisa: 154] He said: “A narrow gate.” . He said: “Kneel down” {And say: “Hatta”} [Al-Baqarah: 58] He said: “For forgiveness,” and they said: “Wheat,” and they entered upon their wheat.” That is the saying of the Most High, “So He changed those who They wronged in words other than what was said to them} [Al-Baqarah: 59] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3040 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3041","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “How can you ask about something when you have the Book of God? I tell you the news about God, and He has told you that they wrote a book with their own hands, and they changed and distorted it, and said: This is from God, and they bought It is a small price, and with you is the Book of God, pure and untainted. By God, none of them will ask you about what was revealed to you. “This is a hadith.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3041 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3042","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Yusuf bin Musa told us, Abd al-Malik bin Harun bin Antara told us, On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The Jews of Khaybar used to fight Ghatafan, so whenever They met, and the Jews of Khaybar were defeated, so the Jews sought refuge with this supplication: O God, we ask you by the truth of Muhammad, the unlettered prophet, whom you promised us You will bring it out for us at the end of time, unless you help us against them. He said: Whenever they met, they would recite this supplication, but they defeated Ghatafan. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent, they disbelieved in him, so God revealed: {And they used to seek victory before.} [Al-Baqarah: 89] “With you, O Muhammad, against the disbelievers.” . . » Necessity led to its inclusion in the interpretation, and it is strange in its hadith.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3042 - There is no need for that, that is, to remove him, for Abdullah is abandoned and perished."
"3043","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali bin Duhaym al-Shaybani told me in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Abu Gharza al-Ghifari, Qabisa told us Ibn Uqba, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim Al-Bateen, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, {And you will find them the most eager of people to Life} [Al-Baqarah: 96] He said: “The Jews” {and among those who associate others} [Al-Baqarah: 96] He said: “The non-Arabs” “The two sheikhs agreed on the support of the Companion’s interpretation, and this An authentic chain of narration based on their condition, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3043 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3044","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both: {One of them wishes that he were lived for a thousand years} [Al-Baqarah: 96] He said: “It is a saying If one of the non-Arabs sneezes, he shakes his head.” Narrated by Qais bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyas, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s words, adding more words"
"3045","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Sahl bin Askar told us, Muhammad bin Yusuf told us, Qays bin Al-Rabi’ told us, On the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Ja'far ibn Iyas, on the authority of Sa'id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty's saying: {And you will find them The people who are most eager for life.} [Al-Baqarah: 96] He said: “These are the People of the Book.” {And among those who associate others, one of them wishes he could be lived for a thousand years, but that is not the case. By removing him from the torment so that he may live longer} [Al-Baqarah: 96] He said: “It is the saying of one of them to his companion: He shook the joy of sending an incense festival.”"
"3046","Ahmad bin Kamil bin Khalaf Al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Ruh Al-Madani told us, Shababah bin Suwar told us, Abu Uqba Al-Homsi told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Ajlan, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “My two ministers From the sky: Gabriel and Michael, and from the people of the earth: Abu Bakr and Omar “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, but it is known This hadith is from the hadith of Sawar bin Musab, on the authority of Atiya al-Awfi, on the authority of Abu Saeed, and it is not a requirement of this book.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3046 - True"
"3047","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Saad Al-Awfi told us, Abi told us, Sawwar bin Musab told us, on the authority of Atiya Al-Awfi, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said, “Indeed, I have two ministers from the people of heaven, and two ministers from the people of the earth. As for my two ministers from the people of heaven: Gabriel and Michael, and as for my two ministers from the people of earth: Abu Bakr and Omar. Narrated by Abu Ubaid. Al-Qasim bin Salam, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Atiya, with another wording"
"3048","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Ali bin Abdul-Aziz told us, Abu Ubaid told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Saad Al-Ta’i, on the authority of Atiya bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, mentioned the owner of the pictures, He said: “Gabriel is on his right, and Mikael is on his left.” Abu Ubaid said: “They are neglected in the hadith.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3048 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3049","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi narrated to us, Muhadhar bin Al-Muwari narrated to us, Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Saad Al-Ta’i, on the authority of Atiya bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Gabriel on the authority of On his right, and Mikael on his left, and he is the one who made the pictures.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3049 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3050","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Husayn bin Abdul Al-Rahman, on the authority of Imran bin Al-Harith, said: While we were with Ibn Abbas, a man came to him and said: “Where did you come from?” He said: From Iraq. He said: “From which of them?” He said: From Kufa. He said: “So what is the news?” He said: I left them while they were talking that Ali was leaving them, so he said: “Don’t say, ‘You have no father.’ If we had felt that, we would not have married his wives.” Nor did we divide his inheritance.” Then he said: “I will tell you about that. The devils were eavesdropping, and one of them used to bring a word of truth.” The people heard it, so they lied with it seventy lies, and it absorbed the hearts of the people. So God informed Solomon, son of David, of that, and he took it. So he buried it under the throne, and when Solomon died, a devil rose in the way and said: Shall I not guide you to the treasure of Solomon, which no one has a treasure like? His unspeakable treasure? They said: Yes, so they took it out, and behold, it was magic, and the nations copied it, and what remained of it was what the people of Iraq were talking about, so God sent down an excuse. Solomon,” and he said: {And they followed what the devils recited concerning the kingdom of Solomon, and Solomon did not disbelieve, but the devils disbelieved} [Al-Baqarah: 102] verse, this is a hadith. . . . . . . . . . . .\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3050 - Sahih. . . . . . . . . . . . . ."
"3051","Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani in Kufa, narrated by Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri, narrated by Ya’la bin Ubaid, narrated by Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Umair Ibn Saeed Al-Nakhai said: I heard Ali, may God be pleased with him, telling the people: “The Arabs call this flower Al-Zahra, and the non-Arabs call it Al-Zahra.” Anahid, and the two angels were judging among the people, so she came to them, and each of them wanted her without the knowledge of the other, and one of them said To its owner: My brother, I have some matter in my mind, I want to mention it to you. He said: Remember him, my brother. Perhaps what is in my soul is like what is in your soul. So they agreed on a matter about that, and the woman said to them: Will you not tell me? By what you ascend to heaven, and by what you descend to earth. They said: In the name of God, the Greatest, with it we go down and with it we ascend. So she said: I am not going to give you what you want until you inform me of it. One of them said to his friend: Teach it to him. He said: How can we suffer from the severity of God’s punishment? The other said: We hope for the vast mercy of God, so he taught it to him, and she spoke it, and she flew to the sky, and an angel in the sky was frightened by her ascension. Then he bowed his head and did not sit up yet, and God transformed it and it became a star.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3051 - True"
"3052","So Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Tamimi narrated to us, Yazid bin Harun informed us, Suleiman informed us Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “Al-Zahra was a woman among her people who was called Bidha.” He said Al-Hakim: “The two chains of narration are authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and the purpose of narrating the two hadiths is to mention Harut and Marut and the previous decree of God. In them, and for Venus.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3052 - True"
"3053","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Bakhtari Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Abu Suleiman, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: It was revealed: {So wherever they turn, there is the face of God} [Al-Baqarah: 115]: “That “You may pray wherever your voluntary mount takes you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it."
"3054","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Adl told me, Ahmad ibn Nasr told me, Amr ibn Talha al-Qannad told me, Asbat ibn Nasr told me, on the authority of al-Suddi, on the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the words of God Almighty: {Those to whom We have given the Book recite it as it should be recited} [Al-Baqarah: 121] He said: “They make lawful what is lawful, and make unlawful what is unlawful, and do not distort it from its proper place.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3054 - Sahih. . . . . . . ."
"3055","Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty saying: {And when his Lord tested Abraham with words} [Al-Baqarah: 124] He said: “God tested him with purity, five times in the head and five times in the body; On the head: trimming the moustache, rinsing the mouth, using the siwak, and parting the head. On the body: trimming the nails, shaving the pubes, Circumcision, plucking the armpits, and washing the place of defecation and urine with water: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3055 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3056","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, on the authority of Makram Al-Bazzaz, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Qasim bin Abi told us Ayoub, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: God said to his Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Purify my house for those who circumambulate and seclude themselves.” And the bowing and prostration” means circumambulation before prayer, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Circumambulation of the Kaaba is in the same position as prayer, except that God The logic has been permissible in it, so whoever speaks does not speak except good.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. “But this is known.” Hadith, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3056 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3057","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Ashyab told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, who said: “God Almighty said to His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Purify them.” “My house is for those who circumambulate and seclude themselves and those who kneel and prostrate.” This circumambulation before prayer follows half of the text, and the second half of the hadith of Al-Qasim ibn Abi Ayyub \"\"\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3057 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3058","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr Al-Humaidi told us, Fudayl bin Iyad, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The circumambulation There is prayer at home, except that God has made speech permissible therein, so whoever speaks therein should only speak good.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3058 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3059","Hamza bin Al-Abbas Al-Aqbi told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Aam told us\n R. Al-Aqdi, Zakaria bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Bishr bin Asim, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, narrated to us, He said: “Ibrahim Khalil al-Rahman came from Armenia with Sakina. A guide for him as to the location of the house, just as a spider occupies its house. Then Abraham dug from under the sakina and revealed some of the rules. He moved the base of it without thirty men. He said: So he said:. . . . . . \"\"\n . . . . ."
"3060","On the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The first thing that was abrogated from the Qur’an, as was mentioned to us regarding The qiblah. God said: {And to God belongs the east and the west. So wherever you turn, there is the face of God.} [Al-Baqarah: 115] So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, faced So he prayed towards the Holy House, and left the ancient House, and God Almighty said: {The foolish among the people will say, “What has turned them away from the direction of direction which they used to worship?” upon it} [Al-Baqarah: 142] meaning the Holy House, so it abrogated it, and God transferred it to the ancient House, and God Almighty said: {And from where you came out, then “Your face is towards the Sacred Mosque, and wherever you are, turn your faces towards it.” [Al-Baqarah: 150] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not They bring it out in this context.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3060 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3061","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih informed us, Muhammad bin Ghalib informed us, Issa bin Ibrahim Al-Baraki told us, Al-Mu’afia bin Imran told us. Al-Mawsili, Musab bin Thabit narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: I was with the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. At a funeral among us in Bani Salamah, I was walking beside the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and a man said: What a fine man. We do not know whether he was chaste and Muslim. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Are you what you say?” He said: O Messenger of God, that was apparent to us, and God knows best the secrets, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is obligatory.” He said: And we were with him in The funeral of a man from Banu Haritha - or from Banu Abd al-Ashhal - and a man said: How miserable a man is. We did not know if it was a harsh word if it was, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Are you what you say?” He said: O Messenger of God, God knows best about secrets, but as for what appeared to us, that is that. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is obligatory,” then he recited The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: {And thus We have made you a moderate nation that you may be witnesses over the people and that the Messenger may be a witness over you} [Al-Baqarah: 143] “This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, but only agreed that it was obligatory.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3061 - Musab is not strong"
"3062","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, he said: It was read on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Dhakwan, on the authority of Abu Saeed, {And thus We have made you a nation In the middle} [Al-Baqarah: 143] He said: “Justly.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3062 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3063","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, Samak bin Harb told us, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was directed to the Kaaba, they said: O Messenger God, what about those who died while praying to the Holy House? “So God revealed: {And God would not make your faith to be lost} [Al-Baqarah: 143] until the end of the verse.” Ubayd Allah ibn Musa said: “This hadith tells you that “Prayer is based on faith.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3063 - True"
"3064","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Umayr bin Ziyad. Al-Kindi, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, {Then turn your face toward the Sacred Mosque} [Al-Baqarah: 144] He said: “Then turn your face towards the Sacred Mosque} [Al-Baqarah: 144] He said: “Then turn your face toward the Sacred Mosque.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3064 - True"
"3065","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, on the authority of Yahya bin Qamtah, who said: I saw Abdullah bin Amr sitting in the Sacred Mosque, facing the drain, so he recited these The verse: {So We will certainly turn to you a qiblah that you will be pleased with.} [Al-Baqarah: 144] He said: “Towards the gutter of the Kaaba.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3065 - True"
"3066","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, about Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul-Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of his mother, Umm Kulthum bint Uqba, and she was one of the first emigrants, according to the saying God Almighty said: {And seek help with patience and prayer} [Al-Baqarah: 45] She said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf was overcome by a faint, so they thought that he had passed away. He found himself in it, so his wife, Umm Kulthum, went out to the mosque, seeking help from what she had been commanded to do of patience and prayer. When he woke up, he said: “I fainted.” “On me earlier?” They said: Yes. He said: “You have spoken the truth. Two angels came to me and said: Go, we will judge you to the Mighty, the Faithful.” Then another angel said: Send him back, for this Among those for whom you have written happiness, while they are in their mothers’ wombs, and whose children enjoy it as God wills. “He lived after that for a month and then died.” This is An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3066 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3067","Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad informed me, Jeddi told me, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti informed me, Hushaym told me, Khalid ibn Safwan, on the authority of Zaid bin Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The obituary of some of his family came to him, and he On a journey, he prayed two rak'ahs, then said: We did what God commanded: {Seek help with patience and prayer} [Al-Baqarah: 153] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3067 - True"
"3068","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi narrated to me, Musaddad bin Qattan narrated to us, Othman bin Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: “How good is justice, and how good is the reward, who, when a calamity befalls them, say: Indeed, we belong to God.” And to Him we will return. Those are the ones upon whom are blessings from their Lord and mercy. What excellent justice. These are the ones who are guided. What an excellent reward this is. It is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it, and I do not know of any disagreement among our imams that Saeed bin Al-Musayyab lived in the days of Omar, may God be pleased with him. But they differed only regarding their hearing from him.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3068 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3069","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Muhammad bin Saeed bin Al-Asbahani told us, Ali bin Mushar told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “This verse was only revealed about the Ansar during pre-Islamic times. It is permissible for them to circumambulate between Safa and Marwa. When we came, they mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so God revealed that: {Indeed, Safa And Al-Marwah is one of the symbols of God} [Al-Baqarah: 158] “until the end of the verse” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3069 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3070","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Usayd bin Asim Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, he said: I asked Anas bin Malik, on the authority of Al-Safa and Al-Marwah, said: “They were among the sentiments of pre-Islamic times, so when Islam was established, we withdrew from them, so God revealed: {Indeed Al-Safa and Al-Marwah are among the rituals of God. [Al-Baqarah: 158] God, so whoever makes the Hajj to the House or performs Umrah, there is no blame on him if he circumambulates them, and whoever volunteers goodness, the verse “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3070 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3071","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl, Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: A man came to him and said: I will start with Safa. Before Marwa, or I start with Marwa before Safa, and pray before I circumambulate, or I circumambulate before I pray, and I shave before Should I slaughter, or should I slaughter before I shave? Ibn Abbas said: “Take that from the Book of God, for it is more worthy of being preserved.” God Almighty said: “Indeed, Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of God.” [Al-Baqarah: 158] “So as-Safa is before al-Marwah,” and he said: “Do not shave your heads until the sacrificial animal reaches its place.” “So slaughtering is before shaving,” and he said: {Purify My House for those who circle around and seclude themselves and those who kneel and prostrate} [Al-Baqarah: 125]: “So the circumambulation before prayer” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3071 - True"
"3072","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Jafar bin Aoun told us, Sufyan bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he had seen them circumambulating between Safa and Marwah. He said: “This is from what my mother bequeathed to you.” Ismail “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3072 - True"
"3073","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saffar al-Adl told us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nasr told us, Amr ibn Talha al-Qannad told us, Asbat ibn Nasr, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {Indeed, Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of God} [Al-Baqarah: 158] He said: In the pre-Islamic era, the devils used to play music throughout the night between Safa and Marwah, and there were gods there who had idols, so when he came Islam The Muslims said: O Messenger of God, we do not circumambulate between Safa and Marwah, for it is something we used to do in the pre-Islamic era. “So God revealed: {So whoever makes the Hajj to the House or performs the Umrah, there is no blame on him if he goes around them} [Al-Baqarah: 158] “He says: There is no sin upon him, but he will have a reward.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3073 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3074","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abu Usama told us, Talha bin Amr told us, Ataa told me Ibn Abi Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that he said: “If it were not for a verse from the Book of God, I would not have told anyone anything.” It was said: What is it, Abu Hurairah? He said: \"\" Verse {Indeed, those who conceal the proofs and the guidance We have sent down, after We have made it clear to the people in the Scripture - those are cursed by God. And the cursers curse them, except those who repent and make amends and explain.} [Al-Baqarah: 160] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3074 - True"
"3075","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, about Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, I think it is on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka`b, he said: “Do not curse the wind, for it is from the breath of the Most Gracious, the Most High, the Most High, saying: {And the changing of the winds and the clouds that are subdued between the sky and the earth} [Al-Baqarah: 164] But say: O God, we ask You for the good of this wind, and the good in it, and the good with which it was sent, and we seek refuge in You from its evil, and the evil of What is in it, and the evil with which it was sent “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and it was transmitted from the hadith of Habib bin Abi Thabit Other than this narration.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3075 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"3076","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad Al-Qantari told me in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba Al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Asim told us, Issa bin Abi Issa told us, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, On the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {And the paths of connection between them are severed} [Al-Baqarah: 166] He said: “affection” this. A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3076 - True"
"3077","Sheikh Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told me from the origin of his book, Musa bin Ayan told us, Abdul Karim bin Malik Al-Jazari told us, about Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, that he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about faith, so he recited this verse: {Righteousness is not that Turn your faces towards the east and the west, but righteousness is he who believes in God and the Last Day} [Al-Baqarah: 177] until he finished the verse. He said: Then He asked him again and he recited it, then he asked him again and he recited it, then he asked him and said: “And when you do a good deed, your heart will love it, and if you do an evil deed, “Your heart hates it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3077 - How, when it is interrupted"
"3078","Ismail bin Muhammad al-Faqih told us about Rayy, Muhammad bin al-Faraj al-Azraq told us, Abu al-Nadr told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, and he told me Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i in Baghdad, Ishaq bin Al-Hassan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Zubaid, On the authority of Murrah ibn Sharahil, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, in the words of God Almighty: {And He gave wealth for love of Him to relatives} [Al-Baqarah: 177] He said: “A healthy, stingy man who hopes to live and fears poverty gives. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3078 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3079","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saffar al-Adl told me, Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nasr told me, Amr ibn Talha al-Qannad told us, Asbat ibn Nasr, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, in the words of God Almighty: {And those who are patient in hardship. And hardship} [Al-Baqarah: 177] and during hardship. Abdullah said: “Misfortune: poverty, and hardship: sickness, and during hardship. He said: during killing” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3079 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3080","Abu Muhammad Jaafar bin Muhammad bin Nusayr Al-Khalidi told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Amr bin A dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {So whoever is pardoned from his brother anything} [Al-Baqarah: 178] He said: “It is the baptism with the consent of its people.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3080 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3081","Ali bin Issa told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas May God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty’s saying: {And render to him with goodness} [Al-Baqarah: 178]. He said: “He performs what is requested with goodness.” This is an authentic hadith based on The conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not include it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3081 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3082","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar Sulayman bin Hayyan told us. Al-Jaafari, Humaid al-Tawil reported on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, “that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decreed retaliation.” . . . . . . . . . . . . . . On the condition of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3082 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3083","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Yunus Ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that “he rose and addressed the people here - meaning in Basra - and he recited Surah Al-Baqarah is upon them, and He explained what is in it, so He mentioned this verse: {If he leaves good, the bequest to the parents} [Al-Baqarah: 180] “He said: “It has been abrogated. Then he mentioned what comes after it. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3083 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3084","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, that Ali, may God be pleased with him, entered upon a man from Banu Hashim who was sick and was visiting him, and he wanted to make a recommendation but he forbade him. He said: “Indeed, God says: {If he leaves behind good} [Al-Baqarah: 180] wealth, then leave your money to your heirs.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3084 - There is a break"
"3085","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told me, Abu Al-Nadr Hashim bin Al-Qasim told me, Al-Masoudi told me, he told me Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him, said: As for the conditions of fasting, “the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he came to Medina and began fasting three days every month, and fasting on the day of Ashura. Then God made fasting obligatory upon him. Then God revealed: {O you who have believed, decreed upon you is fasting as it was decreed upon those before you} [Al-Baqarah: 183] to this verse {and upon those They can afford it as a ransom to feed a poor person.} [Al-Baqarah: 184] So whoever willed may fast, and whoever willed may feed a poor person, and that will be sufficient for him. Then God He revealed the other verse: {The month of Ramadan in which was revealed the Qur’an} [Al-Baqarah: 185] to the Almighty’s saying {So whoever of you witnesses the month, let him fast it} [Al-Baqarah: 185] So God confirmed his fasting for the healthy resident, and permitted it for the sick and the traveler, and established feeding for the elderly who cannot. Fasting, these are two years, and they used to eat and drink, and go to the women as long as they did not sleep, and when they slept they abstained, then a man from The Ansar, called Sarmah, was fasting until evening, so he came to his family and prayed the evening prayer, then he fell asleep and did not eat or drink until In the morning, he was fasting. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . So I lay down and fell asleep, and in the morning I was fasting. Omar had intercourse with some of the women, male or female, after he had slept, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him, and that was mentioned to him, so God revealed: “It is lawful for you on the night of fasting to have sexual intercourse with your wives” [Al-Baqarah: 187] to His saying: “Then complete the fast.” Until the night} [Al-Baqarah: 187] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3085 - True"
"3086","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari and Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrafi Al-Maruzian informed us, saying: Ibrahim bin Hilal, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Dhar Abi Umar, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jarir bin Abd God Almighty, may God be pleased with him, in the words of God Almighty: {Call upon Me, I will respond to you} [Ghafir: 60] He said: “Worship Me, I will respond to you.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3086 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3087","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Maysara, On the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {They are clothing for you and you are clothing for them} [Al-Baqarah: 187] He said: “They are a dwelling place for you. And you are a dwelling place for them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3087 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"3088","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Anas Al-Qurashi told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Haywa told us Ibn Shurayh, Yazid ibn Abi Habib informed me, Aslam Abu Imran, the client of Banu Tajib, informed me, he said: We were in Constantinople and on The people of Egypt were appointed by Uqba bin Amir al-Juhani, and the people of the Levant were led by Fadalah bin Ubaid al-Ansari, so a large column of Romans came out and we lined up. They had a large column of Muslims, so a man of the Muslims carried the Roman column until he entered among them, then he came out to us and shouted to the people, and they said:"
"3089","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Abdul Rahman Al-Subaie informed us, Ahmad bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, about Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa, may God be pleased with him, a man said to him: O Abu Ammarah: {And do not throw yourselves into destruction with your own hands} [Al-Baqarah: 195] Is it? A man meets the enemy and fights until he is killed? He said: “No, but he is the man who committed the sin, and he says: May God not forgive me.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3089 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3090","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salamah, Ali was asked about the words of God Almighty: {And complete the Hajj and the Umrah for God} [Al-Baqarah: 196] He said: “To enter ihram from a circle “Your family.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3090 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3091","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz informed us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab bin Habib Al-Abdi told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, he informed us Abu Ja`far al-Razi, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, that he used to recite it: “So whoever does not “Fasting for three consecutive days” is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3091 - True"
"3092","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, {Hajj is one of the known months} [Al-Baqarah: 197] He said: “Shawwal, Dhul-Qa’dah, and the ten days of Dhul-Hijjah” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3092 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3093","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ziyad bin Husayn, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, said: I was walking with Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, while he was in ihram, and he was riding with camels, and he He said: “And they walked with us whispering.” He said: I said: Should you be in ihram while you are in ihram? He said: “Indecent assault is only that with which women are treated.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3093 - True"
"3094","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar said: “Nasty: sexual intercourse, and immorality: what has befallen us of disobedience to God, such as hunting and other things, and argument: cursing and quarreling.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3094 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3095","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih informed us, saying: It was recited to Yahya bin Ja`far while I was listening, Hammad bin Masada told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, On the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “At the beginning of the Hajj, they used to trade in Mina like the Majaz market. And the seasons of Hajj. When the Qur’an was revealed, they feared selling, so God Almighty revealed: {There is no blame upon you if you seek bounty from your Lord} [Al-Baqarah: 198] in Seasons of Hajj “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3095 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3096","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, about Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, said: {Al-Mash’ar Al-Haram} [Al-Baqarah: 198]: “All of Muzdalifah.” This is an authentic hadith based on The conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not include it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3096 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3097","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abdul Rahman bin Al-Mubarak Al-Aishi told us, Abd told us Al-Warith bin Saeed, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qays bin Makhramah, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us Peace be upon him, peace be upon him, at Arafat, and he thanked God and praised Him, then he said: “As for what follows, the people of polytheism and idols used to be repelled from here.” At sunset, when the sun was on the tops of the mountains like the turbans of men on their heads, our guidance was different from theirs, and they used to push From the Sacred Mash’ar when the sun rises on the tops of the mountains, like the turbans of men on their heads, so our guidance is different from their guidance.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3097 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3098","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Abdullah bin Al-Walid Al-Adni told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Yahya bin Ubaid told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father Al-Sa’ib, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said a salaam between the Yemeni corner and the stone: “{Our Lord, give us good in this world, and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the torment of the Fire} [Al-Baqarah: 201] “This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3098 - True"
"3099","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim Al-Bateen, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: A man came to Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, and said: I have rewarded myself from my people on the condition that They carried me, and I allocated for them some of my wages on the condition that they let me perform Hajj with them. Would that be sufficient? He said: “You are one of those whom God Almighty said: {Those will have a share of what they have earned, and God is quick to judge} [Al-Baqarah: 202] “This is an authentic hadith according to The conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not include it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3099 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3100","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Shu’bah informed us, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of Ata’, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ya`mar al-Dili, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Hajj is Arafat - or Arafat - so whoever reaches Arafat before... The dawn has come, then Hajj has been completed, and the days of Mina are three: {So whoever hastens in two days, there is no sin upon him} [Al-Baqarah: 203] and whoever delays, there is no sin upon him. “This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it. . . »\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3100 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3101","Ahmed bin Mahran. . . . . . ., Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Maysara, on the authority of Omar, he said: When the prohibition of alcohol was revealed, Omar Radi said God said on his authority: “O God, give us a satisfactory explanation regarding wine.” Then the verse “They ask you about wine and gambling” was revealed [Al-Baqarah: 219], which is in Surah Al-Baqarah. So Omar was called and it was read to him, and he said: “O God, make it clear for us.” “Concerning wine, a satisfactory explanation.” Then what was on the table was revealed, and Omar was called and it was read to him. When he reached the age of the Prophet: “So have you made up your mind?” [Al-Ma’idah: 91] Omar said: “We have finished.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3101 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3102","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Khidr bin Aban Al-Hashimi told us, Ishaq bin Yusuf Al-Azraq told us, Saeed bin Ayas Al-Jariri told us, on the authority of Thumama bin Hazn Al-Qushayri, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stood up and said: “O people of Medina, Indeed, God is presenting to me regarding wine a way that I do not know, perhaps He will send down something to me about it.” Then he got up and said: “O people of Medina, God has sent down Prohibiting alcohol, so whoever is touched by this verse and has any of it, let him not drink it or sell it. He said: So they poured it out on the roads. Medina “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3102 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3103","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: When the verse was revealed: {And do not approach the property of the orphan, except with what is best} [Al-An’am: 152] They isolated their wealth from the wealth of the orphans, which caused the food to spoil and the meat to rot. They complained about this to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. “So God Almighty revealed: {Say, ‘A reform is better for them. But if you mix with them, then they are your brothers.’” [Al-Baqarah: 220] “He said: So mix with them.” This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3103 - True"
"3104","Abdul Rahman bin Hamdan Al-Jallab told us, Hilal bin Al-Ala’ Al-Ruqi told us, Abdullah bin Ja’far told us, Ubayd Allah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Abi Anisa, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Zaida Ibn Umair, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about isolation, and he said: You have increased, so if If the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said something about it, then it is as he said, and if he did not say anything about it, then I say: {Your women are your tillage. So come to your tillage however you wish.} [Al-Baqarah: 223] “Then if you wish, isolate yourself, but if you wish, do not do so.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. \"\"\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3104 - True"
"3105","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, heard Aban ibn Salih speaking on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I presented the Qur’an to Ibn Abbas three times. I stop him at each verse and ask him about what was revealed, and what was it like? So I came in accordance with his saying: {Your women are your crops, so come to your crops wherever you wish} [Al-Baqarah: 223] the verse. He said: This neighborhood was among the immigrants. They gave women an unpleasant explanation, whenever they found them coming and going. When they came to Medina, they married women from the Ansar, so they wanted them to be What they were doing to the female migrants, they denied it and complained about it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “So God Almighty revealed: {Your women are your crops, so come to your crops wherever you wish} [Al-Baqarah: 223] Ibn Abbas: But it was only before its back.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3105 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3106","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Yaqoub bin Humaid bin Kasib told us, Ya’la bin Shabib Al-Makki, Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The man used to divorce his wife as long as he wanted. He may divorce her, even if he divorced her one hundred times or more, if he takes her back before her waiting period has expired, until the man says to his wife: By God, no I will divorce you, so you may separate yourself from me, and I will not take you to myself. She said: How is that? He said: I will divorce you, and whenever your waiting period is about to end, I will take you back. Then I will divorce you, and I will do that. The woman complained about this to Aisha, so Aisha mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he remained silent and did not say anything until “the Qur’an was revealed: {Divorce is twice, then withholding.” with kindness or to release him with kindness} [Al-Baqarah: 229] «. . . . . . . . . » This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and no one spoke about Yaqoub bin Humayd with any evidence. Our sheikh, Abu Ahmad Al-Hafiz, discussed with me and mentioned that: Al-Bukhari narrated from him in Al-Sahih, so I said: This is Yaqoub bin Muhammad Al-Zuhri, and he confirmed what he said.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3106 - More than one person has deemed it weak"
"3107","Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us, my father informed me, Waki` informed us, al-Fadl ibn Dulham informed us, On the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Maqil bin Yasar, that his sister was divorced by her husband, and he wanted to take her back. “But Maqil prevented her, so God Almighty revealed: {And when you divorce women, and they have fulfilled their term, do not prevent them from marrying their husbands, if they agree between them in a reasonable manner} [Al-Baqarah: 232] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3107 - Al-Fadl bin Dulham, his weakness is Ibn Ma’in and his strength is others."
"3108","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad, and Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, they said: Saeed bin Yahya bin Saeed told us. The Umayyad, on the authority of Hafs bin Ghayath, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “If she carried him For nine months, she breastfeeds him for twenty-one months, and if she carries him for six months, she breastfeeds him for twenty-four months.” Then he read: {And his gestation and weaning are thirty months} [Al-Ahqaf: 15] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3108 - True"
"3109","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told me, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Warqa’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ataa, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “This verse was abrogated by her waiting period among her family, so she may observe the waiting period wherever she wished, according to the words of God Almighty: {other than Taking out} [Al-Baqarah: 240] “‘Ata’ said: “If she wishes, she may attend the waiting period with her family, and if she wishes, she can go out, according to the words of God Almighty: {But if they go out, there is no blame on you. In what they did within themselves} “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3109 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3110","Muhammad bin Yazid Al-Adl told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Ismail, who is the son of Ulayya, told us, On the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he stood up and addressed the people here, and recited to them Surat Al-Baqarah, And He made clear to them some of it, so He mentioned this verse: {If he leaves behind good, the bequest to his parents and relatives} [Al-Baqarah: 180] And he said: “It has been abrogated.” This,” then he read until he came to this verse: {And those of you who die and leave behind wives} [Al-Baqarah: 234] to the Almighty’s saying {other than Narration} [Al-Baqarah: 240] Then he said: “And this” is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"3111","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Bishr bin Musa told me, Abdullah bin Al-Zubair Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ataa, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {And those of you who die, leaving behind wives, shall wait by themselves for four months. And ten days} [Al-Baqarah: 234] “He did not say that they should observe the waiting period in their homes. The woman whose husband has died may observe the waiting period wherever she wishes.” . . . . . . . . . .\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3111 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3112","Makram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told me, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told me, Abu told us. . . . . . ., Fudayl bin Marzuq told us, Shaqiq bin Uqba Al-Abdi told me, Al-Baraa bin Aazib told me, he said: “When the verse “Guard the prayers” was revealed And the afternoon prayer. We recited it at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as long as he wanted us to recite it. Then God abrogated it and revealed: {Guard On the prayers and the middle prayer} [Al-Baqarah: 238] “Then a man said to him: Is it the afternoon prayer? He said: “I told you how it was revealed and how God abrogated it, and God knows best.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3112 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3113",""
"3114",""
"3115",""
"3116","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Muhammad bin Muadh told us, Abu Asim told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ammar Al-Dahni, on the authority of Muslim Al-Bateen, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The throne is where his feet are, and the throne cannot be measured.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3116 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3117","Ahmad bin Mihran, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel reported, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Najia bin Ka’b, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, He said: “Uzayr, the Prophet of God, left his city, and he was a young man. He passed by a village, and its thrones were empty. He said: How can God revive this? After her death, God caused him to die for a hundred years, then resurrected him, and the first thing He created were his eyes, so he began to look at his bones, and they were arranged one into the other. Then he was covered with flesh, and the spirit was breathed into him, and he was a young man, and it was said to him: How long did you stay? He said: One day or part of a day. He said: Rather, you stayed for a hundred years. He said: So he came to Medina and left behind a young cobbler of his neighbor. A great sheikh: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3117 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3118","Abd al-Baqi bin Qani’ al-Hafiz told us, Ubaid bin Muhammad bin Hatim al-Ijli told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi al-Nadr told us, Ubayy told us, Ziyad told us. Ibn Abdullah Ibn Ulatha, Musa Ibn Muhammad Ibn Ibrahim Al-Taymi narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked Al-Baraa bin Aazib and said: “O Baraa, how did you spend on your family?” He said: He was generous to his family, so he said: O Messenger of God, what do I expect? He said: “If your spending on your family, your child, and your servant is charity, do not follow that with any harm or harm.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it was not “He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3118 - It contains Musa bin Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi, but it is abandoned, said by Al-Daraqutni."
"3119","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abd al-Wahhab bin Ata told us, Harun bin Musa told us, on the authority of Khalid al-Adha, On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “He used to recite it: (with a rā’) with a kasra on the rā’.” He said: And the knoll protruding from the ground, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3119 - True"
"3120","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, I heard Ibn Abi Mulaika, He narrates on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, that he heard him say: Umar asked the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “So what do you think the verse was revealed: {Ayud? “Would any of you have a garden?” [Al-Baqarah: 266]? “They said: God knows best.” He became angry and said: “Say: We know or we do not know.” Ibn Abbas said: I have some of it in my soul, O Commander of the Faithful. Omar said: “Say, my nephew, and do not despise yourself.” Ibn Abbas said: It was given as an example of an action. Omar said: “What work?” He said: For work, and Omar said: “A rich man did good deeds, then God sent devils for him, and he committed sins until all his deeds were drowned.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3120 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3121","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi told us about Marw, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Harun bin Antara, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the words of God Almighty: {A hurricane in which is fire} [Al-Baqarah: 266] He said: “A scent containing strong poisons.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3121 - True"
"3122","Ahmad bin Sahl bin Hamdawayh, the jurist in Bukhara, told us, Qais bin Unif told us, Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered the zakat of fitr to be paid with a saa’ of dates. Then a man brought bad dates, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Abdullah bin Rawaha: “Do not crush these dates.” Then the Qur’an was revealed: “O you! Those who have believed, spend of the good things you have earned and of what We have produced for you from the earth, and do not seek to spend from the evil of it.} [Al-Baqarah: 267] “This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3122 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3123","Abu Abd al-Rahman Muhammad ibn Mahmoud al-Hafiz told me, Hammad ibn Ahmad al-Qadi told me, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq told me, he said: I heard my father saying: Abu Hamza reported, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Sayegh, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with him. On her authority, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, your children are God’s gift to you. He gives females to whomever He wishes, and He gives to whomever He wishes.” He wants the males, so they and their wealth are yours if you need them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, but rather like this. They agreed on the hadith of Aisha: “The best thing a man eats is from his own earnings, and his children are from his own earnings.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3123 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3124","Sheikh Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us. Muhammad bin Ghalib Al-Dhabi told us, and Muhammad bin Sinan told us, they said: Saeed bin Suleiman told us. Al-Wasiti, narrated to us by Abbad, who is Ibn Al-Awwam, on the authority of Sufyan bin Husayn, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif, on the authority of his father, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the giving of charity, so a man came from this desert - Sufyan said: He means the porcupine - so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace be upon him: “Who brought this?” And no one brought anything except that it was attributed to the one who brought it, so the following verse was revealed: {And do not perform tayammum of the evil one; you shall spend, but you will not take it, unless Close your eyes over it.} [Al-Baqarah: 267] “And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade two types of dates from being given as charity: the date and the Al-Hubaiq. Al-Zuhri said: “And the two colors are from the dates of Medina.” Sulayman bin Katheer followed him, on the authority of Al-Zuhri."
"3125","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya the Martyr, and Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, they said: Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi, Suleiman bin Kathir told us, Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hanif, on the authority of his father, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he forbade two types of dates: the juror date and the color of the habeek. So they forbade two types of dates, and the following verse was revealed: “And do not spend on the evil from it” [Al-Baqarah: 267] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3125 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3126","Abu Asim Al-Nabil told us, Abdul-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, Saleh bin Abi Urayb told me, on the authority of Kathir bin Murrah, on the authority of Awf bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out with a staff, and behold, there were vessels hanging in the mosque. He said: “It would not harm the owner of this if he gave something better than this in charity. Indeed, the owner of this will eat dirt on the Day of Resurrection.” Then he said: “By God.” He will leave it humiliated for forty years for the Awafi.” Then he said: “Do you know what the Awafi is?” They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “Birds and wild beasts” this. A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3126 - True"
"3127","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Saffar al-Adl informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nasr informed us, Amr ibn Talha al-Qannad informed us, Asbat ibn al-Qannad informed us. Nasr, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Adi ibn Thabit, on the authority of Al-Bara’ ibn Aazib, in the saying of God Almighty: “And of what We have produced for you from the land, nor “Tryo the evil of it, and spend it.” [Al-Baqarah: 267] He said: It was revealed about the Ansar. The Ansar used to come out whenever the trunk of a palm tree was from its walls. They destroyed the food and hung it on the top of two cylinders in the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the poor immigrants would eat from it. So one of them baptizes and enters the concubine, thinking that it is permissible in the large number of conjuncts that are placed, so it was revealed about whoever did that {And do not perform tayammum. The evil part of it, you spend, and you will not take it, unless you close your eyes to it.} [Al-Baqarah: 267] He says: Had it been given to you, you would not have accepted it except with modesty. From his companion's anger that he sent to you with what he had no need of {And know that God is Self-sufficient} [Al-Baqarah: 267] of your alms {Praiseworthy} [Al-Baqarah: 267] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3127 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3128","Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told me, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Hudhayfah told me, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyas, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “They” hated to submit to their lineage, and they were polytheists, so “It is not upon you to guide them” was revealed. But God guides whom He wills.} [Al-Baqarah: 272] until he reached the message: {And you shall not be wronged} [Al-Baqarah: 272]. He said: So He granted them permission: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3128 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3129","Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, said: When the verse was revealed: “Those who consume usury will not stand except as the one who Satan makes him tossed about due to his touch.} [Al-Baqarah: 275] The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever does not abandon the message, let him be given the warning of a war from God.” And His Messenger, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3129 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3130","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Abu Muslim told us, Ibrahim bin Bashar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Abu Hassan, he said: Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “I bear witness that the advance guaranteed for a specified period has been made lawful by God in the Book.” And He declared it, God Almighty said: {O you who have believed, when you contract a debt for a specified time, write it down} [Al-Baqarah: 282] Verse “This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"3131","Muhammad bin Ali al-Sana’ani told me, in Mecca, Ali bin al-Mubarak al-Sana’ani told us, Zayd bin al-Mubarak al-Sana’ani told us, Muhammad bin Thawr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Mulaika, said: I sent to Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, to ask him about the testimony of the two boys. He said: God Almighty said, “{Among the witnesses you are satisfied with} [Al-Baqarah: 282] but they are not among those we are satisfied with. He said: So I sent to Ibn al-Zubayr to ask him, and he said: Rather, if they were asked, they would be truthful. He said: I did not see the ruling except on what Ibn al-Zubayr said: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3131 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3132","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Waki` told us, Sufyan told us, On the authority of Adam bin Sulaiman, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr, speaking, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: When this verse was revealed {Indeed Whether you reveal what is within yourselves or hide it, Allah will judge you for it.} [Al-Baqarah: 284] This was difficult for them unless something like that was difficult for them, so he said to them. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They said, ‘We hear and obey.’ Then God placed faith in their hearts, and they said: We heard and obeyed.” Then God Almighty revealed: “God does not burden a soul beyond its capacity; for it is what it has earned, and upon it is what it has earned” [Al-Baqarah: 286] to the Almighty’s saying. {Or did we make a mistake?} [Al-Baqarah: 286] He said: I have done so. To the end of Al-Baqarah: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3132 - True"
"3133","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, in Baghdad, Abdullah bin Ruh Al-Madaini told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Sufyan bin Hussein told us, On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, that his father recited, “Whether you reveal what is within yourselves or hide it, God will call you to account for it, and He forgives whom He wills, and punishes Whoever He wills} [Al-Baqarah: 284] Then his eyes shed tears, and his action was reported to Ibn Abbas, and he said: “May God have mercy on Abu Abd al-Rahman. The companions of the Messenger of God have done so.” May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when it was revealed, and the verse that follows it abrogated it: “To her is what she has earned and upon her is what she has earned” [Al-Baqarah: 286] “This is an authentic hadith.” The chain of transmission and they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3133 - True"
"3134","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told us, Muadh bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Khallad bin Yahya told us, Abu Aqeel told us, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, said: When this verse was revealed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “The Messenger believed in what was revealed to him.” From his Lord} [Al-Baqarah: 285] The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “And he has more right to believe.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3134 - Interrupted"
"3135","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah, Muslim bin Ibrahim, Aban Al-Attar, Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Salam, on the authority of Abu Salam, on the authority of Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Recite Al-Zahrawiyin Al-Baqarah and the family of Imran” this. An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3135 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3136","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hassan bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Ali bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Abu Ubaid, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Harun bin Musa, Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqamah, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdul Rahman bin Hatib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him, that he prayed with them “so he recited the word of God There is no god but He, the Living, the Standing.” Abu Ubaid said: As for the reciters after that, they are from the people of the Two Holy Mosques, Mecca and Medina, and the people of Kufa, the Egyptians. And the people of Basra and the people of the Levant and Egypt and other reciters recited it: {Al-Qayyum} [Al-Imran: 2] There is no difference between them concerning it, I know it, and likewise In our view, reading is in agreement with the Book and what the nation is upon, even if there is a way out for these two views in Arabic. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3136 - True"
"3137","Abu Zakaria informed us: Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari: Muhammad bin Abdul Salam, I: Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I: Abdul Razzaq, I: Yahya bin Al-Ala’, on the authority of his uncle Shuaib bin Khalid, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, and he read {Indeed, nothing is hidden from God on earth or in heaven} [Al Imran: 5] and he said: Abdullah bin Amira told me, on the authority of Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, may God be pleased with him, who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. At Batha, a cloud passed by, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you know what this is?” So we said: God and His Messenger know best, and he said: “the clouds,” so we said: the clouds, and he said: “and the scale,” so we said: and the scale, and he said: “and the reins,” so we said: And the reins, then he remained silent, then he said: “Do you know how much distance there is between the sky and the earth?” So we said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “Between them is a journey of five hundred years, and from each heaven to the next heaven is a journey of five hundred years. And every heaven was thickened over the course of five hundred years, and above the seventh heaven there was a sea between its highest and its lowest, as between the heaven and the earth. Then above That is eight tents. Between their knees and their hooves is as between the heaven and the earth. And God Almighty is above that. There are no hidden works from Him. “The children of Adam are something.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3137 - Yahya Wah"
"3138","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us a dictation in Sha`ban of the year three hundred and ninety-nine. I am Ali bin Muhammad Ibn Uqba Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Haytham Ibn Khalid Abu Saeed, on the authority of Abu Nu’aym, on the authority of Ali Ibn Salih, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Qays, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “Among them are decisive verses, which are those in Surah Al-An’am. Say, ‘Come, recite what your Lord has forbidden to you. “Associate anything with Him until the last three verses.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3138 - True"
"3139","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub narrated to us Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani narrated to us Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Ashib narrated to us Omar bin Rashid, on the authority of Yahya bin Abu Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What I fear for my nation is that there will be many among them.” Money, until they compete over it and fight over it, and among what I fear for my nation is that the Qur’an will be opened to them, so that the believer and the unbeliever can read it. And the hypocrite, then the believer is allowed to do so, seeking to explain it until the end of the verse. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3139 - True"
"3140","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi, narrated to us Ibrahim bin Abi Talib, narrated to us Muhammad bin Sahl bin Askar, narrated to us Muhammad bin Yusuf, narrated by Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to often say: “O “The One who turns hearts, make our hearts steadfast in your religion.” We said: O Messenger of God, do you fear for us since we have believed in you? He said: “The hearts of the children of Adam are between two of the fingers of the Most Gracious, like one heart with which He says thus.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. They did not narrate it like this, rather Muslim was the only one to narrate the hadith of Abdullah bin Amr: “The hearts of the children of Adam” only.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3140 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3141","Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid Al-Bayruti told us, Muhammad bin Shuaib bin Shabur told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Busr ibn Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Al-Nawwas ibn Samaan Al-Kalabi, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “The scale is in the hand of the Most Gracious. It raises some people and lowers others, and the heart of the son of Adam is between two of the Most Merciful’s fingers, if He wishes.” He established it, and when He wished, He caused it to deviate.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “O One who turns hearts, make my heart steadfast in your religion.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3141 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3142","Abd al-Samad bin Ali bin Mukarram al-Bazzar told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Ismail al-Sulami told us, Abdullah bin Salih told us, Muawiyah told me Ibn Salih, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Jubayr Ibn Nufayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Miqdad Ibn Al-Aswad, may God be pleased with him, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The heart of the son of Adam is more capricious than pot when it comes together to boil.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the conditions Al-Bukhari and did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3142 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"3143","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told me, Zuhair bin Harb told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of his father, said: I heard Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “reciting {and no one knows its interpretation except God, And those who are firmly established} [Al Imran: 7] in knowledge, they say, “We believe in it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3143 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3144","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Al-Hasan bin Ahmad bin Al-Layth Al-Razi told us, Hammam bin Abi Badr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb, Haywa bin Shurayh told me, on the authority of Aqeel bin Khalid, on the authority of Salamah bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The first book was revealed from a single chapter in one letter. One, and the Qur’an was revealed in seven chapters in seven letters: prohibitive, commanding, lawful, forbidden, decisive, similar, and proverbs. So do what is lawful, and prohibit what is unlawful, and do what you have been commanded to do, and abstain from what you have been forbidden, and consider the likes of it, and act according to its rules. And believe in something similar, and say: We believe in it. It is all from our Lord. And none remember except those of understanding. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it has not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3144 - Interrupted"
"3145","Al-Hasan bin Ali Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak informed, Humaid al-Taweel, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, said: Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, recited, “And fruit and fruit” [Abs: 31], so some of them said Thus, and some of them said thus, so Omar said: Let us leave this and believe in it, all from our Lord. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration on the condition that The two sheikhs did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3145 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3146","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Al-Manhaal Bin Amr, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty saying: “And they kill the prophets unjustly And they kill those from among the people who command justice} [Al Imran: 21] He said: Jesus, son of Mary, was sent with twelve men from among the disciples, teaching The people, so he used to forbid them from marrying a brother’s daughter. There was a king who had a brother’s daughter that he liked, so he wanted her and spent the night with her every day. A need, so her mother said to her: If he asks you about your need, tell him: to kill Yahya bin Zakaria. Then the king said to her: What is your need? She said: My need is for Yahya bin Zakariya to be killed. He said: Ask for something else. She said: I do not ask for anything else. When he came, he ordered him to be killed, and he was slaughtered in A basin, and a drop of his blood came out, and it continued to boil until God sent a victor, and an old woman ran over him, and he decided to continue boiling. Killing until this blood stopped, so in one day, from one attack and one house, seventy thousand were killed. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. He did not narrate it, and it has a strange witness, with a strange chain of narration and text.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3146 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3147","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ibrahim bin Amr Al-Bazzar told us in Baghdad, Abu Ya’la Muhammad bin Shaddad Al-Musami told us, Abu Nu`aym told us, Abdullah bin Habib bin Abi Thabit told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: God revealed to your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Indeed, I killed seventy thousand with Yahya bin Zakariya, and I will kill seventy thousand for your daughter’s son.” One thousand and seventy thousand.” Al-Hakim said: “I had been thinking for a long time that Al-Musami would be alone with this hadith on the authority of Abu Nu’aym until we narrated it to him.” Abu Muhammad al-Subai’i al-Hafiz, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Najiya told us, Humaid bin al-Rabi’ told us, Abu Nu’aym told us and mentioned it with a chain of transmission similar to it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3147 - The text is very objectionable"
"3148","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Abd al-A’la bin Ayn told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Polytheism is more hidden than The crawling of the corn on the row in the dark night, and the lowest thing is that you love something that is unjust, and hate something that is just, and that is religion, except love. And hatred. God Almighty said, “Say, ‘If you love God, then follow me. God will love you.’” [Al Imran: 31] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3148 - Abdul-Ala said Al-Daraqutni is not trustworthy"
"3149","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, my father told me, Abu Hammam told us, Muhammad bin Bishr Al-Abdi told us, he said: I heard Sufyan Ibn Saeed, mentioning on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Ata’ narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “Unless you fear them with complete fear” [Al Imran: 28] He said: Piety is speaking with the tongue and the heart is secure in faith, so he does not extend his hand and kill, nor commit sin, for he has no excuse. This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3149 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3150","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us about Ata Ibn Al-Sa'ib, on the authority of Sa'id Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty's saying: “{Indeed, I have vowed to you what is in my stomach, freed} [Al Imran: 35] He recited to his saying {He found provision with her} [Al Imran: 37] He said: Zechariah sponsored her and entered the sanctuary over her, and found grapes in her Deprived at the wrong time. Zechariah said: “How can you get this?” She said, “It is from God. Indeed, God provides for whomever He wills without reckoning.” [Al Imran: 37] He said: Indeed, the one who provides you with grapes at the wrong time is able to provide me with a son from the barren, old, and sterile one. {There, Zachariah called upon his Lord} [Al Imran: 38] When the good news was given to Yahya, he said: {Lord, make for me a sign. He said: Your sign is that you will not speak to people for three nights together} [Maryam: 10]. He said: Your tongue will be restrained without Illness and you are healthy “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3150 - True"
"3151","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Tanafisi told us, Sufyan bin Saeed told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, every prophet has guardians from among the prophets, and My friend among them is my father and my friend, Abraham.” Then he read, “Indeed, the people closest to Abraham are those who followed him, and this is the Prophet and those who believe, and God is my guardian.” The Believers} [Al Imran: 68] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3151 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3152","Sheikh Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that Israel took him from sciatica, and he spent the night while he had a heresy. He said: So he made it clear that if God healed him, he would not eat meat with veins in it. He said: “Then the Jews made it forbidden,” so it was revealed: “All food is lawful for the Children of Israel except What Israel forbade to itself, before the Torah was sent down. Say, “Then bring the Torah and recite it if you are truthful.” [Al Imran: 93] Indeed, This was before the Torah. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3152 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3153","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “In sciatica, he takes the buttocks of an Arabian ram.” It is not the largest, nor the smallest, so he cuts it into small pieces, then melts it, and he is good at dissolving it, and makes it into three parts, so he drinks Every day, as a portion on one’s own saliva.” Anas Ibn Sirin said: “I have commanded many people to do that, and all of them will be cured, God Almighty willing.” “This is an authentic hadith, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3153 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3154","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us, about Marwa, Ahmad bin Mala’ab bin Hayyan told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, and Muhammad bin Sabiq told us, they said: Israel, Khalid bin Harb told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Arara, he said: A man asked Ali, may God be pleased with him, about {the first house built for the people which Blessed and blessed} [Al Imran: 96] Is it the first house built on earth? He said: No, but it is “the first house in which blessing and guidance were placed, and the place of Abraham, and whoever enters it is safe. And if you wish, I will tell you how.” God Almighty built it. God revealed to Abraham, “Build for me a house on earth,” and he was filled with it. So God sent to him tranquility, which is a wind. Khajuj, it has a head, so one of them followed the other until it ended, then it encircled the place of the House like a serpent, so Abraham built So he himself built a leg every day, until when he reached the place of the stone, he said to his son: I want a stone. So he looked for a stone there until he brought it to him. He found the black stone installed, and his son said to him: Where did you get this? He said: It was brought by the one who did not rely on your building. Gabriel, peace be upon him, brought it from the sky and completed it. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3154 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3155","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Sulayman bin Kathir told us, he said: I heard Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, addressed us and said: “O People, God has ordained the Hajj for you. Al-Aqra’ bin Habis stood up and said: Is it every year, O Messenger of God? He said: “If I had said it, it would have become obligatory, and if it had become obligatory, you would not have performed it, or you would not have been able to perform it. Hajj is done once, so whoever does more, do it voluntarily.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” This is how it was narrated by Sufyan bin Hussein Al-Wasiti, on the authority of Al-Zuhri.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3155 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3156","Abu Hamid Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Shuaib, the ascetic jurist, told us, Sahl bin Ammar Al-Ataki told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Sufyan told us Ibn Husayn, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: Al-Aqra’ ibn Habis asked the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted and said: Hajj once every year? He said: “No, but once, so whoever increases it voluntarily.” And in the chapter on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, with explanation and clarification, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace"
"3157","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told us, Ahmad bin Musa bin Ishaq Al-Tamimi told us, Makhoul bin Ibrahim Al-Nahdi told us, Mansour bin Zazan, Ali bin Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: When this verse was revealed “ {And for God is the obligation of the people to perform the Hajj to the House, whoever is able to make a way to it} [Al Imran: 97] They said: O Messenger of God, is it every year? He remained silent, then they said: Is it every year? He remained silent, then they said: Is it every year? He said: “No, and had I said: Yes, it would have been obligatory.” Then God Almighty revealed {O you who have believed, ask not about things unless they are made clear to you. You will be harmed} [Al-Maeda: 101] “Al-Hakim said: “It was the rule of these three hadiths that they should be mentioned at the beginning of the Book of Rites, so it was not estimated That is for me, so I included it in the interpretation of the verse.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3157 - Makhoul is a Rafidhi and Abd al-A’la is Ibn Aamir, his weakness is Ahmad."
"3158","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Abu Dawud, and Wahb bin Jarir told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, and he told us Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi, in Hamadan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of al-A’mash, on the authority of Mujahid, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited this verse: “O you who have believed, fear God as He should be feared.” And do not die unless you are Muslims.} [Al Imran: 102] He said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if a drop of Zaqqum were dropped into the seas of the earth, it would become corrupt.” And in the hadith of Wahb bin Jarir: “I have ordered the people of this world to have their livelihood, so what about whose food it is?” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3158 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3159","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to me, Muhammad bin Sulaiman bin Al-Harith narrated to me, Ubayd Allah bin Musa, and Abu Nu’aym narrated to us, they said: Mus’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Zubaid, On the authority of Murrah ibn Sharahil, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, in the words of God Almighty: “Fear God as He should be feared” [Al Imran: 102] He said: To be obeyed and not disobeyed, and to be remembered and not forgotten. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3159 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3160","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmad bin Mihran Al-Asbahani told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Israel reported, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His saying, the Almighty, “You were The best nation ever brought forth for mankind} [Al Imran: 110]. He said: They are those who migrated with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Mecca to Medina. “This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3160 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3161","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Abu Muslim Ibrahim bin Abdullah told us, Hajjaj bin Nusayr told us, Abu Umayyah bin Ya`la al-Thaqafi said: I heard Musa bin Uqba reciting the words of God Almighty: {And hasten to forgiveness from your Lord} [Al Imran: 133] and he said: Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talha al-Qurashi told me on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Whoever is pleased that edification will be honored for him and that statuses will be raised for him, let him forgive those who wronged him, give to those whom he deprived of, and be kind to those whom he deprived of. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3161 - Abu Umayyah was deemed weak by Al-Daraqutni, and Ishaq did not perform the act of worship"
"3162","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Muammar reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman told me, he said: Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, used to narrate that Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, entered the mosque while Omar bin Al-Khattab was speaking to the people, so he came to the house in which the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, died. He greeted him and revealed his face to be covered with a blood-red veil. He looked at it and leaned on it to kiss his face, and said: By God, he does not combine May God grant you two deaths after your death after which you will not die. Then he went out to the mosque and Omar was speaking to the people. Abu Bakr said: Sit down, O Omar. He refused, so he spoke to him two or three times, but he refused, so he got up. So he recited the tashahhud, and when he had completed his tashahhud, he said: As for what follows: “Whoever worships Muhammad, then Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, has died, and whoever worships God, For God is living and does not die. Then he recited, “And We have not assigned for human beings before you an eternity” [Al-Anbiya’: 34] “And Muhammad is no more than a messenger. The Messengers. Someone said: The people did not know that this verse was revealed until Abu Bakr recited it. Al-Zuhri said: Then Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab informed me that Omar bin Al-Khattab said: When Abu Bakr recited it: I was barren until I fell to the ground and was certain that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had died. This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it in this context.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3162 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3163","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Suleiman bin Daoud bin Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas bin Abdul told me. Al-Muttalib, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Utbah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not helped. Peace and blessings of God be upon him in a place just as he was defeated on the Day of Uhud. He said: We denied that, and Ibn Abbas said: Between me and whoever denies that is the Book of God Almighty. God Almighty says on the day of Uhud: “And God has fulfilled His promise to you when you treated them kindly by His permission” [Al Imran: 152]. Ibn Abbas says: And the sense of killing {even when you failed and quarreled over the matter, and disobeyed after he had shown you what you love. Some of you want this world, and some of you Who desires the Hereafter, then turns you away from them in order to test you? And indeed He has pardoned you, and God is full of bounty to the believers.} [Al Imran: 152] But He only meant With these archers, that is because the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stationed them in a place and then said: “Protect our backs, for if you see us being killed, do not Support us, but if you see that we have taken spoils, do not associate with us.” When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took spoils and made the polytheist army permissible, it was revealed. All the archers, and they went into the army to plunder.The ranks of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, met, and they stood like this, and he interlaced the fingers of his hands, and they were confused. When the archers left that camp, In which they were, the horses entered from that place upon the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and some of them struck one another and they became confused, and some of them were killed. Muslims are many people, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions were with him at the beginning of the day until he was killed by one of the companions of the banner of the polytheists. Seven or nine, and the Muslims went around towards the mountain, and they did not reach where people say the jungle, but rather it was under the mush. Satan shouted, “Muhammad has been killed.” They did not doubt that he was the truth. We still did not doubt that he had been killed until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appeared. And he greeted between the two lions, and we recognized him by his straightening when he walked. He said: So we rejoiced as if what had befallen us had not befallen us. He said: He walked towards us. And he says: “The wrath of God is most intense against a people who bloodied the face of their Prophet.” He said: And he says again: “O God, it is not for them to exalt us.” Until he came to us, he said: He stayed for an hour and saw Abu Sufyan shouting at the bottom of the mountain, “The height of Hubal, the height of Hubal,” meaning his gods, where is Ibn Abu Kabsha, where is Ibn Abi Quhafa, where is Ibn Al-Khattab? Omar said: O Messenger of God,Shall I not answer him? He said: “Yes.” When he said: “How high is Hubal,” Omar said: “God is most high and most exalted.” Abu Sufyan said: “O Ibn Al-Khattab, it is a day of silence.” Then he returned and said: Where is Ibn Abi Kabsha? Where is Ibn Abi Quhafa? Where is Ibn al-Khattab? Omar said: This is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and this is Abu Bakr. And here I am, Omar. Abu Sufyan said: One day after the day of Badr. And they killed you in the Fire. He said: You claim that. We were disappointed then and lost. Then Abu Sufyan said: As for you, you will find in He killed you as an example, and that was not according to the opinion of our companions. Then the heat of pre-Islamic times overtook him, and he said: If that was not the case, We dislike it. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3163 - True"
"3164","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, and Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, they said: Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad told us Ibn Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Abu Talha al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him, who said: “I raised my head on the day of Uhud and started to look, and what Not one of them was except that he was slumbering under his lid from drowsiness. That is the saying of the Almighty, “Then He sent down upon you after the grief a peace of mind, a drowsiness.” Covering a group of you} [Al Imran: 154] The verse: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3164 - True"
"3165","Ali bin Issa told me, Musaddad bin Qatan told us, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “When your brothers were afflicted with Uhud, God placed their souls in the stomachs of birds, flowing through the rivers of Paradise, eating from their fruits, and taking refuge in the Lamps of gold hung in the shade of the throne. When they found that they had good food, drink and rest, they said: Who will inform our brothers about us? Are we alive in Paradise? We are provided for so that they will not stagnate in jihad, nor become weary in war? Then God Almighty said: I am informing them about you, so God Almighty and Majestic revealed the verse {And do not think of those who were killed in the cause of God} [Al Imran: 169] the verse “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3165 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3166","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Hisham bin Al-Qasim told us, Abu Sa’id Al-Muaddeb told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she said to Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, may God be pleased with them: O son of my sister, did you By God, “your father and your grandfather,” meaning Abu Bakr and Al-Zubair, are among those whom God Almighty said, “Those who responded to God and the Messenger after that.” The ulcer struck them.} [Al Imran: 172] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3166 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3167","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told us, in Kufa, Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Tamimi told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The last words of Abraham were when he was thrown into the fire. That is sufficient for me.” God is the best disposer of affairs, and your Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said something like it: “Those to whom the people said, ‘Indeed, the people have gathered against you, so fear them. So it increased their faith, and they said, “We are sufficient.” [Al Imran: 173] God is the best disposer of affairs. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3167 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3168","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Khaythamah, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, said: “By the One besides Whom there is no god, there is not a soul on the earth but death is better for it if he is a believer. For God says: {But those who fear their Lord will have Gardens under which rivers flow} [Al Imran: 198], and if he is an immoral person, then God says: {Only We give them respite so that they may increase in sin.} [Al Imran: 178] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3168 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3169","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told me, Abu Omar Al-Mustamli told us, Abu Hisham Al-Rifai told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, Abu Ishaq told us, Abu Wael told us, he said: Abdullah said: “They will contain what they were stingy with on the Day of Resurrection.” He said: A snake that has two raisins will devour it in its grave. And he says: I am the owner of the one with whom I was stingy.” I heard Yahya bin Mansour saying: I heard Abu Amr Al-Mustamli saying: I heard Abu Hisham Al-Rifai says: I heard Abu Bakr bin Ayyash saying: By God, I did not lie to Abu Ishaq, and I do not see Abu Ishaq lying to Abu Wael nor I think Abu Wael lied to Abdullah.” Narrated by Al-Thawri on the authority of Abu Ishaq\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3169 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim\n Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan Al-Harbi told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, in his saying “{They will contain what they were stingy with on the Day of Resurrection} [Al Imran: 180] He said: Abdullah said: A snake will come to him. He strokes his head, then necks his neck, then says: I am the owner of the one you were stingy with. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"3170","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Daqqaq told us in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Narsi told us, Abu Badr Shuja’ bin Al-Walid, Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqama told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that “the place A whip in Paradise for something better than this world and what is in it. Read, if you wish, {So whoever is removed from the Fire and admitted to Paradise has certainly succeeded, and what is life? This world is nothing but the enjoyment of delusion.} [Al Imran: 185] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3170 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3171","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaika informed me that Humaid ibn Abd The Most Gracious, informed him that Marwan sent to Ibn Abbas: By God, if every one of us were to rejoice in what he was given and be praised for what he did not do, He tortured us all. Ibn Abbas said: This verse was only revealed about the People of the Book. The Jews came to him, “and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked them about something, but they concealed it. Then they came to him, and he asked them and they told him otherwise, so they went out and saw that they had told him what he had asked them about, and they were thankful for that. “And they rejoiced in what they had been given, despite their concealment of what he had asked them about.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3171 - True"
"3172","Amr bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Sakini Al-Bukhari told us, in Nishapur, Abu Ali Salih bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Omar bin Al-Walid Al-Fahham, Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Ibn Al-Mubarak, he said: I heard Ibrahim bin Tahman, and he recited the saying of God Almighty {who They remember Allah standing and sitting and on their sides} [Al Imran: 191] Then he said: Al-Mukhtab narrated to me on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn. That he had hemorrhoids, “so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to pray on his side.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3172 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3173","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Shaybani told us, my father told me, Abdullah bin Al-Jarrah Al-Qahistani told us, Al-Harith bin Muslim, on the authority of Bahr al-Saqqa’, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: I said to him: Tell me about what God Almighty said. {They want to come out of the Fire, but they will not come out of it} [Al-Maeda: 37] He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed me that they are the infidels. He said: I said to Jabir: His saying {Indeed, whoever you admit to the Fire, you have disgraced him} [Al Imran: 192] He said: God has disgraced him when He burned him with or without fire. \"that disgrace\"\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3173 - Bahr Al-Saqa’ is perished"
"3174","Abu Aoun Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Mahan told us about Al-Safa, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Zayd Al-Makki told us, Ya’qub bin Humaid, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Salamah bin Abi Salamah, a man from the descendants of Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with him. On her authority, she said: O Messenger of God, I do not hear God mention anything about women during the migration. Then God Almighty revealed, “And their Lord responded to them, ‘Indeed, I will not waste the work of any worker among you, whether male or female, some of you from one another.’” [Al Imran: 195] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.” I heard Abu Ahmad Al-Hafiz and he reminded me of two hadiths in Al-Bukhari’s book: Ya’qub on the authority of Sufyan, and Ya’qub on the authority of Al-Darawardi. Abu Ahmad said: He is Ya’qub bin Humaid, and God knows best.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3174 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"3175","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marw, Abdullah bin Ali Al-Ghazal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Al-Mubarak, Musab Ibn Thabit reported, on the authority of Aamir Ibn Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, who said: An enemy from the Negus descended upon the Negus. Then the immigrants came to him and said: We would like to go out to them so that we can fight with you, and you will see our boldness and we will reward you for what you did with us. He said: “There is no cure with God’s help that is better than a cure with people’s help.” He said: And in it was revealed {And indeed, from the People of the Book is he who believes in God and what has been sent down to you, and what has been sent down to them are submissive to God} [Al Imran: 199] “This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3175 - True"
"3176","Abu Abbas Al-Sayyari told us, Abdullah bin Ali told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, that he was informed that Abu Ubaidah was besieged in the Levant and had The people rebelled against him, so Omar wrote to him: “Peace be upon you. As for what follows, no situation of hardship befalls a believing servant except that God will grant him After that there will be relief, and no hardship will overcome with ease {O you who have believed, be patient and be steadfast and be firm and fear Allah that you may succeed} [Al Imran: 200] He said: Then Abu Ubaidah wrote to him: “Peace be upon you. As for what follows, for God says in His Book: ‘Know that the life of this world is only a game and amusement and an ornament. And boasting among you and multiplying in wealth and children} [Al-Hadid: 20] and the end of it. He said: Then Omar took out his book and sat on the pulpit and read to The people of Medina, then he said: O people of Medina, Abu Ubaidah is only attacking you if you desire jihad. “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that Muslim, but they did not expel him.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3176 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3177","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Ahmad bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, Musab bin Thabit told me, Dawud bin Salih told me, he said: Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman said: O my nephew, do you know anything about This verse was revealed: “Be patient, be steadfast, and be steadfast” [Al Imran: 200]. He said: I said: No. He said: O my nephew, I heard Abu Hurairah say: “In the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, there was no raid in which one was stationed, but waiting for prayer “After the prayer.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3177 - True"
"3178","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, and Ahmad bin Nasr told us, they said: Abu Nu’aym told us, Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah Ibn Abi Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, said: I heard Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, saying: “Ask me about Surat An-Nisa, for I recited “The Qur’an when I was young.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3178 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3179","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Abd al-Hamid al-San’ani informed me of Mecca. Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told us, Abd told us Al-Razzaq, Muammar reported, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {Fear God, by whom you will ask And the wombs} [An-Nisa: 1] He said: The ties of kinship will be severed, and the blessings will be denied, and when God brings the hearts close together, nothing will ever move them, then He recited: “If you had spent all that is on earth, you would not have reconciled their hearts” [Al-Anfal: 63]. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The womb is a shield of The Most Gracious, and she will come on the Day of Resurrection speaking with a fluent and fluent tongue. So whoever she indicated with a link, may God bless him, and whomever she indicated “With certainty, God has made it certain.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3179 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3180","Abu Sahl Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ziyad, the grammarian in Baghdad, told us, Yahya bin Jaafar told us, Ali bin Asim told us, Humaid al-Taweel told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: There was a disagreement between Abu Talha and Umm Sulaim, so Abu Talha wanted to divorce Umm Sulaim, and that happened. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The divorce of Umm Salim Lahub” is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3180 - No, by God, Ali bin Asim is weak"
"3181","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Abu Al-Muthanna Muadh bin Muadh Al-Anbari told me, my father told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Shaabi, on the authority of my father Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Three people call upon God, but they are not answered: A man There was a woman of bad character and he did not divorce her, and a man had money from another man but he did not bear witness to it, and a man gave his money to a fool and he... God Almighty said: “And do not give your wealth to the foolish” [An-Nisa’: 5] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not produce it” to stop the companions of Shu’bah of this hadith is attributed to Abu Musa, but they were unanimously agreed upon the chain of transmission of Shu’bah’s hadith with this chain of transmission: “Three will be given their reward twice.” They all agreed to take him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3181 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, but they did not narrate it"
"3182","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told me in Baghdad, Ishaq bin Al-Hassan Al-Harbi told me, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: “And whoever is rich, let him maintain chastity” [An-Nisa: 6] So he does not need the orphan’s money. {And whoever is poor, let him eat reasonably.} [An-Nisa: 6] He eats from his own money such as for sustenance, so that he does not need The Orphan’s Wealth “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3182 - True"
"3183","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Hamid bin Mahmoud told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah Al-Dashtaki told us, Amr bin Abu Qais, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty saying “And when he is present Divide to your kindred and orphans and the needy, so provide for them from it and speak to them a kind word. He said: He will submit to them if it is in the wealth. I apologized to them for negligence. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3183 - True"
"3184","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir reported, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: When God revealed: “And do not approach the property of the orphan except in a way that is best.” [Al-An'am: 152], {Indeed, those who unjustly devour the wealth of orphans are only consuming fire into their bellies, and they will burn in a burning fire} [An-Nisa: 10]. He said: He proceeded. Whoever has an orphan, and he isolates his food from his food, and his drink from his drink, and makes some of his food and drink preferable, then he will be imprisoned until He eats it or spoils it, so that became difficult for them, so they mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and God revealed “And they ask you about Orphans, say: “A reform is best for them, and if you mix with them, then they are your brothers.” [Al-Baqarah: 220] So they mixed their food with their food, and their drink with their drink. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”"
"3185","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Hamid bin Mahmoud bin Harb Al-Muqri told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Saad, Amr bin Abi Qais told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was Peace and blessings of God be upon him. “A friend came to me when I was sick in Bani Salamah, and I said: O Messenger of God, how do I divide my money between my two children?” He did not respond to me at all, so I revealed: “God enjoins upon you regarding your children” [An-Nisa’: 11] “The two sheikhs agreed to narrate the hadith of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muhammad ibn “The one who is disturbed in this matter with words other than these” and this is an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3185 - They have cited its original"
"3186","This is how Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Al-Haytham bin Khalid told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, who said: I heard Muhammad bin Talha bin Yazid bin Rukana, narrating on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, he said: Because I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about “three who are dearer to me than the red camels of the caliph after him, and about a people who said, ‘Click. We pay zakat on our wealth and do not pay it back to you. Is it permissible to fight them? And about Al-Kalaala, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3186 - Rather, they did not go out to Muhammad at all and he did not catch up with Omar"
"3187","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba told us, Al-Haytham bin Khalid told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Ibn Uyaynah told us, he said: I heard Suleiman Al-Ahwal, narrating On the authority of Tawus, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, saying: I was the last of the people to meet Omar, so I heard him say: Say what you said. I said: What did you say? He said: I said: “Kalaala is one who has no children.” This is an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3187 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3188","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba told us, Al-Haytham bin Khalid told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Murrah, on the authority of Omar May God be pleased with him, he said: “There are three that are dearer to me than the world and everything in it, because the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, among them is more beloved to me than the world and what is in it: the caliphate. And usury and usury: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3188 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3189","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, On the authority of Ismail bin Raja’, on the authority of Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “Seven were deprived of lineage and seven of kinship. Then he recited This verse: “Forbidden to you are your mothers, your daughters, your sisters, your paternal aunts, your brother’s nieces, and your sister’s daughters” [An-Nisa: 23]. This is from the lineage {And your mothers who breastfed you, and your sisters through nursing, and the mothers of your wives, and your stepsons who are in your chambers from Your wives with whom you have consummated intercourse, but if you have not consummated your intercourse with them, then there is no blame on you and the relatives of your sons who are from your descendants, and that you combine “Two sisters, except what has already happened, and do not marry any of the women your fathers married.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it and there is a witness for it.” Authentic from the narration of Ikrimah.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3189 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3190","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba told me, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Al-Hasan bin Atiya told us, Ali bin Salih told us, On the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “Seven things were forbidden from lineage and seven from marriage.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3190 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3191","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, On the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he said: This verse {and chaste women, except those she possesses} Your oaths} [An-Nisa: 24] He said: “Every married woman has committed adultery, unless she is taken captive.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3191 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3192","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, Shu’bah told us, Abu Maslamah narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Nadrah saying: I recited to Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {So what of them did you enjoy? So give them their wages as an obligation.} [An-Nisa: 24] Ibn Abbas said: “So whatever of them you enjoy for an appointed time.” Abu Nadrah said: So I said: What? We read it that way. Ibn Abbas said: “By God, God has sent it down just like that.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3192 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3193","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq, Nafi bin Omar, He said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Mulaika saying: Aisha, may God be pleased with her, was asked about the pleasure of women, and she said: Between me and you is the Book of God. He said: And I read this verse {And those who guard their private parts, except for their wives or those whose right hands possess them, then they are not to be blamed. So whoever seeks after} [Al-Mu’minun: 5] what God has married or made king, he has done so except “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3193 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3194","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Bakhtari Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Bishr told us. Al-Abdi, narrated to us by Mas’ar bin Kadam, on the authority of Ma’an bin Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Masoud, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud May God be pleased with him, he said: “Indeed, in Surat An-Nisa there are five verses that make me happy because I have this world and all that is in it. Indeed, God does not do injustice to the weight of an atom.” And if it is a good deed, He will multiply it and give from Himself a great reward.} [An-Nisa: 40] {If you avoid the great sins that you are forbidden, We will pardon you. Your bad deeds and We admit you to a noble entrance} [An-Nisa: 31] {Indeed, God does not forgive that any partner be associated with Him, but He forgives anything less than that to whom He will} [An-Nisa: 48] {And if, when they wronged themselves, they had come to you and asked forgiveness from God, and the Messenger had asked forgiveness for them, they would have found God Forgiving, Merciful} {And whoever does evil or Whoever wrongs himself and then asks God for forgiveness will find God Forgiving and Merciful} [An-Nisa: 110] “Abdullah said: I am not pleased that I have this world and everything in it. “This is an authentic chain of narration, if Abdul-Rahman heard it from his father. There is a difference of opinion about that.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3194 - True"
"3195","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Wahhab told us, Qabisa told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, that she said: O Messenger of God, will the men fight and we do not fight and we do not fight and be martyred, but rather We get half the inheritance. So God revealed: “And do not covet what God has given some of you to preference over others” [An-Nisa’: 32] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, according to the stipulation of the two Sheikhs, if it is A mujahid heard from Umm Salamah.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3195 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3196","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Ja`far Ahmad bin Abdul Hamid Al-Harithi told us, Abu Usama told us, Idris bin Yazid, Talha bin Musrif narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty saying, “And those who Your oaths, so give them their share} [An-Nisa: 33] He said: When the immigrants came to Medina, they used to leave the Ansar as heirs, to the exclusion of relatives, out of mercy. For the brotherhood among whom the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a brotherhood. When it was revealed, {And for each of us We have appointed a guardian from what the parents and relatives have left} [An-Nisa: 33] He said: So I abrogated it. Then he said, “And those to whom I have pledged oaths, give them their share” [An-Nisa: 33] of victory and advice. “This is an authentic hadith.” According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3196 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3197","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abu Khalid informed us Al-Ahmar, Saad bin Tariq Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i told us, Rabi’ bin Harash told us, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: God brought one of His servants to whom God gave money and said to him: What did you do in this world? He said: “And they do not conceal anything from Allah” [An-Nisa: 42]. He said: I have not done anything, O Lord, except that You gave me money. I used to sell allegiance to people, and it was part of my character to Make things easy for the affluent, and give relief to the one who is in difficulty. God Almighty said: I have more right to that than you. They transgressed on behalf of My servant. Uqba bin Amir said. Al-Juhani and Abu Masoud Al-Ansari: This is what we heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and his family and grant them peace, “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that Muslim, but they did not expel him.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3197 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3198","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr al-Marwazi told me, Abd al-Aziz bin Hatim told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Saad told us, Amr told us Bin Abi Qais, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that a man asked him Concerning this verse: “By God, our Lord, we are not partners with God” [Al-An’am: 23] And he said in another verse: “And they do not conceal any speech from God” [An-Nisa’: 42]. Then Ibn Abbas: “As for his saying {By God, our Lord, we were not associators} [Al-An’am: 23], when they saw on the Day of Resurrection that he would not enter Paradise. Except the people of Islam. They said: Come, let us deny it. So God sealed their mouths, and their hands and feet spoke. {And they do not conceal God. A hadith} [An-Nisa: 42] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3198 - True"
"3199","Muhammad bin Ali bin Duhaym Al-Shaybani told us, Ahmad bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Abu Nu’aym and Qubaisa told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Al-Sa'ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: A man from the Ansar invited us before the prohibition of alcohol, so I attended. Maghrib prayer, then a man came forward and recited “Say, O you disbelievers.” Then he became confused, so it was revealed: “Do not approach the prayer while you are intoxicated until you know What do you say?} [An-Nisa: 43] The verse “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.” There is much benefit in this hadith, which is that the Kharijites This drunkenness and this reading are attributed to the Commander of the Faithful, Ali bin Abi Talib, and no one else, and God has exonerated him from it, for he is a narrator. This hadith \"\"\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3199 - True"
"3200","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, Ibrahim bin Hilal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, On the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and his companions came to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him in Mecca. They said: O Prophet of God, we were in glory while we were polytheists, but when we believed we became humiliated. He said: “Indeed, I have been commanded to pardon, so do not fight, but desist.” Then God Almighty revealed: “Have you not seen those to whom it was said, “Restrain your hands, and establish prayer?” And they paid zakat, but when fighting was prescribed for them, suddenly a group of them feared the people.} [An-Nisa’: 77] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but it was not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3200 - according to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"3201","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Al-Jawab told us, Ammar bin Ruzaiq told us, Ata bin Al-Sa’ib told us, On the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: “And if he is of a people who are enemies to you and he is a believer, then free A secure neck} [An-Nisa: 92] He said: The man would come to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and greet him, then he would return to his people and be among them. polytheists, then Muslims attack him by mistake in a troop or raid, and the man frees a slave {even if he is of a people between whom and you there is a covenant, A ransom delivered to his family, and the liberation of a believing slave} [An-Nisa: 92] He said: A man will be a covenant, and his people will be people of a covenant, so he will be delivered to them. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3201 - True"
"3202","Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Faqih told me about Al-Ray, Muhammad ibn al-Faraj told me, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad told me, Ibn Jurayj said: Ya’la ibn Muslim, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “{If you have been harmed by rain or are sick} [An-Nisa: 102] He said: It was revealed about Abd al-Rahman bin Awf who was wounded. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3202 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3203","Abu Abdul Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asbahani Al-Zahid told us, Ismail bin Ishaq told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Ayoub, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj Al-Sawwaf, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhallab, who said: I traveled to Aisha, may God be pleased with her, in this The verse “{It is not your wishes, nor the hopes of the People of the Book. Whoever does evil will be rewarded for it} [An-Nisa: 123] She said: It is what befalls you in this world.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3203 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3204","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Al-Jawab told us, Ammar bin Ruzaiq told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, On the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the words of the Almighty, “And what is recited to you in the Book concerning orphan women” [An-Nisa’: 127] In the first surah of Inheritance, they did not leave a boy as an inheritance until he had puberty. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3204 - True"
"3205","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, about Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, and Sulayman ibn Yasar, on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij, that there was a woman under him who had lost her teeth, So he married a young woman over her, and preferred the virgin over her, but his first wife refused to agree to that, so he divorced her once, even if he remained For her sake, it is easy. He said: If you wish, I will take you back, and be patient in following the consequences, and if you wish, I will leave you until your time is over. She said: Rather, take him back to me and be patient with the matter. So he took her back and then preferred her over her. She was not patient with the matter, so he divorced her for the second time and preferred her over her. The young woman, he said: That is the reconciliation which we have been informed of, that God has revealed concerning it “And if a woman fears disobedience or turning away from her husband, then there is no blame. They must make peace between themselves.} [An-Nisa: 128] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3205 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3206","Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told me, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told me, Abu Hudhayfah told me, Sufyan told me, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Subay’ Al-Kindi, He said: I was with Ali bin Abi Talib, and a man said: O Commander of the Faithful, have you seen the words of God Almighty: {For God will judge between you on the Day of Resurrection, And God will not make a way for the disbelievers over the believers.} [An-Nisa: 141] And they fight them, and they appear and kill? Then Ali said: “Come closer to him, come closer to him,” then he said: {For God will judge between you on the Day of Resurrection, and God will not give the disbelievers a way over the believers} [An-Nisa’: 141] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3206 - True"
"3207","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Abi Issa told us, Abdullah bin Al-Walid told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “{And there is not one of the People of the Book who does not believe in him before his death} [An-Nisa: 159] He said: The emergence of Jesus, son of Mary, may God’s prayers be upon him. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3207 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3208","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmed bin Mahran bin Khaled Al-Asbahani told us, Ubaid Allah told us Ibn Musa, Israel reported, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us He agreed that we should go to the land of the Negus, and the Quraysh heard about this, so they sent for Amr bin Al-Aas and Amara bin Al-Walid, and they gathered for the Negus. We presented gifts, and they approached al-Najashi and brought him a gift. He accepted it, and they prostrated to him. Then Amr ibn al-Aas said: Some of us desired About our religion while they are in your land. Al-Najashi said to them: In my land? He said: Yes, he said: So he sent for us and Ja`far said to us: None of you are speaking. I am your fiancé today. So we ended up with the Negus and he was sitting in the He was sitting, with Amr ibn Al-Aas on his right, Ammar on his left, and the priests from among the monks sitting as two rulers, so Amr and Amara said to him: They do not prostrate to you, so when we reached him, we told the priests and monks from him, “Prostrate to the king.” Ja’far said: We do not prostrate. Except for God. Al-Najashi said to him: What is that? He said: “God has sent among us His Messenger, and he is the Messenger about whom Jesus was given good tidings about a Messenger who will come after him, whose name is Ahmed, so he commanded us to worship God, and we do not associate anything with Him, and we establish prayer, and we pay zakat, and He enjoined us to do what is right, and forbade us from what is wrong. He said: So the people were amazed at his statement. When Amr saw that, he said to him: May God bless the king. They disagree with you regarding Jesus, son of Mary. So Al-Najashi said to Ja’far: What does he say? Is your friend regarding Ibn Maryam? He said: God says about it: He is the spirit of God and His word. He brought it out of a virgin virgin, no human being approached. He said: So the Negus took a stick. From the ground, he raised it and said: O community of priests and monks, these are no more than what you say about the son of Mary, he does not weigh this. Welcome. By you, and by whom you came from, I bear witness that he is the Messenger of God and that he is the one about whom Jesus, son of Mary, was given the good tidings, and had it not been for what I am in, The king, I will come to him to carry his sandals. Stay in my land as long as you want. He ordered them to be given food and clothing, and said: Respond to these two. I guided them, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.” Rather, I narrated it in this place, following the example of our sheikh, Abu Yahya. Al-Khafaf, for He mentioned it in the Almighty’s saying: “The Messiah will not disdain to be a servant of God” [An-Nisa: 172]\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3208 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3209","The sheikh and jurist Abu Al-Walid told me, Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim, and Fayyad bin Zuhair told us, they said: Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar narrated, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul-Rahman, who said: A man came to Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, and said: A man has died. He left a daughter and a sister to his father and mother. He said: “The daughter has half, but the sister has nothing left, so it belongs to her kinsfolk.” Then a man said to him: Omar ibn al-Khattab had decided otherwise, giving the daughter half and half to the sister. Ibn Abbas said: You know best. Mother of God? Muammar said: I did not know the reason for that until I met Ibn Tawus and mentioned the hadith of Al-Zuhri to him, and he said: My father told me that he had heard Ibn Abbas. He says: God Almighty said {If a man dies having no child and having a sister, then to her is half of what he left behind} [An-Nisa: 176]. Ibn Abbas said: So you said: You She gets half, even if he has a son. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3209 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3210","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, he said: It was read to Abdullah bin Wahb, Muawiyah informed you Ibn Salih, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Jubayr ibn Nufayr, who said: I performed Hajj and went to see Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and she said to me: O Jubayr, do you recite? The table? So I said: Yes, she said: “As for it being the last surah to be revealed, so whatever you find of what is lawful in it, make it lawful, and whatever you find of what is forbidden, make it unlawful.” This is An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3210 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3211","Abu Al-Abbas told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, he said: It was recited to Ibn Wahb, Hayy bin Abdullah Al-Maafiri told you, he said: I heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Amr, said that “the last surah to be revealed was Surat al-Ma’idah.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition The two sheikhs did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3211 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3212","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Shadhan Al-Jawhari told me, Mu’alla bin Mansour told us, Ibn Abi Zaida told us, On the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Aban bin Salih, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Salma, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us The people said: O Messenger of God, what is permissible for us regarding this nation that you have ordered to be killed? So God revealed: “They ask you, ‘What has been made lawful for them?’ Say, ‘The good things are made lawful to you, and what you have known of the raptors,’” [Al-Ma’idah: 4] “This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3212 - True"
"3213","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Yahya bin Fudayl told us, Al-Hasan bin Salih told us, on the authority of Samak Ibn Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, he said: “The sacrifices of Jews and Christians were only made lawful because they “They believed in the Torah and the Gospel.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3213 - True"
"3214","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad Al-Qurashi told us in Kufa, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Musab bin Al-Miqdam told us, Sufyan told us Ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the words of the Almighty, “He has placed among you prophets” [Al-Ma’idah: 20] He said: He made prophets from among you {and made you kings} [Al-Ma’idah: 20] He said: The woman and the servant {and He gave you what He has not given to any of the worlds} [Al-Ma’idah: 20] He said: Those who were between me at that time: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3214 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3215","Ali bin Muhammad al-Qurashi told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali told us, Musab bin Al-Miqdam told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Malik bin Husayn, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying: “{Our Lord, show us those who led us astray of the jinn and mankind, We should put them under Our feet} He said: Iblis and the son of Adam who killed his brother “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3215 - True"
"3216","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Muhadhar bin Al-Muwari’ told us, Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, On the authority of Hudhayfah, he heard a reciter reciting: “O you who have believed, fear Allah, and seek the way to Him.” [Al-Ma’idah: 35] He said: the closeness, then He said: The preserved companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, knew that Ibn Umm Abd was among the closest to God as a means of communication.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3216 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3217","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told me, Al-Sari ibn Khuzaymah told me, Sa’id ibn Sulaiman Al-Wasiti told me, Abbad ibn Al-Awwam told me, Sufyan ibn Sufyan ibn Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, he said: “Two verses were abrogated from Surat Al-Ma’idah {So judge between them.” Or turn away from them.} [Al-Ma’idah: 42] Then God Almighty revealed: “And judge between them according to what God has revealed, and do not follow their desires” [Al-Ma’idah: 49]. “The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3217 - True"
"3218","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, On the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, he said: We were with Hudhayfah and they mentioned {And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed - those are the disbelievers} [Al-Ma’idah: 44]. Then a man from among the people said: This is among the Children of Israel. Hudhayfah said: “What good brothers the Children of Israel are, if you have what is sweet and they have what is bitter. “No, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, until you follow Sunnah with Sunnah, like dirt with dirt.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3218 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3219","Ahmad bin Sulaiman al-Mawsili told us, Ali bin Harb told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hujayr, on the authority of Tawoos, he said: He said: Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them: “It is not the disbelief that they go to. It is not disbelief that leaves the religion.” And whoever does not judge by God sent it down - those are the disbelievers} [Al-Ma’idah: 44] Disbelief without disbelief “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3219 - True"
"3220","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad Al-Raqqashi told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, and Sa’id bin Amer, they said: Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, he said: I heard Iyad al-Ash`ari, saying: When it was revealed, “God will bring a people whom He will love.” And they love him.} [Al-Maeda: 54] The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “They are your people, O Abu Musa,” and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gestured with his hand. To Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3220 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3221","Abd al-Samad bin Ali al-Bazzaz told us, in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa al-Qadi told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Harith bin Ubaid, narrated by Ma’bad al-Jariri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to guard until This verse was revealed: “And God will protect you from the people” [Al-Ma’idah: 67]. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took his head out of the dome and said to them: “O you! People, go away, for God has protected me.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3221 - True"
"3222","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying {So We wrote with the witnesses} [Al Imran: 53] He said: “With the nation of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he was greeted, and his nation bore witness to his conveyance of the Message, and bore witness to the Messengers that they had conveyed this hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3222 - True"
"3223","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, On the authority of Masruq, he said: Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, was brought an udder, and he said to the people: Come closer, so they began to feed it, and a man among them was in In a direction, Abdullah said: Come closer. He said: I don't want it. He said: Why? He said: Because I deprived the udder. Abdullah said: This is one of the steps of Satan. Abdullah said: “O you who have believed, do not deprive the good things of God has made lawful for you, but do not transgress; for God does not like transgressors.} [Al-Maeda: 87] Come near and eat, and make atonement for your oath, for this is one of the steps of Satan. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3223 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3224","Al-Fasawi told us the origin of his book verbally, Ya’qub bin Sufyan Al-Fasawi told us, Yahya bin Ya’la bin Al-Harith told us, Abi Ya’la bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jami’ al-Muharbi, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Amer al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with him On his authority, “Two Christian men bore witness to the will of a Muslim man who died among them.” He said: “The people who made the will became suspicious, so they came.” Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari refused them, so he made them swear to God after the afternoon prayer that they had not bought a price for it, nor had they concealed the testimony of God. Indeed, then, we are among those “The sinners.” Amer said: Then Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari said: By God, this is a story. . . . “It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3224 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3225","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Harun bin Sulaiman Al-Asbahani told us, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhail, on the authority of Imran ibn al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: Quraysh said to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Call on God, your Lord, to He turns Al-Safa into gold for us, and we believe in You. He said: “Or do you do that?” They said: Yes, so he called upon God, and Gabriel came to him and said: Indeed, your Lord recites peace upon you, and says: If you wish, Safa will become gold for them, so whoever disbelieves Did I torture some of them with a punishment that I would not torture anyone else in the world, and if I wished, I could open for them the doors of repentance and mercy? He said: “O Lord, the door of repentance and mercy.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3225 - True"
"3226","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz, and Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, saying: Muhammad bin Abdul Wahhab told us Al-Abdi, Ja’far bin Aoun informed, Ismail bin Abdul Rahman informed, Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir informed us, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, He said: When Surah Al-An'am was revealed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, glorified God, then said: “This Surah was recited by a number of angels. The Horizon” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, “For this Ismail is Al-Suddi, and Al-Bukhari did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3226 - No, by God, he did not catch Ja’far Al-Suddi, and I think this is fabricated."
"3227","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “{Then he fulfilled a term and a term appointed with Him} [Al-An’am: 2] He said: They are the term of the term of this world, and the term of the Hereafter appointed. No one knows it except God, and His saying {And if We had sent down to you a book on paper and they had touched it with their hands} [Al-An'am: 7] He said: They touched it and looked at it, they would not have They believe in it. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3227 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3228","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Mandah Al-Asbahani told us, Bakr bin Bakkar told us, Hamza bin Habib told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abu Thabit, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the words of God Almighty, “And they forbid it, And they distance themselves from him.} [Al-An'am: 26] He said: It was revealed about Abu Talib who forbade the polytheists from harming the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and kept his distance. “about what he brought”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3228 - True"
"3229","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told us, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of, who heard Ibn Abbas said, regarding the words of God Almighty, “And they forbid it, and keep away from it” [Al-An’am: 26]. He said: It was revealed about Abu Talib, who was “He forbids the polytheists from harming him and keeps away from him.” The hadith of Hamzah bin Habib is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it."
"3230","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafid told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told me, Muhammad bin Sabiq told me, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Najiya bin Ka’b Al-Asadi, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: Abu Jahl said to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “We may know, O Muhammad, that you You uphold the ties of kinship, and you believe the hadith, and we do not disbelieve you, but we disbelieve what you have brought. Then God Almighty revealed {We may know that what they say grieves you, for they do not disbelieve you, but the wrongdoers deny the signs of God} [Al-An'am: 33] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3230 - They did not go out to Najiya for anything"
"3231","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani told me in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, about Ja`far al-Jadari, on the authority of Yazid ibn al-Asam, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, in the Almighty’s saying {Nations like you} [Al-An’am: 38] He said: “The creation will be gathered together.” On the Day of Resurrection, all of them will be animals, animals, birds, and everything, and it will amount to God’s justice to take for a large number of the Qur’an, then He says: Be dust. That is {the disbeliever says, “Oh, I wish I were dust}” [Al-Naba’: 40] “This Jafar al-Jadari is Ibn Burqan. He was used as evidence.” Muslim, and it is authentic according to its condition, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3231 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3232","Abu Bakr al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, on the authority of Ziyad bin Harmala, He said: I heard Ali bin Abi Talib reciting this verse {Those who believe and do not mix their faith with injustice} [Al-An’am: 82]. He said: “This is in Abraham and his companions are not among this nation.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it. “But they agreed on the hadith of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, that they said: O Messenger of God, who among us has not wronged himself? The hadith is completely lengthy without this interpretation.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3232 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3233","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told me, my grandfather told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Hushaym told us, Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying {He knows its resting place and its place of resting place} [Hud: 6], He said: “The resting place is that which is in the womb. “From what is alive, and from what is already dead, and what is stored is what is in the core.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3233 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3234","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hakam bin Aban, my father told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he was asked: Did Muhammad see his Lord? He said: Yes. “He saw as if his feet were on green land and beneath it was a curtain of pearls. So I said: O Ibn Abbas, does not God say, ‘Sights will not perceive Him?’” And it is He who comprehends sight.} [Al-An'am: 103] He said: O mother of yours, that is his light, and it is his light that when it is manifested with its light nothing can overtake it. This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3234 - Rather, Ibrahim is abandoned"
"3235","Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, “And among the livestock are burdens and furnishings” [Al-An’am: 142]. He said: “The burden is what he carries of camels and small flocks.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3235 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3236","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Amr bin Dinar told us, he said: I said: By Jabir bin Abdullah: They claim that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade the meat of domestic donkeys on the Day of Khaybar.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3236 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim\n He said: Al-Hakam bin Amr used to say that, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he refused that sea, meaning Ibn Abbas, and was satisfied. God said about them, and he recited {Say: I do not find in what was revealed to me forbidden} the verse. The people of pre-Islamic times used to leave dirty things, so God Almighty revealed it in His Book and made clear what was permissible and what was forbidden. So what was permissible is It is permissible, and whatever he forbids is forbidden, and whatever he is silent about, it is pardon. Then he recited this verse: “Say, ‘I do not find in what has been revealed to me forbidden to anyone willing He feeds it unless it is dead carcasses, or spilled blood, or the flesh of a pig} [Al-An’am: 145] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” In this context”"
"3237","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, about Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he heard a man say: Evil is not by destiny. Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “Between us and the people of predestination {those who associate others will say, ‘If God had willed, we would not have associated them, nor would our fathers} [Al-An’am: 148] until he reached: {And if He had willed, He could have guided you all} [Al-An'am: 149] Ibn Abbas said: And incapacity and lack of destiny «This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition The two sheikhs did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3237 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3238","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us, in Marwa, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Malik bin Ismail al-Nahdi told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Abdullah bin Khalifa, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, saying: “In Al-An’am there are decisive verses, they are the mother of the Book, then He recited {Say, “Come, recite what your Lord has forbidden to you}” [Al-An’am: 151] The verse: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3238 - True"
"3239","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir reported, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: When God revealed {And do not approach the property of the orphan except with what is best} [Al-An'am: 152] {Indeed, those who unjustly devour the wealth of orphans are only consuming fire into their bellies, and they will burn in a burning fire} [An-Nisa: 10] He has an orphan, so he separates his food from his food, and his drink from his drink, so he makes some of his food preferable, and it is withheld for him until he eats it, or It became corrupt, so that became difficult for them, so they mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “So God Almighty revealed {They ask you about the orphans. Say “A settlement is better for them, but if you mix with them then they are your brothers.” [Al-Baqarah: 220] So they mixed their food with their food, and their drink with their drink. “This is a hadith.” The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”"
"3240","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Wasiti told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Idris, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Samit, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who He pledges allegiance to me on these verses.” Then he recited {Say, “Come, and I will recite what your Lord has forbidden to you}” [Al-An’am: 151] until he concluded the three verses. So whoever fulfills So his reward is with God, and whoever diminishes anything, God will make him realize it in this world, that is his punishment, and whoever delays it until the Hereafter, his matter is up to God. He will punish him, and if he wills, he will forgive him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.” Rather, they all agreed on the hadith of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Idris, Concerning the worship of “Pledge your allegiance to me that you will not associate anything with God.” Sufyan bin Hussein Al-Wasiti narrated both hadiths on the authority of Al-Zuhri. It should be attributed to illusion in one of the two hadiths if they are combined, and God knows best.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3240 - True"
"3241","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, Asim bin Abi Al-Najood told us, And Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told me, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Sulaiman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, Asim told us, On the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote a line for us, then he wrote on his right, and on the lines to his left, then he said: “This is the path of God and these paths. On each path there is a devil calling to it {and indeed this is my path, straight.” So follow him, and do not follow other paths, lest he separate you from his path} [Al-An’am: 153] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not produce it.” And he witnessed its wording. One hadith: Al-Sha’bi’s hadith, on the authority of Jabir, from an untrusted source.”"
"3242","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “And We created you, then We formed you” [Al-A’raf: 11]. He said: They were created in The crucifixes of men, and their images in the wombs of women. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3242 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3243","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, about Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Do not make faces ugly.” He mentioned the rest of the hadith: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3243 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3244","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Rayh al-Sammak told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Sufyan bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ubaid The author, the author, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, said: “God created four things with His own hand: the throne, and the Gardens of Eden. And Adam, and the Pen, and he was hidden from creation by four things: by fire, and by darkness, and by light, and by darkness. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not produce it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3244 - True"
"3245","Abd al-Samad bin Ali al-Bazzaz told me, in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Abd al-Hamid al-Jafi told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Aban told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Amr bin Qais Al-Malali, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him About them, he said: “The clothes of Adam and Eve were like nails, so when they tasted the tree, they covered themselves with leaves from Paradise.” He said: It is fig leaves. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3245 - True"
"3246","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, he said: I heard Muslim Al-Bateen, narrating on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The woman was circumambulating the Kaaba in Pre-Islamic times, she was naked, with a rag on her private part, and she said: Today some or all of it is visible, so whatever of it is visible I do not make lawful. Then this verse was revealed: “Say, ‘Who has forbidden the adornment of God?’” [Al-A’raf: 32] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3246 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3247","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, Al-Haytham bin Khalid told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Yunus bin Abi told us Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Silah ibn Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The people of Al-A’raf are a people whose good deeds have surpassed them.” Hell, and their evil deeds will be limited to them from Paradise. When their eyes are turned away from meeting the inmates of Hell, they will say: Our Lord, do not put us with The unjust people. While they were like that, your Lord looked upon them. He said: “Arise, enter Paradise, for I have forgiven you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3247 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3248","Muhammad ibn Ali al-San’ani informed me, in Mecca, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abbad informed me, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, Muammar informed me, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed Al-Hijr said: “Do not ask about the verses, for the people of Salih asked them, and he meant the she-camel coming from this valley, and coming from this valley. So they disobeyed the command of their Lord, and disobeyed it, and the cry seized them, and God calmed down all of them under the heaven, except one man, who was in a sanctuary. God. It was said: Who is he? He said: “Abu Righal, when he left the sanctuary, the same thing happened to him that befell his people.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not take it out.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3248 - Sahih according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3249","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib and Hisham bin Ali told us, they said: Affan bin Muslim told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Muhammad bin Ali bin Bakr Al-Adl told me, and the pronunciation for it, Al-Hasan bin Al-Fadl told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Thabit reported, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in the Almighty’s saying: {Then when his Lord appeared to the mountain, He caused it to collapse} [Al-A'raf: 143] Hammad said: Thus, and he placed his thumb on the knuckle of the right little finger. He said: Then Humayd bin Thabit said: Do you speak like this? He said: Then Thabit struck Humaid’s chest with his hand and said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrates it and I do not narrate it?” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3249 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3250","Ali bin Abdullah Al-Hakimi told me, in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Surayj bin Al-Numan told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, On the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The news is not the same as the sighting. God told Moses about what his people had done to the calf, but he did not throw the tablets. When he saw what they had done, he threw the tablets. This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. The two sheikhs did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3250 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3251","Omar bin Muhammad bin Safwan Al-Jumahi told me, in Mecca in the house of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj told us Ibn Minhal, Hammad Ibn Salamah told us, Samak Ibn Harb told us, on the authority of Sa`id Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: He came Aaron was watching the Samaritan as he was making the calf, and he said to him: What are you doing? He said: What is beneficial and does not harm, and he said: O God, give him what he asked of you in himself. Then when he went, he said: “O God, I ask you that he fall asleep and fall down.” And when he prostrated, he bowed down, and when he raised his head, he bowed down, and that was at the invitation of Aaron.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3251 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3252","Abu Ahmad Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Adl told us, Ahmad bin Nasr told us, Amr bin Talha told us, Asbat bin Nasr Al-Hamdani told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul Rahman Al-Suddi, on the authority of Murrah Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, that he said: “The companions of The calf, they said, “Hata Sqamatha, Azbah Mizba,” which in Arabic means strong red wheat, in which there are black hairs. That is the saying of the Almighty, “So He changed those who They wronged themselves in saying other than what was said to them.} [Al-Baqarah: 59] But when they refused to prostrate, He said: God commanded the mountain to fall on them, so they looked at it. They were overwhelmed, so they fell down, prostrating on one side, and they looked at the other side, and God had mercy on them and revealed it from them, and they said: What is a prostration that is more beloved to God Almighty? Of prostration by which the torment was revealed from you, so they prostrated for that in parts. That is the saying of the Almighty: {And when We cleaned the mountain Above them as if it were a canopy} [Al-A’raf: 171] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3252 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3253","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir reported, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: “And Moses chose his people seventy men for our appointment” [Al-A’raf: 155] He said: He called for Moses, and God sent seventy, so he made his supplication when he called him for those who believed in Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and followed his saying {so forgive us And have mercy on us, and You are the best of forgivers.} [Al-A'raf: 155] {Then I will record it for those who fear and pay zakat} [Al-A'raf: 156] and those who follow Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3253 - True"
"3254","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us dictation in Dhul-Hijjah in the year three hundred and ninety-nine. Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told me, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told me, Al-Shafi’i told me, Yahya bin Sulaym told me, Ibn Juraij told us on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: I entered upon Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, while he was reading from the Qur’an before his sight went away, and he was crying, so I said: What makes you cry? O Ibn Abbas, may God make me your ransom? He said: He said: Do you know Ayla? I said: What is Ayla? He said: A village in which there were Jewish people, so God forbade whales to them on the Sabbath, so their whales used to come to them on their Sabbath, according to law. white and plump, like the likes of labor in their courtyards and buildings. If it was other than the Sabbath, they would not find it, and would not reach it except on hardship and heavy provisions, so some of them said to one another, or whoever among them said that: Perhaps if we took it on the Sabbath and ate it in... Other than Saturday. So a family among them did that, so they took it and grilled, and their neighbors smelled the smell of grilling, and they said: By God, we do not see the companions of the Banu So-and-so. Something, then others took it until it spread among them, and it became widespread, so they separated into three groups, one group ate, and the other group forbade.And a group said: “Why do you preach to a people? It is God who will destroy them or punish them” [Al-A’raf: 164] with a severe punishment. Then the group that forbade said: We warn you of the wrath of God and His punishment, lest He befall you with an attack or slander or with some of what He has. Torment, by God, I will not make you sleep in a place while you are in it. They left the wall and attacked it the next day. They struck the door of the wall, but he did not answer them. Uhud, so they brought a ladder and leaned it against the wall, then one of them climbed onto the wall and said: O servants of God, they are monkeys, and by God they have howling tails. Three times, then he descended from the wall and opened the wall, so people entered upon them, and the apes knew their lineage from humans, but humans did not know their lineage from Monkeys, he said: Then the monkey comes to his relative and relative of the human, and rubs against him, and clings to him, and the human says: Are you so-and-so? He gestures with his head, saying yes, and cries, and the monkeys come to her relative and relative of the human, and he says to her: Are you so-and-so? Then she gestured with her head, “yes,” and cried.Then the man will say to them: Did we not warn you that God’s wrath and punishment might befall you with an eclipse or a transformation or some of the torment with Him? Ibn Abbas said: So listen to God saying, “So We saved those who forbid evil, and We seized those who did wrong with a miserable punishment because they were defiantly disobedient.” I do not know what the third group did. Ibn Abbas said: How many evil things we have seen and did not forbid them. Ikrimah said: So I said: What do you see? May God make me your ransom? Indeed, they denied it and hated it when they said, “Why do you preach to a people whom God will destroy or punish with a severe punishment?” He liked my saying that, and he ordered me two thick sacks of cloth, which he covered me with. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3254 - True"
"3255","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim al-Ghifari told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Abu Ja`far Issa told us Ibn Abdullah Ibn Mahan, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ Ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ubayy Ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, in his saying, the Almighty {And when your Lord took from the children of Adam from their backs their offspring and made them testify against themselves} to His Almighty’s saying {Will We then destroy you for what He did? The false ones} [Al-A’raf: 173] He said: “He gathered them together for Him that day, all that will exist until the Day of Resurrection, and He made them spirits, then formed them. And He summoned them and they spoke, and He took from them the covenant and covenant, and made them testify against themselves. Am I not your Lord? They said: Yes, we bore witness, lest you say on the Day of Resurrection, “Indeed, we were unaware of this,” or you say, “Our fathers only participated before, and we were offspring after them. Will you destroy us because of what the false people did? He said: For I bear witness against you the seven heavens and the seven earths, and I bear witness against you. Your father, Adam, lest you say on the Day of Resurrection, “We did not know,” or say, “Indeed, we were unaware of this,” so do not associate anything with Me, for I will send to you My messengers, they remind you of my covenant and my covenant, and I send down to you my writings, and they said: We bear witness that you are our Lord, and our God is no Lord but you.We have no god but You, and their father Adam looked up to them and saw in them the rich and the poor and good appearance and other things, and said: My Lord. If you made your servants equal, and he said, “I love to be thanked,” and he saw among them the prophets like lamps, and they were singled out for another covenant with the message. And prophecy, that is what the Almighty said: “And when We took from the prophets their covenant, and from you and from Noah” [Al-Ahzab: 7] the verse. And it is the Almighty’s saying: “So set your face upright toward religion, upright. It is the nature of God which He created mankind. There is no altering of God’s creation.” [Al-Rum: 30] and that. His saying {This is a warner of the first wars} [An-Najm: 56] And His saying {And We did not find most of them to have any covenant, but if We found most of them disobedient} [Al-A'raf: 102] And this is His saying: {Then We sent after him messengers to their people, and they brought them clear proofs, but they would not believe in what they disbelieved in. Before} he was aware of what they acknowledged, who would deny it and who would believe in it, so the spirit of Jesus was one of those spirits upon which he was taken. The covenant was made in the time of Adam, and He sent that spirit to Mary when she withdrew from her family to an eastern place.So she took a veil from them as a veil, so We sent to her Our Spirit, and he appeared to her as sound human beings.} [Maryam: 17] to his saying {decrees} [Maryam: 21] So she carried him. He said: She carried the one who spoke to her, which is the spirit of Jesus, peace be upon him. Ka’b said: Someone entered it, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3255 - True"
"3256","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Hamid bin Abi Hamid Al-Muqri told us, Ishaq bin Sulayman told us, he said: I heard Malik Ibn Anas, he mentions, and Abu Bakr Ibn Abi Nasr told me, Ahmad Ibn Muhammad Ibn Issa told me, Abdullah Ibn Maslamah told me, regarding what was read to Malik on the authority of Zayd ibn Abi Anisa, that Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab informed him on the authority of Muslim ibn Yasar Al-Juhani said that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, was asked about this verse: {And when your Lord took from the children of Adam from their backs Their descendants and make them bear witness against themselves. Am I not your Lord? They say, “Yes, we bear witness,” lest you say on the Day of Resurrection, “Indeed, we were heedless of this.” [Al-A'raf: 172] Then Omar bin Al-Khattab said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was asked about it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God created Then Adam wiped his back with his right hand and produced offspring from him, and said: I created these for Paradise, and for the deeds of the people of Paradise they will do. Then he wiped On his back, and He produced offspring from him, and said: I created these for Hell, and they will do the work of the people of Hell. Then a man said: O Messenger of God, So what is the work? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, when God created a man for Paradise, He would use him to do the work of the people of Paradise.” The hadith is authentic according to Muslim’s condition. And they did not take him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3256 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3257","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Bishr bin Musa Al-Asadi told us, and Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, they said: Abu Nu’aym told us, Hisham bin Saad told us, On the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When God created Adam He wiped his back, and from his back fell every breath of which He is the Creator until the Day of Resurrection, like an atom. Then He placed it between the eyes of every human being among them. And a ray of light. Then he showed them to Adam, and Adam said: Who are these, O Lord? He said: These are your descendants. Then Adam saw a man among them that he admired, and a glint between his eyes flashed and he said: O Lord, who is this? He said: This is your son David. He will be among the last of the nations. Adam said: How long have you given him to live? He said: Sixty years. He said: O Lord, increase his life by forty years, until his life is one hundred years. Then God Almighty said: “Then it will be written and sealed and will not be changed.” When Adam’s life was over, the angel of death came to him to take his soul. Adam said, “Are there not forty years left of my life left?” The angel of death said to him, “Did you not give it to your son David?” He said: He denied, so his offspring denied, and he forgot, and his offspring forgot, and he sinned, so his offspring sinned. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and he did not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3257 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3258","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdul Hamid Al-San’ani told me in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Al-Thawri reported, on the authority of Al-A’mash, and Mansour, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, in his saying “And recite to them the story of the one to whom We gave Our signs and he separated from them” [Al-A’raf: 175]. He said: He is Balaam bin Ba’ura.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3258 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3259","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Wahb bin Jarir bin Hazim told us, my father told me, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Ishaq, says: Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Abu Umamah, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Samit, may God be pleased with him, he said: I asked him about Al-Anfal. He said: Among us, on the day of Badr, the people were in three houses, a third fighting the enemy, and a third gathering belongings and taking them. The captives, and a third at the tent, guarding the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When he collected the belongings, they disagreed about it, so those who gathered it and took it said, The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, has performed a voluntary voluntary act. Every one of us has done what he likes, so he is ours rather than you. And those who fight the enemy and seek it said: By God, had it not been for us, you would not have injured him, for we occupied the people. And the guards said: By God, we would not have injured him. You have more right to it than us. We thought that we would fight the enemy when God gave us their shoulder to take the goods when no one was preventing them from doing so. But we feared that the enemy would surprise the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so we stood up before him. He said: So God snatched it from our hands and gave it to the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. “So he divided it equally. There were not five in it at that time, so there was fear of God, obedience to Him, and obedience to His Messenger, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but he did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3259 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3260","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulayman told us, he said: I heard Dawud bin Abi Hind, He narrated on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever does such-and-such or does such-and-such or does In such-and-such a place, he has such-and-such.” So the young men hastened to that, and the old men stood firm under the banners. When God granted victory over them, the young men came. They ask for what has been appointed for them, and the elders said: Indeed, we were a response to you and we were under the banners, so God Almighty revealed {They ask you about the Anfal Say: “The Anfal belongs to Allah and the Messenger, so fear Allah and make peace among yourselves” [Al-Anfal: 1] “This is a hadith with a sound chain of transmission, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3260 - True"
"3261","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished with the dead, he was told: The camel is upon you, and there is nothing besides it. So Abbas called him. While he was confident that he was not fit for you, he said: “Why?” He said: “Because God promised you one of the two groups, and He has fulfilled to you what He promised you.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3261 - True"
"3262","Muhammad bin Ali bin Mukhlid Al-Qadi told us, in Baghdad, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Ibrahim Al-Dawrqi told us, Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Sadoosi told us, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, in this verse “{And who He will turn to them that day His back.} [Al-Anfal: 16] He said: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim” was revealed among us on the day of Badr, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3262 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3263","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told me, Jeddi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Muhammad bin Falih told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father, he said: Ubayy ibn Khalaf came on the day of Uhud to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He wanted him, so some of the believers objected. “So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered them to let him go, so Mus’ab bin Umair met him.” Brother of Banu Abd al-Dar. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw Ubay’s collarbone from the gap between the back of the shield and the egg, so he stabbed him. With his spear, Ubayy fell from his horse, and no blood came out of his stab, so he broke one of his ribs, so his companions came to him while he was bellowing. The bull bellowed, and they said to him: What is wrong with you? It is only a scratch. Then he mentioned to them what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Rather, I am killing my father.” Then he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, if this had happened to the people of Dhu al-Majaz, they would all have died. Then my father died and was taken to Hell, and he was crushed by the inmates of the burning fire before he reached Mecca, so God revealed: “And you did not throw when you threw, but God threw.” [Al-Anfal: 17] The verse: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3263 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3264","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi informed us, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i informed us, and the word for it is that Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ya’qub ibn Ibrahim bin Saad, my father narrated to me, Salih narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, Abdullah bin Tha’labah bin Abi Suair Al-Adhri narrated to me, he said: The questioner was Abu Jahl, for he said when the people met: “O God, whichever of us has severed ties of kinship and given us what we do not know, so be gracious to him.” In the morning, that was its opening, so God revealed {If you seek victory, victory has certainly come to you} [Al-Anfal: 19] to His saying: {And indeed, God is with The Believers} [Al-Anfal: 19] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3264 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3265","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul God, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty saying {He separates between a person and his heart} [Al-Anfal: 24] He said: “It comes between the disbeliever and faith, and it comes between the believer and sin.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3265 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3266","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan bin Maimun told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Othman bin Khathim, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubaid bin Rifa’ah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered Quraysh and said: “Are there anyone else among you?” They said: “Our sister’s son is among us, our ally is among us, and our master is among us.” He said: “Our ally is among us, our sister’s son is among us, and our master is among us. “Among you are the righteous.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3266 - True"
"3267","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told me, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told me, Saeed bin Abi Ayyub told me, Yazid bin Abi Habib told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “And prepare against them whatever force you are able” [Al-Anfal: 60]. Al-Bukhari included it because Salih bin Kaysan stopped it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3267 - According to the condition of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, and some of them agreed on it"
"3268","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, about Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The ties of kinship will be severed, and the blessings will be atoned, and if God brings the hearts close, He will not Something moved it, then he recited: “If you had spent all that is on earth, you would not have reunited their hearts” [Al-Anfal: 63] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.” And they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3268 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3269","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told us about Al-Ray, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris told us, Malik bin Ismail Al-Nahdi told us, he told me Muhammad bin Fudayl bin Ghazwan, on the authority of his father, and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, narrated to me Ya’la bin Ubaid, Fudayl bin Ghazwan told me, he said: I met Abu Ishaq after his sight had gone, so I said to him: Do you know me? He said: I know you and I love you, then he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told me, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, that he said: “It was revealed This verse is about those who love one another for the sake of God: {If You were to spend all that is on earth, You would not reconcile their hearts} [Al-Anfal: 63] The verse: “This is the wording of the hadith of my father.” Hatim: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3269 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3270","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, consulted Abu Bakr about the captives and said: Your people and your clan, so let them go. So he consulted Omar and said: Kill them. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ransomed them. Then God Almighty revealed: “It is not for a prophet to have captives until he has established strength in the land.” [Al-Anfal: 67] To his saying {So eat of what you have gained, lawful and good} [Al-Anfal: 69] He said: Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, met Omar, and he said: He was about to attack us. Your disagreement is a scourge “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3270 - Sahih according to Muslim’s conditions"
"3271","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Zakaria bin Adi told us, Ubaid Allah bin Amr Al-Raqi told us, On the authority of Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Khaythamah, he said: Saad ibn Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him, was among a group of people who mentioned Ali. They insulted him, and Saad said: “Wait about the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for we have attained this world with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Then God Almighty revealed: “If it had not been for a Book from God that had preceded, a great punishment would have touched you for what you took” [Al-Anfal: 68]. So I hope that it will be a mercy from In the sight of God, it preceded us. Some of them said: By God, he used to hate you and called you Al-Akhnas. Saad laughed until he laughed loudly, then he said: Isn’t it possible for a person to blame his brother in a matter that is between him and him, and then he does not reach that point? His honesty and he mentioned another word: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3271 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3272","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Saad Al-Awfi told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Awf bin Abi Jamila told us, on the authority of Yazid Al-Farisi, he said: Ibn Abbas told us, he said: I said to Uthman bin Affan: What made you resort to al-anfal, which is from al-Muthanna and al-Muthanna? Bara’a, which is one of the two hundred, so you joined them together, and did not write “In the Name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful,” and you placed it among the seven long letters, so what made you do so? That? Othman said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was one of those whom time would come, and he used to send down to him numerous surahs. He said: And he was When something befalls him, he calls someone to write for him, and he says: “Put this in the surah that contains such-and-such.” And the Anfal were of the At the beginning of its revelation in Medina, it was clear from the end of the Qur’an, and its story was similar to hers, so I thought it was from it. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested, and he did not explain to us that it was one of them, so I did not write a line between them. In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, “This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3272 - This was presented and it is true"
"3273","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Junaid told us, Muhammad bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, Yaqoub bin Ja’far bin Suleiman Al-Hashimi told us, My father told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas, he said: I heard my father saying: I asked Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him: Why was it not written in Baraa’ah, “In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful?” He said: Because “In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, security and innocence were revealed by the sword, there is no security in it.”"
"3274","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah Al-Yashkari told us, Al-Qasim bin Al-Hakam Al-Arni told us, Sufyan bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salamah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “You do not read a quarter of it, meaning Bara’ah, and you call it Surat Al-Tawbah, and it is Surat Al-Aqab.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3274 - True"
"3275","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, Shu’bah informed us, about Suleiman Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Muharrar ibn Abi Hurairah, on the authority of his father, he said: I was in the mission sent by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He went with Ali, may God be pleased with him, innocently to Mecca, and his son, or another man, said to him: What were you calling out to? He said: We used to say: “No one will enter Paradise except a believer, and no polytheist will perform Hajj after the year, and no naked person will circumambulate the Kaaba, and whoever is between him and The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a covenant, and his term was four months, so I called out until my voice became sound. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and it was not \"He takes him out\"\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3275 - True"
"3276","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told me about Al-Tabaran, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Sulayman bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Dimashqi told me, Al-Walid told me Ibn Muslim, Hisham Ibn al-Ghaz told us, Nafi’ informed me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stood on the day The sacrifice between the pebbles during the Hajj in which he performed Hajj, and he said to the people: “What day is this?” They said: This is the Day of Sacrifice. He said: “What country is this?” They said: This is the Sacred Land. He said: “What month is this?” They said: The sacred month. He said: “This is the greatest day of Hajj. Your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred to you, just as this country is sacred on this day.” Then he said: “Have I not conveyed the message?” They said: Yes. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, began saying: “O God, bear witness.” Then he bid farewell to the people, and they said: This is the Farewell Pilgrimage. This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, but they did not mention it in this context.” Most of this text is included in the two Sahih books, except for his saying: “The greatest day of Hajj is the day of “Sacrifice is a Sunnah.” There are opinions about it from the Companions and Followers, may God be pleased with them, and there is a disagreement among them about it. Among them are those who said: The Day of Arafat. And among them are those who said: “The Day of Sacrifice.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3276 - True"
"3277","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Abu Jafar Al-Razi informed us, Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told me about Hamdan, Ishaq bin Ahmad al-Khazzaz told us, Ishaq bin Sulayman al-Razi told us, Abu Ja`far al-Razi, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever leaves the world for sincerity To God alone, with no partner, and to establish prayer and pay zakat. He departed from it, and God was pleased with him. It is the religion of God that the messengers brought. And they communicated it from their Lord before the confusion of hadiths and the differences of desires, and the confirmation of that in the Book of God {Then if they repent and establish prayer, and perform Zakat, so clear their way} [At-Tawbah: 5] And the Almighty said: {And if they repent} [At-Tawbah: 5] He says: Put down the idols and worship them {and establish prayer And give the zakat, then they are your brothers in religion.} [At-Tawbah: 11] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3277 - The beginning of the report is raised and the rest of it is included, as I see it"
"3278","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Shadhan al-Jawhari narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, on the authority of my father Ishaq, on the authority of Silah ibn Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying: “{So fight the imams of disbelief. Indeed, they have no faith} [Repentance: 12] He said: They have no covenant. Hudhayfah said: They were not killed after “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3278 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3279","Abu Bakr bin Balwayh told me, Muhammad bin Shazan told me, Ali bin Abdullah told me, Abu Dawud told me, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, in his saying “{So fight the imams of disbelief} [At-Tawbah: 12] He said: Abu Jahl bin Hisham and Umayyah Ibn Khalaf, Utbah Ibn Rabi’ah, Abu Sufyan Ibn Harb, and Suhail Ibn Amr, and they were the ones who broke God’s covenant and intended to expel the Messenger. From Mecca: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3279 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3280","Da'laj bin Ahmad Al-Sijzi told us, Ahmad bin Bishr bin Saad Al-Marthadi told us, Khaled bin Khaddash told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr ibn al-Harith told me, on the authority of Darraj, on the authority of Abu al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “If you see a man attending the mosque, do not be embarrassed to bear witness that he is a believer, for God says, ‘He only maintains the mosques of God. Whoever believes in God} [At-Tawbah: 18] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3280 - True"
"3281","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri told us, Yahya bin Ya’la bin Al-Harith Al-Muharbi told us, My father, Ghailan bin Jami’ told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Qattan Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyas, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. About them, he said: When “Those who hoard up” [At-Tawbah: 34] gold and silver but do not spend them in the way of God was revealed, that was hard for the Muslims. They said: It is not possible for any of us to leave money to his son that will remain after him. So Omar said: I will release you. He said: So they set off, and Omar set off, and Thaban followed him, and they came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Omar said: O Prophet. God, this verse is difficult for your companions. The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God did not impose zakat except to enrich with it what was left of your wealth. Rather, He imposed inheritances.” In the wealth that will remain after you.” He said: Then Omar said “Allahu Akbar” and then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Shall I not tell you of the best that a person can hoard? “A righteous woman, when he looks at her, she pleases him, when he commands her, she obeys him, and when he is absent from her, she protects him.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3281 - I do not know Othman, and the news is strange"
"3282","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi told me, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Safwan bin Amr informed, Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr told me on the authority of his father. He said: We sat with al-Miqdad bin al-Aswad in Damascus while he was on a coffin. There was merit on his part, and a man said to him: If you had stayed away from the attack for a year. He said: “The Resurrection has come upon us, meaning Surat Al-Tawbah. God Almighty said, ‘Go forth, light and heavy.’ [At-Tawbah: 41] And I find nothing but light.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3282 - True"
"3283","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, {Indeed, it is God who accepts repentance from His servants and takes alms} [At-Tawbah: 104] He said: Indeed “God accepts charity, if it is good, then he takes it with his right hand, and a man gives in charity something similar to a morsel, and God grows it for himself as “One of you raises his offspring, or his foal, and it grows in the palm of God, or in the hand of God, until it is like Uhud.” The two sheikhs agreed to narrate the hadith of Abu Al-Hubab Saeed bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, without this wording: “This is an authentic hadith according to their conditions, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3283 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3284","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar told us: Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Nasr, Abu Naim Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, Abdullah bin Aamer Al-Aslami told us, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad Al-Sa’idi, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about the mosque that was founded on piety. He said: “It is This is my mosque.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “And the hadith of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri is more authentic than it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3284 - True"
"3285","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Musa bin Ishaq Al-Ansari told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Waki’ told us, Usama bin Abi Shaybah told us. Zaid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa`id al-Khudri, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, that he said: “The mosque that was founded on piety is a mosque The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3285 - True"
"3286","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid ibn Ibrahim al-Hafiz in Hamdan told us, Umair ibn Mirdas told us, Mutarrif ibn Abdullah told us, Sahbal told us Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: Two men strove in The mosque that was founded on piety. One of them said: It is the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the other said: It is the Quba Mosque, so they agreed. To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about that. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The mosque that was founded on piety is my mosque.” 60 this”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3286 - Its chain of transmission is good"
"3287","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anbari told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Hisham bin Ammar Al-Sulami told us, Sadaqa bin Khalid told us, about Utbah bin Abi Hakim told me, Talha bin Nafi’ told me, Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, Jabir bin Abdullah, and Anas bin Malik told me May God be pleased with them, when this verse was revealed {in it are men who love to purify themselves} [Al-Tawbah: 108] The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O community of Ansar, God has praised you with goodness in purification, so what is this purification of yours?” They said: We perform ablution for prayer, we wash ourselves from ritual impurity, and we clean ourselves with water. He said: This is that, so you should do it. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3287 - True"
"3288","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Sulayman bin Musa Al-Muddhikir told us, Junayd bin Hakim Al-Daqqaq told us, Hamid bin Yahya Al-Balkhi told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about “ The tourists, and he said: “They are the fasting ones.” This is an authentic hadith according to the two sheikhs’ conditions, and they did not narrate it on the grounds that it was sent by most of the companions of Ibn Uyaynah. They did not mention Abu Hurairah in its chain of transmission.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3288 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, it was sent by most of the companions of Ibn Uyaynah."
"3289","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdul-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Muhammad al-Barti told us, Abu Nu’aym and Abu Hudhayfah told us, they said: Sufyan told us, Ali bin Isa bin Ibrahim told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told me, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told me, Waki’ told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of my father Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard a man asking forgiveness for his parents, and they were polytheists, so I said: No. You ask forgiveness for your parents, and they are polytheists. He said: Didn’t Abraham ask forgiveness for his father while he was a polytheist? So I mentioned it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it was revealed: “It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to ask forgiveness for the polytheists, even if they are relatives after that.” It did not become clear to them that they were the inmates of Hell, and Abraham’s request for forgiveness for his father was no more than a promise he had made to him. When it became clear It is because he is an enemy of God that he has disavowed. Indeed, Abraham is stubborn and forbearing.} [Al-Tawbah: 114] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3289 - True"
"3290","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz informed me, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Jundi told me about Mecca, Abu Hammah Al-Yamani told us, Sufyan bin Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: When Abu Talib died, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Have mercy on you.” May God forgive you, uncle, and I will continue to ask forgiveness for you until God Almighty forbids me.” So the Muslims began to ask forgiveness for their dead who They died while they were polytheists, so God Almighty revealed {It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to ask forgiveness for the polytheists, even if they were relatives after that. It has become clear to them that they are the inmates of Hell.} [At-Tawbah: 113] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.” Abu Ali said to us after him: No. “I know someone who received this hadith on the authority of Sufyan other than Abu Hammah Al-Yamani, and he is trustworthy, and the companions of Ibn Uyaynah sent him.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3290 - True"
"3291","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Sufyan bin Hussein told us, about Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: When Abu Talib’s death was near, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to him. He greeted him, and with him were Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah and Abu Jahl bin Hisham. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Uncle, you are the greatest of them.” I have a right over me, and they have the best hand with me, and because you have a greater right over me than my father, say a word that will make it necessary for you to intercede for me on the Day of Resurrection. Say no. There is no god but Allah.” So they said to him: Do you renounce the religion of Abdul Muttalib? He remained silent, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, repeated it to him, and said: I follow the religion of Abdul-Muttalib, so he died, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I will certainly ask forgiveness for you as long as I have not forbidden you,” so God Almighty revealed, “It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to ask forgiveness for the polytheists.” [At-Tawbah: 113] The verse {And Abraham did not seek forgiveness for his father} [At-Tawbah: 114] until the end of the verse “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, for Yunus And Aqeel they sent, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3291 - True"
"3292","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Hani, On the authority of Masruq ibn al-Ajja`, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out to look into The graves, and we went out with him, so he ordered us to sit down, then he walked past the graves until he came to one of them, where he conversed with him for a long time, then his wailing rose. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was crying, and we cried because of his crying. Then he came to us and Omar bin Al-Khattab met him and said: O Messenger of God, what is the matter? He made you cry. He made us cry and frightened us. Then he came and sat with us and said: “Did my crying frighten you?” So we said: Yes, O Messenger of God, and he said: “Indeed, the grave in which you saw me conversing is the grave of my mother, Aminah bint Wahb, and I have sought permission from my Lord in to visit her, so he gave me permission to do so, so I asked him for permission to ask forgiveness for her, but he did not give me permission to do so, and he revealed to me {It is not for the Prophet and those who believe that... They ask forgiveness for the polytheists.} [At-Tawbah: 113] until he concluded the verse: “And Abraham’s seeking of forgiveness for his father was not except as a result of a promise he had made to him} [At-Tawbah: 114] Then it touched me the way a child takes his father from Raqqa. That is what made me cry. “It was true to their condition and they did not take him out like this.” Driving “Only a Muslim narrated the hadith of Yazid ibn Kaysan on the authority of Abu Hazim on the authority of Abu Hurairah in which it is summarized.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3292 - Ayyub ibn Hani’ was deemed weak by Ibn Mu’in"
"3293","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told me, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told me, Abu Hudhayfah told me, Sufyan told me, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Minhaal. Bin Amr, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he was asked about the Almighty’s saying: “And his throne was upon Water} [Hud: 7] What was the water on? He said: On the surface of the wind “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3293 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3294","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Isfaraini told me, Umair bin Mirdas told me, Abdullah bin Bukayr Al-Ghanawi told us, Hakim bin Jubayr told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saad, Ali’s client, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wanted to launch a campaign as his own. He said: So he called Jafar and ordered him to stay behind in Medina, and he said: I will never stay behind after you, O Messenger of God. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called me and came to me when I lagged behind before I could speak. He said: So I cried, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What makes you cry, Ali?” I said: O Messenger of God, more than one characteristic makes me cry. The Quraysh will say tomorrow: How quickly he left behind his cousin and let him down, and one characteristic makes me cry. Another: I wanted to engage in jihad in the path of God, because God says: “And they shall not tread upon any place that enrages the disbelievers, nor shall they inflict punishment upon an enemy.” Until the end of the verse, I wanted to be exposed to God’s grace, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As for your saying that the Quraysh say, ‘How quickly He lagged behind his cousin and let him down. You have an example in me, they said: a magician, a soothsayer, and a liar. Aren’t you satisfied to be to me in the same position as Aaron? From Moses except that there is no prophet after me? As for your saying, “I am referring to God’s grace,” these are spices of pepper that we brought from Yemen, so sell them and enjoy them, you and Fatima, until “May God bestow upon you of His bounty, for the city is not fit except with me or with you.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3294 - How can he keep company when the situation is overwhelming him?"
"3295","Al-Hussein bin Halim Al-Maruzi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed, Abdan informed, Abu Khalda informed, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, He said: I was going around the Kaaba with Ibn Abbas, and he was taking my hand and teaching me the tone of speech. He said: O Abu Al-Aaliyah, “Do not say You have departed from the prayer, but say: “You have completed the prayer” [An-Nisa: 103], for God Almighty says: “They departed; God has turned their hearts away} [At-Tawbah: 127] “This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3295 - True"
"3296","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, Abu Amer Abd Al-Malik bin Amr Al-Aqdi told us, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, and Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, on the authority of Ubayy bin Kaab, may God be pleased with them About him, he said: “The last thing that was revealed from the Qur’an is: ‘Indeed there has come to you a messenger from among yourselves. To him is hard what you have troubled. He is anxious for you as a believer, compassionate. Merciful} » The hadith of Shu’bah on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid “is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3296 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3297","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told me in Bukhara. Abu Ismah Sahl bin al-Mutawakkil told us, Amr bin Marzuq told us, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying: “And give good news to those who believe that for them A predecessor of truthfulness with their Lord.} [Yunus: 2] He said: A predecessor who was truthful in the sight of their Lord.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3297 - True"
"3298","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, Uyaynah bin Abd al-Rahman al-Ghatfani, said: I heard my father speaking, on the authority of Abu Bakra, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No.” Desire and do not be a transgressor, for God says: “Your transgression is only against yourselves” [Yunus: 23] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not produce it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3298 - True"
"3299","Abu Al-Tayyib Tahir bin Yahya Al-Bayhaqi told me about it from the origin of his uncle’s book. Khali Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Bayhaqi told us, Abdullah bin Salih, Al-Layth narrated to me, Khalid bin Yazid narrated to me, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, who said: I heard Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hussein reciting This verse {And God invites to the abode of peace and guides whomsoever He wills to a straight path} [Yunus: 25] Then he said: Jabir bin Abdullah told me. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us one day and said: “Indeed, I saw in a dream as if Gabriel was at my head and Michael was at my side.” My two feet, one of them says to his friend: Set him as an example. So he said to him: Listen to what your ear has heard, and understand with the understanding of your heart. The likeness of you and your nation is like a king who took a house, then built a house in it, then He made a banquet there, then sent a messenger to invite the people to their meal. Some of them responded to the messenger, and some of them left behind, for God is the King. The abode is Islam, and the home is Paradise, and you, O Muhammad the Messenger, whoever responds to you will enter Islam, and whoever enters Islam will enter Paradise, and whoever He entered Paradise and ate from it. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not expel it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3299 - True"
"3300","Ali bin Issa told us, Muhammad bin Amr Al-Harashi told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulayman Al-Taymi told us, Ubi told us, Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Saad, the client of Abu Usayd al-Ansari, who said: Uthman ibn Affan, may God be pleased with him, heard that a delegation of the people of Egypt had They came, so he welcomed them, and when they heard about him, they came in the same way. He said: He disliked that they should come to Medina against him. He said: So they came to him and said to him: Call for the Qur’an, and open the seventh, and they called it the seventh Surah Yunus. So he recited it until he came to this verse “{Say, ‘Have you seen what was revealed? God has provided for you, but you have made of it forbidden and lawful. Say, “Has God given you permission? Or is it something against God that you invent?” [Yunus: 59] Then they said to him: Stop, have you seen what you have protected? Is it a fever? Has God given you permission, or is it something you invent against God? He said: So he said: Go ahead, it was revealed in such-and-such and such. As for the fever, the fever period before me was for the camels of charity, so when I took office, and the camels increased Charity, so I increased my fever, when he increased in charity “It is true according to the condition of a Muslim and they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3300 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3301","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Numan told us, Ismail bin Aliya told us, Ayoub, on the authority of Nafi’, said: Al-Hajjaj prolonged the sermon and Ibn Umar put his head in my lap, so Al-Hajjaj said: Ibn Al-Zubayr changed the Book of God. Then Ibn Umar sat down and said: “Neither you nor Ibn al-Zubayr can do that. {There is no changing the words of God} [Yunus: 64]. Then Al-Hajjaj said: You have been given knowledge. If it helps you, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3301 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3302","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Ubadah Ibn al-Samit, may God be pleased with him, said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the saying of God Almighty. {For them is good news in the life of this world and in the Hereafter} [Yunus: 64] He said: “It is a good vision, a man sees it, or it is seen for him.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3302 - True"
"3303","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi informed us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, Shu’bah informed us, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr, speaking, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “He made Gabriel puts clay in Pharaoh’s mouth for fear that he will say: There is no god but Allah. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it” except that Most of Shu’bah’s companions attributed it to Ibn Abbas.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3303 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3304","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hassan bin Ayyub told us, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Zakaria Al-Makki told us, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Al-Walid Al-Azraqi told us, Muslim bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him When the stone came down, in the Battle of Tabuk, he stood up and addressed the people, and said: “O people, do not ask your Prophet about the signs, for these The people of Salih asked their Prophet to send them a sign, so God sent them a she-camel, and she used to come back from this dawn and drink their water on the day of And they drink from its milk, just as they used to drink from their water. But they disobeyed the command of their Lord, so they became obstructed, so God promised them three For several days, and it was a promise from God, not a lie, then the cry came to them, and God destroyed whoever was under the easts and wests of the heavens. Among them was the exception of a man who was in the Sanctuary of God, and the Sanctuary of God prevented him from the punishment of God. They said: O Messenger of God, who is he? He said: “Abu Raghal” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3304 - True"
"3305","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl informed us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab informed us, Ja’far bin Aoun informed us, Ismail bin Abi Khaled informed us, On the authority of Abraham, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, in the words of God Almighty: “He knows its resting place and its shelter” [Hud: 6] He said: Its resting place is in the wombs and its depository is where it dies. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3305 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3306","Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told me, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told me, Abu Hudhayfah told me, Sufyan told me, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he was asked about the Almighty’s saying: “And His throne was upon the water” [Hud: 7] on which Something like water? He said: On the surface of the wind “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3306 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3307","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad Al-Daqqaq told us in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah bin Abi Dawud Al-Munadi told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Abu Sakhrah Jami` ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Safwan ibn Mahrez, on the authority of Buraydah al-Aslami, he said: A people entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. They began to ask him, saying: Give us. Until that upset him, and others entered upon him and said: We have come to greet the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and agree with him about religion, and ask him about starting This matter. He said: “There was God and nothing else but Him, and the Throne was over the water, and He wrote everything in the Remembrance, then He created seven heavens.” He said: Then someone came to him, and he said: Your camel is gone. He said: I wish I had left it. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3307 - True"
"3308","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Harun bin Sulaiman told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Razin, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “And if We delay the torment from them for a specified time.” [Hud: 8] He said: For a specified time. This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3308 - True"
"3309","Muhammad bin Ali al-Sana’ani told me, in Mecca, Ali bin al-Mubarak al-Sana’ani told us, Zayd bin al-Mubarak al-Sana’ani told us, on the authority of Abd al-Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Basri, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “There is no one from this nation who hears of me, neither Jew nor Christian, nor believes in me, but he will enter Hell. So I began to say: Where Do you believe it in the Book of God? Until I found this verse {And whoever of the factions disbelieves in it, the Fire is his appointed time} [Hud: 17]. He said: The factions are all sects. This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3309 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3310","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Musa bin Yaqoub Al-Zumai told us, Faid, the servant of Ubayd Allah bin Ali bin Abi Rafi’, told me that Ibrahim bin Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abi Rabi’ah, He told him that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If God had mercy on one of Noah’s people, to the womb of the boy’s mother.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Noah had stayed among his people for a thousand years, minus fifty years, calling on them until he was At the end of his time, he planted a tree, and it became great, and took away every sect. Then he cut it down, then made a ship to build it, and they passed by and asked him. So he says: Make it a ship. They mock him and say: You make a ship on land, and how does it sail? He said: You will know. When he finished, the oven gushed, and water poured into the vessels. The boy’s mother was afraid for him, and she loved him very much. So she went out to the mountain until she reached a cleft, and when the water reached her, she went out with it until she came to rest on the mountain, and when the water reached her neck, she raised it. With her hand until the water washed it away, so if God had mercy on one of them, he would have mercy on the boy’s mother. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3310 - Its chain of transmission is dark, and Moses is not like that"
"3311","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abu Yahya Al-Hammani told us, Al-Nadr Abu Omar Al-Khazzaz told us, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “There were three hundred years between Noah and the destruction of his people, and the dragon had fled in India and a ship sailed... Noah was in the Kaaba for a week.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3311 - An-Nadr is weak"
"3312","Maymun bin Ishaq Al-Hashimi told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Al-Mufaddal bin Salih told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Hanash al-Kinani, he said: I heard Abu Dharr saying, as he was approaching the door of the Kaaba: O people, whoever knows me, I am the one you know, and whoever He denied me, for I am Abu Dharr. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The likeness of my family is like Noah’s Ark. Whoever boards it is saved, and whoever He left her behind and drowned. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but he did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3312 - A favorite that Al-Tirmidhi included, only they declared it weak"
"3313","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Ashib told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abu Hind, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Wadi Al-Azraq and said: “What “This?” They said: Wadi Al-Azraq, and he said: “It is as if I am looking at Musa ibn Imran descending and bellowing to God with the takbir.” Then he came to a thief. He said: “What is this second?” They said: The second of such-and-such? He said: “It is as if I am looking at Yunus ibn Matta on a red camel with a wrinkled rump and a fibrous muzzle, and he is wearing the talbi, and he is wearing a wool robe.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3313 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3314","Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Ja`far ibn Muhammad ibn Matar narrated to me, and I asked him. He said: Abu Muhammad Ja`far ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr narrated to me. Al-Hafiz, Abu Kurayb told us, Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, told the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: I see you have grown old. He said: “I have turned gray due to the incident and they were wondering, and when the sun was turning.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3314 - according to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"3315","Abu Al-Hasan Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told me, my grandfather told me, Abu Thabit Muhammad bin Ubaidullah Al-Madani told me, Ibrahim bin Saad told me, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ibrahim Al-Khalil, peace be upon him, inspired this Arabic language with inspiration.” This is a strange and authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. If Al-Fadl ibn Muhammad preserved it continuously on the authority of Abu Thabit, then Abu Ali the Hafiz narrated it to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasa’i informed us, Ubaid narrated to us Allah bin Saad Al-Zuhri, on the authority of my uncle, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Towards him\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3315 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3316","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani, the memorizer of dictation, told us, Hammad bin Mahmoud Al-Muqri told us, Issa bin Ja’far Al-Razi told us, Sufyan bin Saeed, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, on the authority of Ata’, regarding the words of God Almighty {May God’s mercy and blessings be upon you, Ahl al-Bayt} He said: I was with Abdullah bin Abbas when a man came to him and greeted him, so I said: May God’s peace, mercy, blessings, and forgiveness be upon you. Ibn Abbas said: “End to what the angels have reached.” This is a strange and authentic hadith by Al-Thawri. I do not know that we wrote it except with this. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3316 - Sahih Gharib"
"3317","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim Al-Adl told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Saeed bin Suleiman Al-Wasiti told us, Khalid bin Abdullah told us. Al-Wasiti, on the authority of Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, said: Ibn Abbas said: When the messengers of God came to Lot, he thought that they Two guests met him, so he brought them closer until he seated them near, and he brought his daughters, who were three, and seated them among his guests and among his people, so he came His people were rushing to him, and when he saw them he said: “These are my daughters. They are more pure for you, so fear God and do not be disgraced in my presence.” [Hud: 78] They said: “What do we have in Your daughters are a right, and indeed you know what we want.} [Hud: 79] {He said, “If only I had power over you or could take refuge in a strong corner} [Hud: 80] Then Gabriel turned to him. Peace be upon him, and he said, “Indeed, we are the messengers of your Lord. They will never reach you.” [Hud: 81] He said: So he obscured their eyes, and they returned behind them, riding one another until They went out to those at the door and said: We have come to you from the sorcerer of people, who has blinded our sight. So they went off, riding one after another, until they entered. The village was raised at some point of the night, until it was between the sky and the earth, to the point that they could hear the voices of birds in the air of the sky, then it was turned over. So the plague came out upon them. Whoever the plague overtook, it killed, and whoever went out, it followed him. Where there was a stone, it killed him. He said: So he departed. With his daughters, and they were three, until he reached such-and-such a place in the Levant, then his eldest daughter died, and a spring emerged from her, called Then he set off wherever God willed him to reach, and the youngest died, and a spring came out from her, called Al-Ra'una, and all that remained of them was Al-Wusta: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” Perhaps someone is delusional and thinks that this and others like it are in the circumstances and not Likewise, if a companion explains the recitation, it is a chain of transmission according to the two Sheikhs.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3317 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3318","Muhammad bin Ali bin Duhaim Al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, Muhammad bin Muslim Al-Taifi, Amr bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: People saw a fire in the cemetery, so they went to it. Then, behold, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was in the grave, and behold, he was saying: “Give me your companion, and behold, he is the weak man who raises His voice in remembrance: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3318 - True"
"3319","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Handali told us, Amr bin Muhammad Al-Qurashi told us, Khallad bin Muslim Al-Saffar, on the authority of Amr bin Qais Al-Malali, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, according to the saying God Almighty {We narrate to you the best of stories} [Joseph: 3] verse. He said: “The Qur’an was revealed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it was recited to them for a period of time, and they said: O Messenger of God, if only you would narrate it to us. Then God Almighty revealed {These are the verses of the clear Book} [Joseph: 1] followed by His saying: {We narrate to you the best of stories} [Joseph: 3] the verse. So he recited to them for a while, and they said: O Messenger of God, if only you had spoken to us. Then God Almighty revealed: “God has sent down the best of hadiths, a book that is similar” [Az-Zumar: 23]. All of this is commanded by the Qur’an. “This is an authentic hadith.” The chain of transmission and they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3319 - True"
"3320","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told me, Zuhayr bin Harb told me, Waki’ told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of my father Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, said: “The most honorable of people are three: Al-Aziz when he said to his wife, ‘Honor his resting place, perhaps it will benefit us. Or do we take him as a son, and she said: “O father, hire him. Indeed, the best of those you hire is the strong and trustworthy.” [Al-Qasas: 26] And Abu Bakr when he spied on Omar, may God be pleased with them, said: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3320 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3321","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I heard Abu Wael, saying: I heard Abdullah bin Masoud, “reciting {and she said, ‘It is for you’” [Yusuf: 23] and he was told and he said: This is how we were taught. “This is an authentic hadith.” According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3321 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3322","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, On the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: “{Had he not seen the proof of his Lord} [Joseph: 24] He said: Jacob appeared to him, and he struck his chest, and his desire came out from his fingertips. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3322 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3323","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran Al-Asbahani told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, about Khasif, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “Joseph stumbled upon three stumbles when he was about to do so, and he was imprisoned, and he said to the man: {Remember me before your Lord} [Joseph: 42] So he remained in prison for a few years, and Satan made him forget the remembrance of his Lord, and His saying to them {Indeed, you are thieves} [Joseph: 70] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3323 - It is bad news"
"3324","Sheikh Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told me, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Musa bin Masoud told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amara bin Al-Qaqa’ Al-Dhabi, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, “{The matter about which you are asking a fatwa has been decided} [Joseph: 41] He said: When they narrated what they saw, and Joseph, peace be upon him, passed by, one of them said: We did not see anything, so he said: The matter that was in it was decided You ask: “This is an authentic hadith, but they did not narrate it.”"
"3325","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman, the jurist in Baghdad, told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Amr told us, about Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The Noble One is the son of the Generous One, the son of the Generous One, the son of The Generous, Yusuf bin Yaqoub bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim Khalil al-Rahman. If I had remained as long as Yusuf had stayed and then the supplicant came to me, I would have responded when he came to him. The Messenger and said: Return to your Lord, and ask Him what is the matter with the women who cut off their hands. Indeed, my Lord is All-Knowing of their plots. “This is an authentic hadith on the authority of Muslim’s condition, and they did not narrate it in this context. Rather, they agreed on the hadith of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id and Abu Ubaid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: “If I had stayed In prison, Joseph only stayed\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3325 - They agreed on the hadith of Saeed and Ibn Ubaid on the authority of Abu Hurairah."
"3326","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, Musa bin Ali bin Rabah told us, on the authority of his father, He said: A man asked permission for Omar, may God be pleased with him, and he said: Ask permission for the son of the good people, so Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: Allow him. When he entered, Omar said to him: Who are you? He said: I am so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, the son of so-and-so. He said: So he started counting men from the pre-Islamic nobles, and Omar said to him: “You are Yusuf bin Ya’qub bin Ishaq bin Abraham? He said: No. He said: That is the son of good people, and you are the son of evil people. You only consider me the men of the people of Hell. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not He takes him out.” “Ali bin Rabah is a great Tabi’i.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3326 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3327","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Muzaki told me about Marw, Abdullah ibn Ruh al-Madaini told me, Yazid ibn Harun told me, Hisham informed us Ibn Hassan, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: Omar said to me: O enemy of God and enemy of Islam, you have betrayed the wealth of God. He said: I said: I am not the enemy of God, nor the enemy of Islam, but I am the enemy of those who are hostile to them, and I have not betrayed the wealth of God, but it is the price of camels and arrows. She met. He said: So he returned it to me and I repeated these words to him. He said: So he fined me twelve thousand. He said: So I stood up for the morning prayer and said: O God, forgive me. For the Commander of the Faithful. After that, he wanted me to do the job, but I refused. He said: Why did Joseph ask for the job and he was better than you? So I said: Joseph is a prophet, the son of a prophet, the son of a prophet, the son of a prophet, and I am the son of Umaima and I fear three and two. He said: Don’t you say five? I said: No. He said: What are they? I said: “I fear that I will speak without knowledge, that I will give a fatwa without knowledge, that my back will be beaten, that my honor will be insulted, and that my money will be taken.” “By beating.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3327 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3328","Sheikh Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told us, Hisham bin Bishr told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi told us. Ghaniyah, on the authority of Husayn ibn Umar, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It was The Prophet Jacob, peace be upon him, was a brother and friend in God. One day he said: O Jacob, what made your sight blind and what made your back bend? The one who made my sight go away was crying over Joseph, and the one who made my back hardened was the sadness over my son Benjamin. He said: Then Gabriel, peace be upon him, came to him and said: O Jacob, God extends his greetings to you, and says to you: Are you not ashamed to complain of me to others? God said: Then Gabriel said: I know what you doubt, O Jacob. He said: Then Jacob said: Yes, my Lord, have you not had mercy on the old man? You have taken away my sight. And you arched my back, so return my fragrance to me, so that I may smell it before death, then do to me whatever you wish. He said: Then Gabriel came to him and said: Indeed, God He extends his greetings to you, and says to you: Be glad, and let your heart rejoice, for by My glory, if they were dead, I would spread them apart, so prepare food for the poor, for The most beloved of My servants to Me are the prophets and the poor. Do you know why I took away your sight, and bent your back, and why Joseph’s brothers did to him what they did to him? You slaughtered a sheep, and a poor orphan came to you while he was fasting, and you did not feed him anything of it. He said: Then Jacob was after that, when he wanted Lunch was ordered by a caller, and he called out: Whoever of the poor wants lunch, let him have lunch with Jacob. And when he was fasting, he ordered a caller, so he called out to whomever he was fasting. If one of the poor is fasting, let him break his fast with Ya’qub.” Al-Hakim said: This is what I heard in the handwriting of Hafs bin Umar bin Al-Zubayr. I think Al-Zubayr is an illusion from The narrator is Hafs bin Omar bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha Al-Ansari, the son of my brother Anas bin Malik. If that is the case, then the hadith It is authentic, and Imam Abu Ya’qub Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Handali narrated this hadith in a mursal interpretation.”"
"3329","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam informed us, Ishaq informed us, Amr ibn Muhammad informed us, Zafir ibn Sulaiman informed us, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Jacob had a close brother,” and he mentioned Hadith is similar to it"
"3330","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali Al-Maamari told us, Abu Muslim Abdul Rahman bin Waqid Al-Harrani told us, Ibrahim bin Saad told us, Saleh bin Kaysan told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, he said: I said: For her: God Almighty’s saying: “Until when the messengers despaired and thought that they had been lied to.” [Joseph: 110] I said: Indeed they despaired that they had been lied to. Really? She said: God forbid that the Messengers should think that about their Lord, but they were the followers of the Messengers, when victory was late for them and it became difficult for them. The affliction. The messengers thought that their followers had lied. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3330 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3331","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi and Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, they said: Musa bin Ismail told us, Sadaqah told us. Bin Musa, on the authority of Muhammad bin Wasi’, on the authority of Samir, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Indeed, your Lord Almighty He says: If My servants had obeyed Me, I would have given them rain by night, and made the sun shine on them by day, and would not have made them hear the sound of thunder. A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3331 - Rather, Sadaqah bin Musa is false"
"3332","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the words of God Almighty {God erases whatever He wills} [Al-Ra’ad: 39] He said: “From anyone The two Scriptures are two Scriptures. God erases what He wills from one of them {and confirms, and with Him is the mother of the Book} [Al-Ra’ad: 39], meaning the entirety of the Book “He has provided evidence.” Muslim with Hammad, and Al-Bukhari cited Ikrimah as evidence.” This is strange and authentic from the hadith of Sulayman al-Taymi, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3332 - Sahih Gharib"
"3333","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Hamid bin Mahmoud told us, Ishaq bin Suleiman Al-Razi told us, Hanzalah told us, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “Being careful about destiny is of no use, but God erases through supplication whatever destiny He wishes.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3333 - True"
"3334","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty and Majestic saying: “Have they not seen that We bring the earth to reduce it from its outskirts?” [Al-Ra’ad: 41] He said: The death of its scholars and jurists. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3334 - Talha bin Amr said: Ahmad is abandoned"
"3335","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Yazid bin Abi told us Hakim, Al-Hakam bin Aban told us, he said: I heard Ikrimah say: Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “Indeed, God has favored Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” He greeted the inhabitants of heaven and favored him over the inhabitants of the earth. They said: O Ibn Abbas, because God has favored him over the inhabitants of heaven. He said: God Almighty said: {And whoever among them says, “Indeed, I am a god besides Him,” that is We reward him with Hell. Thus do We reward the wrongdoers.} [Al-Anbiya: 29] And he said to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, {Indeed, We have opened for you a clear victory, so that God may forgive you. Whatever of your sins preceded and whatever comes later} [Al-Fath: 2] the verse. They said: Why did God favor him over the people of the earth? He said: God Almighty says: “And We did not send a messenger except in the language of his people” [Ibrahim: 4] the verse, and He said to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, “And what We have sent you to all mankind as a bringer of good tidings and a warner.} [Saba: 28] So He sent him to the jinn and mankind: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission.” The ruling is Ibn “Aban has been cited as evidence by a group of the imams of Islam, but the two sheikhs did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3335 - True"
"3336","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmad bin Mihran Al-Asbahani told us, Ubaid Allah bin Moses informed Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, that he said in the words of God Almighty “And they put their hands back in their mouths” [Ibrahim: 9] He said: They bit it. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3336 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3337","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abd Al-Razzaq informed us, Al-Thawri informed us, about Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, in the Almighty’s saying: “And they put their hands in their mouths” [Ibrahim: 9] Abdullah said: Thus he put his hand in his mouth and bit his hand. He said: They bit their fingers in anger, “This is an authentic hadith, in addition to their condition.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3337 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3338","Sheikh Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed me, Muhammad ibn Shadhan al-Jawhari informed me, Sa`id ibn Sulaiman al-Wasiti informed us, Muhammad ibn Yazid informed us. Ibn Khunais, on the authority of Abdul Aziz Ibn Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: When God Almighty revealed On his Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: {O you who have believed, protect yourselves and your families from the Fire} [Al-Tahrim: 6] recited by the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on One night, or he said one day, a young man fell down unconscious, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed his hand on his heart. He moved, so he said: “O boy, say there is no god but Allah.” So he said it and gave him good tidings of Paradise. Then his companions said: O Messenger of God, who is among us? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Have you not heard the words of God Almighty: {This is for him who fears my position and fears My threat} [Ibrahim: 14] «This is a hadith The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”"
"3339","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Safwan bin Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Busr, on the authority of Abu Umamah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in the Almighty’s saying {And he will be given to drink of purulent water He sips it} [Ibrahim: 17] He said: “It is brought near to him and he dislikes it, but when he is brought near to him his face becomes blackened and his scalp falls out. He cut his intestines until he came out of his anus. God says, “And they gave them boiling water to drink, and it cut their intestines.” [Muhammad: 15] And God Almighty says, “And if They cry out for relief. They are helped with water like mulch that scalds the faces. What a miserable drink} [Al-Kahf: 29] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3339 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3340","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Anas Al-Qurashi told me, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Abdullah bin Waqid, Muhammad ibn Malik narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Bara’ ibn Azib, may God be pleased with him, “Their greeting on the day they meet him is greeting” [Al-Ahzab: 44] He said: On the day They will meet the angel of death. There is no believer whose soul is taken except that he greets him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission.” And they did not take it out.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3340 - Abdullah bin Waqid said, Ibn Adi said that the hadith is dark, and Muhammad bin Malik said that Ibn Hibban does not take it as evidence."
"3341","Al-Hussein bin Ayyub told us, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Al-Alaa bin Abdul-Jabbar Al-Attar told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Shuaib Ibn Al-Habhab, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought with a mask of secret. “He recited” like a word “Good, like a good tree.” He said: “It is the palm tree.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3341 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3342","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ali al-Shaybani told me about Kufa, Ahmad ibn Hazim al-Ghafari told me, Abu Nu`aym told me, Bassam al-Sayrafi told me, Abu Al-Tufayl Amer bin Wathilah said: I heard Ali, may God be pleased with him. He stood up and said, “Ask me before you lose me, and after me you will not ask someone like me.” So he stood up. Ibn Al-Kawa’ said: “Who are those who exchanged the blessings of God for disbelief and made their people dwell in the abode of destruction?” He said: The hypocrites of Quraysh. He said: Who are those who have gone astray? Their striving in the life of this world while they think that they are doing well. He said: Among them are the people of Harawraa. “This is an authentic and high hadith.” And Bassam. Ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sayrifi is one of the trustworthy narrators of the Kufans, whose hadiths are collected but they did not narrate it.”"
"3343","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ali bin Maymun Al-Ruqi told us, Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faryabi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Amr Dhu Murr, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, in His Almighty saying, “And they made their people dwell in an abode of destruction” [Ibrahim: 28]. He said: They The two Afjrans from Quraysh, Banu Umayyah and Banu al-Mughirah. As for Banu al-Mughirah, God cut off their backs on the day of Badr. As for Banu Umayyah So they were entertained for a while: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3343 - True"
"3344","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Harun told us, Uqba bin Makram Al-Dhabi told us, Mahboub bin Al-Hassan told us, Dawud bin Abu Hind, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited {the day the Earth other than the earth, and the heavens, and they emerge before God, the One, the Supreme.} I said: Where will the people be on that day? He said: On the path: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3344 - True"
"3345","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, On the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “God continues to intercede, and admit us into Paradise, and show mercy and intercede until He says: Who He was one of the Muslims, so let him enter Paradise. That is when he says {Perhaps those who disbelieved wish they were Muslims} [Al-Hijr: 2] “This is an authentic hadith.” The chain of transmission and they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3345 - True"
"3346","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told me, Abu Omar Hafs bin Omar told me, Nuh bin Qais told us, Amr bin Malik told us, On the authority of Abu al-Jawza, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: A beautiful woman of He was the best of people, and some people would go forward in the first row because he would not see her, and some of them would delay until they were in the back row. So when he bowed, he said thus, and looked under his armpit and wiped his hands, then God Almighty and Majestic revealed a verse about them. Those who are the predecessors among you, and indeed We knew the latter ones.} [Al-Hijr: 24] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.” Amr ibn Ali said: He did not speak. It is narrated on the authority of Nuh ibn Qais al-Tahi, with proof, and its origin is from the hadith of Sufyan al-Thawri.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3346 - True"
"3347","Abu Bakr al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu al-Jawza, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “The ones who come forward are the front rows and the ones who come back are the back rows.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3347 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3348","Abu Al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Harun Al-Faqih told us dictation, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nasr told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Aban ibn Abdullah told us Al-Bajli, Nu’aym bin Abi Hind told me, Rabi’ bin Harash told me, he said: I was sitting with Ali, may God be pleased with him, when Ibn To Talha, he greeted Ali, may God be pleased with him, and he welcomed him and said: Do you welcome me, O Commander of the Faithful, when you killed my father and took my money? He said: “As for your money, it is isolated in the treasury, so go to your money and take it. As for your saying that you killed my father, I hope that I will be Your father and I are among those whom God Almighty said, “And We removed from their breasts any hatred as brothers on beds facing each other” [Al-Hijr: 47]. Then a man from Hamadan said: Indeed, God is more just than that. Then Ali shouted at him with a cry that caused the palace to crumble. He said: Who then is it if we are not those people? “The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3348 - True"
"3349","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, The companion of Al-Dastawa’i, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “When believers are saved from Hell, they will be imprisoned in a bridge between Hell and Paradise, redressing grievances that occurred between them in this world, until they are cleansed.” And they were purified, they were allowed to enter Paradise, and by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, a gift to one of them for his abode in Paradise is given by one of you to his abode in This world” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it “because Muammar bin Rashid narrated it on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu Sa’id This is not an error, for Hisham al-Dastawa’i is more knowledgeable about the hadith of Qatada than anyone else.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3349 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3350","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, Samak bin Harb told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “Indeed, in that is a sign” [Al-Hijr: 77] He said: Do you not see the man sending his seal to his family, saying: Bring Such and such, and if they see it, they know that it is true.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3350 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3351","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Hamid Al-Harithi told us, in Kufa, Abu Usama told us, Abdul Hamid bin Jafar told us. Al-Ansari, on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Abdul-Rahman bin Yaqoub, the client of Al-Harqa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of God, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The seven repeated verses are the opening of the Book.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration according to the condition of Muslim, and it was not They bring it out: “I have dictated the paths of this hadith in the Book of the Virtues of the Qur’an.”"
"3352","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim Al-Bateen, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was given seven of the double, long ones, and Moses was given Six: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3352 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3353","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Mahran told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Muslim Al-Bateen, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty saying: {And We have given you seven Of the repeated verses, and the Great Qur’an} [Al-Hijr: 87] He said: Al-Baqarah, the Family of Imran, the women, the table, the livestock, the customs, and Surah Al-Kahf. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3353 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3354","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying {just as We sent down to the dividers those who made the Qur’an into two parts} [Al-Hijr: 91] He said: “ Those who divided themselves were the Jews and Christians, and His saying: {They made the Qur’an divided} [Al-Hijr: 91] He said: They believed in part and disbelieved in part. This is an authentic hadith based on The condition of the two sheikhs and they did not include it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3354 - This was included by Al-Bukhari"
"3355","Abu An-Nadr al-Faqih told me, Muadh ibn Najda al-Qurashi told me, Qubaisa ibn Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of al-Aswad ibn Qays, on the authority of Amr Ibn Sulaym, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he was asked about this verse: “You take from it intoxication and good provision” [An-Nahl: 67] He said: Intoxication is that which is forbidden from its fruit, and good sustenance is that which is made lawful from its fruit. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3355 - True"
"3356","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Aban bin Taghlib, on the authority of Al-Minhal ibn Amr, on the authority of Zirr ibn Hubaysh, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying “{sons and grandsons} [An-Nahl: 72] He said: The two granddaughters, the two sisters. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3356 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3357","Ali bin Issa told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told me, Ibn Abi Umar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murrah, on the authority of Stolen, he said: Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, said, in the words of God Almighty, “{We have increased for them a punishment above the punishment} [An-Nahl: 88] He said: scorpions Its tusks are like tall palm trees. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3357 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3358","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Mu’tamir bin Suleiman told us, he said: I heard Mansour ibn al-Mu'tamir, narrating, on the authority of Amer, who said: Shutair ibn Shakal and Masruq ibn al-Ajja' sat, and one of them said to his companion: Narrate what I heard from Abdullah and I believe you, or I tell you and believe me. He said: I heard Abdullah say: “Indeed, the most comprehensive verse in the Qur’an about good and evil in Surah An-Nahl: {Indeed, God commands justice and charity and giving to relatives and forbids indecency, abomination and transgression. He advises you Perhaps you will remember} [An-Nahl: 90] He said: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3358 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3359","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi informed us, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, Uyaynah bin Abdullah informed us. Al-Rahman Al-Ghatfani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakra, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no sin more worthy of That the punishment in this world be hastened for its owner along with what is stored up for him in the Hereafter, of transgression and severing of ties of kinship.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not take it out.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3359 - True"
"3360","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Qazwini told us, Muhammad bin Saeed bin Sabiq told us, Amr bin Abi told us Qays, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, {Let us give him a good life} [An-Nahl: 97] He said: Contentment said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray and say: “O God, make me content with what You have given me, and bless me in it, and grant me all the burdens that are absent from me.” Fine. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3360 - True"
"3361","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Waqid told me, he told me My father, on the authority of Yazid the grammarian, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying “” {We do not abrogate a verse} [Al-Baqarah: 106] The verse. And He said in Surat An-Nahl {And when We substituted a verse in place of another} [An-Nahl: 101] And He said in His saying, the Almighty, the Majestic: {Then indeed your Lord is for those who emigrated after They were not tempted} [An-Nahl: 110] the verse. He said: He is Abdullah bin Saad or someone else who was a governor in Egypt, writing to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he stumbled and joined the infidels. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered him to be killed on the day of the conquest, so Othman bin Affan sought help from the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rewarded him, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3361 - True"
"3362","Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamdan al-Jallab informed us, about Hamdan, Hilal ibn al-Ala al-Ruqi told us, Ubayy told us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr al-Raqi told us, on the authority of Abd Al-Karim, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Muhammad bin Ammar bin Yasser, on the authority of his father, who said: The polytheists took Ammar bin Yasser and did not leave him until he cursed him. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, spoke well of their gods, then they left him. When he came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “What is behind you?” He said: Evil, O Messenger of God. I was not spared until I got rid of you and mentioned their gods with goodness. He said: How do you find your heart? He said: He is assured of faith. He said: “If they return, then return.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3362 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3363","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan bin Ahmad al-Asadi told me about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Warqa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: “{Only a human being teaches him the language of atheists.” To him is a non-Arab, and this is a clear Arabic language.} [An-Nahl: 103] They said: Muhammad only teaches Abd ibn al-Hadrami, and he is the author of the books. Then God said, “The tongue of those to whom they atheist is foreign, and this is a clear Arabic language. It is only those who invent lies who do not believe in the signs of God who invent lies.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.” We have narrated on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah who recited this verse and cited it in “liars”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3363 - True"
"3364","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ja’far bin Darastuwaih Al-Farisi told us, and I asked him. He said: Ya’qub bin Sufyan Al-Farisi told us, he told me Abdullah bin Al-Zubair Al-Humaidi, he said: We were sitting with Sufyan bin Uyaynah in Al-Khaif Mosque in Mina when a man, a storyteller, stood up and said: Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us Uyaynah, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, then he began a long story, so Ibn Uyaynah stood up and leaned on his staff, and said: “{But Those who do not believe in the signs of God invent lies.} [An-Nahl: 105] “I have never narrated this, nor do I know him.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3364 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3365","Sheikh Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi informed us, Muawiyah ibn Amr informed us, Abu Ishaq informed us. Al-Fazari, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Abu Sadiq, he said: Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: “Indeed, you will be subjected to captivity.” So revile me, and if I propose to you that you will be freed from me, then do not disown me, for I am a follower of Islam, so let one of you stretch out his neck, for his mother has bereaved him. For he has neither this world nor the hereafter after Islam. Then he recited {except him who is forced and whose heart is at rest with faith} [An-Nahl: 106] «Sahih The chain of transmission and they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3365 - True"
"3366","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi told us about the origin of his book, Abu Muhammad Ubaid bin Qunfud Al-Bazzar told us, we told him Yahya bin Abdul Hamid Al-Hamani, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of his father, he said: Hajr bin Qais Al-Madri Among those specialized in serving the Commander of the Faithful was Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him. One day, Ali said to him: O Hujr, you will stand up after me. Then you are ordered to curse me, so curse me and do not disown me.” Tawus said: I saw Hijr al-Madri, and Ahmad ibn Ibrahim, the caliph of the Umayyads, had set it up in the mosque and was appointed to curse Ali or kill him. Then Hajr said: Prince Ahmed bin Ibrahim ordered me to curse Ali, so if he curses me, may God curse him. Tawus said: God blinded their hearts to the point that none of them understood what he said.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3366 - Yahya Al-Hammani is weak"
"3367","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, and Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin told us Abd al-Salam, Ishaq told us, Abd al-Razzaq reported, al-Thawri reported, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Masruq, he said: I read with Abdullah Ibn Masoud {Indeed, “Abraham was a nation obedient to God} [An-Nahl: 120] He said: Ibn Masoud said: Indeed, Muadh was a nation obedient to God. He said: So they attacked him again and he repeated, then he said: Do you know what a nation is? The one who teaches people good, and the obedient one who obeys God and His Messenger “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3367 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3368","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, Issa bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliya, he said: Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, told me: On the day of Uhud, four of the Ansar were injured. Sixty men, and six of the immigrants, so they were mutilated, and among them was Hamza. The Ansar said: If only we had afflicted them with a day like this. Let us raise them. When it was the day of the conquest of Mecca, God Almighty revealed: {And if you punish, then punish with the same way you were punished, and if you are patient, it is better. For those who are patient.} [An-Nahl: 126] Then a man said: There will be no Quraysh after today. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Cut off from the people except four.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3368 - True"
"3369","The distinguished ruler Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us in the month of Rabi’ Al-Awwal in the year four hundred and said: Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr al-Khawas told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz al-Baghawi told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, On the authority of Asim ibn Abi al-Najjoud, on the authority of Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I was in a gathering in which Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman was present, and I said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He greeted him and entered Al-Aqsa Mosque. He said: Then Hudhayfah said: How did you know that, O bald man? I know your face but I do not know what it means. Your name, what is your name? So I said to him: I am Zurr bin Hubaysh Al-Asadi. He said: Then he said: How did you know that he entered the mosque? He said: So I said: By the Qur’an. Hudhayfah said: Whoever follows the Qur’an will succeed. He said: So I recited: {Glory be to Him who took His servant by night from the Sacred Mosque to the Aqsa Mosque, whose surroundings We have blessed.} [Al-Isra: 1] Hudhayfah said: Do you think he entered it? I said: Yes. He said: By God, he did not enter it, and if he had entered it, it would have been prescribed for you to pray therein. He said: Then he said: And he did not leave the light of Buraq until he saw Paradise and Hell, and he promised him the entire Hereafter. He said: I said: O Abu Abdullah, what is Al-Buraq? He said: An animal higher than a donkey and less than a mule. His stride extended as far as his gaze. “This is an authentic hadith.” The chain of transmission and they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3369 - True"
"3370","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Abu Tamila told us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Junada, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When we reached the Holy House, Gabriel said with his finger, and he pierced the stone with it and held it tight. Al-Buraq” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “And Abu Tamailah and Al-Zubair are trustworthy.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3370 - Sahih and Al-Zubayr Maruzi is trustworthy"
"3371","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Ahmed bin Mahran told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, On the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, on the authority of Salman, he said: “When Noah ate food or put on clothing, he would thank God, so he was called a grateful servant.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3371 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3372","Al-Amash, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara, on the authority of Tawus, said: I was with Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, and with us was a man from the Qadariyya. So I said: Some people say: There is no destiny. He said: Is any of them more loyal to the people? I said: If it had been, what would you have done with it? He said: “If there had been one of them, I would have taken his head, then recited to him such-and-such verse {And We decreed to the Children of Israel in the Scripture, You will certainly cause corruption in the earth twice, and you will declare great exaltation.” [Al-Isra: 4]\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3372 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3373","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abu Usama told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: It was Abdullah bin Masoud often recited this verse {Indeed, this Qur’an guides to that which is most upright and gives good tidings to the believers} [Al-Isra: 9] Light. Uthman said: This is Hamza’s reading: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3373 - Al-Dhahabi was silent about it in his summary"
"3374","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya the Martyr told us, Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, Al-Layth bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Yazid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that a man said: Oh Messenger of God, I have a lot of money, and I have a family and children, so how should I make or spend? He said: “Pay the obligatory zakat in purity.” Purify yourself and maintain family ties, and know the rights of the beggar, the neighbor, the needy, and the wayfarer.” He said: O Messenger of God, tell me less. He said: “Then give the relative his due, and the needy, and the wayfarer, and do not be extravagant.” He said: O Messenger of God, when you pay zakat to the Messenger of God Messenger of God, so I gave it to God and to His Messenger? He said: “Yes, if you give it to his Messenger, then you have given it, and you will have its reward, and the sin of whoever changes it.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. The two sheikhs did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3374 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3375","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar said: Abu Al-Ubaidin came to Abdullah, and he was a blind man. Abdullah was introduced to him, and he said: O Abu Abdullah. The Most Gracious, who do we ask if we do not ask you? He said: “So what do you need?” He said: What is the mistake? He said: “The Most Merciful.” He said: What is the container? He said: “People do not cooperate among themselves.” He said: What is waste? He said: “Spending money where it is not intended.” He said: What is the nation? He said: “The one who teaches people good.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3375 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3376","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Al-Walid bin Kathir told us, on the authority of Ibn She studied, on the authority of Asma’ bint Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with her, who said: When “The hands of Abu Lahab repented” was revealed [Al-Masad: 1], the one-eyed woman, Umm Jamil, approached. Bint Harb, and she had a wala, and in her hand was a scroll, and she was saying: We blame our father and his religion, and we disobeyed his command, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting in the The mosque, and Abu Bakr was with him. When Abu Bakr saw her, he said: O Messenger of God, she has come and I am afraid that she will see you. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “She will not see me.” And he recited a Qur’an, so he adhered to it as he said: “And recited” {And when you recite the Qur’an, We make Between you and those who do not believe in the Hereafter there is a hidden veil} [Al-Isra: 45] So she stood over Abu Bakr and did not see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: O Abu Bakr, I was told that your friend has provoked me. He said: No, by the Lord of this House, he has not mocked you. So she left, saying: “The Quraysh have learned that I am the daughter of their master.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3376 - True"
"3377","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl informed us, Muhammad bin Abdul Wahhab informed us, Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: He told me Abdullah bin Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: We asked him about the words of God Almighty: {or creation Of what grows in your breasts} [Al-Isra: 51] What did he mean by that? He said: “Death.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3377 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3378","Muhammad bin Ali bin Duhaym Al-Shaybani informed us, in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Qubaisah bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, On the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “A group of mankind was worshiping a group of jinn. So the group of the jinn submitted to Islam, and the humankind adhered to their worship, so God Almighty revealed: “Say, ‘Call upon those whom you have claimed besides Him, and they will not have control.’” He has removed harm from you, and there is no turning it around. Those are those whom they call upon, seeking the way to their Lord.} [Al-Isra: 57] “Both of them are with the Ya” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3378 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3379","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyas, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The people of Mecca asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to make They will have the pure gold, and the mountains will be removed from them so that they may plant therein. And God Almighty said: If you wish, We will give them what they asked. But if they disbelieve, they will be destroyed. Just as I was destroyed before them, and if you wish, let us keep company with them so that we may be free of them. So God revealed this: {And nothing prevented us from sending signs except that the ancients denied them. And We gave Thamud the she-camel, seeing.} [Al-Isra: 59] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3379 - True"
"3380","Muhammad Ibn Ali Ibn Abd al-Hamid al-San’ani informed us, in Mecca, Ishaq Ibn Ibrahim Ibn Abbad informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he informed us Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {And We did not create the vision which We have shown you nothing but a test for the people.} [Al-Isra: 60] He said: “It is a vision of an eye that he saw on the night on which he was taken on a journey.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3380 - according to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"3381","Muhammad ibn Ali informed us, Ishaq informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Uyaynah informed us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {and the tree cursed in the Qur’an} [Al-Isra: 60] said: “It is Al-Zaqqum.”"
"3382","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Amara, On the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, he said: Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, was praying the Maghrib prayer and we saw that the sun was rising. He said: So we looked One day, he said: “What are you seeing?” They said: To the sun. Abdullah said: “This, by the One besides Whom there is no god, is the appointed time for this prayer,” then he said: “{Establish the prayer from the setting of the sun until the dusk of the night} [Al-Isra: 78], This is the setting of the sun. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, in this context.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3382 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3383","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Yazid bin Abd Rabbuh Al-Jurjusi, and Sulayman bin Abd told me. Al-Rahman Al-Dimashqi, they said: Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik, on the authority of Ka’b bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “People will be raised on the Day of Resurrection, and I and my nation will be on a hill.” And my Lord will clothe me with a green robe, then He will give me permission and I will say what God wills that I should say, for that is the Praiseworthy Place.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3383 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3384","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Silah ibn Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, I heard him say in His Almighty saying: {It may be that your Lord will raise you to a praiseworthy station} [Al-Isra: 79] He said: The people will be gathered in one place, and the caller will hear them, and sight will take them away, barefoot and naked, just as they were created. Silent, no soul speaks without it. With His permission, he said: Then Muhammad will be called and say: “I live with you and I am happy with you, and good is in your hands and evil is not against you. Al-Mahdi is whom you have guided and your servant is in your hands.” And to You and to You there is no refuge or refuge from You except to You. You have been blessed and exalted. Glory be to the Lord of the House. That is the praised place that God said {perhaps That your Lord will raise you to a place of praise.” [Al-Isra: 79] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.” With this context, Muslim only narrated the hadith of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Rab’i ibn Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah, to bring them out of the Fire only. \"\"\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3384 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3385","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abdul Rahman bin Al-Mubarak Al-Absi told us, Al-Sa'q bin Hazan, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Uthman bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: A son came Malika, two of the Ansar, said: O Messenger of God, our mother protects Baal and honors guests, and she performed in pre-Islamic times, so where is Our mother? He said: “Your mother is in Hell.” So they got up and it was difficult for them, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called them and they returned and said: “My mother is with your mother.” Then a hypocrite among the people said to me: This man will not help his mother except what the two sons of Mulaika will help their mother while we were trampling on his heels. Then a young man from Al-Ansar: I have never seen a man who asked more questions to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than him: O Messenger of God, I see your parents in Hell. He said: “What? I asked my Lord for them, and He will give me them. And on that day I will stand at the Praiseworthy Station.” He said: The hypocrite said to the young Ansari: Ask him and what is the Place? What is praiseworthy? He said: O Messenger of God, what is the praised place? He said: “The day when God descends upon His Throne and descends upon it as a traveler descends upon it, due to its hardship as wide as the space between the heaven and the earth, and brings you.” Barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised. So Abraham will be the first to be clothed. God Almighty says: “Clothe my boyfriend with two white stripes from the stripes of Paradise.” Then I will clothe myself. Then I will stand at the right hand of God Almighty, a place where the first and the last will enjoy me, and a river will open for me from Al-Kawthar to my basin.” He said: The hypocrite says: I have never heard anything like it today. Rarely has a river flowed unless it was in pottery or ground. Ask it: What does the river flow? He said: “In a state of musk and contentment.” He said: The hypocrite says: I have never heard anything like today. Rarely has a river flowed unless it has vegetation. He said: “Yes.” He said: What is it? He said: “Rods of gold.” He said: The hypocrite says: I have never heard anything like it today. By God, no rod grew except that it bore fruit. So ask it, does it Do those rods bear fruit? He said: “Yes, pearls and jewels.” He said: The hypocrite said: I have never heard anything like it today. Ask him about the drink from the basin. The Ansari said: Oh. Messenger of God, what is the drink from the basin? He said: “Whiter than milk and sweeter than honey, whoever God gives him a drink of which he does not feel thirsty after it, and whoever deprives him of it does not quench his thirst after that.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “And Uthman bin Umair is Ibn Al-Yaqzan.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3385 - No, by God, Uthman was deemed weak by Al-Daraqutni, and the rest are trustworthy."
"3386","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan informed me, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak informed me, Ja`far bin Suleiman, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadra Al-Abdi, on the authority of Asir ibn Jabir, who said: A friend of mine said to me while I was in Kufa, Do you have a man? Do you look at him? I said: Yes. He said: This is his terrace, and it is Uwais al-Qarni, and I think he will pass by now. He said: So we sat for him and he passed by, then a man was on it. He said: And the people trampled on his heels. He said: And he would come and be harsh to them and speak to them about that, but they would not desist from it. So we went on. He accompanied the people until he entered the Kufa Mosque, and we entered with him. He moved to a pole and prayed two rak’ahs, then he turned to us with his face and said: “O you! People, what do I have to do with you? You step on my heels in every way, and I am a weak person. When I have a need, I cannot handle it. You do not do that, may God have mercy on you. Whoever has a need of me, let him meet me here.” He said: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, asked a delegation who came to him: Had he fallen ill? Here comes a man of a generation whose condition is many and different? So the man said to Uwais: The Commander of the Faithful mentioned you, but he did not mention that, as it is said: That was not his mention of what I am conveying to you.He said: Uwais had taken from the man a covenant and covenant that he would not tell it to anyone else. He said: Then Uwais said: “This assembly will be attended by three people.” A person is a believer who is jurist, a believer who has not agreed upon it, and a hypocrite. And that in this world is like rain falling from the sky to the earth and striking a tree. A leafy, fruitful tree, as it increases the beauty of its leaves and increases its freshness. Likewise, it increases its goodness and increases the quality of the tree. Which has no fruit, He increases its elegance, and its leaves increase its beauty, and it has fruit, so it is like its sister, and it infects the wildfire from the tree. Then He will smash it and take it away.” He said: Then he recited the verse: “And We send down of the Qur’an that which is a healing and a mercy for the believers, and He does not increase the wrongdoers except Loss} [Al-Isra: 82] This Qur’an does not sit with anyone except that he acts on his behalf by adding or subtracting, for the decree of God, which He has decreed, is healing and mercy. For the believers, and He only increases the wrongdoers in loss. O God, grant me a testimony whose breaking precedes its harm, and its security, its dismay, necessitates life and sustenance. Then he remained silent. A prisoner said: Then my companion said to me: How did you see the man? I said: I have only increased my desire for it, and I cannot be separated from it. So we stuck together and only stayed for a short while until the delegation of the Commander of the Faithful struck the people. Ali, may God be pleased with him,Then the owner of the carpet, Uwais, went out in it, and we went out with him in it, and we were walking with him and camping with him until we landed in the presence of the enemy.\n Ibn Al-Mubarak said: Then Hammad bin Salamah informed me, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Asir bin Jabir, who said: Then a herald called Ali, may he be pleased with him. God said: O horses of God, ride and give good tidings. He said: So he lined up two-thirds of them, and the owner of the velvet, Uwais, drew his sword until his eyelid was broken, and he threw it, then he started saying: “O people, come together, come together.” To complete many faces, then do not turn away until you see Paradise. O people, go, go, go.” He started saying that and walking while he was saying that and walking when a shot came at him and struck his heart, so he became cold as if he had been dead since he had died. A long time ago, “Hammad said in his hadith, ‘So we buried him in the dust.’” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it “with this context” and Asir bin Jabir He was born during the lifetime of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was one of the great companions of Omar, may God be pleased with him.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3386 - Sahih and according to the conditions of Muslim"
"3387","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil bin Khalaf bin Shajarat Al-Qadi told us, dictating, Abdullah bin Ruh Al-Madaini told us, Shababah bin Suwar told us, Shababah bin Suwar told us, Nu`aym ibn Hakim, Abu Maryam told us, on the authority of Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, set off with me until he brought me The Kaaba and he said to me: “Sit down.” So I sat next to the Kaaba, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose on my shoulders, then he said to me: “Get up.” So I got up, and when he saw my weakness under him, he said to me: “Sit down.” So I went down and sat down. Then he said to me: “O Ali, get on my shoulders,” so I climbed on his shoulders. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up with me, and when he got up with me, it seemed as if I had wanted to reach the horizon of the sky, so I ascended above the Kaaba, and the Messenger of God stepped aside. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me: “Throw their largest idol, the idol of Quraysh.” It was made of copper and held up with iron pegs to the ground. So he said to me: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Treat him.” And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: Eh, eh. He was bored} [Al-Isra: 81] “So I continued to treat him until I got control of him, and he said, ‘Throw it.’ So I threw it, and it broke, and I fell from the top of the Kaaba. So I and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, set out in pursuit, and we were afraid that someone from Quraysh and others would see us. Ali said: So he did not go up with him until now."
"3388","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Handali told us, Shababah bin Siwar told us, So he mentioned something similar to him. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3387 - Its chain of transmission is clean and the text is munkar"
"3389","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Walid bin Abdullah bin All, on the authority of Abu Tufayl Aamir ibn Wathilah, on the authority of Hudhayfah ibn Asid, Abu Sariha al-Ghifari, who said: I heard Abu Dhar al-Ghifari, may God be pleased with On his authority, he recited this verse {And We will gather them on the Day of Resurrection on their faces blind, mute, and deaf} [Al-Isra: 97]. Then Abu Dharr said: Tell me. The truthful, the trustworthy, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The people will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection in three groups, feeding, sitting, and riding, and a group walking. And they run, and a group of angels drag them on their faces. We said: We know these two, so what are those who walk and run? He said: “God places the blight on the back until there is no back left until a man gives the garden that admires the stray with the stump.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3389 - According to Muslim’s condition, but it is objectionable"
"3390","Abu al-Fadl al-Hasan ibn Ya`qub ibn Yusuf al-Adl informed us, Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata told us, he informed us Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “The Qur’an was sent down in its entirety to the lowest heaven, then it was sent down After that in twenty years, and the Almighty said: {And they bring you no example unless We have brought you the truth and the best explanation} [Al-Furqan: 33] He said: {And a Qur’an. We divided it into parts so that you might read it to the people over a period of time, and We sent it down in a final manner.} [Al-Isra: 106] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3390 - True"
"3391","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman, the jurist in Baghdad, informed us, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammam bin Yahya informed us, On the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salim ibn Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ma’dan ibn Abi Talha, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said: “Whoever memorizes ten verses from the beginning of Surah Al-Kahf will be protected from the Antichrist.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3391 - True"
"3392","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told us, Nu’aym ibn Hammad told us, Hushaym told us, Abu Hashim told us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qays ibn Abbad, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, whoever recites Surah “The cave on Friday was illuminated by the light between the two Friday prayers.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3392 - Naeem Dhu Munakir"
"3393","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Saeed bin Hubayra told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, Safwan bin Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Busr, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in his Almighty saying: {And he will be given to drink of purulent water, which he will gulp} [Ibrahim: 17] He said: “It will be brought near to him, but he will hate it. When he is brought near to him, his face will be blackened and his scalp will fall off.” His head, and when he drinks it, it cuts his intestines until it comes out of his anus.” God Almighty says: “And they were given hot water to drink, and it cut their intestines.” [Muhammad: 15] And God Almighty says: “And if they call for help, they will be helped with water like clay that scalds the faces. What an evil drink” [Al-Kahf: 29] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not take it out.”"
"3394","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Abu Imran Musa bin Harun bin Haroun bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz told us, my father told me, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi, Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: Tell me Ubayy ibn Ka’b said that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When Musa met Al-Khidr, peace be upon them, a bird came and dropped its beak into the water, and said: Al-Khidr told Moses, “Contemplate what this bird is saying.” He said: “And what is it saying?” He said: He says: He did not teach you and the knowledge of Moses regarding the knowledge of God except as he took my beak out of water. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3394 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3395","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Bishr bin Musa told me, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Maysara, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them: {And their father was righteous} [Al-Kahf: 82] He said: “In order to preserve the righteousness of their father and what he mentioned “Sahih according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3395 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3396","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Ali bin Salih told us, on the authority of Maysara bin Habib Al-Nahdi, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {And beneath it was a treasure for them} [Al-Kahf: 82] He said: “It is neither gold nor silver, it is layers of knowledge.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. He did not narrate it, and the narration against it has been authentic. On the authority of Abu al-Darda’\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3396 - True"
"3397","Professor Imam Abu Al-Walid, may God be pleased with him, told us, dictating, Hussam bin Bishr and Al-Hassan bin Sufyan bin Aamer Al-Shaibani told us, They said: Safwan bin Salih al-Dimashqi told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Yazid bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Umm Al-Darda’, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in the words of God Almighty: {And beneath it was a treasure for them} [Al-Kahf: 82] He said: “Gold and silver.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3397 - Rather, Yazid bin Yusuf is abandoned"
"3398","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Abu Al-Walid told us, Nafi’ bin Omar Al-Jumahi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, He said: Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, was asked about the children: Are they in Paradise? He said: “Sufficient for you is what Moses and Al-Khidr disputed over.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3398 - Sahih according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3399","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Abdullah bin Saleh bin Muslim Al-Ajli told us, Abdul Rahman bin Thabit bin Thaban, on the authority of Ata’ bin Qurrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Damrah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Indeed, the descendants of the believers are in Paradise, and Abraham, peace be upon him, will take care of them.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. The two sheikhs agreed to narrate the hadith of Saeed bin Jubayr on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them: that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about The children of the polytheists, and he said: “God knows best what they were doing.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3399 - True"
"3400","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, and Abu Zakaria told us Al-Anbari, and the pronunciation of it, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam narrated to us, Ishaq narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, he said: I said to my father, “Shall we inform you of those who will lose in deeds, those whose striving has gone astray in the life of this world while they think that they are doing well?” [Al-Kahf: 104] What are the Haruriyya? He said: “No, but they are the owners of the hermitages, and the Haruriyyah are a people who deviated, so God made their hearts deviated.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs and did not \"He takes him out\"\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3400 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3401","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saffar al-Adl informed me, Ahmad ibn Nasr told me, Khallad al-Saffar told me, Amr ibn Qays al-Malali told me, Amr ibn Murrah told me, on the authority of Musaab bin Saad, he said: I was reciting to my father until I reached this verse {Say: Shall we inform you of those who lose in deeds?} [Al-Kahf: 103] The verse, I said, Father, are they the most important of the Kharijites? He said: No, my son, read the verse that comes after it: “Those are those who disbelieve in the signs of their Lord and the meeting with Him, so their works are worthless, so We will not raise up for them.” on the Day of Resurrection.} [Al-Kahf: 105] He said: “They are the diligent Christians. Their disbelief in the signs of their Lord regarding Muhammad and his meeting” and they said: It is not in Paradise is food and no drink, but the Kharijites are the transgressors who break God’s covenant after its covenant and sever what God has commanded to do. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not produce it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3401 - True"
"3402","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saffar told me, Ahmad ibn Nasr told me, Amr ibn Talha told me, and he recited the words of God Almighty: {It was Theirs is the Gardens of Firdaus as a resting place.} [Al-Kahf: 107] Amr said: Israel ibn Yunus informed, on the authority of Ja`far ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of al-Qasim, on the authority of Abu Umamah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ask God for Paradise, for it is the secret of Paradise.” This is a hadith that we did not write except from this. The chain of transmission, and we found no alternative to narrating it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3402 - Jaafar Hulk"
"3403","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail told me, Abu Qurrah Al-Asadi told me, He said: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, speaking on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, it was revealed To me, whoever hopes to meet his Lord, let him do righteous deeds and not associate in the worship of his Lord anyone who has a light from Abyan to Mecca. “The angels crushed him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3403 - Abu Qurrah is ignorant and has not been weakened"
"3404","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, and recited {So let him do righteous deeds And he does not associate anyone in the worship of his Lord.} [Al-Kahf: 110] He said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed, on the authority of Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Muslim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that a man said: O Messenger of God, a man strives in the cause of God and he seeks honor. From this world, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no reward for him.” The people appreciated that, so the man came back and said: “There is no reward for him.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3404 - True"
"3405","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Qazwini told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah Al-Dashtaki told us, Amr bin Abu Qays, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, the Almighty’s saying: “He disobeys” [Maryam: 1] He said: Sufficient is from Generous, and here is from Guide, and O from Wise, and Eye from Knowledgeable, and Sad from Truthful. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3405 - True"
"3406","Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saffar told me, Ahmad bin Nasr told me, Amr bin Talha Al-Qannad told me, Sharik told me, on the authority of Salem Al-Aftas, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, the Almighty said: {Kayyis} [Maryam: 1] He said: “Sufficient, Guided, Trustworthy, Mighty, and Truthful” is this. An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3406 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3407","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us about Samak. Ibn Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the words of God Almighty: {We had not given him a name before.} [Maryam: 7] He said: “He was not named Yahya. Before him, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3407 - True"
"3408","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Hamza Al-Maruzi told us, Abu Saleh Hadiya told us. Ibn Abd al-Wahhab, Muhammad Ibn Shuja` reported, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ziyad al-Yashkari, on the authority of Maymun Ibn Mihran, that Nafi` Ibn al-Azraq asked Ibn Abbas, and he said: Tell me about the words of God Almighty: “And I have reached the level of arrogance, and I have attained an extreme level of arrogance” [Maryam: 8]. What is an oppressive person? He said: “Misery comes from old age.” The poet said:\n [light sea]\n Only the newborn is excused, and not...the one who was old in time is excused.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3408 - Ahmad ibn Hanbal Muhammad ibn Ziyad Al-Yashkari said: Al-Tahan is a malicious liar who fabricates hadiths, and I am a brave son of the weak in narration."
"3409","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {So He revealed to them that they glorify God morning and evening} [Maryam: 11] He said: “It was “He commands them to pray morning and evening.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3409 - True"
"3410","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan Al-Harbi told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, the Almighty said: {And tenderness from Us} [Maryam: 13] He said: “Being compassionate with mercy.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3410 - True"
"3411","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar Al-Ataridi told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: Yahya bin Saeed narrated to me, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him, narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him He said: “Every human being will come on the Day of Resurrection with a sin, except for Yahya bin Zakariya.” He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a mistake. Then he placed his hand on the ground and took a small stick. Then he said: “That is because he did not have anything that men have except such a stick for that reason.” “God called him ‘Lord, Champion, and Prophet from among the righteous.’” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3411 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3412","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Shaybani informed us about Kufa, Ahmad ibn Hazim al-Ghafari informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, Abu Ja`far al-Razi informed us, about Al-Rabi’ bin Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The spirit of Jesus, son of Mary, was one of those spirits that A covenant was taken from her in the time of Adam, so God sent him to Mary in the form of a human being {so he appeared to her as a normal human being} [Maryam: 17], {she said, “How can I have A boy, and no human being has touched me, nor have I been a transgressor.} [Maryam: 20], so he picked up the one who was speaking to her and someone entered into her. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3412 - True"
"3413","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told us, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib In His saying, the Almighty the Majestic: {Your Lord has placed a secret beneath you} [Maryam: 24] He said: “It is the stream, the small river.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not take him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3413 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3414","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Hafid informed us, Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Labbad informed us, Abu Nu’aym informed us, Sufyan informed us, about Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both: {And We brought him near as a deliverer} [Maryam: 52] He said: “He heard the gnashing of the pen when He wrote on the tablet, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3414 - True"
"3415","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Amr bin Muhammad Al-Anqazi told us, Israel told us, about Samak. Ibn Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, the Almighty said: “And mention in the Book Abraham. Indeed, he was truthful.” A prophet} [Maryam: 41] He said: “The prophets were from the Children of Israel except ten: Noah, Salih, Hud, Lot, Shuaib, and Abraham. And Ishmael, and Isaac, and Jacob, and Muhammad, may blessings and peace be upon them, and there were none of the prophets who had two names except Israel and Jesus. “Israel is Jacob and Jesus the Messiah.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3415 - True"
"3416","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told me, in Mecca, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Zakaria bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Yazid al-Muqri, followed by Haywa ibn Shuraih, Bashir ibn Abi Amr al-Khawlani told me that Al-Walid ibn Qays al-Tajibi told him that, He heard Abu Sa`id Al-Khudri say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, reciting this verse {So after them a successor was left behind} [Al-A’raf: 169] and he said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “There will be a successor after sixty years who neglected prayer and followed desires. They will meet destruction. Then there will be a successor who will read... The Qur’an is nothing more than their throats, and three people recite the Qur’an: a believer, a hypocrite, and an immoral person.” Bashir said: So I said to Al-Walid: Who are these three? He said: The hypocrite is an infidel, the immoral person eats from it, and the believer believes in it. He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3416 - True"
"3417","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told me about Al-Ray, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told me, Abu Ayyub Suleiman bin Abdul Rahman told me Al-Dimashqi, Abdullah bin Wahb told me, Malik bin Khair Al-Ziyadi told us, on the authority of Abu Qabil, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, may God be pleased with him, He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The People of the Book and the People of Lebanon will perish from my nation.” Uqba said: What are the People of the Book, oh? Messenger of God? He said: “A people who learn the Book of God and argue with it with those who believe.” He said: So I said: Who are the people of Al-Laban, O Messenger of God? “He said: ‘A people who follow desires and neglect prayers.’ This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3417 - True"
"3418","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told me, in Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, in His Almighty’s saying: {They will meet with evil} [Maryam: 59] He said: “A river in Hell, far from the bottom, with an evil taste.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3418 - True"
"3419","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali al-Shaybani told us, Ahmad bin Hazim al-Ghafari told us, Abu Nu`aym told us, Asim bin Raja bin Haywa told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, reported the hadith. He said: “Whatever God has made lawful in His Book is lawful, and what He has forbidden is forbidden, and He did not remain silent.” On his authority, it is well-being, so accept well-being from God, for God is not forgetful.” Then he recited this verse: “And your Lord is not forgetful” [Maryam: 64]. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3419 - True"
"3420","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Waki` reported, and Yahya ibn Adam, they said: Israel told us, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {Does You will learn His name.} [Maryam: 65] He said: “No one has named the Most Merciful other than Him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3420 - True"
"3421","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Al-Sadi, He said: I once asked Al-Hamdani about the words of God Almighty: {And there is not among you except one who will come to it. It is upon your Lord a certainty and decree.} [Maryam: 71] So he spoke to me. Abdullah bin Masoud told them on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “People will return to the Fire, then they will be reconciled with their deeds. The first among them will be “Like the flash of lightning, then the howling of the wind, then like the mount of a horse, then like a rider, then like the mounting of a saddle, then like their walking.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. Muslim and they did not take him out\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3421 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3422","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Ishaq Al-Qurashi, on the authority of Al-Nu’man Ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Al-Mughirah Ibn Shu’bah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The slogan of the Muslims On the path on the Day of Resurrection: Oh God, grant us peace. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3422 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3423","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saffar informed us, Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, Amr ibn Talha al-Qannad informed us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, {And there is not one of you except that he will go to it} [Maryam: 71] He said: “The path over Hell is like the edge of a sword, so it passes through.” The first group is like lightning, the second is like the wind, the third is like the best of horses, and the fourth is like the best of camels and livestock. Then they will pass. And the angels say: O Lord, grant us peace. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3423 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3424","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani, Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub, and Ibrahim bin Asmah told us, they said: Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abu Ghassan Malik told us. Ibn Ismail al-Nahdi, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb told us, Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu Khalid al-Dalani told us, al-Minhal ibn told us Amr, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “God will gather the people on the Day of Resurrection. He said: Then a herald will call: O people, are you not satisfied with your Lord, who created you, provided for you, and fashioned you, to assign every human being among you to whomever he was in charge of in this world? He said: And for those who worshiped Uzair, the devil Uzair will appear to them until the tree, the stick, and the stone appear to them, and the people of Islam remain crouched. Then it will be said to them: Why do you not go as the people go? Then they will say: Indeed, we have a Lord whom we have not seen yet. He said: Then it will be said: How do you know? Your Lord, if you see Him? They said: There is a sign between us and him, and if we see him we recognize him. It was said: What is it? They said: He uncovers a leg. He said: At that time he uncovers a leg. He said: Then the one who had a plate on his back would prostrate, and there would remain people whose backs were like cows’ backs. They wanted to prostrate but were unable.Then they will be ordered to raise their heads and be given their light in proportion to their deeds. He said: Among them are those whose light is given like a mountain before Him. And among them is he who is given his light above that, and among them is he who is given his light like a palm tree with his right hand, and among them is he who is given less than that with his right hand until The last of that will be the one whose light is placed on the toe of his foot. It shines sometimes, then goes out sometimes. When it shines, his foot shines, and when it is extinguished, he gets up and passes. And they pass on the path, and the path is like the edge of a sword striking a slip, and it is said: Save according to the measure of your light. For among them are those who pass by like the passing of a star, and among them are Some pass like a wind, and among them are some that pass like the wind, and among them are some that pass like a man’s strength, and sand like sand, so they pass according to their deeds until that which His light is on the big of his foot. He said: He drags a hand and hangs a hand. He drags a foot and hangs a foot and his sides are covered with fire. He said: Then they will be saved. And behold, They were saved and said: Praise be to God who saved us from you after He had shown you. God has given us what He has not given to anyone else. Masruq said: It did not reach Abdullah. He laughed at this part of this hadith, and a man said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, you have narrated this hadith many times as long as you have reached your age. This is where I laughed,Then Abdullah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, speaking to him repeatedly, and he did not reach this point in this conversation except that he laughed until His abysses appear and the last of his molars appear, for the human being says: Are you mocking me when you are the Lord of the worlds? He says: No, but I am able to do that, so they asked me: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3424 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3425","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Abdul-Wahhab, Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, they said: Abdul-Rahman bin Ishaq Al-Qurashi told us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Sa’d, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, in this verse: {On the Day when We will gather the righteous to the Most Gracious as a delegation} [Maryam: 85] Ali said: By God, no delegation will be gathered over They will not be led on their feet, but they will be brought with camels the likes of which no creation has ever seen, with rims of gold and rims of aquamarine, so they ride. upon it until they strike the gates of Paradise. “This hadith is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3425 - Rather, Abd al-Rahman did not narrate to him a Muslim nor to his uncle al-Nu’man, and they declared him weak."
"3426","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Hatim Al-Muzaki told us about Marwa, Abd al-Aziz bin Hatim told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Saad told us, we told him Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Aoun, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, that he recited {except he who takes The Most Gracious, a covenant} [Maryam: 87] And He said: Make a covenant with the Most Gracious, for God will say on the Day of Resurrection: Whoever has a covenant with Me, let him do so. He said: So we said: So teach us, O Abu Abd al-Rahman. He said: “Say: O God, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen. I know To you in this worldly life, that I bear witness that there is no god but You alone, without any partner, and that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger. If you entrust me to myself, you will bring me closer to evil and distance me from good, and I will not trust except in your mercy, so make it a covenant for me with you. Give it to me on the Day of Resurrection. You will not break your promise. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3426 - True"
"3427","Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saffar told me, Ahmad bin Nasr told me, Amr bin Talha told me, Omar bin Abi Zaida told me, he said: I heard Ikrimah, It is mentioned on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: {Taha} [Surah: Taha, Verse No.: 1] He said: “It is like your saying: O Muhammad, in the language of the Ethiopians” This is a hadith The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3427 - True"
"3428","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Yahya ibn Al-Ala’, on the authority of his uncle Shuaib bin Khalid, who said: Samak bin Harb told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amira, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: We were sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Batha, when a cloud passed by, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you know what this is?” So we said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “The clouds,” so we said: The clouds. He said: “And Al-Muzn,” so we said: “And Al-Muzn.” He said: “By the sky,” then he was silent, then he said: “Do you know how much distance there is between the sky and the earth?” So we said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “Between them is a journey of five hundred years, and between each sky to the next heaven there is a journey of five hundred years. Five hundred years, and above the seventh heaven there is a sea between the top and the bottom as between the heaven and the earth, and then above that eight tents between Their knees and their hooves are as between the heaven and the earth. And God is above that. Nothing is hidden from Him of the deeds of the children of Adam. This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3428 - It has been mentioned and it is authentic"
"3429","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar Al-Zahid told us, Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Abu Ghassan Malik told us Bin Ismail, told by Sharik, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amira, on the authority of Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, may God be pleased with him, in The words of God Almighty: {And the throne of your Lord will bear above them on that day eight} [Al-Haqqah: 17] angels in the shape of tentacles between their hooves. And they rode a journey of sixty-three years or sixty-five years. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3429 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3430","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Hamid bin Abi Hamid Al-Muqri told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah Al-Dashtaki told us, Amr bin Abi told us Qays, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: {He knows the secret and what is hidden} [Taha: 7] He said: “{The secret} [Taha: 7] What you knew {and hidden} [Taha: 7] what God has cast into your heart that you did not know. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3430 - True"
"3431","Sheikh Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq informed us, Muhammad ibn Ghalib informed us, Omar ibn Hafs ibn Ghayath informed us, Ubayy and Khalaf ibn Khalifa informed us, On the authority of Humaid bin Qais, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said And peace be upon him: “On the day God spoke to Moses, he was wearing a robe of wool, a cloak of wool, breeches of wool, his sleeves were wool, and his shoes were made of the skin of an unsmart donkey.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3431 - Rather, it is not according to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"3432","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Abu Hilal told us, Qatada told us, on the authority of Abu Hassan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “used to tell us most of his nights about the children of Israel who did not stand up.” “Except for a great prayer.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3432 - True"
"3433","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Uthman bin Saleh al-Sahmi told us, my father told me, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, On the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Zuhr, on the authority of Ali ibn Yazid, on the authority of Al-Qasim ibn Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Umamah, he said: When Umm Kulthum bint gave birth The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the grave. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “From it We created you, and to it We will return you, and from it We will bring you out another time.” Another, in the name of God and in the path of God and according to the religion of the Messenger of God.” Then when he built on it alone, he began throwing grains to them and saying: “Block through Milk.” Then he said: “This is nothing, but it is good for the soul of the living.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3433 - He did not talk about it, and it is weak news because Ali bin Yazid was abandoned."
"3434","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Sulaiman bin Al-Harith told me, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told me, Israel informed us, Abu Ishaq told us about Amara bin Amr Al-Saluli, and Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Sulami, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: “When Moses hastened to his Lord, he baptized the Samaritan So he gathered all the jewelry he could find, the jewelry of the children of Israel, and struck a calf at it. Then he put the fist into its stomach, and behold, it was a calf bellowing. Then the Samaritan said to them: This is your God and the God of Moses. Then Aaron said to them: O my people, did your Lord not promise you a good promise? When Moses returned to the children of Israel, who had been led astray by the Samaritan, he took his brother’s head, and Aaron told him what he had said. Moses said to the Samaritan what What's wrong with you? The Samaritan said: I took a handful of the traces of the Messenger and threw it away, and likewise my soul made peace with me. He said: So Moses went to the calf and placed the axes on it and cooled it with them while it was at the mouth of a river. None of those who were there drank any of that water. He worshiped that calf, but his face turned yellow like gold. So they said to Moses: Why did we repent? He said: Some of you kill one another. So they took knives, and the man started killing his father and brother, not caring who he killed, until seventy thousand of them were killed, so God revealed to Moses Order them to raise their hands, for I have forgiven whoever is killed and repented of whoever remains. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3434 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3435","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Hanathili told me, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Affan told us, Abu Awanah told us, Abu Al-Hussein told us, Ja’far told us, Sa’d bin Abdul Hamid told us, Hisham told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. May God be pleased with them both. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “May God have mercy on Moses. The one who sees is not like the one who informs. His Lord told him that his people They were put under trial after him, but he did not throw the tablets. So when he saw them and examined them, he threw the tablets. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God have mercy on Moses. If he had not hastened, he would have narrated part of his hadith other than what he narrated.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not take him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3435 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3436","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Mahran told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Ibrahim bin Nafi told us, he said: I heard Al-Hasan bin Muslim, saying: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr, speaking on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “God created Adam from the skin of the entire earth, so he was named Adam.” He said Ibrahim bin Nafi’: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr saying: I asked Ibn Abbas and he said: “God created Adam, but he forgot, so he was named man, and God Almighty said.” God Almighty: {And We had made a covenant with Adam before, but he forgot, and We found in him no resolve} [Taha: 115] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and we did not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3436 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3437","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Muddhikir told me, Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Dunya told me, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid told me, Abbad told me. Ibn Al-Awwam, on the authority of Sufyan Ibn Husayn, on the authority of Ya’la Ibn Muslim, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “When Adam ate from the tree that was forbidden. God Almighty said: “What made you disobey Me?” He said: My Lord, Eve has become beautiful for me. He said: “I commanded her not to get pregnant except with difficulty, and not to give birth except with difficulty, and I made her doll twice a month.” When Eve heard that, she rang, and he said to her: “On you, the reindeer and your daughters.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3437 - True"
"3438","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl bin Ghazwan told us, Ata bin Al-Sa’ib told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “Whoever reads the Qur’an and follows what is in it, God will guide him from misguidance, and protect him from the Day of The Resurrection is a bad reckoning, and that is because God Almighty said: {So whoever follows my guidance will neither go astray nor be miserable} [Taha: 123] “This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3438 - True"
"3439","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim Al-Madani, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Abi Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said {A straitened living} [Taha: 124] He said: “The torment of the grave.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3439 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3440","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, Mas’ar told me, Alqamah bin Marthad told me, On the authority of Al-Mughirah Al-Yashkari, on the authority of Al-Ma’roor ibn Suwayd, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: Umm Habibah bint Abi said: Sufyan: Oh God, grant me success with my husband, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with my father Sufyan and my brother Muawiyah. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “You have called upon God for known terms, divided provisions, and attained effects. He will not be hastened.” Some of it must be done before it is permissible, and none of it can be delayed after it is permissible. If you pray to God to protect you or ask God to protect you or protect you from... The torment of the Fire or the torment of the grave would be better or better.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3440 - True"
"3441","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told me, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Uwaisi told us, he told us Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she said: The Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The trial of the grave is within me, so when you are asked about me, do not doubt.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3441 - Rather, Muhammad is unanimously agreed upon his weakness"
"3442","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Ahmad bin Musa Al-Muzaki told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Ya’qub bin Ka’b Al-Halabi told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Zuhair bin Muhammad Al-Anbari, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited the saying of God Almighty: “And they do not intercede except for whom He is pleased” [Al-Anbiya’: 28]. Then he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “My intercession is for the people of great sins from my nation.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3442 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3443","Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Khallad bin Yahya told us, Sufyan told us, Talha bin Amr told us, on the authority of Ata’, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: {Have those who disbelieved not seen that the heavens and the earth were joined together?} Then We separated them. He said: “The heavens were divided “With rain, and the earth bursting with vegetation.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3443 - Talha bin Amr Wah"
"3444","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us about dictation and reading, Muhammad bin Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqqi told us, Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faryabi told us, Yunus told me Ibn Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Ibrahim Ibn Muhammad Ibn Saad, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Saad, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A supplication Dhul-Nun, when he supplicated with it while he was in the belly of the whale: There is no god but You, Glory be to You. Indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers. No Muslim man supplicated with it in Nothing was ever answered unless it was answered.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3444 - True"
"3445","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying: {So he called out in the darkness} [Al-Anbiya’: 87] He said: “The darkness of the night, the darkness of the belly of the whale, and the darkness of the sea.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3445 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3446","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Ahmad bin Nasr told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Talha bin Amr told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas May God be pleased with them both, in the words of God Almighty: {And We made good for him his wife} [Al-Anbiya’: 90] He said: “There was in the tongue of Zechariah’s wife a long So God Almighty fixed it. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3446 - Talha bin Amr Wah"
"3447","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Musa bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Abi Shaybah told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, Abdullah told us Al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid Al-Qurashi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aqeem, he said: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, addressed us. On his behalf, he praised God and praised him for what he deserved, saying: “I advise you to fear God, and to praise him for what he deserves, and to Mix desire with dread, for God praised Zechariah and his family, saying, “Indeed, they used to hasten to do good deeds and call upon Us out of hope.” And in fear, and were humble to Us.} [Al-Anbiya’: 90] Then know, servants of God, that God has made your souls a pledge by His rights, and has made your covenants upon that. And He bought from you a little that perished for much that remained. And this is the Book of God among you. Its light will never be extinguished, nor will its wonders end, so shine with its light. And seek advice from His Book and seek light from it on the day of darkness, for He only created you to worship Him, and appointed over you noble scribes who know what You do so, then know, O servants of God, that you will go in the morning and go during a term whose knowledge has escaped you. If you are able to pass the deadlines, And you are in the work of God, so do it, and you will not be able to do that except by God, so be ahead of your deadlines before your deadlines expire, and He will restore you. To the evil of your deeds, for there are some people who set their appointed times for others and forgot themselves, so He has forbidden you from being like them. So revelation upon revelation, Then he escaped, escaped, for behind you there is a seeker who is coming forward quickly. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3447 - Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq is a weak Kufi"
"3448","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman, the jurist in Baghdad, told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Awwam bin Hawshab told us, On the authority of Jablah bin Suhaim, on the authority of Muthhir bin Ghafara, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: “When he was captured on the night the Prophet was taken prisoner May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He met Abraham, Moses, and Jesus, and they remembered the Hour. They started with Abraham and asked him about it, but he did not have any of it. Knowledge, then Moses, but he had no knowledge of it, so they went back to the conversation to Jesus, and Jesus said: “God made a covenant with me in matters other than its obligation, so I did not We know it. He said: Then mention the emergence of the Antichrist, so go down and kill him, and the people will return to their countries, and Gog and Magog will meet them. And they descend from every direction. They do not pass by water without drinking it, and they do not pass by anything without spoiling it. Then they turn to God and call upon God. Then He will kill them, and the earth will roar to God with their wind, and they will rush to Me. So call upon God, and He will send water from the sky and carry their bodies. So he throws it into the sea, then he blows up the mountains, and the earth expands with the tide of eternal life. So God has made a covenant with me: If that happens, then the Hour will come from the people. Like a pregnant woman who has died, her family does not know when she will surprise them with her birth, day or night. “Abdullah bin Masoud said: I found it believable. That is in the Book of God Almighty: “Until when Gog and Magog are conquered, and they are dissipating from every direction, and the true promise draws near.” [Al-Anbiya’: 97] The verse, he said: And all the people from every place they come from on the Day of Resurrection will be humpbacked. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.” So as for It is influential, but it is not unknown. “It was narrated on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud and Al-Baraa bin Azib, and a group of followers narrated on his authority.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3448 - True"
"3449","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, Muhammad bin Musa bin Hatim told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, on the authority of Yazid the grammarian, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: When the verse was revealed {Indeed, you and what you worship besides God are Hell, you will enter it.} [Al-Anbiya’: 98] Then the polytheists said: Are the angels, Jesus, and Ezra worshiped besides God? He said: If these were the ones who worshiped gods, they would not have turned away from it. He said: Then it was revealed: “Indeed, those for whom the best of Us has preceded are far away from it.” [Al-Anbiya’: 101] Jesus, Uzair, and the angels: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3449 - True"
"3450","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Ashib told us, Shayban bin Abdul Rahman told us, On the authority of Qatada, Al-Saghani said: Ruh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Sa’id ibn Abi Arouba narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran ibn Husayn, may God be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: During some of his travels, he missed the journey among his companions, so he carried these two The two verses are his voice: “O people, fear your Lord. Indeed, the earthquake of the Hour will be a great thing. On the day you see it, every nursing woman will be astonished at what she has breastfed. And every pregnant woman will lay down her burden, and you will see the people drunk, but they are not drunk, but the punishment of God is severe.} [Al-Hajj: 2] When his companions heard that, they urged Al-Mutti and they knew that he had something to say, so when they gathered around him, he said: “Do you know what day that is?” They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “That is the day when Adam, peace be upon him, will be called, and his Lord will call him and say: O Adam, send forth the source of the Fire. Then He will say: O Lord, and what is the source of the Fire? He says: Of every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine are in Hell and one is in Paradise. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw that, he said: “Work and give good tidings. By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are the same as two creatures who were not together. Nothing except you multiply it, Gog and Magog and all the children of Adam and the children of Satan.” He said: This was explained to the people, so he said: “Do And give good tidings, for by the One in whose hand is Muhammad’s soul, you are nothing among the people but like a mole on the arm of an animal or like a mole on the side of a camel.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it. Most of the imams of Basra are of the opinion that Al-Hasan heard from Imran, but the two sheikhs did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3450 - It has been corrected"
"3451","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq informed us, Muhammad ibn Ghalib informed us, Al-Hasan ibn Bishr informed us, Al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, about Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to recite “And you will see people drunk and They are drunk, but the punishment of God is severe.} [Al-Hajj: 2] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”"
"3452","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad al-Faqih told us about Rayy, Sa`id bin Yazid al-Taymi told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah al-Dashtaki told us, Amr bin Abi Qais, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: {created and not created} [Al-Hajj: 5] He said: “The created being is that which is living, and the uncreated is that which is fallen.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3452 - True"
"3453","Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. May God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty’s saying: “Whoever thinks that God will not help him” [Al-Hajj: 15] He said: “That is, whoever thinks that God will not help him.” “Allah is Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3453 - True"
"3454","Abu Abdullah Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Abdul Rahman Ahmad bin Shuaib, the jurist in Egypt, told us, Saeed bin Yahya Al-Umayyad told us, My father told me, Sufyan bin Saeed Al-Thawri told me, on the authority of Abu Hashim Al-Wasiti, I think it is on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qays bin Abbad, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, said: {These are two adversaries who have disputed about their Lord} [Al-Hajj: 19] He said: “It was revealed about us and those who disputed.” On the day of Badr, Utbah, Shaybah, and Al-Walid” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, and the two sheikhs agreed to narrate it from Hadith Al-Thawri"
"3455","As Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Waki’ told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim Al-Rummani. Yahya bin Dinar al-Wasiti, on the authority of Abu Majliz, Lahiq bin Humaid al-Sadusi, on the authority of Qays bin Abbad, said: I heard Abu Dharr, “swearing This verse was revealed about these six groups on the day of Badr: Ali, Hamza, Ubaidah, Shaybah, Utbah ibn Rabi’ah, and Al-Walid ibn Threshold {These are two adversaries who have disputed about their Lord} [Al-Hajj: 19] up to the Almighty’s saying: {We will make him taste of a painful punishment} [Al-Hajj: 25] And Solomon followed Al-Taymi Abu Hashim, based on his narration on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Ali, like the first."
"3456","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Hamid bin Abi Hamid Al-Muqri told us, Ishaq bin Sulayman told us, Abu Ja’far Al-Razi told us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Lahiq ibn Humayd, on the authority of Qays ibn Abbad, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: {These are two adversaries who disputed over Their Lord} [Al-Hajj: 19] Among those who stood out on the day of Badr: Hamzah bin Abdul-Muttalib, Ali, Ubaidah bin Al-Harith, and Utbah bin Rabi’ah. And Shaybah bin Rabi’ah and Al-Walid bin Utbah. “Ali said: I will be the first to kneel down to dispute before God on the Day of Judgment. Resurrection “The hadith has been authenticated with these narrations on the authority of Ali, just as it has been authenticated on the authority of Abu Dhar al-Ghifari, even if they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3456 - True"
"3457","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi told me, Muawiyah ibn Amr told me, Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “ This verse was revealed about Hamza and his companions: “And do not think that those who were killed in the cause of God are dead, but rather alive in the presence of their Lord” [Al Imran: 169] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3457 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3458","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed us, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed us, Ibn Al-Mubarak informed us, Saeed bin Al-Mubarak informed us. Yazid, on the authority of Abu Al-Samh, on the authority of Abu Hujairah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, and he recited the saying of God Almighty {So as for those who disbelieve, it will be cut off for them. Clothes of fire} [Al-Hajj: 19] Then he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, hot water will be poured on their heads and it will penetrate the skull until He will reach his stomach and whatever is in his stomach will spill out until he tears his feet while it is melting, then he will be restored to how it was. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration and it is not \"He takes him out\"\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3458 - True"
"3459","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Salman, may God be pleased with him, said: “Fire is black and neither its flame nor its embers give light.” Then he recited this verse {Whenever they wanted to go out Therein they were returned with grief.} [Al-Hajj: 22] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3459 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3460","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Usayd bin Asim Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Once, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying: {And whoever responds therein to heresy} [Al-Hajj: 25] We will make him taste a torment of injustice. Alim said: “If a man were to intend to commit a sin, that is, if he did not commit it, it would not be prescribed for him, and if a man were to intend to kill a man at home... While he was in Aden and Abyan, God made him taste a painful punishment.” Shu’bah narrated it, on the authority of Ismail bin Abd al-Rahman al-Suddi, on the authority of Murrah.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3460 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3461","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Musa bin Imran Al-Faqih told us from the origin of his book, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Hashim Ziyad bin Ayoub, Yazid ibn Harun informed, Shu`bah informed, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he raised it in God Almighty says: {And whoever inclines to atheism with injustice, We will make him taste of a painful punishment} [Al-Hajj: 25] He said: “If only a man were to incline to atheism. “And he is in Aden, Abyan, and God will make him taste a painful punishment.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3461 - Yazid bin Harun, I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah, raising it on the condition of Muslim."
"3462","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Bakr Al-Adl told us, Ibrahim bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Muhammad ibn Kunasa told us, Ishaq ibn Issa ibn Asim told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar came to Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr and said: Oh Ibn al-Zubayr, beware of atheism in the Sanctuary of God, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Indeed, a man from the Quraysh will commit atheism therein if “His sins will be weighed with the sins of the two heavy ones, and they will be outweighed.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3462 - Abu Hatim bin Kanasa is not used as evidence"
"3463","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, Abdullah bin Ali Al-Ghazal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, Amr bin Saeed bin Abi Hussein informed me, Ibn Abi Mulaika informed me, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. About them, he said: “A thief approached the Kaaba, and when he was in the middle of the clouds, God sent upon him such a wind that the one who was standing could hardly stand except with difficulty. And the one who was standing went away, then he sat down and was struck down, and she stood up against him, and they encountered hardship from her. Tuba’ called his rabbis and asked them, “What is this that was sent against me?” They said: Do you believe us? He said: “You are safe.” They said: You want a house that God will prevent from anyone who wants it. He said: “So what does this say about me?” They said: Strip into two garments, then say: Here you are, here you are, then go in and walk around that house and do not irritate any of its people. He said: “If I agree on this, this odor will go away from me?” They said: Yes. So he stripped naked and then pelted himself. Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said, “Then the wind moved like pieces of a dark night.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3463 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3464","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. May God be pleased with them both. He said: When Abraham finished building the House, he said: My Lord, I have finished. He said: “Tell the people to perform Hajj.” He said: My Lord, what does my voice reach? He said: “Adhan and it is upon me to deliver the message.” He said: Lord, how should I say? He said: “Say: O people, the Hajj has been prescribed for you, the Hajj of the Ancient House. He heard it from between the heavens and the earth. Do you not see that they are coming from Do they reach the farthest reaches of the earth? “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3464 - True"
"3465","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told me, Jeddy told me, Abdullah bin Salih told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Khaled bin Musafir, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Muhammad bin Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his uncle Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, may God be pleased with him, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God only called it the Ancient House because He freed it from the tyrants, so no tyrant ever appeared over it.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3465 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3466","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, and Mansour, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: I said to him: His Almighty said: {And the body We have made for you among the rituals of God for you. Therein is good, so remember the name of God over it in rows.} [Al-Hajj: 36] He said: “If you want to slaughter the camel, make it stand still, then say: God is great, God is great.” Greater than you and yours, then poison it, then slaughter it.” He said: I said: And I say that about the sacrifice? He said: “And the sacrifice.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3466 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3467","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Bazzar told us in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Wasiti told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Salam informed us Ibn Miskin, on the authority of Aid Allah Ibn Abdullah Al-Mujashi’i, on the authority of Abu Dawud Al-Subaie, on the authority of Zayd Ibn Arqam, may God be pleased with him, he said: We said: O Messenger of God, what are these sacrifices? He said: “The Sunnah of your father Abraham.” He said: We said: What do we have from it? He said: “With every hair there is a fine hair.” We said: O Messenger of God, what about wool? He said: “Every hair of wool is good.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3467 - May God protect us. Abu Hatim said the hadith is denounced"
"3468","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ayyash Al-Qatbani, On the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever finds the space to offer the sacrifice does not offer it. He will not attend our prayer.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3468 - Ibn Ayyash was deemed weak by Abu Dawud\n On the authority of Abdullah bin Ayyash Al-Masry, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Whoever sells the skin of his sacrifice does not have the right to sacrifice it.” This is an authentic hadith like the first, but they did not narrate it."
"3469","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim Al-Batin, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he used to recite it: {Permission is given to those who fight because they have been wronged, and indeed God is over Their victory is powerful.} [Al-Hajj: 39] He said: “It is the first verse revealed in battle.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3469 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3470","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Ibn Lahi’ah, and Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told me, Ishaq bin Issa told me, Ibn Lahi’ah told me, Musharrah told me Ibn Ha'an said: I heard Uqba bin Amir, may God be pleased with him, saying: I said: O Messenger of God, did you prefer Surat Al-Hajj with two prostrations? He said: “Yes, so whoever does not prostrate them should not recite it.” This is a hadith that we did not write with a chain of transmission except from this chain of transmission and Abdullah bin Lahi’ah. Ibn Uqba Al-Hadrami is one of the imams, but he was criticized for his mingling at the end of his life. “The narration about him was authentic according to the words of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, And Abdullah bin Abbas, and Abdullah bin Omar, and Abdullah bin Masoud, and Abu Musa, and Abu Darda, and Ammar, may God be pleased with them. Hadith of Omar bin Al-Khattab \"\"\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3470 - The narration in this matter is authentic, based on the words of Amr Taifa"
"3471","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Yazid bin Harun, and Saeed bin Amir told us, they said: Tell us Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tha’labah, “He prayed with Omar, may God be pleased with him, in the morning, so he prostrated two prostrations during the Hajj.” As for the hadith of Ibn Abbas:\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3471 - True"
"3472","So Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Omar bin Hafs bin Ghayath told us, Ubayy told us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Abi Al-Aaliyah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “In Surah Al-Hajj there are two prostrations.” As for the hadith of Ibn Umar:\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3472 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3473","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, he told me Makhramah bin Bukayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, that he “prostrated two prostrations during Hajj.” As for the hadith of Abd “Allah bin Masoud and Ammar, may God be pleased with them.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3473 - True"
"3474","So Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Muadh bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zar, on the authority of Abd. Allah bin Masoud and Ammar bin Yasser, may God be pleased with them, “they used to prostrate twice during Hajj.” As for the hadith of Abu Musa,"
"3475","So Muhammad bin Yazid Al-Adl told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Ismail bin Aliya told us, Yunus told us Ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Bakr Ibn Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Safwan Ibn Mahrez, that Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, “prostrated in Surah Al-Hajj He prostrated two times, and he recited the prostration at the end of Surah Al-Hajj, so he prostrated and we prostrated with him.” As for the hadith of Abu Al-Darda’:"
"3476","So Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Khumayr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr, said: I saw Abu al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, “prostrating two prostrations during the Hajj.”"
"3477","Abdullah bin Saad Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Saeed Al-Abdi, and Hussam bin Bishr bin Al-Anbar told us, they said: Al-Hakam bin Musa Al-Qantari, Yahya bin Hamza told us, Al-Hakam bin Abdullah told us, that he heard Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, speaking on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, She asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about this verse {And He has not placed upon you in religion any hardship} [Al-Hajj: 78]. He said: “Distress.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3477 - Rather, the ruling was left by the people of Aila"
"3478","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Yunus Al-Dhabi told us, Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, Zuhayr bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, on the authority of Abd Allah Ibn Muhammad Ibn Aqeel Ibn Abi Talib, on the authority of Ali Ibn Al-Hussein, may God be pleased with them both, {For every nation We have appointed a place of worship to which they will perform} [Al-Hajj: 67] He said: A slaughter they are slaughtering.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3478 - Suhail is a maniac and Ibn Aqeel is not strong\n Abu Rafi’ told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to buy two fat, salty rams with horns when he offered a sacrifice. He prayed and slaughtered one of the two rams himself with a knife, then he said: “O God, this is on behalf of my entire nation, whoever bears witness to your monotheism and bears witness to me.” With the conveyance,” then he brought the other one and slaughtered it and said: “O God, this is on behalf of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad.” Then he fed them to the poor and he himself ate. And his family were among them, so we stayed for years. God has sufficed us with the debt and our provisions. Not one of Banu Hashim sacrifices. “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and no one from Banu Hashim sacrifices.” He brings him out.”"
"3479","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told us, and Abu Zakaria al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us: Abd al-Razzaq told me, Yunus bin Sulaym told me, he said: Yunus bin Yazid al-Aili dictated to me. The companion of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman ibn Abdul-Qari, he said: I heard Omar ibn Al-Khattab, may God bless him and grant him peace. On his authority, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent down to him, he would hear a noise like the sound of bees, so we stayed for an hour. So he faced the Qiblah and raised his hands and said: “O God, increase us and do not diminish us, honor us, do not degrade us, give us, do not deprive us, favor us, and do not influence us, and be pleased with us and our earth.” Then he said: “Ten verses have been revealed to me. Whoever establishes them will enter Paradise.” Then he recited {He has succeeded. The believers are those who are humble in their prayers.} [Al-Mu’minun: 2] The verses: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3479 - Abd al-Razzaq was asked about his sheikh, and he said, “I don’t think it is anything.”"
"3480","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ali bin Asim told us, Humaid Al-Taweel told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik May God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God created the Garden of Eden, and planted its trees with His own hand, and said to it: Speak. She said: The believers have succeeded. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3480 - Rather, it is weak"
"3481","Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Qays bin Unif told us, Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Ja’far bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Abu Imran, on the authority of Yazid bin Babanus said: We said to Aisha, may God be pleased with her: O Mother of the Believers, what was the character of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: “The character of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was the Qur’an.” Then she said: Do you read Surat Al-Mu’minin? Recite {Indeed, the believers have succeeded} [Al-Mu'minun: 1] until the ten days were reached. She said: This was the character of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3481 - True"
"3482","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Abdul Rahman informed Al-Masoudi, Abu Sinan told me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, that he was asked about his saying Almighty, the Almighty: {Those who are humble in their prayers} [Al-Mu’minun: 2] He said: “Humility is in the heart, and that you soften your shoulder towards the Muslim man, and that you do not “You turn around in your prayer.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3482 - True"
"3483","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub al-Thaqafi narrated to me, Abu Shu`ayb al-Harrani narrated to me, my father narrated to me, Ismail Ibn Ulayya narrated to me, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he prayed, he would raise his gaze to the sky and it descended.” {Those who are humble in their prayers} [Al-Mu’minun: 2] So he lowered his head, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, had it not been for a dispute over it concerning Muhammad, for It was said about him that he was sent, but they did not bring him out.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3483 - The correct one is mursal"
"3484","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Nafi’ bin Omar told us Al-Jumahi said: I heard Abdullah bin Ubaidullah bin Abi Mulaika say: I asked Aisha, may God be pleased with her, about the pleasure of women and she said: “Between me and you is the Book of God,” he said, and I read this verse, “And those who guard their private parts, except with their wives or those in possession of them.” Their oaths, they are not to be blamed, so whoever seeks after} [Al-Mu’minun: 6] whatever God has married or made king, has lost anything except “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3484 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3485","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying: {Those are the heirs} [Al-Mu’minun: 10] He said: “They shall inherit their dwellings. “And the dwellings of their brothers, which were prepared for them if they obey God.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3485 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3486","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Sabiq told us, Malik bin Mughul told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Bin Saeed bin Wahb, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: I said: O Messenger of God, the words of God Almighty: {Those who give what they give And their hearts are in fear.} [Al-Mu’minun: 60] Is it the man who commits adultery, steals, and drinks alcohol, and yet he fears God Almighty? He said: “No, but he is a man who fasts, prays, and gives alms, and yet he fears God Almighty.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. \"\"\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3486 - True"
"3487","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saffar informed me, Ahmad ibn Nasr informed me, Amr ibn Talha told me, Israel informed me, on the authority of Abd al-Ala, on the authority of Sa`id. Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Samar were only disliked when this verse was revealed {You were arrogant about it, and you deserted Samar} [Al-Mu’minun: 67] He said: “They were arrogant regarding the House, saying: We, its people, are abandoning it.” [Al-Mu’minun: 67] He said: They used to abandon it and would not inhabit it. This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3487 - True"
"3488","Abu Abbas Al-Sayyari told me, Muhammad bin Musa bin Halim told me, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told me, Al-Hussein bin Waqid told me, he told me Yazid, the grammarian, said that Ikrimah told him, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: Abu Sufyan came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he greeted him, and said: “O Muhammad, I adjure you, by God and the Most Merciful, we have eaten dung, meaning dander and blood, so God, the Almighty and Majestic, revealed {And indeed We took them.” With torment, but they did not submit to their Lord, nor did they supplicate.} [Al-Mu’minun: 76] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not produce it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3488 - True"
"3489","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Hakam bin Salam Al-Razi told us, Amr bin Abu Qays, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Minhal ibn Amr, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: A man came to him and said To him: O Ibn Abbas, I have something in my soul from the Qur’an. He said: “What is it?” He said: Doubt. He said: “Woe to you. Have you asked anyone but me?” He said: No. He said: “Bring it.” He said: I hear God saying: {And God has power over all things} [Al-Ahzab: 27] This was a matter that had happened. And He said, “There will be no lineage between them that Day, nor will they question each other.” [Al-Mu’minun: 101] And He said in another verse, “And some of them would approach one another, questioning each other.” [Al-Saffat: 27] Then he mentioned things, and Ibn Abbas said: As for the Almighty’s saying: “And God has power over all things” [Al-Ahzab: 27], for He has not ceased nor has He is still the First and the Last, the Manifest and the Inward, and as for His Almighty’s saying: {There will be no lineage between them that Day, nor will they question} [Al-Mu’minun: 101] This is at the first blast, when nothing will remain on the earth, and there will be no lineage between them on that day, nor will they question. As for the Almighty’s saying: {Then He will come. [Al-Saffat: 50] And when they entered Paradise, they would turn to one another, questioning one another. “This is an authentic hadith.” The chain of transmission and they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3489 - True"
"3490","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Saeed bin Yazid informed. Abu Shuja`, on the authority of Abu al-Samh, on the authority of Abu al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: {Talfah Their faces are the Fire, and they are therein like stones.” [Al-Mu’minun: 104] He said: “The Fire distorts and shrinks his upper lip until it reaches the middle of his head and relaxes.” His lower lip until it hits his navel. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it."
"3491","Muhammad bin Ishaq al-Saffar told me, Ahmad bin Nasr told us, Amr bin Talha told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying: {And they will be therein like a lion} [Al-Mu’minun: 104] He said: “Like the palm of a head.” Al-Nadhij “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3491 - True"
"3492","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl narrated to us, Yahya bin Abi Talib narrated to us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata narrated to us, Saeed bin Abi narrated to us Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-Aas, who said: “The people of Hell call an angel, but he does not answer them.” For forty days, then he replies to them, “Indeed, you are staying.” He said: “Their supplication has become weak, and by God there is a master, and there is a master who is master.” They said, “Our Lord, you have defeated us.” We were distressed, and we were a people astray.} [Al-Mu’minun: 106] {He said, “Be humiliated therein and do not speak to me.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration.” And they did not produce it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3492 - True"
"3493","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Uthman bin Saleh Al-Sahmi told us, my father told me, Ibn Wahb, Yunus bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, Humaid bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf told me, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, He heard Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, saying: “Learn Surat Al-Baqarah, Surat An-Nisa, Surat Al-Ma’idah, and Surat Al-Hajj. And Surah An-Nur, for among them are the obligatory prayers.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3493 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3494","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Sulayman told us, Abd Al-Wahhab bin Al-Dahhak told us, Shuaib bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not put them in the rooms or “Teach them writing,” meaning women, “and teach them the spindle and Surat An-Nur.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3494 - Rather, it is subject"
"3495","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil ibn al-Hasan ibn Issa informed us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani informed us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti told us, Hushaym, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-Aas, in the Almighty’s saying: “The adulterer does not marry anyone except An adulteress or a polytheist} [An-Nur: 3] He said: “There were women who frequented Medina, and a Muslim man used to marry one of their women to spend on him, but they were forbidden.” About that: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3495 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3496","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdan Al-Ahwazi told us, Amr bin Muhammad Al-Naqid told us, Muhammad bin Yusuf told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Jafar bin Iyas, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, in the Almighty’s saying: {Do not enter houses other than your own until Ask yourselves} [An-Nur: 27] He said: “The writer made a mistake so that you ask for permission.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3496 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3497","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Thabit bin Amara told us, he said: I heard Ghanim Ibn Qays, saying: I heard Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Any woman who perfumes herself Then she passed by a people so that they could smell her fragrance, so she is an adulteress.” This hadith was included by Al-Saghani in the interpretation, when God Almighty said: {Say to the believers: They lower their gaze} [An-Nur: 30] and it is an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3497 - True"
"3498","Abu Sahl Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Nahwi told us in Baghdad, Ja`far ibn Muhammad ibn Shakir told us, Qubaisa ibn Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yunus Ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Amr Ibn Saeed, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah Ibn Amr Ibn Jarir, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about Suddenly, he ordered me to look away. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and Muslim narrated it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3498 - Sahih and reported by Muslim"
"3499","Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydalani told me, Ismail bin Qutaibah told me, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, {And let them not display their adornment} [An-Nour: 31] He said: “No anklets, no sash, no earrings, no necklace.” {Except what appears of it} [An-Nur: 31] He said: “Clothes.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3499 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3500","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad Al-Zahid told us in Baghdad, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Ibrahim bin Nafi’, said: I heard Al-Hasan bin Muslim, narrating on the authority of Safiya bint Shaybah, on the authority of Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, may God be pleased with her, who said: When This verse was revealed: “And let them draw their veils over their bosoms” [An-Nur: 31]. So they concluded by saying, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3500 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3501","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib told me that Abdullah bin Habib told him, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he acknowledged that he said: {And give them of the wealth of God which He has given you} [An-Nour: 33]. He said: “A quarter shall be left for the recipients.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and it was not They narrate it: “Abdullah bin Habib is Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, and Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated it on the authority of Ali in another narration.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3501 - Sahih and narrated on a conditional basis"
"3502","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Abu Al-Zubayr told me, He heard Jabir saying: “There was a prostitute to some of the Ansar, and she said: My master is forcing me to engage in prostitution, so it was revealed: {And do not force Your young women engage in prostitution if they want to be protected.} [An-Nur: 33] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3502 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3503","Abu Abdullah Al-Dashtaki told us, Amr bin Abi Qais told us, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, In His saying, the Almighty, the Majestic: “Allah is the light of the heavens and the earth. The light of him who believes in God is like a niche.” He said: “And it is the grave, meaning the alcove.” Sahih. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3503 - True"
"3504","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Mahran told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa bin Abdul Rahman bin Abu Laila, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Usayd, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Eat oil and anoint yourself with it, for it is one of the “A blessed tree.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission. They did not narrate it, but it has another witness with an authentic chain of transmission.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3504 - True"
"3505","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, in Egypt, Safwan bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed Ibn Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari said: I heard my grandfather, speaking on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Eat oil and anoint them with it, for it is good and blessed.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3505 - Abdullah bin Saeed Wah"
"3506","Abu Abbas Ahmad ibn Ziyad al-Faqih told us in Ahwaz, Muhammad ibn Ayyub told us, Muhammad ibn Sa`id ibn Sabiq told us, Amr ibn Abu Qays, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both: {In houses that God has permitted to be raised and to be remembered in them. His name is glorified therein in the mornings and the evenings, men whom neither trade nor selling distracts from the remembrance of God.} [An-Nur: 37] He said: “God struck this man.” The parable” His saying: “The likeness of His light is like a niche in which is a lamp, like a lamp in a bottle” [An-Nour: 35] “For those are the people who are not distracted by commerce.” And there is no selling apart from the remembrance of God. They used to trade with people and I would sell to them, but neither their trade nor their selling distracted them from the remembrance of God. A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3506 - True"
"3507","Ahmad ibn Salman al-Faqih informed us, al-Hasan ibn Makram al-Bazzaz informed us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Abu Ghassan Muhammad informed us Ibn Mutarrif Al-Laythi, Abu Hazim told us, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Salam, may God be pleased with him, he said: “The mosques pegs whose pegs are for them sitting among the angels, and if they are absent they are asked about them, and if they are sick they visit them, and if they are in need “Help them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. It is mawqoof and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3507 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3508","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi narrated to me, Musaddad bin Qattan narrated to us, Othman bin Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Ata’, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, may God be pleased with him, said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, so we took turns. The people, when my shift was done, I sent my camels away, then I came back and went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was addressing the people, and I heard him say: “What? If a Muslim performs ablution and performs the ablution properly, then stands for his prayer and knows what he is saying, he will be disintegrated as on the day his mother gave birth to him from sins, not He is guilty of a sin.” He said: “I couldn’t help myself at that time if I said: Blah blah.” Omar said: And I was beside him, wondering at this? He said: Before you come, something better than that. So I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you? He said: He said: “There is no man who performs ablution and performs it well, then says when he has finished his ablution: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah.” And I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, that eight gates of Paradise will be opened for him, and he may enter through whichever one he wishes.” Then he said: “The people will gather in One level. Their sight will penetrate them, and the caller will hear them, and a herald will call out. He will inform the people of the crowd, “Who is on the vineyard today?” three times, then he will say: “Where “Those whose sides used to turn away from their beds.” Then he says: “Where are those who were {neither trade nor selling distracted them from the remembrance of God} [An-Nour: 37] Until the end of the verse, then a herald will call out and tell the crowd who is generous today. Then he says: “Where are the praisers who used to praise their Lord?” This is an authentic hadith and it has narrations on the authority of Abu Ishaq, but they did not narrate it. It was our right to narrate it in the Book of Ablution, but we could not. So when I found Imam Ishaq Al-Hanzali stated his ways when he said: {Men who are not distracted by trade or selling from the remembrance of God} [An-Nur: 37] I followed him.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3508 - True"
"3509","Muhammad bin Musa bin Imran al-Faqih told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told me, Muhammad bin Sahl bin Askar told me, Abd al-Razzaq told me, Al-Thawri reported, on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, that he called for a drink, and it was brought. He said: “Give it to the people.” They said: We are fasting. He said: “But I am not fasting.” Then he ordered him to drink it, then he said: “They fear a day in which hearts will be tossed and turned.” And the sighted} [An-Nur: 37] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3509 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3510","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Abu Jafar told us Al-Razi, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, in the words of God Almighty: “{Allah is the light of the heavens And the earth.} So he recited the verse, then said: {And those who disbelieve, their deeds are like a mirage in a valley, which the thirsty person thinks is water, until when he comes to it he finds it nothing. And he found God with Him, and He paid him his account; and God is quick to reckon. Indeed, there is good for him with God. He will find it, and God will cause him to enter the Fire.” He said: And he gave another example for the disbeliever, and said: “Or like the darkness in a deep sea that covers it.” Above it are waves, above them are clouds of darkness, one upon another. When he takes out his hand, he can hardly see it, and for whomever God does not make it light, but he has no light” [Al-Nur: 40], so He transports him through five types of darkness: his speech is darkness, his work is darkness, his entrance is darkness, and his exit is darkness. Darkness, and his destination is to darkness and to Hell on the Day of Resurrection. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3510 - True"
"3511","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Safwan bin Amr, Sulaym bin Amer told me, he said: We went to a funeral in the Damascus Gate, with us Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, may God be pleased with him, and when he prayed for The funeral and they began to bury it. Abu Umamah said: “O people, you have spent the morning and evening in a house in which you divide good deeds and bad deeds, and you are about to proceed from it to the other house, and this refers to the grave, the house of loneliness, and the house of darkness. And the house of worms, and the house of distress, except what God encompasses, then you will move from it to the places of the Day of Resurrection, for you will be in some of those places until A matter of God’s command overwhelms the people, and their faces become white and their faces turn dark, then you move from there to another place, and darkness overwhelms the people. severe, then the light is divided and the believer is given light, and the infidel and hypocrite are left behind and are not given anything. This is the example that God Almighty gave in His Book: {Or like the darknesses in a deep sea covered by waves; from above them are waves, and above them are clouds; darknesses, one upon another. When He brings forth He could hardly see his hand, and for whomever God has not made light, he has no light.} [An-Nur: 40] And the disbeliever and the hypocrite will not be illuminated by the light of the believer as no The blind is illuminated by the insight of the one who sees. The hypocrite says to those who believe: “Wait for us that we may draw from your light.” It was said, “Go back and seek light.” [Al-Hadid: 13] It is a deception with which the hypocrite was deceived. God Almighty said: {They deceive God, and He is deceiving them} [An-Nisa: 142] So they return to The place where the light was divided, but they did not find anything, so they turned to it, and a wall had been set up between them, with a door, the inside of which was mercy and the outside of it. From before Him is the punishment. They will be called, “Were we not with you?” Do we pray with your prayers and fight with your campaigns? “They said, ‘Yes, but you misled yourselves, and waited and doubted, and were deceived by hopes, until the command of God came, and deceit deceived you about God.’” [Al-Hadid: 14] He continued to his saying: {And wretched is the destination} [Al-Hadid: 15] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3511 - True"
"3512","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Abu Sa’id Muhammad bin Shazan told me, Ahmad bin Sa’id al-Darimi told me, Ali bin al-Husayn bin Waqid, my father told me, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came The Arabs, peace and blessings of God be upon him, and his companions took the city, and the Ansar sheltered them. The Arabs shot them down in a single bow. They did not spend the night except with weapons or When they woke up in the morning, they said: “Do you see that we will live until we sleep safe and secure, fearing no one but God?” Then it was revealed: {Allah has promised those among you who believe and do righteous deeds that He will surely appoint them as successors in the land, just as He appointed successors to those before them, and will make things easy for them. Their religion which He chose for them, and He will certainly replace them with security after their fear. {Those are the transgressors} [Al Imran: 82] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3512 - True"
"3513","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ahmad bin Musa Al-Tamimi narrated to us, Munjab bin Al-Harith narrated to us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying: “Those whom your right hands possess may seek your permission” [An-Nour: 58] He said: “Women, for men ask permission.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3513 - True"
"3514","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed me, Abdan informed me, Abdullah informed me, Muammar informed me, he said: I heard Amr bin Dinar, narrating on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {So when you enter houses, greet yourselves} [An-Nour: 61] He said: “It is the mosque. When you enter it, say: ‘Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God.’ It is authentic according to the stipulation of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3514 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3515","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Ayyub al-Alaf told us in Egypt, Muhammad bin al-Hasan bin Abi al-Hasan told us Al-Makhzoumi in Medina. Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Fudayl Al-Khutmi told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When you enter your homes, greet its people, and when you eat food, mention the name of God. And if one of you says Salam when he enters his house and mentions the name of God over his food, Satan will say to his companions: There is no place for you to sleep or have dinner. And if he does not say Salam One of you, and he did not name the name, Satan says to his companions: You have spent the night and dinner. “This is a strange hadith with a strange chain of narration and text in this matter. And Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Makhzoumi feared that he was the son of rubbish, but they did not take him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3515 - Strange\n Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us a dictation in Rajab of the year four hundred"
"3516","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us, about Hamdan, Abu Hatim al-Razi told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Maysara bin Habib, on the authority of Al-Minhal ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The middle of the day does not come on the day of Resurrection until one and the other have rested, then he recited {Indeed, their return is to Hell} [Al-Saffat: 68] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and it was not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3516 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3517","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, On the authority of Abu Dawud al-Subai’i, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked: How will the people of Hell be gathered on Their faces? He said: “Indeed, He who made them walk on their feet is able to make them walk on their faces.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3517 - True"
"3518","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told us, Ahmed bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, he said: Tell me who heard Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, say: A man said: O Messenger of God, how will those who are gathered on their faces be gathered? He said: “Indeed, He who made them walk on their feet is able to gather them upon their faces.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration if the two chains of narration are combined. And they did not take it out.”"
"3519","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Khalid bin Mukhlid Al-Qatwani told us, Musa bin Yaqoub Al-Zam’i told us, on the authority of His uncle Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Ma’ad bin Adnan bin Adad bin Zand bin Al-Baraa bin Araq Al-Thara.” She said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: “He destroyed Ad and Thamud.” And the companions of the land, and many centuries between that, no one knows except God.” Umm Salamah said: The descendants of the deceased are Ismail bin Ibrahim and Zand. Hamisa’ and Bara’: Nabt: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3519 - True"
"3520","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Ibrahim told us, Yazid bin Harun told me, Sulayman Al-Taymi told me, on the authority of Al-Hasan Ibn Muslim, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “There is no year that has rained more than any other, but God disperses it wherever He wishes, then he recited: {And We have distributed it among them} [Al-Furqan: 50] The verse: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3520 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3521","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, about Mansour ibn al-Mu`tamir, Sa`id ibn Jubayr told me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza ordered me to ask Ibn Abbas about these two things. The two verses: “What is their command” which are in Surah Al-Furqan: {And those who do not call upon any other god with God, nor kill any soul which God has made sacred, except in truth} [Al-Furqan: 68], which is in Surah An-Nisa: {And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell} [An-Nisa: 93] the verse. He said: So I asked Ibn Abbas about that. He said: “When what was revealed in Surat Al-Furqan, the polytheists of Mecca said, ‘We have killed the soul that God has made sacred. Unjustly, and with God we call upon another god, and We commit immoral acts.” He said: “Except those who repent and believe and do righteous deeds” [Al-Furqan: 70] the verse. He said: “These are for those.” He said: “And as for what is in Surah An-Nisa {And whoever kills a believer intentionally} [An-Nisa: 93] the verse, he is the man who has known He converted to Islam and did the work of Islam, then he intentionally killed a believer, and his recompense is Hell, for which there is no repentance. He said: So I mentioned that to Mujahid, and he said: Except for those who regret it. “It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3521 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3522","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Adam told us, Ibn Abi Zaida told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ali Ibn Muslim, on the authority of Sa`id Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: A man from the polytheists said: O Messenger of God, “and They killed and committed more and committed adultery than that. This is the best thing you are calling us to, if you had told us that we would not have made atonement. Then God Almighty revealed: {And those who call upon not with God any other god} [Al-Furqan: 68] the verse. And it was revealed: “Say, ‘O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of God.’” [Az-Zumar: 53] “It is true according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it is not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3522 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3523","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Yunus bin Abu Ishaq, he recited the words of God Almighty: {And We revealed to Moses, “I am pleased with My servants. Indeed, you will be followed} [Al-Shu’ara’: 52] verses. Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa Al-Ash’ari said, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, descended with a Bedouin and honored him and said to him: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “We pledged to come.” Then the Bedouin came to him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “What do you need?” He said: A camel is riding, and my family is milking its milk. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This man is incapable of being like the old people of the Children of Israel.” So his companions said to him: “How old are the Children of Israel.” O Messenger of God? He said: “When Moses wanted to lead the children of Israel, he lost his way, so he said to the children of Israel, ‘What is this? He said: Then the scholars of the Children of Israel said to him: When death approached him, Joseph, peace be upon him, took a covenant from God upon us that we would not leave Egypt. So that his bones may be carried with us. Then Moses said: Which of you knows where Joseph’s grave is? Then the scholars of the Children of Israel said: No one knows the location of his grave except an old man of the Children of Israel. So he sent Moses to her and said: Show us a grave. Yusuf said: No, by God, until you give me my ruling. He said to her: What is your ruling? She said: My judgment is that I will be with you in Paradise. It was as if he hated that. He said: Then it was said to him, “Give her her ruling.” So he gave her her ruling, and she went with them to a lake with swampy water, and she said: For them, drain this water. And when they were exhausted, she said to them, “Dig.” So they dug and took out Joseph’s bones. And when they had picked him up from the ground, the road was as bright as daylight. An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.” Perhaps a delusional person thinks that Yunus bin Abi Ishaq heard from Abu Burdah a hadith: “There is no marriage without Paulie” as his father heard him.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3523 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3524","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Wahib bin Khalid told us, Abu Waqid told us, on the authority of Abi Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she said: O Messenger of God, Abdullah bin Jad’an used to honor the guest and maintain family ties. And he does and does. Does that benefit him? He said: “No, he never once said: My Lord, forgive me my sin on the Day of Judgment.” It is an authentic chain of narration, and they did not take it out.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3524 - True"
"3525","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told me, Sulaiman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Al-Kharit, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The hoopoe was guiding Solomon to the water.” So I said: How is that when a trap is set for the hoopoe and dust is thrown on it? He said: “Has God made your father bless you with them or not? When the judgment comes, your sight goes away.”"
"3526","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash told us, about Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {I will surely punish him with a severe punishment} [An-Naml: 21] He said: “Pluck its feathers.” Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “Suleiman bin Dawud used to place six hundred thousand chairs for him, and then the nobles of mankind would come until They sit next to them, then the nobles of the jinn come until they sit next to the humans, then he calls the birds and they shade them, then he calls the wind. So you would carry them, and in the same morning he would travel a month’s journey. While he was walking in a desert, he needed water. Then the hoopoe came and made He digs the ground and hits a place of water, so the devils come and skin that place like a skin is flayed, so they hit the water.” Nafi’ said. Ibn al-Azraq: O Waqaf, have you seen the hoopoe come and peck the ground and reach the place of water and it comes to the trap and it sees it? Until it falls on his neck? Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “When destiny comes, it hinders sight.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3526 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3527","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Al-Shafi’i told us, and Asad bin Musa told us, they said: Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They know now.” Indeed, what I used to say to them in this world is true, and God Almighty said to His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Indeed, you do not make the dead hear, nor do you make the deaf hear the supplication of When they turn away, turning away.} [An-Naml: 80] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3527 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3528","Maymun bin Ishaq Al-Hashimi informed us, in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash and Al-Hasan bin Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah, {Whoever brings a good deed} [Al-An’am: 160] He said: “Whoever brings there is no god but Allah” {And whoever “He brought evil.” [Al-An’am: 160] He said: “With polytheism.” It is valid according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not include it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3528 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3529","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, the Almighty’s saying: {And Fouad The mother of Moses, empty.} [Al-Qasas: 10] He said: “Empty of everything except the remembrance of Moses.” {If she was about to reveal it} [Al-Qasas: 10] He said: “Lest you say, ‘O his children.’” {And she said to his sister: Qusayyah} [Al-Qasas: 11] Seeking his influence. {And We had forbidden to him wet nurses before} [Al-Qasas: 12] He said: “A breast-feeding woman shall not be brought. So he accepts it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it, and Hassan is Ibn Abbad, and they all used it as evidence.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3529 - Hassan bin Abi Abbad does not know who he is"
"3530","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran Al-Asbahani told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him: {Then one of them came to him, walking timidly} [Al-Qasas: 25] He said: “She used to come while she was She had an abscess and a woman with her hand on her face, so Moses stood up with her and said to her: Walk behind me and clear the way for me while I walk in front of you, for I do not We look into the backs of women, then she said: {O father, hire him. Indeed, the best of whom you hire is the strong and trustworthy} [Al-Qasas: 26] because she saw of his strength. And because he said to her what he said, this increased his desire, so he said: {I want to marry you one of these two daughters of mine on the condition that you rent to me for eight. Proofs, so if you complete ten, then from you, and I do not want to be difficult for you. You will find me, God willing, among the righteous.} [Al-Qasas: 27] That is, in good company. And fulfilling what I said. Moses said: {This is between me and you. As long as I decide between the two terms, there is no transgression against me} [Al-Qasas: 28]. He said: Yes. He said, “God is a disposer of affairs over what we say.” So he married him off and lived with him to provide for him and work for him in taking care of his sheep and whatever he needed from them, and he married him to Zipporah or her sister Sharqaa. They were the ones who used to say “Sahih according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3530 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3531","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi told me, with Marwa, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi told us, Hafs bin Omar Al-Adni told us, Al-Hakam bin Aban, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked: Which of the two terms did Moses fulfill? He said: He said: “Keep them away and give them the best food.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3531 - Hafs Wah"
"3532","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Abu Amr Ahmad bin Al-Mubarak Al-Mustamli told us, Muhammad bin Al-Walid Al-Fahham told us, Sufyan told us Bin Uyaynah, Ibrahim bin Yahya, a man from the people of Aden, told me, Al-Hakam bin Aban told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked Gabriel: “Which of the two terms did Moses fulfill? He said: “He completed them.” This is an authentic hadith, but he did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3532 - Ibrahim bin Yahya is not known"
"3533","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Mis’ar told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Burdah, On the authority of his father, he said: I prayed next to Ibn Omar Al-Asr, and I heard him say while bowing: “My Lord, for what You have bestowed upon me, I will never be a supporter of criminals.” When he left, he said: “I have not prayed a prayer except that I hoped that it would be atonement for the one before it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. \"\"\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3533 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3534","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil al-Qadi in Baghdad told us, Muhammad bin Saad al-Awfi told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Awf told us, on the authority of Abi Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “God has not destroyed a people, nor a century, nor nation, and no people of a town since the Torah was sent down on the face of the earth have been subjected to punishment from heaven other than the people of the town that was transformed into apes. Have you not seen the God Almighty says: {And We gave Moses the Scripture after We had destroyed the first generations, as insights for the people and guidance and mercy that they might remember.} [Al-Qasas: 43] “It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3534 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3535","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan Al-Shaybani told us, Uqba bin Makram Al-Dhabi told us, Abu Qatn Amr bin Al-Haytham bin Qattan bin Ka’b, Hamza Al-Zayat told us, on the authority of Sulayman Al-Amash, on the authority of Ali bin Mudrak, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, {And you were not beside the Mount when We called} [Al-Qasas: 46] He said: “Call, O nation of Muhammad. I have answered you before you called upon Me and I have given you before You ask me: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3535 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3536","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash told us, about Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: When Moses came He commanded his people to pay zakat, so Qarun gathered them together and said to them: “He brought you prayer and brought you things, so you tolerated them, so be patient to give him.” “Your money.” They said: We cannot bear to give him our money, so what do you think? So he said to them: “I would like to send to the prostitute of the children of Israel, so that we may send her to him, and she may accuse him because he wanted her to harm herself.” So he called Moses. against them, so God commanded the earth to obey him, so Moses said to the earth: Take them, and it took them back to their heels. So they began to say: O Moses, oh Moses, Then he said to the earth: “Take them,” and it took them to their knees. So they started saying: O Moses, oh Moses. Then he said: “Take them to the earth.” So it took them to their necks. They began to say: O Moses, oh Moses. Then He said to the earth: “Take them.” So it took them and concealed them. So He revealed God to Moses, O Moses, my servants asked you and pleaded with you, but you did not answer them, and by My glory, if they had called upon Me, I would have answered them. Ibn Abbas said: That is the saying of God Almighty, “So We caused the earth to swallow him and his abode.” [Al-Qasas: 81] He was swallowed up to the lower earth. “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3536 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3537","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Musa bin Ishaq Al-Khattami told us, Abdullah bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Yunus Hatem bin Abi Saghira, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Umm Hani’, may God be pleased with her, who said: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace Concerning the words of God Almighty: {And you will come to your abominable club} [Al-Ankabut: 29] He said: “They used to kidnap the people of the road and mock them, so it was “The abomination they were committing” is valid according to Muslim’s condition, but they did not take it out.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3537 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3538","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Yazid bin Al-Haytham told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Layth told me Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Al-Sa'ib, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Rabi'ah, said: Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, asked me about the saying of God Almighty: {And in remembrance of God Greater} [Al-Ankabut: 45] So I said: The remembrance of God with glorification, praise, and greatness, and he said: “No remembrance of God is greater than your remembrance of Him.” Sahih. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3538 - True"
"3539","Muhammad bin Al-Khalil Al-Asbahani Abu Abdullah told me, Musa bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told me, my father told me, Ma’an bin Issa told us, Muawiya told us Ibn Abi Salih, on the authority of Marthad Ibn Sumayy Al-Khawlani, who said: I heard Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, saying: “There will come a people who recite: “It defeated the Romans” [Al-Rum: 2], but it only defeated “the chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not produce it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3539 - True"
"3540","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Muawiyah bin Amr bin Al-Muhallab Al-Azdi told us, Abu Ishaq told us Al-Fazari, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amra, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: It was The Muslims would love for the Romans to prevail over Persia because they are the People of the Book, and the polytheists would love for Persia to prevail over the Romans. Because they are people of idols. The Muslims mentioned that to Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him. Then Abu Bakr mentioned that to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “But they will be defeated.” Abu Bakr mentioned that to them, so they said: Make it between us and you. A term. If they support you, you will have such-and-such, and if we support you, you will have such-and-such. So he appointed a period of five years between them, but they did not appear. He mentioned That is Abu Bakr to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Have I not made him, I see him?” He said: less than ten. He said: Then the Romans appeared after that. That is what God Almighty says: “Have you not defeated the Romans in the nearest part of the earth? And yet, after their defeat, they will be defeated.” [Al-Rum: 2] He said: So the Romans were defeated, then they were victorious afterward. The matter belongs to Allah before and after, and on that day the believers will rejoice in the victory of Allah.” Sufyan said: And I heard that they appeared on the day of Badr. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3540 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3541","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Razin, who said: Nafi’ ibn al-Azraq came to Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, and said: “The five daily prayers in The Qur’an? He said: Yes, so he recited {Glory be to God when you touch} [Al-Rum: 17]. He said: “The Maghrib prayer {and when you wake up} [Al-Rum: 17] the morning prayer {and the evening prayer} [Maryam: 11] The afternoon prayer {And when you appear} [Al-Rum: 18] the noon prayer, and he read {And after the evening prayer there are three private parts for you} [Al-Nur: 58] “This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3541 - True"
"3542","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, Safwan bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Humaid Al-Kharrat told us, on the authority of Ammar Al-Duhni, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Al-Sahba, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: {And among the people is he who buys hadith for his own sake. That he may stray from the path of God.} [Luqman: 6] He said: “By God, he is the One who is sufficient.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3542 - True"
"3543","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Halabi told us, Al-Harith bin Sulayman told us, Uqba bin Alqamah told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Musa bin Sulaiman, said: I heard Al-Qasim bin Mukhaymrah, speaking on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Luqman said to his son while he was advising him: “O my son, beware of masking yourself, for it is frightening and humiliating at night.” “By day.” This is a text with an authentic chain of transmission, and God knows best.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3543 - True"
"3544","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Yazid bin Al-Haytham told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Layth told me, Al-Ashja’i told me, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais, on the authority of Nabih Al-Anazi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, and he recited what Luqman said to his son {And be intentional in your walk and lower your gaze. From your voice} [Luqman: 19] He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he went out, they would walk in front of him and leave his back to the angels.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3544 - True"
"3545","Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr al-Khawas told us, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Abu al-Nadr Hashim bin al-Qasim told us, Abu Khaythamah Zuhair bin Muawiyah said: I said to Abu al-Zubayr: I heard that Jabir mentioned that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “would not sleep until he recited the revelation of the prostration.” And blessed be He in whose hand is the dominion.” Abu al-Zubayr said: Safwan or Abu Safwan narrated it to me. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not They take it out because its context is based on the hadith of Laith bin Abi Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3545 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3546","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ali al-Shaybani told me about Kufa, Ahmad ibn Hazim al-Ghafari told me, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, Israel informed us, Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {He directs the matter from the heaven to the earth, Then it will come back to Him on a day whose equivalent is a thousand years of what you count.} [Al-Sajdah: 5] He said: “From the six days in which God created the heavens.” And the earth, then it ascends to it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not take it out.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3546 - True"
"3547","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam ibn Bashar informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Yahya informed us Ibn Al-Ala’, on the authority of his uncle Shuaib Ibn Khalid, Samak Ibn Harb told me, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amira, on the authority of Al-Abbas Ibn Abd al-Muttalib, may God bless him and grant him peace. On his authority, he said: We were sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Batha, when a cloud passed by, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you know what this is?” So we said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “The clouds,” so we said: The clouds. He said: “And Al-Muzn,” so we said: “And Al-Muzn.” He said: “By the sky” and he remained silent, then he said: “Do you know how much distance there is between the sky and the earth?” So we said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “Between them is a journey of five hundred years, and from each heaven to the next heaven there is a journey of five hundred years, and the thickness of each heaven is five hundred years.” A year, and above the seventh heaven there is a sea between its highest and its lowest, as between the heaven and the earth, and God is above that, and the deeds of the sons of God are not hidden from Him. “Adam is something.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3547 - That Yahya bin Al-Alaa is weak"
"3548","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nadr al-Azdi told me, Muawiyah ibn Amr told me, Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari, on the authority of Al-Amash, and Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, and the pronunciation is his, Muhammad bin Abdul-Salam told us, Ishaq told us, he informed us Jarir, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, and Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, on the authority of Maymun bin Abi Shabib, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with On his authority, he said: While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the Battle of Tabuk, the heat had struck, and the people dispersed until I looked. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is the closest to me. He said: So I approached him and said: O Messenger of God, inform me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise. And keep me away from the Fire. He said: “You have asked about something great, and it is easy for whomever God has made it easy for. You worship God and do not associate anything with Him and perform the prescribed prayers. And you pay the obligatory zakat, and fast Ramadan.” He said: “And if you wish, I can inform you of the gates of Paradise.” I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “Fasting is a shield, charity expiates sin, and a man standing up in the middle of the night seeking the face of God.” He said: Then he recited this verse. {Their sides turn away from their beds. They call upon their Lord in fear and hope, and spend out of what We have provided them.} [Al-Sajdah: 16] He said: “And if you wish, I will inform you. “At the head of the matter, its pillar, and the top of its hump.” He said: I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “As for the head of the matter, it is Islam. As for its pillar, it is prayer. As for its peak, it is jihad in the path of God. If you wish, I informed you of the ownership of all of that.” He remained silent and saw two riders being placed before us. I was afraid that they would distract him from my needs. He said: So I said: What is it, oh? Messenger of God? He said: “So he lowered his finger into his mouth.” He said: So I said: O Messenger of God, will we be taken to task for what we say with our tongues? He said: “May your mother be bereft of you, son of Jabal. Does anything that topples people on their noses in Hell except the harvests of their tongues?” This is the wording of the hadith of Jarir, and Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari did not mention in his hadith Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and he did not mention He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3548 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3549","Abd al-Samad bin Ali al-Bazzar told us, in Baghdad, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Sa`id bin Abi Maryam told us, Abdullah bin Suwayd bin Hayyan, Abu Sakhr told me, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, he said: While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace while he was describing Paradise until he finished, then he said: “In it is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no thought has entered the heart of mankind.” Then he recited {Their sides will stay away from their beds} [Al-Sajdah: 16] until the end of the verse. Abu Sakhr said: So I mentioned it to Al-Qurazi, and he said: Indeed, they concealed something for God’s sake. He performed a deed and concealed a reward for them, so they presented it to God, and those eyes were filled with joy. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3549 - True"
"3550","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abi Ubaidah, said: Abdullah said: “It is written in the Torah: God has prepared for those whose sides turn away from “Bed-beds are things that no eye has seen, no ear heard, and which has not entered the heart of man, and which no prophet sent nor angel near has known.” He said: “We” We recite it: “But no soul knows what has been hidden from them of comfort for eyes as a recompense for what they used to do” [Al-Sajdah: 17] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it has not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3550 - True"
"3551","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Dhuha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, {And We will certainly make them taste of the lesser torment apart from the greater torment} [Al-Sajdah: 21] He said: “The Day of Badr” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3551 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3552","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us, in Hamdan, Ishaq bin Ahmad bin Mahran al-Kharraz told us, Ishaq bin Suleiman al-Razi told us, he said: I heard Malik bin Anas, and he recited the words of God Almighty: {And We made from among them imams who guided by Our command when they were patient} [Al-Sajdah: 24] and he said: Tell me. Al-Zuhri said that Ata’ bin Yazid narrated to him, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that he heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “No servant was given “It is better for him and there is nothing greater than patience.” The two sheikhs agreed to include this word at the end of his hadith with this chain of transmission: that people from the Ansar"
"3553","Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saffar told me, Ahmad bin Nasr told me, Amr bin Talha told us, Asbat bin Nasr told us, on the authority of Al-Sadi, on the authority of Ikrimah, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the words of God Almighty: {And they say: When will this conquest be? If you are truthful, say: On the day of conquest, no. “Their faith will benefit those who disbelieve, and they will not be given respite.” [Al-Sajdah: 29] He said: “The day of Badr was opened for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but it did not benefit those who disbelieved.” “Their faith after death” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n ["
"3554","Abu Abbas Ahmad bin Harun Al-Faqih told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim, On the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, he said: “Surat Al-Ahzab was parallel to Surat Al-Baqarah, and it contained: the sheikh and the sheikha. If they commit adultery, stone them absolutely. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3554 - True"
"3555","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub al-Thaqafi told us, Abu Shu`ayb al-Harrani told us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid told us, Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah told us, Qaboos bin Abi Dhabyan told us that his father told him, saying: I said to Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that God Almighty said: {What God has made For a man with two hearts inside him} [Al-Ahzab: 4] What is meant by that? He said: “The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rose and took a dangerous risk, and the hypocrites who were praying with him said, ‘Don’t you see that he has two hearts, one with them and one with them? With you? Then God Almighty revealed, “God has not made for a man two hearts within his belly” [Al-Ahzab: 4] “This is a hadith with a sound chain of transmission, but they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3555 - Qaboos bin Abi Dhabyan is weak"
"3556","Muhammad bin Amr al-Bazzaz told us, in Baghdad, Ishaq bin al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, “He used to recite this verse.” The Prophet has more right to the believers than their souls, and he is their father."
"3557","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ali bin Bakr Al-Adl told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told me, Shababah bin Suwar told me, Ishaq told me Bin Yahya bin Talha, on the authority of his uncle Musa bin Talha, who said: Among us, Aisha bint Talha said to her mother, Umm Kulthum bint Abi Bakr: My father Better than your father. So Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, said: Shall I not judge between you? Abu Bakr entered upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “O Abu You are a virgin, you will be freed from the Fire by God.” I said: From that day on, he was named Ateq, and Talhah entered upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: “You, O Talhah, are among those who “His death has passed.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not take him out.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3557 - Rather, Ishaq bin Yahya bin Talha is abandoned, said Ahmad."
"3558","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Dinar told us, Sharik bin Abi Nimr, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, that she said: In my house this verse was revealed {He only wants May God remove impurity from you, O People of the House.” [Al-Ahzab: 33] She said: So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent for Ali, Fatima, and Al-Hasan. And Al-Hussein, may God be pleased with them all, said: “Oh God, these are my family.” Umm Salamah said: O Messenger of God, I am not one of the people of my family. The house? He said: “You are my best family, and these are my family, O God, my family. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3558 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3559","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid told us, my father told me, he said: I heard Al-Awza’i saying: Abu Ammar told me, he said: Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’, may God be pleased with him, told me: I came looking for Ali, may God be pleased with him, but I did not find him. Fatima, may God be pleased with her, said: He went to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to invite him, so he sat down, and he came with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. So he went in and I went in with them. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called Hassan and Hussein, and each one of them sat on his thigh and approached Fatima. From his lap and her husband, then he wrapped his garment over them, and I was a witness, and he said: “Allah only desires to remove impurity from you, O People of the House. And purify you with a thorough purification} [Al-Ahzab: 33] Oh God, these are my family. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”"
"3560","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Usayd bin Asim told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan bin Saeed told us, On the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, she said: I said: O Messenger of God, men are mentioned but women are not mentioned. So God Almighty revealed {Indeed, the Muslim men and Muslim women, the believing men and believing women} [Al-Ahzab: 35] the verse. And He revealed: “Indeed, I will not waste the work of any worker among you, whether male or female.” [Al Imran: 195] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3560 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3561","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Al-Aghar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id and Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with them, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If a man wakes his wife up from That night, they prayed two rak'ahs prescribed for men and women who often remember God. The chain of transmission was transmitted by Issa bin Jaafar, who is trustworthy. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"3562","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Abu Awanah told us, Omar bin Abi Salamah told me, On the authority of his father, he said: Osama bin Zaid, may God be pleased with him, told me: I was in the mosque, and Al-Abbas and Ali came to me and said to me: Oh Osama Ask permission for us to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I entered upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him for permission, and I said to him: Al-Abbas and Ali are seeking permission. He said: “Do you know what they need?” I said: No, by God, I do not know. He said: “But I know, give them permission.” So they entered upon him and said: O Messenger of God, we have come to you to ask you which of your family is most beloved to you? He said: “The most beloved of my family to me is Fatima bint Muhammad.” They said: O Messenger of God, we are not asking you about Fatima. He said: “It is Osama bin Zaid, upon whom God has bestowed blessings, and I have bestowed upon him.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3562 - Omar bin Abi Salamah is weak"
"3563","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar Al-Adl told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: Zaid bin Haritha came to complain to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about Zainab bint A colt, may God be pleased with her. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Seize your family.” So she descended: “And hide within yourself what God will reveal” [Al-Ahzab: 37]\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3563 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3564","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, about Abu Uthman, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Zainab, Umm Sulaym sent Hays to Taur. Stones. Anas said: Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me: “Go and invite whomever you meet among the Muslims.” So I went and did not see anyone except that I invited him. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, put his hand in the food and called for it, and said: “What God wills.” He said: So they started eating and leaving, and I remained. A group in the house, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, became ashamed of them, and they prolonged the conversation, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out and left them in House, so God revealed: {O you who have believed, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless permission is given to you to eat food without looking at its content} [Al-Ahzab: 53] meaning Without being careful until it reached {that is purer for your hearts and for their hearts} [Al-Ahzab: 53] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3564 - True"
"3565","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Awf Al-Tai told us, Abdul-Quddus bin Al-Hajjaj told us, Safwan bin Amr told me, Safwan bin Amr told me. Sulaym bin Aamer said: A man came to Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, and said: O Abu Umamah, I saw in my dream that the angels were praying. It is upon you whenever you enter, whenever you go out, whenever you stand, and whenever you sit. Abu Umamah said: “O God, forgive us. We have prayed on your behalf, and if you had wished, the angels would have prayed over you.” Then he recited: {O you who have believed. Remember God abundantly, and glorify Him morning and evening. It is He who prays over you and His angels to bring you out of darkness into light. And it was Merciful to the believers} [Al-Ahzab: 42] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3565 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3566","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Abu Sahl Bishr bin Sahl Al-Labbad told me, Abdullah bin Saleh Al-Masry told me, Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Saeed bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abd al-Ala bin Hilal, on the authority of Irbad bin Sariyah, may God be pleased with him, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “I am the servant of God, and the Seal of the Prophets, and my father is tangled in his clay.” And I will tell you about that. I am the call of my father Abraham, the good news of Jesus, and the vision of my mother Aminah who saw.” And so do the mothers of the prophets. And when the mother of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, she placed it on him, she saw a light that illuminated the palaces of the Levant for her. Then he recited {O Prophet, indeed, We have sent you A witness, a bringer of good tidings, a warner, a caller to God by His permission, and an illuminating lamp} [Al-Ahzab: 46] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3566 - True"
"3567","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Hamid bin Abi Hamid Al-Muqri narrated to us, Ishaq bin Suleiman Al-Razi narrated to us, he said: I heard mushrooms Ibn Khalifa, narrating on the authority of Al-Hasan Ibn Muslim Ibn Yannaq, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he recited the words of God Almighty: {O you who have believed, when you marry believing women, then divorce them before you have touched them} [Al-Ahzab: 49] He said: “There is no divorce until there is “Marriage” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. Al-Hakim said: “I am astonished by the two imam sheikhs, how they neglected this hadith and did not include it in the two Sahih books, as a hadith was authenticated according to their conditions. Ibn Omar, Aisha, Abdullah bin Abbas, Muadh bin Jabal, and Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them. As for the hadith of Abdullah bin Omar\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3567 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3568","So Abu Ali, Abu Al-Hussein bin Al-Muzaffar Al-Hafiz, Abu Hamid bin Sharik Al-Faqih, Abu Ahmad Al-Sha’bi, and Abu Ishaq Al-Razi among others said: Yahya bin Muhammad bin Sa’id told us, Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Quta’i told us, Asim told us, Ayyub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no divorce except after marriage.” As for the hadith of Aisha:"
"3569","So Abu Imran Musa bin Saeed Al-Hanzali, the memorizer of Hamdan, told us, Abu Muslim Ibrahim bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Minhaal, Hisham Al-Dastawi narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said: “There is no divorce except after marriage, and there is no emancipation except after possession.” As for the hadith of Ibn Abbas,"
"3570","So Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Ayyub Al-Alaf told us, in Egypt, Amr bin Khaled told us. Al-Harrani, Ayoub bin Suleiman Al-Jariri told us, on the authority of Rabia bin Abi Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no divorce for one who does not own property.” As for the hadith of Muadh bin Jabal,"
"3571","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Abd told us. Al-Majid bin Abdul Aziz, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “There is no divorce except after marriage, and there is no emancipation except after possession.” As for the hadith of Jabir,"
"3572","So Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi, Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari, Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih, Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl, and Muhammad narrated to us. Bin Ja`far al-Muzaki, they said: Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Abdi told us, Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Yazid al-Dimashqi told us, Sadaqah told us. Ibn Abdullah Al-Dimashqi said: I came to Muhammad Ibn Al-Munkadir when I was angry, and I said: By God, did you make it permissible for Al-Walid Ibn Yazid or Umm Salamah? He said: Me, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Jabir bin Abdullah Al Ansari told me that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “There is no divorce for the one who does not own, and there is no emancipation for the one who does not own.”"
"3573","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdullah bin Mahmoud told us, Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Hakim told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Ata’, and Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No divorce Before marriage.” Al-Hakim said: “The narration of this hadith is based on two weak chains of narration: Jarir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Al-Nazzal bin Sabra, on the authority of Ali, And Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather. For this reason, the two sheikhs did not inquire into seeking these authentic chains of narration, by God. I know"
"3574","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, about Al-Sadi, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Umm Hani, may God be pleased with her, said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, proposed to me, so I apologized to him and he excused me. And God Almighty revealed {O Prophet, indeed We have made lawful to you your wives} [Al-Ahzab: 50] to the Almighty’s saying: {Those who emigrated with you} [Al-Ahzab: 50] She said: I was not permissible for him. I did not emigrate with him. I was one of the freedmen. “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3574 - True"
"3575","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told me, Affan bin Muslim told us, Hammad bin Salama told us, Thabit reported. Al-Bunani, that he recited the words of God Almighty: “Indeed, God and His angels send blessings upon the Prophet. [الأحزاب: 56] فَقَالَ ثَابِتٌ: قَدِمَ عَلَيْنَا سُلَيْمَانُ مَوْلَى الْحَسَنِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ فَ"
"3576","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih and Abu Al-Hasan Al-Anbari told us, saying: Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Saleh Mahboub bin Musa told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari, on the authority of Al-A’mash, and Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “Indeed, God has angels who travel on earth, informing me of my nation’s peace.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not take it out. “And they have exalted us in The hadith of Al-Thawri is famous for it. As for the hadith of Al-A’mash on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, we did not write it except with this chain of transmission.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3576 - True"
"3577","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ahmed bin Ali Al-Abar told us, Ahmed bin Abdul-Rahman bin Bakkar Al-Dimashqi told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Abu Rafi’ told me, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Masoud al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “Pray for me often on Friday, for no one prays for me on Friday except that his prayers will be offered to me.” This hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, because this Abu Rafi’ is Ismail bin Rafi’, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3577 - Ismail bin Rafi’ Abu Rafi’ is weak"
"3578","Abu Al-Hussein Ali bin Abdul Rahman bin Issa Al-Subai’i told us about Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Tufail bin Ubayy bin Ka’b, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, he said: It was When a quarter of the night had passed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up and said: “O people, remember God. O people, remember God. People, remember God. The trembling came, followed by the synonym. Death has come with what is in it. Death has come with what is in it. Then Ubayy bin Ka’b said: O Messenger of God, I pray for you often, so how much of it should I give you? He said: “Whatever you want.” He said: A quarter? He said: “Whatever you want, and if you increase, it is better for you.” He said: Half? He said: “Whatever you want, and if you increase, it is better for you.” He said: Two-thirds? He said: “Whatever you want, and if you add more, that is better.” He said: O Messenger of God, shall I make it all yours? He said: “Then your worries will be satisfied, and your sins will be forgiven.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3578 - True"
"3579","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amsh told us, about Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {Do not be like those who harmed Moses} [Al-Ahzab: 69] the verse. He said: “His people had clothes on him, so he went out one day to wash himself, and he put his clothes on a rock, and the rock came out pulling his clothes.” So Moses went out and followed it, naked, until it reached the gatherings of the children of Israel, and they saw him, but he did not turn away. That is what God Almighty says: {And he healed him. God is from what they said, and he is of honor in the sight of God.} [Al-Ahzab: 69] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3579 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3580","Muhammad bin Musa Al-Faqih told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Amr bin Abi Mazour told us, Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: {Indeed, We have offered the trust to the heavens and the earth. And the mountains, but they refused to lift them and were afraid of them. Did I warn you? He said: I accept. He said: It was only between the afternoon prayer until the sun had set until the sin occurred. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not He takes it out\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3580 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3581","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Ubayy Ibn Ka’b, in His Almighty’s saying: {Indeed, We have offered trustworthiness to the heavens and the earth and the mountains} He said: “Part of trustworthiness is that a woman She was entrusted with her private parts.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3581 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3582","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan bin Maimun told me, Affan told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Thabit told us, On the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, when God Almighty said: {And We have made iron for him, lest he should do righteous deeds} [Saba: 11]. Anas said: “Indeed, Luqman was With Dawud, as he was undressing the shield, he twisted it like this with his hand, which made Luqman wonder and want to ask him, but his wisdom prevented him from doing so. He asked him, and when he finished, he poured it on himself and said: Yes, this is the armor of war. So Luqman said: Silence is a part of wisdom, and few do it. I wanted to ask you, but I remained silent until you were enough for me: “It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3582 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3583","Abu Muhammad Al-Muzani told us, Ahmad bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Abdul Wahhab told me Ibn Mujahid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {And estimate in the narration} [Saba: 11] He said: “Do not knock Widen the nails and they become smooth, but do not thicken the nails and narrow the throat and they become split, and make it a measure.” This is a strange letter in the interpretation, and Abd Al-Wahhab is among those who did not expel it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3583 - Abd al-Wahhab did not narrate it due to its weakness"
"3584","Abu Amr Ismail bin Nujaid Al-Sulami narrated to me, Muhammad bin Ayyub narrated to me, Abu Ghassan Muhammad bin Amr Al-Tayalisi narrated to me, Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “Suleiman bin Dawood, peace be upon them, died while he was He was standing and praying, but the devils did not know about it until the earth devoured his staff. Then he fell down, and whenever a tree grew, he would ask it: What disease are you suffering from? He said: So you inform him as God Almighty told him: {And for Solomon the wind, its beginning was a month and its rest a month, and We sent down for him a spring of rain} [Saba: 12] All the verses. When the carobs sprouted, he asked them: What did they grow for? She said, “Because of the ruin of this mosque.” He said: This mosque will not be destroyed until I die, so he stood up and prayed, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3584 - True"
"3585","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Anas Al-Qurashi told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Abdullah bin Ayyash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hubayra al-Sabai, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Wa’ala, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. About them, he says: A man asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about Saba: What is a man, a woman, or a land? He said: “He is a man who gave birth to ten children, six of his children in Yemen and four in the Levant. As for the Yemenis, they are Madhhij and Kinda. The Azd, the Ash'arites, Anmar, and Himyar are all good, and as for the Levantines, they are Lakham, Judham, Amilah, and Ghassan. This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission, but they did not narrate it “and it is witnessed by the hadith of Farwah bin Musayk al-Muradi”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3585 - True"
"3586","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, saying: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Faraj bin Saeed bin Alqamah told us, On the authority of Sa`id bin Abyad bin Hammal al-Maribi, Abu Thabit bin Sa`id bin Abyad’s uncle told me, on the authority of his father Farwa bin Musayk al-Muradi, He told him that he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about Saba, and he said: O Messenger of God, is Saba a man, a mountain, or a valley? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Rather, it is a man who gave birth to ten, and four suffered from leprosy, and six fell ill with leprosy. And Ghassan, and Tiaman, Himyar, and Mazhaj, and Al-Azd, and Kindah, and the Ash'arites, and the Anmar, of which is Bigilah.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3586 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3587","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Kamil ibn Khalaf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jarir al-Faqih narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, I heard Abu Usama and he was asked about the saying God Almighty said: {And We have not sent you except as a bringer of good news and a warner to mankind} [Saba: 28] And he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, On the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, he said: I sought the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night and found him standing and praying. He prolonged the prayer, then said: “I have been given Tonight is the fifth night, and no prophet before me was given it. I was sent against the red and the black,” Mujahid said: “Humans and the jinn, and I was supported by terror, so that the enemy would be terrified, while he was on the march of a month.” The earth was made for me a place of mosque and purification, and the spoils were made lawful for me, but they had not been lawful for anyone before me. And it was said to me: Ask and it will be given to you. So I hid them as intercession. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context, but rather They extracted separate words from the hadith.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3587 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim and they departed from it"
"3588","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: “And how can they fight from a far away place?” [Saba: 52] He said: “They ask Refutation, but not at the time of refutation. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3588 - True"
"3589","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz informed us, Hamid bin Abi Hamid Al-Muqri informed us, Ishaq bin Sulayman told us, Abd informed us Al-Rahman bin Abdullah Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mukhariq bin Sulaym, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: “When We narrate to you a hadith, We bring to you confirmation of that in the Book of God. Indeed, when a servant says: Glory be to God and praise be to God, and no There is no god but God, and God is greatest, and blessed be God. An angel seized them, took them under his wing, and took them up without passing by a crowd of people. The angels will not ask forgiveness for their speaker until the Face of the Most Gracious comes to them. Then Abdullah recited: “To Him ascend good words and righteous deeds.” He raises it up} [Fatir: 10] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3589 - True"
"3590","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Abu Al-Walid told us, Ubayd Allah bin Iyad bin Laqit told us, Iyad told me Ibn Laqit, on the authority of Abu Rimthah, said: I set off with my father towards the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and my father greeted him and we sat for an hour and talked. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to my father: “This is your son?” He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba. He said: “Indeed.” He said: I bear witness to it. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, smiled and laughed because my resemblance to my father was proven and who my father swore about that. He said: Then he said: “As for this son of yours He will not commit injustice against you, and you should not commit injustice against him.” He said: And the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited “Should no bearer of burden bear the burden of another” [Al-Najm: 38] to his saying. God Almighty {This is a warner from the first wars} [An-Najm: 56] “The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3590 - True"
"3591","Abu Ahmad Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah told us, Nasr bin Ali told us, Al-Mu’tamar bin Suleiman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: When “Praise the Name of Your Lord” was revealed The highest one said: “All of them are in the scrolls of Abraham.” Then when they descended, and when the star descended, it reached {And Abraham is the one who fulfilled} [An-Najm: 37] He said: And in {Will you not visit? One bearer of another burden} [An-Najm: 38] to the Almighty’s saying: {This is a warner from the first vows} [An-Najm: 56] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it has not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3591 - True"
"3592","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir informed us, he told me Al-Amash, on the authority of a man who named him, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say in his saying, Glory be to Him. And the Almighty said: {And among them is unjust to himself, and among them is the thrifty, and among them is the one who is the first to do good deeds} [Fatir: 32] He said: “The one who is the first and the thrifty will enter Paradise.” without reckoning, and the wrongdoer to himself will be given an easy reckoning, then he will enter Paradise.” The narrations differed from Al-A’mash regarding the chain of transmission of this. The hadith was narrated on the authority of Al-Thawri, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Thabit, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him. It was said on the authority of Shu'bah, on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of a man from Thaqif, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda'. It was also said on the authority of Al-Thawri, on the authority of Al-A’mash, who said: He mentioned Abu Thabit, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’. “And if there are many narrations in the hadith, it will appear that the hadith has a basis.”"
"3593","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, in the chain of transmission of Musaddad bin Mashad, Abu Al-Muthanna informed us on the authority of Musaddad, Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, Abu Shuaib al-Salt ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, Uqba ibn Sahban al-Harrani narrated to me, he said: I said to Aisha, may God be pleased with her: O mother Believers, have you seen the words of God Almighty: “Then We gave the Book to inheritance to those whom We have chosen from among Our servants. But among them is wrongdoer to himself, and among them is He is thrifty, and among them is he who is proactive in doing good deeds, God willing. That is the great virtue.} [Fatir: 32] Then Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: “As for The previous one is the one who passed through the life of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and bore witness to his life and provision. As for the Muqtisadid, he is the one who follows their footsteps and does by their deeds until he joins them, and as for the wrongdoer to himself, he is like me and you and whoever follows us, and all of them will be in Paradise.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it. \"\"\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3593 - Al-Salt, Al-Nasa’i said, “He is not trustworthy,” and Ahmad said, “He is not strong.”"
"3594","Abu Ali Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Dawud Al-Muttazzar Al-Misri told me, in Mecca, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad bin Al-Abbas Al-Masry told us, Amr bin Sawad Al-Sarkhasi, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Samh, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri May God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited the words of God Almighty: “The Gardens of Eden, which they will enter, and therein will be placed in bracelets of Gold} [Fatir: 33] Then he said: “Indeed, upon them are crowns. Infinitely nearer is a pearl than them, to illuminate what is between the east and the west.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission is as Abu Al-Abbas told us, on the authority of Al-Dawri, on the authority of Yahya bin Ma’in, that he said: The most correct chain of transmission of the Egyptians is Amr, on the authority of Darraj, On the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id “\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3594 - True"
"3595","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Al-Hasan bin Al-Muthanna bin Muadh Al-Anbari told me, my father told me, Muadh bin Hisham told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Amr bin Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Jawza, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {Praise be to God who has removed our sorrow} [Fatir: 34] He said: “Sorrow is the Fire.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3595 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3596","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman. Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: “Have We not given you life in which whoever remembers will remember?” [Fatir: 37] He said: “Sixty years.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3596 - True"
"3597","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abdullah bin Saleh told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If a man from my nation reaches sixty years of age, he will “May God excuse him during his lifetime.” It is authentic according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3597 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3598","Abu Al-Hasan bin Al-Fadl Al-Samiri told us, in Baghdad, Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Arafa Al-Abdi told us, Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad Al-Muharbi told us, On the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The lives of my nation are what Between sixty and seventy, and the least of them is permissible.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3598 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3599","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Bakra Bakkar bin Qutaybah, the judge in Egypt, told us, Mutarrif bin Mazin told us, Muammar bin Rashid told us, I heard Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman al-Ghafari saying: I heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “God has excused himself to a servant who was sixty or seventy years old.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3599 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3600","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani informed us, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abdul Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, about A sheikh from Ghaffar, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “God has indeed made excuses to a servant. He lived until he reached the age of sixty or seventy. God has made excuses for him.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3600 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3601","Sheikh Abu Bakr told us from the origin of his book, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, On the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever of my nation lives for seventy years, God will excuse him.” “In Al-‘Umr” is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3601 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3602","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saffar told me, Ahmad ibn Nasr told me, Amr ibn Talha told me, Israel told me, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, He said: Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, read, {And if God were to hold people accountable for what they have earned, He would not have left any animal on its back, but He would delay them} [Fatir: 45] The verse. He said: “The scarab was almost tortured in its hole for the sin of the son of Adam.” Authentic chain of narration.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3602 - True"
"3603","Ali bin Abdul Rahman Al-Subaie told us, in Kufa, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hakam Al-Hiri told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Hussein Al-Arni told us, Amr bin Thabit told us Abi Al-Miqdam, on the authority of Muhammad bin Marwan, on the authority of Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Ali, who said: “Whoever finds hardness in his heart, let him write Yasin while the Qur’an is in He had a bowl of saffron, then he drank it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3603 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3604","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Yusuf told me. Al-Azdi, my grandfather told me, Sufyan bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan Tarif bin Shihab, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, He said: Banu Salamah was in a part of the city and they wanted to move near the mosque, so God Almighty revealed: {Indeed, we salute The dead, and We record what they have put forward and their traces.} [Yasin: 12] Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called them and said: “Indeed, he is recording your traces.” Then he read. The verse was upon them, so they left out “This is an authentic and wondrous hadith from the hadith of Al-Thawri.” Muslim narrated some of this meaning from a praiseworthy hadith on the authority of Anas.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3604 - Ishaq Al-Azraq was the only one to narrate it from him, and it is authentic"
"3605","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Razi told us, Abu Zur’ah told us Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Karim, Abu Hafs Amer bin Saeed told us, Al-Qasim bin Malik Al-Muzani narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Sayyar Abi Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: “When the companion of Yasin said: O my people, follow the messengers. He said: They strangled him to death. Then he turned to the prophets and said: {Indeed, I have believed in your Lord, so listen} [Yasin: 25] meaning, bear witness for me. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3605 - Ibn Ishaq is weak"
"3606","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told us, Jeddi told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Hushaym told us, Abu Bishr told us, about Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: Al-Aas bin Wael came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a large barrier. He turned him around and said: O Muhammad, will God send this man after what he sent? He said: “Yes, God will raise this man to kill you, then bring you back to life, then admit you to the fire of Hell.” He said: Then the verses were revealed: “Has man not seen that We created him from a drop of drop, so when he is a clear adversary.} [Yasin: 77] until the end of the surah: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3606 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3607","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ali al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ahmad ibn Hazim al-Ghifari informed us, Qubaisa ibn Uqba informed us, Sufyan informed us, On the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, in His Almighty saying: {And the rows of rows} [Al-Saffat: 1] He said: The angels {so they rebuke, rebuking} [Al-Saffat: 2] He said: “The angels” {So the following ones, mentioning} [Al-Saffat: 3] He said: “The angels” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3607 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3608","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wael Shaqiq bin Salamah said: Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, recited: {Rather, I am astonished, and they mock} [Al-Saffat: 12]. Shurayh said: “Indeed, God is not amazed at anything.” Only those who do not know are astonished.” Al-A’mash said: So I mentioned it to Ibrahim, and he said: Shurayh liked his opinion, that Abdullah was more knowledgeable than Shurayh, and Abdullah was reciting it: {Rather, I am amazed} [Al-Saffat: 12] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3608 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3609","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, Samak bin Mahran told us Harb, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying: {Gather together those who do wrong and their wives} [Al-Saffat: 22] He said: “Those like them are those like them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3609 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3610","Omar bin Ja’far Al-Basri told us, Al-Hasan bin Ahmad Al-Tustari told us, Ubayd Allah bin Muadh Al-Anbari told us, Al-Mu’tamir bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is no reason for a man to do something except He was standing with him on the Day of Resurrection, bound for him and being led with him. Then he recited this verse: “Stop them. Indeed, they will be questioned” [Al-Saffat: 24] “Thus. It was narrated by Al-Hasan bin Ahmad Al-Tustari on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Muadh, on the authority of him, and if it were permissible for us to accept it from him, we would authenticate it on the condition of the two sheikhs. But we say that he is correct.”"
"3611","What Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Mu’tamir bin Suleiman informed us, he said: I heard Laith bin Abi Sulaym, speaking on the authority of Bishr, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “Whoever invites his Muslim brother to something, and if a man invites another man, he will be detained with him on the Day of Resurrection, bound to him and will be led with him.” Then he recited The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Stop them. Indeed, they will be questioned.” [Al-Saffat: 24] “Al-Hakim said: It was clear, based on the narration of the Imam of his time, Abu Ya’qub. Al-Hanzali said that the hadith has a basis with a chain of transmission"
"3612","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Shibl bin Abbad told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying {And indeed, of his followers belong to Abraham} [Al-Saffat: 83] He said: “Who The followers of Noah, Abraham, on his method and his Sunnah. With him, the effort grew until his effort reached the effort of Abraham in deeds, so when they submitted to what they were commanded to do. And he turned to the forehead and put his face to the ground and said: Do not slaughter me while you are watching. Perhaps you will have mercy on me and do not attack me. Bind my hands to My neck, then put my face on the ground. When he put his hand in to slaughter it, he did not scratch the knife until it was called, “O Abraham, you have confirmed the vision.” [Al-Saffat: 105] So he held up his hand and raised his saying, “And We ransomed him with a great slaughter” [Al-Saffat: 107] with a great, coming ram. “And Ibn Abbas claimed that the sacrifice Ismail “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3612 - According to Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3613","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad al-Zahid al-Hairi informed me, Muhammad bin Ishaq al-Sana’ani told me, Sana’a, Yemen, Muhammad bin Jasham told us. Al-San’ani, Sufyan Al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of Samak ibn Harb, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “A vision “The prophets are revelation.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3613 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3614","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ya’qub bin Muhammad Al-Zuhri told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Sharik bin Abdullah bin Abi Nimr, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “his eyes slept but his heart did not sleep.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3614 - Jacob is weak and no Muslim narrated from him"
"3615","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us dictation, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Iyadh bin Abdullah bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited the Quran while he was on the pulpit. When he reached the point of prostration, he descended and prostrated, and the people prostrated with him. When it was another day, he recited it. When he reached the time of prostration, the people prepared to prostrate, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is the repentance of a prophet, but I saw that you prepared. To prostrate.” So he descended and prostrated, and the people prostrated with him. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3615 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3616","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Al-Walid told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, that Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, said: I saw what the sleeper saw as if I had opened Surah S. I ended up prostrating, and the inkwell, the pen, and everything around it prostrated, so I was informed of that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “so he prostrated in it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3616 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3617","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Ubi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Yahya bin Amara, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: Abu Talib fell ill Then the Quraysh came and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and a man was sitting at the head of Abu Talib, so Abu Jahl stood up so that he could prevent him, and they complained to him. Abi Talib said: O son of my brother, what do you want from your people? He said: “Uncle, I only want a word from them that will humiliate the Arabs and pay them the tribute of the non-Arabs.” He said: One word? He said: “One word.” He said: What is it? He said: “There is no god but Allah.” He said: So they said: Make the gods one god. Is this a strange thing? He said: “And the Qur’an is revealed among them” [p. He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3617 - True"
"3618","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, my father told me, he said: I heard Muhammad Ibn Ishaq, he said: Al-Abbas Ibn Abdullah Ibn Ma’bad Ibn Abbas told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “ {By the Qur’an, Dhikr} [Page: 1] was revealed among them and in their assembly. That means the assembly of Abu Talib and Abu Jahl and the gathering of the Quraysh to them when They disputed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3618 - According to the condition of Muslim and Al-Abbas is trustworthy"
"3619","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar Al-Zahid told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Muhammad bin Sabiq told us, Israel told us, on the authority of my father Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Tamimi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {And there will never be a time of escape} [p. 3] He said: “Not by the time of desire nor by “Fleeing.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3619 - True"
"3620","Ismail bin Muhammad al-Faqih told us about irrigation, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris told us, Suleiman bin Daoud al-Hashimi told us, Abd al-Rahman told us Ibn Abi Al-Zinad, on the authority of Musa Ibn Uqba, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “What befell David did not befall him after Destiny is nothing but a wonder at which He astonished Himself, and that is because He said: O Lord, there is not an hour of night or day without a worshiper from the family of David. Your servant prays for you, or glorifies God, or exalts God and mentions things, but God disliked that and said: “O David, this would not have happened except through me. Had it not been for “Help me in whatever you are strong enough to do, and by my glory I will surely destroy you to yourself one day.” He said, “O Lord, tell me about it.” Then the temptation befell him that day. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3620 - True"
"3621","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, Muhammad bin Saad Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Dimashqi, narrated to us, may God forbid, Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said: “David, peace be upon him, said: My Lord, I ask you for your love and the love of whoever loves you, and for the deeds that make your love reach me. My Lord, make your love more beloved.” Save me from myself and my family, and from the cold water.” Whenever the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, mentioned David and spoke about him, he said: “He was the servant of mankind.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate him.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3621 - Rather, this is Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Dimashqi. Ahmad said his hadiths are fabricated."
"3622","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saffar informed us, Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, Amr ibn Talha al-Qannad informed us, Sharik informed us, on the authority of al-Suddi, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “Dawud, peace be upon him, died suddenly on a Saturday, and he was hibernating and the birds would flock to him. So you shade him.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3622 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3623","Al-A'mash, on the authority of Al-Minhal, on the authority of Sa'id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty's saying: {And We placed him on his throne In the flesh} [p. 34] He said: “He is Satan who was on his throne and spent forty days among the people. And Solomon had a slave girl called Jarada.” And there was a dispute between some of its people and his people, so he decided between them justly, but he wanted the right to belong to its people, so God revealed to him That a calamity will befall you, and he did not know whether it would come from the sky or from the earth. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3623 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3624","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Rabi’ah told me Ibn Yazid, he said: Abdullah Ibn Al-Dailami told me, he said: I entered upon Abdullah Ibn Amr Ibn Al-Aas in a wall in Taif called: Al-Waht says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Suleiman bin David, peace be upon them, asked God for three and He gave him two. I hope he gave him the third; He asked him for a ruling that coincided with his ruling, so he gave it to him, and he asked him for a kingdom that no one after him should have, so he gave it to him, and he asked him, “Which man He left his house, wanting only to pray in this mosque, meaning the Holy House. He is free from his sin, as on the day his mother gave birth to him.” The Messenger said. God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “And we hope that God has given him that.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3624 - Abdullah is the son of Fairuz, trustworthy"
"3625","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told me, Sulayman bin Harb told me, Hammad bin Zaid told me, Abu Lubabah said: I heard Aisha, may God be pleased with her, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast until we could tell him what he wanted to break his fast. He would break his fast until we could tell him what he wanted to fast, and every night he would recite Surah Bani Israel and the Zumar.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3625 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3626","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Abu Usama, and Abdah bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr Ibn Alqamah, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Hatib, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of al-Zubayr Ibn al-Awwam, may God be pleased with them both, He said: When this verse was revealed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, {Indeed, you will die and they will die, then on the Day of Resurrection you will You dispute with your Lord.} [Az-Zumar: 31] I said: Will what happened between us in this world be repeated to us, along with the specific sins? He said: “Yes, they will repeat that to you until He gives to everyone what is due his due.” Al-Zubair said: By God, the matter is severe.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3626 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3627","Abdul Rahman bin Abi Al-Zubayr told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, Muhammad bin Amr told me. Al-Laythi, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdul-Rahman bin Hatib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, he said: When this verse was revealed, he mentioned the hadith, Al-Zubayr did not mention in his chain of transmission: “It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3627 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3628","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Qari narrated to me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi narrated to me, Al-Hasan bin Al-Rabi’ narrated to us, Abdullah bin Idris narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq told me, he said: And Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar, he said: We used to say that no one who is tempted can repent, and what God will accept something from him, so when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina, the verse was revealed among them: “O My servants who have transgressed against themselves! Be despondent of the mercy of God. Indeed, God forgives all sins. Indeed, He is the Forgiving, the Most Merciful. [Al-Zumar: 53], and the verses that follow it. Omar said: So I wrote it down and sat on my camel, then I circumambulated Medina, then “the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stayed in Mecca awaiting God’s permission for him to enter.” “Hijra and his companions among the immigrants,” and Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, stayed waiting for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to be called to prayer. Then it comes out with, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”"
"3629","Abu al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Muzaki told us, Muhammad bin Amr al-Jarashi told us, Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus told us, Abu Bakr told us Ibn Ayyash, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “All the people of He will see his seat in Paradise and say: If only God had guided me, then it would be a regret for him. And all the people of Paradise will see his seat in Hell and he will say: Had it not been that God had guided me and there would be thanks to Him, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited {Lest a soul say, “Oh, how unfortunate I am for what I have neglected” God} “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3629 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3630","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us on the authority of Anbasa bin Saeed, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amra, on the authority of Mujahid, said: Ibn Abbas said to me: Do you know the capacity of Hell? I said: No. He said: Yes, by God, you do not know that there are valleys of pus and blood between the lobe of someone’s ear and his head, a distance of seventy autumns’ journey. I said to him: Rivers? He said: No, but valleys. Then he said: Do you know how spacious Hell is? I said: No. He said: Yes, by God, you do not know. Aisha, may God be pleased with her, told me that she asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about what God Almighty said. And glory be to Him: {And the entire earth I will hold on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens will be rolled up with His right hand} I said: Where will the people be on that day, O Messenger of God? He said: “On the bridge of Hell.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3630 - True"
"3631","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, about Suleiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Bishr bin Shaghaf Al-Tamimi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in his saying: Glory be to And the Majestic: {And the trumpet was blown} [Az-Zumar: 68]. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is a horn into which the trumpet is blown.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3631 - True"
"3632","Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Yaqoub, the memorizer of dictation, told us, Muhammad ibn Abdul-Wahhab told us, Muhadhar ibn al-Mu’ri’ informed us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she used to say to the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: A woman is not ashamed to She gives herself away? So God revealed this verse about the wives of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: {You may let whomever you wish of them and take to yourself whomever you wish} [Al-Ahzab: 51] so she said Aisha told the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “I see your Lord hastening for you in your desires.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this. \"driving\"\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3632 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, and they did not narrate it in this context"
"3633","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim Al-Adl told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told me, Musa bin Ismail told me, Wahib told me, Ibn Jurayj told me, in God Almighty says: “It is not lawful for you to have women afterward, nor for you to exchange them.” [Al-Ahzab: 52] Ibn Jurayj said: Ata’ told me, on the authority of Ubaid ibn Umair, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not die until God made it lawful for him to marry.” This hadith It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3633 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3634","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, He said: Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: “The verses are the brocade of the Qur’an.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3634 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3635","Sufyan said: Habib bin Abi Thabit told me, on the authority of a man, that he passed by Abu Darda’ while he was building a mosque and said: What is this? He said: “This is for the family of Hamim.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3635 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3636","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed, he informed us Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, in His Almighty saying {Our Lord, We have given birth to two And We gave life to two.} [Ghafir: 11] He said: “It is like that of the cow. {You were dead, and He gave you life. Then He will put you to death, then He will bring you to life. Then to Him is the return. You will be returned} [Al-Baqarah: 28] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3636 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3637","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “A herald will call out before the Hour: O people, the Hour has come for you, and the living and the dead will hear it.” And God descends to the lowest heaven and calls: To whom is the kingdom today? To God, the One, the Supreme. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3637 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3638","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammam bin Yahya told us, about Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Wahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, he said: I was informed of a hadith On the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about retaliation, but I did not hear it, so I bought a camel. So I set off on my journey to support him, then I traveled for a month until I came to Egypt, so I came to Abdullah bin Unais and said to the doorman: Tell him, Jabir is at the door. He said: Ibn Abdullah? I said: Yes. So he came to him and told him, so he stood up and folded his garment until he came out to him, so he embraced me and I embraced him, so I said to him: A hadith that has been conveyed to me about you that I heard from the Messenger of God. May God bless him and grant him peace. I did not listen to him in the retaliation, so I was afraid that I would die or she would die before I heard him. Then Abdullah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God will gather the servants - or he said: the people - naked, with their uncircumcised.” He said: We said: What's wrong with them? He said: “There is nothing with them, then he calls them in a voice that can be heard from afar as well as from near: I am the king, I am the judge. It is not permissible for any of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise, and it is not befitting for any of the people of Hell to enter Hell, while he has a wrongdoing until I repay him. From it until the blow. “He said: We said: How is that? We only bring to God uncircumcised with them?” He said: “With good deeds and bad deeds.” He said: And the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: “Today every soul will be recompensed for what it has earned. No injustice today” [Ghafir: 17] “The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3638 - True"
"3639","Abu al-Abbas al-Sayyari and Abu Ahmad al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, saying: Ibrahim bin Hilal told us, Ali bin al-Hasan bin Shaqiq told us, I heard My father says: Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “Whoever says there is no god but God, Then let him say, “Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.” He means the Almighty’s saying: “Call upon Him, sincere in religion for Him. Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds” [Ghafir: 65] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3639 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3640","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told me, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Saeed bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Samh, On the authority of Issa bin Hilal Al-Sadfi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If That a bullet like this and pointed like a skull was sent from heaven to earth, a distance of five hundred miles. A year that would have reached the earth before nightfall, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited {When the shackles were on their necks and the chains were being dragged in the intimate waters} [Ghafir: 72] The verses: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3640 - True"
"3641","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Al-Khidr Al-Shafi’i told me, Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Uqaili told me, Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim told me. Al-Zuhri, my uncle told us, my father told me, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He recited {an Arabic Qur’an for a people who know} [Fussilat: 3]. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Ismail was inspired by this language.” “Inspiration” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3641 - The focus of the hadith is on Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Asili, and he was one of those who stole hadiths."
"3642","Ali bin Al-Hussein, the judge in Bukhara, told me, Abdullah bin Mahmoud bin Shaqiq told us, Abu Tamaila told us, on the authority of Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, {with a clear Arabic tongue} [Al-Shu’ara’: 195] He said: “with the tongue of Jurhum.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and it is not “He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3642 - True"
"3643","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Asqalani told us, Abu Umair Issa bin Muhammad told us, Damrah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Abdullah bin Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, heard a man reciting, and he composed Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Advise your brother.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3643 - True"
"3644","Ishaq bin Saad bin Al-Hasan bin Sufyan Al-Shaybani told us, my grandfather told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, he told me Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Explain “The Qur’an and seek out its strange things.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the doctrine of a group of our imams, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3644 - Rather, there is consensus on its weakness"
"3645","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Bazzaz told me in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Salamah told me, Yazid bin Harun told me, Saeed bin Iyas told me Al-Jariri, on the authority of Hakim bin Muawiyah bin Haidah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “They will come on the day Resurrection, and upon their mouths will be sacrifice, and the first of a human being to speak will be his thigh and his palm.” This is a famous hadith by Bahz ibn Hakim. On the authority of his father, and Al-Jariri followed him, so he narrated it on the authority of Hakim bin Muawiyah, and the hadith was authentic, but they did not narrate it. “And it was narrated by Abu Qaza’ah Al-Bahili also, on the authority of Hakim bin Muawiyah\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3645 - Followed by Bahz bin Hakim on the authority of his father, Sahih"
"3646","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Ashyb told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, he reported Abu Qaza’ah Al-Bahili, on the authority of Hakim bin Muawiyah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You will be gathered there.” Here and he gestured with his hand to the Levant, on foot and on horseback, and on your faces, and you will be presented before God, and on your mouths will be sacrifices, and he will be the first to express On the authority of one of you, his thigh,” and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: “And you did not conceal yourself lest your hearing nor your eyes should bear witness against you.” Nor your skins} [Fussilat: 22]\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3646 - Abu Qaza Suwayd bin Hujair is trustworthy"
"3647","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, and Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, saying: Muhammad bin Kathir Al-Akbari told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salama Ibn Kuhail, on the authority of Malik Ibn Husayn Ibn Uqba Al-Fazari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali Ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, and he was asked about a saying God Almighty: {Our Lord, show us those who led us astray of the jinn and mankind} [Fussilat: 29] He said: “The son of Adam who killed his brother and Iblis.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3647 - True"
"3648","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abdullah bin Idris told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani told us, On the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, he said: What do you say about the saying of God Almighty? And glory be to Him {Indeed, those who said, “Our Lord is God,” then they remained upright} [Fussilat: 30] and the Almighty’s saying: {Those who believed and were not confused} [Al-An’am: 82] Is their belief unjust? So they said: Those who said, “Our Lord is God,” then they remained upright and did not pay attention to His saying: nor did they mix up their faith with wrongdoing with sin. Abu Bakr said: “You carried it in a way that was not intended for it, then they remained upright and did not turn to any god other than Him, and they did not cover their faith with injustice, that is, “With polytheism.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3648 - True"
"3649","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Bakhtari Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Abu Usama told us, Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Suleiman bin Surad, may God be pleased with him, who said: Two men snubbed near the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and one of them became angry, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “I know of a word that, if he had said it, his anger would have gone away from him: I seek refuge in God from the accursed Satan.” Then the man said: Am I crazy? Do you see me? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: “And if some temptation causes you to be moved by Satan, seek refuge in God. Indeed, He is the Hearer, the Knower.” [Fussilat: 36] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3649 - True"
"3650","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Musa bin Ishaq Al-Khutami told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Ibn Fudayl told us, Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that “he used to prostrate with the last two verses of the heart of the prostration, Abu Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Masoud, used to prostrate with the first of them. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3650 - True"
"3651","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mal ibn al-Hasan ibn Issa told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, Abdullah ibn Salih told me, Mu’awiyah ibn Salih told me, On the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Zaid bin Arta’at, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: “Indeed, those who disbelieved in the Reminder when it came to them, and indeed it is a Mighty Book, to which falsehood does not come from before it. And behind it is no revelation from the Wise, the Praiseworthy.} [Fussilat: 42] Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You will never return to God with anything more beloved to Him.” From something that emerged from it,” meaning the Qur’an, “this is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not produce it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3651 - True"
"3652","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Farwa bin Nawfal Al-Ashja’i, said: I was the neighbor of Al-Khabab bin Al-Art, and we once left the mosque, and he took my hand and said: “O here, draw near to God as much as you are able, for you will not draw near to Him with anything more beloved to Him than His words.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and it is not “He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3652 - True"
"3653","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, the Almighty said: {The heavens are almost exploding from above them} He said: “From the heaviness.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3653 - True"
"3654","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Abd al-Samad bin Abdul-Warith told us, Hammam told us, about Qatada, then Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “Between Adam and Noah there were ten generations, all of them following a law of truth, so when They disagreed. God sent the prophets and messengers and sent down His Book, so they were one nation. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3654 - according to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"3655","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam informed us, Ishaq informed us, Hakam ibn Salam al-Razi informed us, and he was trustworthy, Abu Ja`far al-Razi, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Qais ibn Abbad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty saying: {And what was revealed to The two angels in Babylon, Harut and Marut} [Al-Baqarah: 102] the verse. He said: “The people after Adam fell into polytheism. They took these idols and worshiped other than God. He said: Then the angels began to supplicate against them.” And they say: Our Lord, You created Your servants and created them well, and provided for them well, so they disobeyed You and worshiped others. Oh God, Oh God. They called upon them, and the Lord Almighty said to them: “They are in an absence, so make no excuse for them.” So He said: “Choose two from among you that I will bring down to The land, so he commanded them and forbade them. “So they chose Harut and Marut - he said: and he mentioned the hadith in its length about them - and he said in it: when they drank wine And they got high and fell into the woman and killed the soul, so the controversy increased between them and the angels, so they looked at them and what they were doing, and it was about that. {And the angels glorify the praise of their Lord, and seek forgiveness for those on earth} [Al-Shura: 5] the verse was revealed. He said: After that, the angels began to excuse the people of the earth and pray for them, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3655 - True"
"3656","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told me, Ahmad bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told me, Ismail bin Omar Abu Al-Mundhir told us, a lot of news. Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Al-Muttalib Ibn Abdullah Ibn Hantab, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that he was standing in Arafat and looked To the sun when it hung down like a shield for the setting, so he wept, and his weeping became intense, and he recited the words of God Almighty: {It is God who sent down the Book in truth. And the Balance, and what can make you know? Perhaps the Hour is near.} [Al-Shura: 17] To {The Strong, the Mighty} [Hud: 66] Then his servant said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I have stood with you many times and you did not do this. He said: I mentioned the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was standing in this place of mine, and he said: “O people, there is nothing left of this world of yours.” “He passed, except for what remains of this day of yours as it passed.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3656 - Katheer bin Zaid considered it weak by Al-Nasa’i and others reported it."
"3657","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrafi told us, Ahmad bin Ubayd Allah al-Narsi told us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri told us, Imran bin Zaida bin Nashit, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Khaled al-Walbi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited {Whoever is Whoever desires the tillage of the Hereafter, We will increase for him his tillage. And whoever desires the tillage of this world, We will give him thereof, and he has no share in the Hereafter.} [Al-Shura: 20], then The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God Almighty says: Son of Adam, devote yourself to worshiping Me, fill your chest with wealth, and alleviate your poverty, or else “I have filled your chest with work but have not satisfied your poverty.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3657 - True"
"3658","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Saeed bin Sulaiman Al-Wasiti told us, Abu Aqeel Yahya bin Al-Mutawakkil told us, on the authority of Omar bin Muhammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever makes worries one concern, God will suffice him with the worries of his world, and whoever has many worries, God will not care which valleys he is in.” “This world is destroyed.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3658 - True"
"3659","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Shadhan Al-Jawhari told me, Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Ashib told us, Qaza’ah bin Suwayd Al-Bahili told us, Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I do not ask you about anything.” “I have given you clear proofs and guidance to reward you, unless you love God and draw near to Him by obedience to Him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They narrated it, but they agreed in interpreting this verse on the hadith of Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah al-Zarrad, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. “On their authority, they are related to the family of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3659 - True"
"3660","Abu Al-Abbas Ahmad bin Harun Al-Faqih told us, Ali bin Abdul-Aziz told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Hushaym told us, Dawud told us, about Al-Sha’bi, he said: Most of the people are against us in this verse {Say: I do not ask you for any reward for it except love for my kin} [Al-Shura: 23], so we wrote To Ibn Abbas, we asked him about this. Ibn Abbas wrote: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “was the most modest family among the Quraysh, not a family of people.” Their bellies, except that He gave birth to Him.” Then God Almighty said: “Say, ‘I do not ask you for any reward for it.’” [Al-An’am: 90] “Unless you invite me to what I invite you to do.” Because of my kinship with you and you protect me by it, Hushaym said: Husayn told me on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, something like: That. “This is a hadith, and they did not narrate it with this addition, and it is authentic according to their condition.” The hadith of Ikrimah is authentic according to the condition of Al-Bukhari and the hadith. Dawud bin Abi Hind is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim.”"
"3661","Ali bin Issa Al-Hiri told me, Musaddad bin Qattan told me, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told me, Jarir told us, and Abdullah bin Idris told me, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq ibn Salamah, on the authority of Salamah ibn Sabra, said: Muadh ibn Jabal, may God be pleased with him, addressed us and said: “You are the believers and you are the people of Paradise, by God, I hope that most of the people you afflict with Persia and the Romans will be in Paradise, for one of them does good and says: Well done. May God bless you. You have done well, may God have mercy on you. And God says: {And He responds to those who believe and do righteous deeds, and He increases them of His bounty} [Al-Shura: 26] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3661 - True"
"3662","Abu Al-Hussein Ahmad bin Uthman bin Yahya Al-Muqri informed us, in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba Al-Raqashi told us, Abd Al-Samad bin Abd told us. The heir, Hisham bin Abi Abdullah told us, Qatada told us, and he recited, the saying of God Almighty: “And if God had extended the provision to His servants, they would have transgressed in Earth, but He sends down in proportion as He wills.} [Al-Shura: 27] He said: Khalid bin Abdullah Al-Asri narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace: “The sun never rose unless two angels were sent at its sides. Indeed, the people of the earth can hear it, except the heavy ones: O people, Come to your Lord, for what is little and sufficient is better than what is many and distracts. And the sun never sets without two angels beside it calling out, O God He hastened succession for a spender and hastened loss for one who held it. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3662 - True"
"3663","Abdullah bin Saad Al-Hafiz narrated to me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib narrated to me, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sukhbra, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: “No one spent the morning in Kufa except a gentle person. Indeed, the lowest of them in status drinks from the water of the Euphrates, and he sits in the shade, and eats from the land, and this verse was only revealed about the people of description {And if God had extended the provision for His servants They have transgressed in the land, but He sends down in proportion as He wills.} [Al-Shura: 27] That is because they said: “If only it were Ours, then they would wish for the world.” This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3663 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3664","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Faqih Bal-Ray told me, Muhammad bin Al-Faraj told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, Yunus bin Abi told us Ishaq, Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abu Juhayfah, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever commits a sin in This world, and he is punished with it, then God is more just than to extend His punishment to His servant. And whoever commits a sin, God will cover him and pardon him, then God will He is more honorable than to go back on something that he has forgiven.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “Rather, it was narrated by Ishaq bin Ibrahim.” When God Almighty says: “And whatever calamity befalls you, it is because of what your hands have earned” [Al-Shura: 30]\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3664 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3665","Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Faqih told me in Bukhara, Saleh ibn Muhammad ibn Habib al-Hafiz told me, Ya’qub ibn Ibrahim, and Ahmad ibn Mani’ told us, And Ziyad bin Ayyub, they said: Hushaym told us, Mansour bin Zazan reported, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may God be pleased with him, he said: He entered Some of his companions were against him, and he was afflicted in his body, and some of them said to him: We truly deplore what happened to you. He said: Do not despair at what you see, for it was revealed because of a sin, and God does not pardon him more. He said: “Then Imran recited this verse {and what Whatever calamity befalls you, then it is because of what your hands have earned, and He pardons much.” [Al-Shura: 30] until the end of the verse: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3665 - True"
"3666","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, he said: We were displaying the Qur’an with Alqamah, and he recited this verse: “Indeed, in that are signs for those who are certain.” He said: Abdullah said: Certainty is faith. All of it, and he recited this verse: {Indeed, in that are signs for every patient and grateful person} [Ibrahim: 5]. He said: Then Abdullah said: “Patience is half of faith.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3666 - True"
"3667","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, Issa bin Ubaid told us, On the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, he said: Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, narrated to me, saying: “It was the day of Uhud that one of the Ansar was injured.” Sixty-four, and six of them, including Hamza. They were mutilated, and the Ansar said: If only we were to suffer from them a day like this. We will surely raise a burden upon them. Then when the day of the conquest of Mecca came, God revealed {And if you punish, then recompense with the same as that with which you were punished, and if you are patient - it is a delusion. It is better for those who are patient.} [An-Nahl: 126] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”"
"3668","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Yahya bin Fudayl told us, Al-Hasan bin Saleh bin Saleh told us Bin Hayy, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, {And indeed, you guide to a straight path} [Al-Shura: 52] He said: “The straight path is Islam, and it is the widest distance between the heavens and the earth.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3668 - True"
"3669","Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah May God be pleased with him, in His Almighty’s saying {And indeed, you guide to a straight path} [Al-Shura: 52] He said: “The Book of God.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3669 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3670","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us a dictation in Shawwal of the year four hundred. Abu Awn Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Khazzaz in Mecca, Muhammad bin Ali bin Zaid told us, Sa’id bin Mansour told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr. He said: I said to Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both: And they made the angels who are servants of the Most Gracious or servants of the Most Merciful? He said: Servants of the Most Gracious. I said: It is in the Mushaf of Abd al-Rahman that he said: “Then erase it and write, ‘Servants of the Most Gracious.’” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3670 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3671","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Wahhab told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, Ibn Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Sabah bin Muhammad, On the authority of once, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, {Do they divide the mercy of your Lord? We have divided it among them} [Al-Zukhruf: 32] The verse, so Abdul said God: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, God has divided among you your morals just as He has divided among you your livelihood, and God will give This world belongs to the one who loves and the one who does not love, and does not give the debt except to the one he loves. So whoever gives him the religion has loved it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. “He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3671 - True"
"3672","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Hasab told us, Muhammad bin Thawr told us, about Muammar, on the authority of Qatada, in the Almighty’s saying: {Then whether we take you away, for indeed we will take revenge on them} [Al-Zukhruf: 41] Then he said: Anas said: “The Messenger of God went God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the vengeance remained, and God did not see in his Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, anything that he hated in his nation until he passed away, and there was no prophet. Except he saw the punishment in his nation, except your Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” Authentic chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3672 - True"
"3673","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told me, Musaddad bin Qattan told me, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, Sufyan told us, Al-Mughirah bin Al-Numan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “People of My companions are in the north, so I say: My companions are my companions. It will be said: Indeed, they did not cease to be apostates after you, so I say as the righteous servant Jesus, son of Mary, said: {And I was a witness over them. I lived among them, but when you took me to death, you were the watcher over them.” [Al-Maeda: 117] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3673 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3674","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl informed us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Farra’ informed us, Ja’far bin Aoun informed us, Al-Hajjaj bin Dinar informed us, On the authority of Abu Ghalib, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No people go astray after guidance unless they are given controversy.” Then The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, read: “They did not strike it for you except out of argument. Rather, they are an adversarial people” [Al-Zukhruf: 58] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it has not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3674 - True"
"3675","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fudayl told us, Muhammad bin Sabiq told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying {And indeed it is knowledge of the Hour} [Al-Zukhruf: 61] He said: “The emergence of Jesus, son of “Maryam” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3675 - True"
"3676","Abu Al-Qasim Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Sakouni told us in Kufa, Ubaid bin Kathir Al-Amiri told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Darimi told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Darimi told us, Abd al-Razzaq, Ibn Uyaynah reported, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Suqa, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him {And indeed it is knowledge of the Hour} [Al-Zukhruf: 61] He said: “The stars are a security for the inhabitants of the heavens, so when they go, what they are promised comes to them, and I It is security for my companions as long as I am, so when I go, they will receive what they are promised, and my family is safety for my nation, so when my household goes, they will receive what they are promised. They were promised.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not take it out.\n [Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3676 - I think it is fabricated"
"3677","Abu Al-Hussein Ali bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Subaie told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hakam Al-Hiri told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {And they called, O Master, to destroy us. Your Lord} [Al-Zukhruf: 77] He said: “He stayed with them for a thousand years, then He said: ‘Indeed, you will remain.’ This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3677 - True"
"3678","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Qabbani told me, Abu Uthman Saeed bin Yahya bin Saeed Al-Umawi told us, My father told me, Othman bin Hakim told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “You see a man walking in"
"3679","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {Then the heaven and the earth did not weep over them} [Al-Dukhan: 29] He said: “With “The believer for forty mornings.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3679 - True"
"3680","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris told us, Muhammad bin Yazid bin Sinan Al-Rahawi told us, my grandfather Sinan told me Ibn Yazid said: We went out with Ali when he went to Muawiyah, and Jarir Ibn Sahm Al-Taymi was in front of him, saying:\n [The sea of rage]\n O my horse, walk, and my mother is the shama... and cut the awls and flags.\n And fight me whoever disagrees with the Imam... because I hope that if we meet the general\n Gathering the Banu Umayyad al-Taghama... to kill al-Qadi and al-Hammam.\n And to remove from important men\n He said: When we reached Al-Mada'in, Jarir said:\n [full sea]\n The winds blew over the outlines of their homes... it was as if they had been on time.\n He said: Then Ali said to me: How did you say, brother of Banu Tamim? He said: The verse was returned to him, and Ali said: Didn’t you say: “How many gardens and springs and crops and noble positions and blessings they have left behind, in which they were of great benefit.” And We made it an inheritance to other people} [Al-Dukhan: 26]. Then he said: Oh, my brother, these were heirs, so they became heirs. Indeed, these disbelieved in the blessings, so they were lawful. They have vengeance. Then he said: “Beware of denying blessings, lest vengeance befall you.” Abu Hatim said: I said to Muhammad bin Yazid bin Sinan: Your grandfather Sinan was old in age."
"3681","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told me, Abu Amr Ahmad bin Al-Mubarak told me, Muhammad bin Rafi’ Al-Qushayri told me, Abd Al-Razzaq told me, Muammar reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she said: “He was followed by a righteous man. Do you not see that God Did God Almighty criticize his people but not him? This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3681 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3682","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us, in Hamadan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I do not know whether I follow whether he is cursed or not, and I do not know “Whether Al-Qarnayn was a prophet or not, and I do not know whether the punishments are expiation for those who fulfill them or not?” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3682 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3683","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Al-Qasim bin Sulaiman Al-Dahli told us, Al-Hasan bin Ismail bin Subaih Al-Yashkari told us, my father told me, Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the words of God Almighty: {And We did not create the heavens and the earth. And there is no play between them.} Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: How long were the heavens and the earth created? He said: “God created the first day of Sunday, and the earth was created on Sunday, and on Monday, and mountains were created and rivers were divided. And he planted the fruits in the earth, and his strength was estimated in every land on Tuesday and Wednesday. Then he rose up to the sky while it was smoke, and said to it: And for the earth: {They come, willingly or by compulsion. They said, We come willingly.} [Fussilat: 11] So He caused them to decree seven heavens in two days, and revealed in every heaven His commandment in On Thursday and Friday, and the last creation was in the last hours on Friday, but when it was Saturday there was no creation on it, so she said The Jews said about it, so God Almighty revealed their denial: {And We created the heavens and the earth and what is between them in six days, and We did not touch them. From Laghub} “This is a hadith sent by Abd al-Razzaq, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, and he did not mention Ibn Abbas in it, and we wrote it connected from This narration, and God knows best.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3683 - Narrated by Abd al-Razzaq, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, in a mursal form. Ibn Abbas was not mentioned."
"3684","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, On the authority of Hammam ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, he said: A man recited to him {Indeed, the tree of Zaqqum is the food of the sinful} [Al-Dukhan: 44] and he said Abu Al-Darda’: “Say the food of the sinful.” The man said: “The food of the sinful.” Abu Al-Darda’ said, “Say: ‘The food of the ungodly.’ This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3684 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3685","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, Safwan bin Issa told us, Ibn Ajlan told us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who narrated it, saying: “Indeed, God has three garments: He who girds himself with pride, who shrouds mercy, and who wears Pride, so whoever is strengthened by something other than what God has strengthened, that is the one to whom it will be said: {Taste that indeed You are the Mighty, the Most Generous} [Al-Dukhan: 49] and He who is merciful to people. By the mercy of God, he is the one who puts on his garment that is appropriate for him, and whoever takes off from God his cloak that is appropriate for him, God says: No. It is necessary for whoever disputes with me to admit him to Paradise “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3685 - True"
"3686","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, and Abu Dawud said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, read this verse {Fear God, truly Fear it, and do not die except as you have submitted.} [Al Imran: 102] And by the One in Whose Hand is Muhammad’s soul, if even a drop of Zaqqum were dropped on the earth. It has ruined the livelihood of the people of the world, so what about whose food it is? “This is a hadith narrated by Imam Abu Ya’qub al-Handali in explaining his saying: ‘Take him and take him to the level of hell, then pour His head is from the torment of the burning.} [Al-Dukhan: 48] “And it is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"3687","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, on the authority of Omar bin Habib Al-Makki, on the authority of Humayd ibn Qays al-Araj, on the authority of Tawus, who said: A man came to Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-Aas, asking him: What created creation? He said: “From water, light, darkness, wind, and dust?” The man said: What are these people created for? He said: “I don’t know.” Then the man came to Abdullah bin Al-Zubair and asked him, and he said the same as Abdullah bin Amr said. He said: Then the man came to Abdullah Ibn Abbas asked him and he said: What was creation created from? He said: “From water, light, darkness, wind, and dust.” The man said: What are these people created for? Then Abdullah bin Abbas recited: {And He has subjected to you all that is in the heavens and all that is in the earth, all of it} Then the man said: No one would have had this for us except a man from The family of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3687 - The news is objectionable"
"3688","Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Hibban al-Qadi told us, Abu Khalifa al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Salam al-Jumahi told us, he said: I heard Abu Amer al-Aqdi, He says: I heard Sufyan Al-Thawri, and he recited the words of God Almighty: “Or do those who committed evil deeds suffice that We should make them like those who believed and did evil deeds?” Good deeds - whether they live or die - evil is what they judge.} [Al-Jathiya: 21], Then he said: I heard Al-Amash narrating, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Every servant will be resurrected as he died.” Abu told us Abdullah Al-Saffar, Ahmed bin Mahran told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, and he mentioned it. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3688 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3689","Sheikh Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq told us, Ahmad ibn Bishr al-Murthadi informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani’ told us, Abu Yusuf al-Qadi Ya’qub ibn Ibrahim, Mutarrif narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Iyas, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The man was an Arab.” He worships a stone, so when he finds something better than it, he takes it and throws the other. Then God Almighty revealed {Have you seen him who takes his own desires as his god?} [Al-Jathiya: 23] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3689 - True"
"3690","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Ibn Uyaynah told us, he said: The people of pre-Islamic times used to say: It is time that destroys us, it is the one that causes us to die and gives us life. So God responded to their saying, Al-Zuhri said, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “God Almighty says: The son of Adam curses me by cursing eternity, while I am the eternity who disturbs his night.” And its day, so if you wish, you can take them.” Sufyan recited this verse: “It is nothing but our worldly life. We die and we live, and none destroys us except Al-Dhahr} [Al-Jathiya: 24] The two sheikhs agreed to narrate the hadith of Al-Zuhri: “This is without this context, and it is authentic according to their conditions.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3690 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, and they narrated it in this context"
"3691","Abu Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahboubi informed us, Sa`id ibn Masoud informed us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, On the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God Almighty said: I borrowed from my servant, but he refused to lend to me, and my servant cursed me, not knowing, saying: “By eternity, by eternity, and I am eternity.” This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of a Muslim, and they did not take it out in this context.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3691 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3692","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Abd al-Hamid al-San’ani informed me of Mecca. Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told us, Abd told us Al-Razzaq, Muammar reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “God Almighty said: The son of Adam will hurt me by saying: O disappointment of time. So let none of you say, O disappointment of age, for I am time. His night and his day, so if you wish, I can take them. “This is an authentic hadith according to their condition, and they did not narrate it like this.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3692 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3693","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Al-Sa'ib, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The first thing that God created the pen, He created it from the spelling before the alif and the lam. So he imagined a pen of light, and it was said to him: “A reward in the preserved tablet.” He said: O Lord, with what? He said: What will happen until the Day of Resurrection. When God created creation, He assigned guardians to creation to preserve their deeds. When the Resurrection came, Their deeds were presented to them, and it was said: “This is Our Book speaking to you with the truth. Indeed, We were abrogating what you used to do.” [Al-Jathiya: 29] with the two books, so they are alike.” Ibn Abbas said: Are you not Arabs? Is the copy only from a book? “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3693 - True"
"3694","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Al-Ash’ath Al-Sijistani told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us Al-Abdi, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in his saying God Almighty {or traces of knowledge} [Al-Ahqaf: 4] He said: “It is the calligraphy.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it, and it was transmitted on the authority of “The revolutionary from an unsupported point of view.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3694 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3695","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Muzaki told us, truly and not as usual, Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Hammam bin Abi Badr, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, Abu Uthman Amr bin Al-Azhar Al-Basri told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty’s words {or traces of knowledge} [Al-Ahqaf: 4] He said: “The quality of the handwriting.” This is more than Ibn Abbas said, “There is something strange in this hadith.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3695 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3696","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Nasr al-Darabardi and Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Halimi informed us of the passing of the Prophet, saying: Abu al-Mawjih reported, Abdan reported, Abdullah reported, Muammar reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Kharijah bin Zayd bin Thabit, on the authority of Umm Al-Ala Al-Ansariyya, may God be pleased with her, who had pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Othman bin Mad’un flew for us to live when The Ansar cast lots for the immigrants’ housing. She said: Then he complained, so we nursed him until he died until we put him in his clothes. She said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered. May God bless him and grant him peace. So I said: May God have mercy on you, Abu Al-Sa’ib. My testimony is that God has honored you. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “And what makes you know?” She said: I do not know, by God, O Messenger of God. He said: “As for him, certainty has come to him, and I hope for the best from God for him.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited {Say: I was not an innovation from Messengers, and I do not know what will be done to me or to you.} [Al-Ahqaf: 9] Umm Al-Ala said: By God, I will never purify anyone after him. Umm Al-Alaa said: I saw that Uthman had an eye running through his sleep in his sleep, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I mentioned that, and he said: “That was his action.” “This is a hadith. The two sheikhs differed regarding its narration. Al-Bukhari narrated it, on the authority of Abadan, in brief, and no Muslim narrated it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3696 - It was presented in Al-Bukhari in brief"
"3697","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Bishr bin Musa told me, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, Safwan bin Abdullah bin Safwan says: Saad asked permission to come to Ibn Amir, and underneath him were a silk veil, so he ordered it to be taken, and it was lifted, and he entered upon him, wearing a cloak. He was ashamed and said to him: You asked for permission to come over me while I was wearing silk shawls. I ordered them to be removed and he said to him: “What an excellent man you are, O Ibn Amir, if you are not... Among those whom God Almighty said: “Have you taken away the good things you did in your worldly life?” [Al-Ahqaf: 20] By God, if I lay down on the coals of anger, I would love to “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” The hadith of Omar ibn al-Khattab witnessed it from the narration Al-Qasim bin Abdullah Al-Omari\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3697 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3698","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Abdullah bin Al-Jarrah told us, Al-Qasim bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that Omar, may God be pleased with him, saw a dirham in the hand of Jabir bin Abdullah, and he said: “What is this? The dirham? He said: I want to buy meat for my family with a dirham. They threw it to him, and Omar said: “You have bought whatever you desired. None of you wants to fill his stomach for his cousin, and his female slave should go.” This verse is about you: “You took away the good things you did in your worldly life and enjoyed them” [Al-Ahqaf: 20]\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3698 - Al-Qasim Wah"
"3699","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Muadh bin Najdah Al-Qurashi told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “God has not sent upon a wind except the size of this my seal.” Sahih The chain of transmission is based on the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. “Muslim was the only one to narrate it, the hadith of Masoud bin Malik on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “I was victorious through youth.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3699 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3700","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me that Abu Al-Nadr told him On the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that she said: “I never saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. مُسْتَجْمِعًا ضَاحِكًا حَتَّى أَرَى مِنْهُ لَهَوَاتِهِ إِنَّمَا كَانَ يَبْتَسمُ» . She said: And whenever he saw clouds or winds, he would recognize his face, so I said: O Messenger of God, when people see clouds they rejoice that there is rain in them. And he saw that when you saw him, he recognized the hatred on your face. He said: “O Aisha, what gives me peace of mind that there will be a torment in it. Some people have been tormented with wind, and He brought a people with torment,” and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: “And when they saw him crossing their valleys, they said: This is a rain-stormer for us.” [Al-Ahqaf: 24] The verse: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3700 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3701","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdan Al-Ahwazi told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “They descended on the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was reciting the Qur’an under the top of a palm tree, and when they heard him, they said: Listen. They said: Shh. And they were nine, one of them a whirlwind, so God Almighty revealed {And when We turned to you a group of the jinn listening to the Qur’an. Then when they attended it, they said: Listen.} [Al-Ahqaf: 29] The verse refers to {clear error} [Al-Imran: 164] “The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not produce it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3701 - True"
"3702","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told me, Othman bin Saeed told me, Abdullah bin Salih told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Abu Thalabah Al-Khushani, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The jinn are of three types. They have wings and fly in the air, and a variety of snakes and dogs, and a variety that they loose and spread.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3702 - True"
"3703","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, he informed us Israel, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty saying: {Those who disbelieve and turn away from the path of God has misled their deeds. [Muhammad: 1] He said: “Among them are the people of Mecca.” He said: {And set their affairs right} [Muhammad: 2] He said: “He commanded them.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3703 - True"
"3704","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed us, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, Safwan bin informed us. Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Bishr, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in the Almighty’s saying {And it shall be given to drink from He swallows purulent water.} [Ibrahim: 17] He said: “He brings it near to him and he hates it. When he is brought near to him, his face is scalded and his scalp is bruised. When he drinks it, it cuts his intestines until it comes out of his anus. God Almighty says: {And they were given hot water to drink, so it cut their intestines} [Muhammad: 15]. God Almighty says: God Almighty: {And if they call for help, they will be helped with water like clay that scalds the faces. What an evil drink} [Al-Kahf: 29] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”"
"3705","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, a partner told us, about Othman Abi Al-Yaqzan, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, in His Almighty saying: {Until when they depart from With you, they said to those who were given knowledge, “What did he say above?” [Muhammad: 16] He said: “I was among those who were asked.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3705 - True"
"3706","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid ibn Ibrahim al-Hafiz in Hamadan told us, Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah al-Sukari told us, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Mughirah, said: I heard Hudhayfah, and he recited the words of God Almighty, “So know that there is no god Except Allah, and ask forgiveness for your sin.} [Muhammad: 19] He said: I was a man who hurled his tongue against my family, so I said: O Messenger of God, I am afraid that he will let me in. My tongue is fire. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “So where are you regarding seeking forgiveness? Indeed, I seek forgiveness from God a hundred times a day.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out like this.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3706 - True"
"3707","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abu Usama told us, Hussein bin Dhakwan told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Bashir bin Ka’b, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ The master of seeking forgiveness is for the servant to say: Oh God, you are my Lord, there is no god but You, you created me, and I am your servant, and I abide by your covenant and promise. I am able, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done, I acknowledge my sins to You, and I acknowledge Your grace upon me, so forgive me, for He does not forgive sins except You: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3707 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3708","Abdullah bin Ja’far bin Darastuwaih Al-Farisi told us, Ya’qub bin Sufyan Al-Farisi told us, Yahya bin Ya’la bin Al-Harith told us, Ubayy told us, Ghaylan bin Jami’ told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Harb, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: I was sitting with Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, when he heard a woman screaming and said: “O Yarfa, see what this sound is?” So he went off and looked, then he came and said: A Quraysh slave girl whose mother is being sold, he said: Then Omar said: “Pray for me, or he said: Ali, for the Muhajireen and the Ansar.” He said: He did not stay for more than an hour until the house and the room were filled. He said: “So Omar thanked God and praised him, then he said: “As for what follows? Do you know that one of the things that Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, brought was estrangement? They said: No. He said: “For it has become widespread among you. Then he recited {So has It is possible that if you were given power, you would spread corruption in the land and sever your ties of kinship.} [Muhammad: 22], Then he said: What severing of ties is more severe than the sale of a man’s mother? Among you, and God has made ample room for you? “They said: So do whatever you want.” He said: “It was written in the horizons that the mother of a free man should not be sold, for she is a herd, and it is not permissible.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3708 - True"
"3709","Ja`far bin Muhammad al-Khalidi told us, Muhammad bin Ali bin Zaid al-Sayegh told us, Sa`id bin Mansour told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, Al-Alaa bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: When it was revealed: {And if you turn away, He will replace you with a people other than you} [Muhammad: 38] They said: O Messenger of God, who are these people who, when we turn away, will be replaced by us? And Salman was next to him, and he said: “They are this horse and his people.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3709 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3710","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told me, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, my father told me, Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, and Marwan ibn Al-Hakam, who said: “Surat Al-Fath was revealed in the midst of Mecca. “And Medina in the area of Al-Hudaybiyyah from its beginning to its end.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3710 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3711","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi and al-Abbas bin al-Fadl al-Asfati told us, they said: Thana Ismail bin Abi Uwais, Mujja’ bin Yaqoub told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Muja’ bin Jariyah, may God be pleased with him, saying: Accept us with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Hudaybiyyah until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reached the clouds, and then the people were drawing towards the Messenger of God. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and some people said to others: What do the people have? They said: It was revealed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then some of the people said: So we moved until we found the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, standing at the edge of the clouds. When the people gathered around him, he recited to them. {Indeed, We have opened for you a clear conquest} [Al-Fath: 1] Then some people said: Or is it a conquest? He said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it is a conquest.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3711 - Muslim did not narrate anything to a scholar or to his father, and they are both trustworthy."
"3712","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Ali bin al-Madini told us, Harami bin Amara bin Abu Hafsa, narrated by Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying: “{Indeed, We have granted you a conquest.” Making it clear} [Al-Fath: 1] “He said: The Conquest of Khaybar {so that God may forgive you for your previous sins and those that will follow} [Al-Fath: 2] So they said: O Messenger of God, congratulations to you So what do we have? Then God Almighty revealed: “{That He may admit the believing men and believing women to Gardens beneath which rivers flow} [Al-Fath: 5] “This is an authentic hadith according to The condition of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.” Rather, Muslim narrated it on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of Muhammad bin Shu’bah with his chain of transmission {Indeed We have opened for you a clear conquest} [Al-Fath: 1] He said: The conquest of Khaybar. This alone, and Al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated this hadith in a way that he mentioned Hunayn and told all of them.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3712 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, and Muslim narrated the beginning"
"3713","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib and Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, they said: Al-Hasan bin Bishr bin Salem told us, Al-Hakam told us. Ibn Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, he said: When we returned from Hudaybiyyah and the companions of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, They were mixed with sadness and depression as they slaughtered their sacrifice in their places, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A verse was revealed to me. She is dearer to me than the whole world, three times.” We said: What are they, O Messenger of God? He said: “So he recited {Indeed, We have given you a clear conquest, that God may forgive you your previous sins and those that will follow, and complete His blessings upon you, and guide you.” A straight path} [Al-Fath: 2] until the end of the two verses. We said: Congratulations to you, O Messenger of God, so what do we have? “So he recited {that He may admit the believing men and believing women into Gardens beneath which rivers flow to abide therein, and to remit from them their evil deeds, and it was This is with God a great victory.} [Al-Fath: 5] Then when we came to Khaybar, they saw the Khamis of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, meaning his army, they turned away, fleeing. To the fort, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Khaybar has been destroyed. When we camped in a people’s square, the morning of those who had been warned would be bad.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3713 - Al-Hakam bin Malik is weak. He cited it as a martyr’s citation"
"3714","Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him: {It is He who sent down tranquility into the hearts of the believers} [Al-Fath: 4] He said: “Tranquility has a face like the face of man, and then it is “After a strong wind.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3714 - True"
"3715","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Baqiya bin Al-Walid told me, Mubashir bin Ubaid told me, On the authority of Al-Hajjaj ibn Artaat, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both: What is the Almighty’s saying: {And you should excuse him} [Al-Fath: 9]? He said: “Striking in the hands of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a sword.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3715 - Ahmad Mubashir bin Ubaid said he used to fabricate hadith"
"3716","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari and Abu Ahmad Al-Sayrafi told us about Marw, saying: Ibrahim bin Hilal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid told me, Thabit Al-Bunani told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal Al-Muzani, may God be pleased with him, he said: We were with the Messenger of God May God bless him and grant him peace, in Al-Hudaybiyyah, at the root of the tree that God Almighty said in the Qur’an, and there was a branch from the branches of that tree on the back of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I lifted him off his back, while Ali bin Abi Talib and Suhail bin Amr were sitting in front of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Ali: “Write.” So he mentioned lines from the hadith extracted in the two books from the narration of Suhail bin Amr Abdullah bin Mughaffal said: While we were like that, thirty young men armed with weapons came out against us, and they revolted against us, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, supplicated against them. May God bless him and grant him peace. So God took their sight, so we stood up to them and took them. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: “Have you come to Is anyone’s covenant, or has anyone given you security? They said: Oh God, no. So he cleared their way, so God Almighty revealed {And it is He who withheld their hands from you, and your hands from them, in the interior of Mecca after I will give you victory over them, and God is ever Seeing of what you do.} [Al-Fath: 24] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, as it is not far from hearing a hadith from Abdullah bin Mughaffal” and they agreed to narrate the hadith of Muawiyah bin Qurrah on the hadith of Humayd bin Hilal on the authority of him and Thabit, who is older than both of them."
"3717","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, On the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abaya bin Rabi’i, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying: {And oblige them to the word of piety} [Al-Fath: 26] He said: “There is no god but God and God is great.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3717 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3718","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Khaythamah, He said: A man recited Surah Al-Fath to Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, and when he reached it {like a crop that put out its shoots, so he strengthened him and became strong, so he became Its stems astonish the farmers, in order to anger the disbelievers with them.} [Al-Fath: 29] He said: “In order to anger God with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with his disbelieving companions.” He said: Then he said: Abdullah: “You are the seed and your harvest is approaching” is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3718 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3719","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq al-Faqih told us, Musa bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Usama and Waki` told us, On the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, {so that the disbelievers may be enraged by them} [Al-Fath: 29] She said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, “They were commanded to ask forgiveness for them, but they took them captive.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3719 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3720","Ali bin Abdullah Al-Hakimi told us in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad bin Hatim Al-Duri told us, Saeed bin Amir told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “When {Indeed, those who lower their voices in the presence of the Messenger of God} [Al-Hujurat: 3] was revealed, may God bless Peace and blessings of God be upon him. Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, said, “By the One who sent down the Book to you, O Messenger of God, I will not speak to you except as a secret brother until God Almighty gave this “an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3720 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3721","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Sulayman bin Abdul Rahman Al-Dimashqi told me, Sulayman bin Utba told me, he said: I heard Yunus bin Maysarah bin Halbas speaking, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, was asked and said: O Messenger of God, do you think what we are doing is something that has already been completed or something we can resume? He said: “Every person is prepared for what he was created for.” Then Yunus bin Maysarah went to Saeed bin Abdul Aziz and said to him: Believing this The hadith is in the Book of God Almighty. Saeed said to him: “And where are you, Ibn Halbas?” He said: Do you not hear God say in His Book {And know that among you is the Messenger of God. If he had obeyed you in many matters, you would have been cursed, but God loves To you is faith and has beautified it in your hearts, and has made disbelief and immorality and disobedience amiss for you. Those are the rightly guided, a bounty from God and a blessing.} [Al-Hujurat: 8] Have you seen, O Saeed, if these people were neglected as the wicked say: Wherever they go, where they are loved and made good for them, or where Did he hate them and hate them? “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3721 - Rather, Ibn Ma’in said nothing about Suleiman bin Utbah"
"3722","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmad bin Mahdi told us, Bishr bin Shuaib bin Abi Hamza told us, he told me My father, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Hamza bin Abdullah bin Omar told me that while he was sitting with Abdullah bin Omar, a man from The people of Iraq, and he said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, by God, I have set out to imitate your character and follow your example in the matter of disuniting people. I shun evil as much as I can, and I read a decisive verse from the Book of God that has taken my heart, so tell me about it. Have you seen what God Almighty says? And the Almighty: {And if two parties of believers fight, and make peace between them, then if one of them transgresses against the other, then fight the one it rebels until it repays. To the command of God, but if it is fulfilled, then make peace between them with justice and be just. Indeed, God loves those who are just.} [Al-Hujurat: 9] Tell me about this. The verse. Abdullah bin Omar said: “What is the matter with you? That is why you left me.” So the man got up and set off until when we had disappeared, Abdullah bin Omar came to us and said: “I did not find it within myself to do anything about this matter.” The verse, “except when I found in myself that I did not fight this transgressing group as God Almighty commanded me.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3722 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3723","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Abu Mawdud informed, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: “And do not blame yourselves” [Al-Hujurat: 11] He said: “He should not be stabbed.” “One of you over the other.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3723 - True"
"3724","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Dawud bin Abu Hind, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abu Jubayrah ibn Al-Dahhak, in this verse: {And do not exchange nicknames} [Al-Hujurat: 11] He said: “The nicknames in Pre-Islamic times, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called a man from among them by his surname, and he was told: O Messenger of God, he hates him, so God Almighty revealed {And do not call one another by nicknames} [Al-Hujurat: 11] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3724 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3725","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Wahhab Al-Farra told us, Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Makhzoumi told us, in Medina, Umm Salamah bint Al-Alaa bin Abdul-Rahman bin Yaqoub told me, on the authority of her father, on the authority of her grandfather, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Indeed, God Almighty will say on the Day of Resurrection: I commanded you and you neglected what I entrusted you with it, and I exalted your lineage.” Today I exalt my lineage and put your lineages in low place. Where are the pious? Where are the pious? Indeed, the most honorable of you in the sight of God is the most pious of you. “This is a loud hadith with a strange chain of narration. And the text, but they did not narrate it.” And there is evidence for it from the hadith of Talha bin Amr, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3725 - Al-Makhzoumi is a fallen son of rubbish"
"3726","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ahmad Al-Hafid told us, Ahmed bin Nasr told us, Abu Ghassan Al-Nahdi told us, Talha bin Amr told us, On the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that he recited the words of God Almighty: “Indeed, the most honorable of you in the sight of God is the most pious of you.” [Al-Hujurat: 13] Then he said: “Indeed, God will say on the Day of Resurrection: O people, I have made a lineage and you have made a lineage, so I have made the most noble of you the most pious of you.” And you refused except to say that so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, is more honorable than so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, and today I exalt my lineage and put your lineage in low standing, where are the pious? “The righteous.” Talha said: Then Ata’ said to me: O Talha, how many names will be on the Day of Resurrection after my name and yours. When he is called upon, no one will stand up except Who was cursed?\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3726 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3727","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Salih bin Hayyan, on the authority of Abd Allah Ibn Buraydah, in the words of God Almighty: {Q and the Glorious Qur’an} [Q: 1] He said: “A mountain of emeralds surrounding the world, with the covering of the sky upon it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3727 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3728","Ibrahim bin Mudarib told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told me, Hashim bin Al-Qasim told me, Al-Masoudi told me, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, on the authority of his uncle Qutba Ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “reciting in the morning prayer,” so when he came to this verse {and the palm trees With large stems that have a fresh crop} [Q: 10] Qutubah said: So I started to say to him: What is with its stems? He said: Its length. “Muslim narrated this hadith. Other than this context, he did not mention the interpretation of basuq in it, and it is correct according to his condition.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3728 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3729","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Attab Al-Abdi told us in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Malaab bin Hayyan told us, Khaled bin Mukhlid told us Al-Qatwani, Musa bin Yaqoub told us, on the authority of his uncle Al-Harith bin Abdullah bin Abi Rabi’ah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, She said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Ma’ad bin Adnan bin Adad bin Zand bin Bari bin Araq Al-Thara.” She said: Then he recited The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He destroyed Ad, Thamud, and the Companions of the Land, and many centuries in between, and no one knows them except God,” Umm said. Salamah: And the descendants of the rich are Ismail bin Ibrahim, Zand: Ibn Hamisa’, and Bari: Nabat: “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3729 - True"
"3730","Abu Abdul Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Tajer told me, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he was asked about this verse: “He does not utter a word but there is a watcher by him.” Atid} [Q: 18] He said: Then Ibn Abbas said: “Indeed, good and evil are only recorded. O boy, saddle the horse, and O boy, give me water to drink. “He writes good and evil.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3730 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3731","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Muhammad bin Nu’aym told me, Qutaibah told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Hadi, On the authority of Musa bin Sarjis, he said: I heard Al-Qasim bin Muhammad narrating, and he recited the words of God Almighty: {And the agony of death came in truth. That is what You were deviating from him} [Q: 19] Then he said: Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, may God be pleased with her, told me: I saw the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He was greeted while he was dying, and he had a cup of water in it, and he put his hand into the cup, then wiped his face with water, and then said: “O God, help me.” “On death throes.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3731 - True"
"3732","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl and Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Darabardi told us, saying: Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Surayj bin Al-Numan told us. Al-Jawhari, Abdullah bin Nafi’ told us, on the authority of Asim bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Salem, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will be the first for whom the earth will open, then Abu Bakr, then Omar, then I will come to the people of Al-Baqi’. They will be gathered with me, then I will wait for the people of Mecca.” Abdullah bin Omar recited: “On the day the earth will split open before them, that will be a gathering upon us.” “This is a simple hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3732 - Abdullah bin Nafi’ is weak"
"3733","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Qurashi told us, with nonsense, Saeed bin Mansour Al-Makki told us, Abbad bin Al-Awwam, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, greeted a man whose horses were trembling. He said to him: “Take it easy, for I am the son of a woman from Quraysh who used to eat porridge during this time.” Al-Batha’, he said: Then Jarir bin Abdullah Al-Bajli recited: {And you are not a tyrant over them, so remind of the Qur’an whoever fears its threat} [Q: 45] “This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3733 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3734","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Muslim Al-A'war, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to go back to the sick person and follow the funerals, and respond The call of the king and he rides the donkey, and there was a day of Khaybar and the day of Qurayzah on a donkey whose muzzle was a rope of fibre, and underneath it were shrouds of fibre.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3734 - True"
"3735","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Sufyan bin Hussein told us, On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “come Weak Muslims, and he visits them and visits their sick, and attends their funerals.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3735 - True"
"3736","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Tanafisi told us, Bassam bin Abd told us Al-Rahman Al-Sayrifi, Abu Tufayl told us, he said: I saw the Commander of the Faithful Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, stand up on the pulpit and said: “Ask me.” Before you do not ask me, and you will not ask someone like me after me.” He said: Then Ibn al-Kawwa’ stood up and said: O Commander of the Faithful, what is {the offspring} [Al-Dhariyat: 1] He said: “The winds.” He said: “What are the [bearing] clouds?” He said: “The clouds.” He said: What about {the female slaves of ease}? He said: “the ships.” He said: What are {the ones who divide a matter}? He said: “The angels.” He said: Among “those who exchanged the blessings of God for disbelief and made their people the abode of destruction, Hell” [Ibrahim: 28]. He said: “The hypocrites of the Quraysh.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3736 - True"
"3737","Abu Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Wazir told me, Abu Hatim al-Razi told me, Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, in this verse {They used to sleep for a little of the night and did not sleep} [Al-Dhariyat: 17] He said: “They used to pray during the evening prayer.” “And the Maghrib.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3737 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3738","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Mahran told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us about the ruling, On the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: “They used to sleep for a short part of the night” [Al-Dhariyat: 17] He said: “A night will not pass by when they sleep until they pray the morning in it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and it has a chain of narration from \"another face\"\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3738 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3739","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told us in Mecca, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Jari told us, Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Fudayl Al-Khattimi told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: It was part of a supplication The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of the wind, from the evil of what the wind brings, and from the north wind, for it is a sterile wind.”"
"3740","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Layth told us, Al-Ashja’i told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khasif, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: “And in ‘Ad when We sent upon them the sterile wind” [Al-Dhariyat: 41] He said: “Which does not fertilize anything.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3740 - True"
"3741","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Sahl bin Bakkar told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Samad al-Ammi told us, Ata’ told us. Ibn Al-Sa'ib, on the authority of Sa'id Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty saying {and Al-Tur} [Al-Tur: 1] He said: This is a mountain A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3741 - True"
"3742","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Affan and Suleiman bin Harb told us, they said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Al-Bayt Al-Ma’mur is in the seventh heaven, and he enters it every day.” “Seventy thousand angels will not return to it until the Hour comes.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3742 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3743","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr Al-Maruzi told me, Ahmad bin Issa Al-Qadi told me, Abu Nu’aym and Abu Hudhayfah told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Khalid bin Arara, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying: {By the raised roof} [At-Tur: 5] He said: “The heaven.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3743 - True"
"3744","Muhammad ibn Ali al-San’ani informed us of Mecca, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abbad informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, on the authority of Amr Ibn Murrah, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {We have joined them with their descendants and Have We not given them?} [At-Tur: 21] He said: “Indeed, God will raise the believer’s offspring with him in his rank in Paradise, even if they are below him in deeds.” Then he read. {And those who believed and whose descendants followed them in faith - to them We will join their descendants, but We will not follow them.} [At-Tur: 21] He says: “And We have not diminished them.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3744 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3745","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ishaq, the reciter of justice in Baghdad, told us, Abd al-Malik bin Muhammad told us, Abd al-Samad bin Abd told us. The heir, my father told me, Ayoub told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “prostrated in it.” Meaning, by the star, and the Muslims, the polytheists, the humans, and the jinn prostrated therein.” It is authentic according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it in this context.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3745 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3746","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Yahya bin Adam informed us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, in His Almighty saying: “The heart does not deny what it sees” [Al-Najm: 11] He said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw Gabriel in a cloud that filled what is between the sky and the earth.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3746 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3747","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, Ubayy told us, about Qatada, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “Do you wonder that the companion was for Abraham, and the speech was for Moses? “And the vision of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and may God’s prayers and peace be upon them all.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3747 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"3748","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandmother, Asmaa bint Abi Bakr, may God be pleased with them, she said: I heard the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, describing Sidrat al-Muntaha. He said: “The rider travels on the vehicle for a hundred years, and for a hundred of them he takes shade on the vehicle.” Riding therein is a bed of gold.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3748 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3749","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {The sight does not wander} [An-Najm: 17] He said: “He did not go to the right or to the left” {And he did not wander} [An-Najm: 17] He said: “Whatever exceeds” this is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3749 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3750","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Zakaria bin Ishaq Al-Makki told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty saying: {Those who avoid great sins Sins and immoralities, except minor ones.} [An-Najm: 32] He said: He becomes aware of them and then repents from them. Ibn Abbas said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “\n [The sea of rage]\n\n If You forgive, O God, You will forgive a lot...And any servant of Yours who has no pain.”\n This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3750 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3751","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, that Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: In the words of the Almighty, the Almighty, {except the words} [An-Najm: 32] He said: “The adultery of the eyes is looking. The fornication of the lips is kissing, the fornication of the hands is forcefulness, the fornication of the feet is walking, and this is confirmed or disbelieved by the private part, if he comes forward with his private part “He was an adulterer, otherwise he is a liam.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3751 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3752","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ubaid bin Sharik Al-Bazzaz told us, Yahya bin Abdullah bin Bukair told us, Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Saleh, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “On every soul of the son of Adam is written a share of fornication. This inevitably happens. For the eye’s fornication is looking, and the man’s fornication is Walking, the fornication of the ear is hearing, the fornication of the hand is force, the fornication of the tongue is speech, and the heart wishes and desires and believes it or Distraction belies him. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3752 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3753","Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Karazi told us, Ali bin Abdul-Aziz told us, Mu’alla bin Rashid told us, Wahib told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “The arrows of Islam are thirty arrows that no one completed before Abraham, peace be upon him. God Almighty said: And glory be to Him: {And Abraham is the One who fulfilled} [An-Najm: 37] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3753 - True"
"3754","Ali ibn Issa told me, Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Jarudi told me, Nasr ibn Ali told me, al-Mu’tamir ibn Sulayman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: When “Glorify the Name of your Lord Most High” was revealed, he said: “It is all in the scriptures of Abraham.” And when it descended, and when the star descended, it reached {And Abraham, who fulfilled his duty that no bearer of burden should bear the burden of another} [An-Najm: 38] until his saying: {This is a warner. Of the first vows} [An-Najm: 56] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3754 - True"
"3755","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Daoud Al-Munadi told us, Abdul-Malik bin Amr Al-Aqdi told us, Zuhair told us Ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Usayd Ibn Abi Usayd, on the authority of Musa Ibn Abi Musa Al-Ash’ari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The dead That he will be tormented by the crying of the living.” Then when she said: “And support him, and defend him, and support him, and cover him, preferring the dead.” Then it was said, “I will support her, you, support her.” You, I support her? “He said: So I said: Glory be to God. God Almighty said: {And no female bearer of burden bears the burden of another} [Al-An’am: 164] So he said: Woe to you! I am telling you on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and you say this? Which of us has lied? By God, I did not lie to Abu Musa, and Abu Musa did not lie to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration.” And they did not bring it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3755 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3756","Abu Mansour Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah Al-Farisi told us, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Muhammad bin Saeed bin Sabiq told us, Israel told us, Samak bin Harb narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Nakha’i, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying: {And the moon was split asunder} [Al-Qamar: 1] He said: “I saw the moon as it was split, and I saw the mountain between the two sides of the moon.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They bring it out in this context and with this wording.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3756 - True"
"3757","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam informed us, Ishaq informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Uyaynah informed us, and Muhammad ibn Muslim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: “I saw the moon split apart.” With two splits twice in Mecca before the departure of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one split on Abu Qubays, and one split on Suwayda. They said: The magic of the moon. Then, “The Hour has drawn near, and the moon has been split asunder” was revealed. [Al-Qamar: 1] He says: “Just as you saw it splitting apart, then what I told you about the approaching of the Hour is true.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not include it in this context. “But they agreed on the hadith of Abu Muammar on the authority of Abdullah in brief.” This is a hadith in which we cannot do without the Companions following each other to provoke the people of atheism, for it is the first verse of the Sharia.” So I looked. So, on the subject of what they did not narrate on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, Abdullah bin Amr, and Jubayr bin Mutim, may God be pleased with them, and they did not They take him out of it, except for the hadith of Anas: “As for the hadith of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3757 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3758","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, my father told us, Bakr bin Mudar told me, Ja’far bin Rabia, on the authority of Arak bin Malik, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The moon split at the time of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. As for the hadith of Abdullah bin Amr,\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3758 - True"
"3759","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq Al-Basri told us in Egypt, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with him, in His saying, the Almighty, “The Hour has drawn near and the moon has been split open” [Al-Qamar: 1] He said: This was during the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The moon was split into two parts, one part below the mountain, and one part behind the mountain. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, bear witness.” As for the hadith of Jubayr:\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3759 - True"
"3760","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Ahmad bin Yahya Al-Halwani told us, Saeed bin Sulaiman Al-Wasiti told us, Hushaym told us, he reported Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Jubayr bin Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mutim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, in his saying: Glory be to And Glorious is He: {The Hour has drawn near, and it has been split.} [Al-Qamar: 1] The moon said: “The moon was split while we were in Mecca at the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Al-Hakim said: “All of these evidences for the hadith of Abdullah bin Masoud are authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate them.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3760 - True"
"3761","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Zahid told us in Baghdad, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar reported, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The people of Mecca asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a sign and the moon split open.” In Mecca twice, God Almighty said: {The Hour has drawn near and the moon has been split open} [Al-Qamar: 1] “The two sheikhs agreed on the hadith of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Anas: The moon split during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they did not narrate it in the context of the hadith of Muammar, and it is authentic according to their conditions.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3761 - And in the two Sahihs there is a hadith by Qatada on the authority of Anas when the moon split open during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"3762","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Wael bin Daoud, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he used to recite: (with their eyes humbled) with the alif “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration and it was not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3762 - True"
"3763","It was told to us by Ali bin Muhammad bin Saeed al-Muqri in Kufa, to us by Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Hadrami, to us by Abu Hisham Muhammad bin Yazid, to us by Hussein bin Ali Al-Jafi, I heard Aban bin Taghlib “reciting: (with their eyes humbled) like Hamza"
"3764","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Yahya Al-Hamani told us, Al-Nadr Abu Omar Al-Khazzaz told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “There were three hundred years between the call of Noah and the destruction of Noah’s people, and the mouse of the oven was In India, Noah’s Ark circled around the House for a week.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not take it out.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3764 - True"
"3765","Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Anbasa told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that he recited the saying of God Almighty {Indeed The criminals are in error and iniquity.} [Al-Qamar: 47] The verse refers to {by measure} [Al-Qamar: 49] and he said: Saeed bin Al-Musayyab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The last word about fate is for the wicked of this nation.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3765 - Anbasa is trustworthy, but they did not narrate it"
"3766","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told us, my father told us, Hisham bin Ammar told us, and Abu Muslim Abd Al-Rahman bin Waqid Al-Harrani said: Al-Walid bin Muslim narrated to us, Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited Surah Ar-Rahman to his companions until he had finished, he said: “What is the matter with me that I see you remaining silent about the jinn? Better than you in responding. Never once have I read to them, {Then which of the favors of your Lord will you deny?} [Al-Rahman: 13] except that they said: Not by any of your grace, our Lord. We deny, so praise be to You. “It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3766 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3767","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Waki` informed us, and Yahya bin Adam told us, They said: Israel told us, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {Do you know his Sumayya} [Maryam: 65] He said: “No one is called the Most Merciful other than Him.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3767 - True"
"3768","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar Al-Adl told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, and Abu Ghassan told us, they said: We told us Israel, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {The sun and the moon are taken into account} [Al-Rahman: 5] He said: “With an account and stations.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3768 - True"
"3769","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Yahya bin Al-Yaman told us, Al-Minhal bin Khalifa told us, about Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {And the star and the tree} [Al-Rahman: 6] He said: “The star is what the earth and the tree produce.” “It was not on a leg.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3769 - Minhal bin Khalifa was deemed weak by Ibn Ma’in"
"3770","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: “The poisons from which God created the jinn are one out of seventy “A portion of the fire of Hell.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3770 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3771","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafid told us, my grandfather told us, Ahmad bin Harb told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza Al-Thumali, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {Every day is about a matter} [Al-Rahman: 29] He said: “Indeed, of what God has created A tablet preserved from a white pearl, with a cover of a red ruby, its pen is light, and its book is a light upon which three hundred and sixty people look every day. Or once, for in every sight of it He creates, provides, gives life, causes death, honors, humiliates, and does whatever He wills. That is the Almighty’s saying {All A day when it will be about a matter.} [Al-Rahman: 29] “The chain of transmission is authentic, and they have not produced it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3771 - The name of Abu Hamzah is Thabit, and it is somewhat weak"
"3772","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa Al-Adl told me, Ismail bin Qutaibah told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abd al-Samad bin Abd told us. The heir, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juni, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, {And for those who fear The standing place of his Lord is two gardens.} [Al-Rahman: 46] He said: “Two gardens of gold for those who came before, and two gardens of silver for those who follow.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3772 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3773","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told us, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra bin Yarim, On the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying: “Its linings are made of Ibraq” [Al-Rahman: 54] He said: “You were informed With the ventricles, what about the epithelia? It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3773 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3774","Abu Ali Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Masri Al-Hafiz narrated to me, in Mecca, Allan bin Ahmed bin Sulaiman narrated to us, Amr bin Sawad Al-Sarhi narrated to us, Abdullah bin Wahb, Amr bin Al-Harith informed me, on the authority of Abu Al-Samh, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in His Almighty’s saying: {As if they were rubies and coral} [Al-Rahman: 58] He said: “He looks at his face in her cheek. It is clearer than a mirror, and there is a pearl upon it to illuminate what is between the east and the west, and there are seventy garments upon it. His sight penetrates it until he sees the marrow of her leg from behind that.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3774 - Daraj, owner of wonders"
"3775","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub, the memorizer of dictation, told us, Hamid bin Abi Hamid Al-Muqri told us, Ishaq bin Sulayman told us, Anbasah bin Saeed, Amr bin Abi Qais, and others, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, in the saying God Almighty: {And His throne was upon the water} [Hud: 7] He said: “God’s throne was upon the water, then He took for Himself a garden, then He took a garden other than it.” another until I join it with a single pearl.” Then God said, “And apart from them are two gardens.” [Al-Rahman: 62] He said: “And it is the one that the creatures do not know “What is in it?” He said: And it is what God Almighty said: {So no soul knows what has been hidden from them of comfort to eyes as a recompense for what they used to do} [Al-Sajdah: 17] He will come to them. Among them is a masterpiece every day. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3775 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3776","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asbahani Al-Zahid told us, Usayd bin Asim Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hussein bin Jaafar told us, Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty saying: {In them are fruits and palm trees And pomegranates} [Al-Rahman: 68] He said: “The palm trees of Paradise, whose trunks are green emeralds, whose branches are red gold, and whose branches are a covering for the people of Paradise.” Among them are their harvests and their garments, and their fruit is like a pot or buckets, whiter than milk, sweeter than honey, and softer than butter. “And she has no non-Arabs.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3776 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3777","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ja`far al-Muzaki told me, Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Abdi told us, Musaddad bin Mashad told us, Abu al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of my father Ishaq Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, he said: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, said, I asked the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace. How old are you? He said: “Surat Hud, and the incident, and the mursalat, and they were wondering, and when the sun was circled.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and it was not “He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3777 - according to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"3778","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Safwan bin Amr told us, on the authority of Sulaym bin Amir, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: God helps us with the Bedouins and their questions are more acceptable. A Bedouin one day said: O Messenger of God, God has mentioned in the Qur’an a tree that is harmful, and I did not see that there was a tree in Paradise that would cause harm. Her friend. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What is it?” He said: Sidr tree, for it has thorns. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “{In a fertilized fig tree} [Al-Waqi’ah: 28] God cuts down its thorns and places a fruit in the place of every thorn. It produces fruit, and the fruit is divided into seventy-two colours, none of which resembles the other. “The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not produce it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3778 - True"
"3779","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Assam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both: {And the shadow of someone who is feverish} [Al-Waqi’ah: 43] He said: “From black smoke.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission is based on the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3779 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3780","Professor Imam Abu Al-Walid, may God be pleased with him, told us, Abu Abdullah Al-Bushangi told us, Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar reported, on the authority of Shaddad ibn Jaban al-San’ani, on the authority of Hujr ibn Qais al-Madri, who said: I spent the night with the Commander of the Faithful, Ali ibn Abi Talib. May God be pleased with him, “So I heard him reciting the night prayer, so he passed by this verse {Have you seen what you believe? Do you create it or We are the Creators} [Al-Waqi’ah: 59] “He said: ‘Rather, you, O Lord, three times.’” Then he recited {Have you seen what you till? Do you plant it or do we Al-Zari’oon} [Al-Waqi’ah: 63] “He said: Nay, You, O Lord, Nay, You, O Lord, Nay, You, O Lord.” Then he recited {Have you seen the water that you drink? Did you bring him down from the mountain, or are we the ones who will be sent down?} [Al-Waqi’ah: 68] He said: “Rather, you, O Lord, three times.” Then he recited {Have you seen the fire that you are burning? Have you Did you produce its tree, or are we the originators?} He said: “Rather, you, O Lord.” Three times: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3780 - True"
"3781","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil informed me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti told me, Hushaym told me, Husayn informed us Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The Qur’an was sent down from the sky on the Night of Decree.” From the highest to the lowest heaven all in one sentence, then he divided the years. He said: And he recited this verse: {So I swear by the locations of the stars} [Al-Waqi’ah: 75] He said: “He descended dispersed.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3781 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3782","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Yazid said: We were with Salman, may God be pleased with him, and he went off to do something and hid from us, then he came out to us and there was no water between him and us. He said: So we said to him: O Abu Abdullah, if you performed ablution, we would ask you about things from the Qur’an. He said: So he said: “Ask, for I will not touch him.” He said: “Only the purified touch it.” Then he recited, “Indeed, it is a noble Qur’an in a hidden book, which no one touches except the purified.” [Al-Waqi’ah: 78] “This is a hadith.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3782 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3783","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told me, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told me, Musa bin Ayyub Al-Ghafiqi told me, Iyas bin Amir Al-Ghafiqi said: I heard Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani saying: When “So glorify the name of your Lord Almighty” was revealed [Al-Waqi’ah: 74] he said The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told us: “Put it in your bowing,” and when “Praise the name of your Lord the Most High” was revealed [Al-A’la: 1], he said: “Put it in your prostration.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3783 - The hadith is authentic"
"3784","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein bin Dizel told us, Abdullah bin Salih Al-Masry told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told me, On the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, that he heard Abu Dharr and Abu al-Darda’, may God be pleased with them both, They said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will be the first to be permitted to prostrate on the Day of Resurrection, and the first to be permitted to raise His head, so I raise my head and look between my hands and recognize my nation from among the nations, and I look to my right and recognize my nation from among the nations. And I will look to my left and I will recognize my nation from among the nations.” Then a man said: O Messenger of God, how do you recognize your nation from among the nations between Noah and Your nation? He said: “They are white-haired from the effect of ablution, and it is almost impossible for any of the nations other than them. And I know that they give their Scriptures with their oaths. And I recognize them by their marks on their faces from the traces of prostration, and I recognize them by their light that is before them and by their right and by their left.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3784 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3785","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abdullah bin Qutaybah told us. Idris, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Minhal ibn Amr, on the authority of Qays ibn Al-Sakan, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, in His saying, the Almighty, {He seeks Their light is before them.} [Al-Hadid: 12] He said: “They will be given their light in proportion to their deeds. “His thumb turns it off one time and turns it on again.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3785 - according to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"3786","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Razi told us, Abu Zur’ah told us Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Karim, Ahmed bin Hashim Al-Ramli told us, Damra bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Maimun, on the authority of Bilal bin Abdullah, the muezzin of the Holy House, said: “I saw Ubadah bin Al-Samit, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, in the Mosque of Bayt al-Maqdis, facing the east or the wall, I doubt, while he was crying while reciting this verse {so he struck among them, With a wall that has a door, inside of which is mercy.} [Al-Hadid: 13], then he said: Here the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, showed us Hell. “This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3786 - Rather, it is evil, and its afterlife is false"
"3787","Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydalani told us, Ubayd Allah bin Sharik Al-Bazzar told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Musa bin Yaqoub told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim That Amer bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair told him on the authority of his father that Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, told him, saying: “There was no Their Islam, and between the time when this verse was revealed, God punished them, except for four years (and do not be like those who were given the Scripture before, Al-Amad) until the end of the verse “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3787 - True"
"3788","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl informed us, Yahya bin Abi Talib informed us, Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata informed us, Saeed bin Abi Arouba informed us, On the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Hassan al-Araj, that Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “The people of The pre-Islamic people say: “The calamity is only in the woman, the animal, and the house.” Then I read, “No calamity has afflicted on the earth nor within yourselves except in A Book before We bring it forth. Indeed, that is easy for God.} [Al-Hadid: 22] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not produce it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3788 - True"
"3789","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa Al-Saydalani told me, Ismail bin Qutaibah told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {So that you may not grieve over what you have missed, nor Rejoice in what He has given you.} [Al-Hadid: 23] He said: “Is there no one who does not grieve and rejoice, but he who turns calamity into patience, and turns joy into gratitude.” The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3789 - True"
"3790","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya the Martyr told us, Abdul Rahman bin Al-Mubarak told us, Al-Saqq bin Hazan told us, On the authority of Aqeel bin Yahya, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, {And He placed us in the hearts of Those who followed him showed compassion, mercy, and monasticism, which they invented. We did not prescribe it for them except to seek the pleasure of God, but they did not take care of it as it should be cared for. So We gave those of them who believed their reward, but many of them are transgressors.} [Al-Hadid: 27] Ibn Masoud said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “O Abdullah bin Masoud, so I said: At your command, O Messenger of God, three times. He said: Do you know which of the bonds of faith is strongest? I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “The strongest faith is loyalty to God through love for Him and hatred for Him, O Abdullah bin Masoud.” I said: At your command, O Messenger of God, three times. Repeatedly, he said: “Do you know which people are better?” I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “The best people are the best in deed if they understand their religion, O Abdullah bin Masoud.” I said: “Labbayk and Sa`diq, three times.” He said: “Do you know which people I know best?” I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “The most knowledgeable of people is the one who sees the truth when the people disagree, even if he is negligent in his work, even if he creeps on his side, and those who disagree.” There were seventy-two sects before us, of which three survived, and the rest of them perished. The son of Mary until they were killed, and a group who did not have the strength to compete with the kings, so they stayed among the backs of their people and called them to the religion of God. And Jesus, son of Mary, was judged, and the kings killed them, and sawed them with saws, and a group who had no power to compete with the kings or to stand. between the backs of their people, so they called them to God and to the religion of Jesus, son of Mary, so they traveled in the mountains and became terrified therein, so they are the ones God said {And monasticism they invented. We did not prescribe it for them except to seek the pleasure of God, but they did not care for it as it should be cared for} [Al-Hadid: 27] to his saying. {Disobedient} [Al-Hadid: 27] So the believers who believe in me and believe in me and the sinners who disbelieve in me and deny me “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3790 - It is not correct"
"3791","Sheikh Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah bin Maan told us. Al-Masoudi, my father told me, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Tamim bin Salamah Al-Sulami, on the authority of Urwa, he said: Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: Blessed be He whose hearing encompasses all things. Indeed, I hear the words of Khawla bint Tha’labah, and some of them are hidden from me, and she is complaining about her husband to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: O Messenger of God, he ate up my youth and I spread my belly for him, so that when my age grows and my apparent son is cut off from him, O God I complain to you. Aisha said: “It was not until Gabriel, peace be upon him, revealed these verses: {God has heard the words of the woman who disputes with you regarding her husband} [The argument: 1], He said: And her husband Aws bin Al-Samit “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.” It was narrated on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, briefly\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3791 - True"
"3792","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub, Ibrahim bin Asma, and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, they said: Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Abu Al-Numan Muhammad bin Al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, “that Beautiful was the wife of Aws ibn al-Samit, and Aws was a man of vengeance, so when his eloquence intensified it became apparent from his wife, so God sent down “It contains expiation for zihaar.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3792 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3793","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub and Ibrahim bin Asmah told us, saying: Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Haywa bin Khuzaimah told us. Shuraih, Ibn Abi Karimah told me, he said: I heard Ikrimah say: I heard Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, saying: {God will raise up those who believe. And those who have been given knowledge are in ranks among you.} [Al-Mujadila: 11] He said: “Allah raises those who have been given knowledge among the believers in ranks over those who have not been given knowledge.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3793 - True"
"3794","Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydalani told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told me, Yahya bin Al-Mughirah Al-Saadi informed me, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, who said: Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The In the Book of God is a verse that no one has ever acted upon, and no one will act upon after me, the Verse of Negotiations. “O you who have believed, when you speak to the Messenger, present between My hand is your confidentiality} [Al-Mujadila: 12] as charity of the verse. He said: I had a dinar, so I sold it for ten dirhams, so I spoke to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so whenever I spoke to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, I presented it in front of me. My negotiables were a dirham, then they were abrogated and no one acted upon them, so the verse was revealed: “Have you the fear that you should present charity before your negotiables?” [Al-Mujadila: 13] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3794 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3795","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Amr bin Muhammad Al-Anqazi told us, Israel told us, Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in the shade of a room and he was almost The shadow would shrink, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, a person will come to you and look at you with the eyes of a devil. When he comes to you, he will not Speak to him.” They did not wait long enough when a one-eyed blue man appeared upon them and said: When he saw him, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called him and said: “What do you accuse me of?” You and your companions.” He said: “Leave me, and I will bring them to you.” So he went and called them, and they swore that they would not say or do anything until they would be betrayed. “So God Almighty revealed {the day God will raise them all together, and they will swear to Him as they swear to you, and they think that they are upon something. Indeed, it is they who are the liars.} [Al-Mujadila: 18] “This is An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3795 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3796","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told me, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaydah told us, he reported Al-Sa'ib bin Hubaysh Al-Kala'i, on the authority of Ma'dan bin Abi Talha Al-Yamari, said: Abu Al-Darda' said to me: Where is your residence? So I said: In a village below Homs. Abu al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “There are no three in A village, and no Bedouins among whom prayer is not performed unless Satan has taken control of them, so you must join in congregation, for the wolf only devours the remote part.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “The distinguished ruler Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us a dictation in Dhul-Hijjah in the year Four hundred\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3796 - True"
"3797","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Sana’ani told me in Mecca, Ali bin Al-Mubarak Al-Sana’ani told us, Zayd bin Al-Mubarak Al-Sana’ani told us, Muhammad bin Thawr, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The raid of Banu al-Nadir, who were a group of The Jews, six months after the Battle of Badr, had their house and palm trees near Medina, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, besieged them. peace be upon him, until they descended on the evacuation, and that they had as much luggage and property as camels had except the ring, meaning the weapons, so he sent down God is among them {All that is in the heavens and all that is in the earth glorify God} up to His saying: {For the first of the assembly, you did not think that they would emerge} [Al-Hashr: 2] So the Prophet fought them. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, until he made peace with them regarding evacuation, so he evacuated them to the Levant, and they were from a tribe that had not been afflicted by evacuation, and God had decreed They are obligated to do that, and had it not been for that, He would have punished them in this world with killing and captivity. As for His saying, “For the first of the gathering” [Al-Hashr: 2], that was their exile. That was the first gathering in this world to the Levant. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3797 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3798","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Mansour bin Hayyan told us, about Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Omar and Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, that they bore witness against the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he “forbade” On the authority of al-Dabba`, al-Naqir, al-Hantam, and al-Muzaffat. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited {Whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you about it. So they concluded} [Al-Hashr: 7] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it with this addition.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3798 - Sahih Mansour, narrated by Muslim"
"3799","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah Al-Sukkari told us, in Hamadan, Al-Qasim bin Al-Hakam Al-Arni told us, Ubaid Allah bin Al-Walid told us, On the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The head of a sheep was given as a gift to a man from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “My brother so-and-so and his family are in greater need of this than we are.” He said: So he sent to him, and he continued sending him one to another until they exchanged them. Seven verses until it returned to the first and was revealed: {And they prefer themselves over themselves, even though they were in poverty} [Al-Hashr: 9] until the end of the verse: “This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3799 - Ubayd Allah bin Al-Walid is weak"
"3800","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Yunus Al-Dhabi told us, Abu Badr Shuja’ bin Al-Walid told us, Abdullah bin Zubaid, on the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif, on the authority of Mus’ab ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Sa’d ibn Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The people were in three houses, so they departed.” Two of them and one remained, so it is best for you to be in this position that remained. Then he read {For the poor emigrants who were expelled from their homes and their wealth} [Al-Hashr: 8] the verse, then he said: These are the emigrants and this is the status It had passed, then he recited {and those who lived in the land and the faith before them} the verse, then he said: These are the Ansar and this is the status It had passed, then he recited {And those who came after them say, “Our Lord, forgive us and our brothers who preceded us in faith} the verse. He said: These two positions have passed and this status remains, so it is best for you to be in this status that It remains: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3800 - True"
"3801","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Abdul Razzaq informed us, Al-Thawri informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Humaid bin Abdullah Al-Saluli, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, he said: “A monk was worshiping in a hermitage and a woman was decorated.” He fell on her and she became pregnant, so Satan came to him and said: Kill her, for if they rebel against you, she will be exposed. So he killed her and buried her. So they came to him, took him, and took him away. While they were walking, Satan came to him and said: I am the one who has been made beautiful for you, so prostrate to Me and I will save you. So he prostrated to him, and God Almighty revealed {like Satan when he said to man, “Disbelieve.” But when he disbelieved, he said, “Indeed, I am free from you.” [Al-Hashr: 16] the verse “This is A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3801 - True"
"3802","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told me about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Warqa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {O you who have believed, do not take my enemy And your enemies are friends, to whom you extend affection.} [Al-Mumtahina: 1] to his saying: {And God is All-Seeing of what you do} [Al-Mumtahina: 3] revealed in a letter. Hatib bin Abi Balta’ah and those with him to the infidels of Quraysh, warning them, and the Almighty says: {Except the saying of Abraham to his father} [Al-Mumtahina: 4] They forbade That they may be inspired by Abraham’s asking forgiveness for his father, so they ask forgiveness for the polytheists, and the Almighty says: “Our Lord, do not make us a test for those who disbelieve.” [Al-Mumtahina: 5] Do not punish us by their hands or with a punishment from you, for they will say, “If these people had been upon the truth, it would not have befallen them.” This is an authentic hadith based on The conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not include it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3802 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3803","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {Indeed, you have among them a good example} [Al-Mumtahina: 6]. He said: “In making “Ibrahim and those with him, except when he asked forgiveness for his father while he was a polytheist.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3803 - True"
"3804","Abu Abbas Al-Sayyari told us, Abdullah bin Ali Al-Ghazal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he told me Musab bin Thabit bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, who said: Qayla bint Al-Uzza bint Asaad came. From the Banu Malik bin Hasal, her daughter, Asmaa bint Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with them, was married to her. Abu Bakr had divorced her in the pre-Islamic era. So she presented her daughter with gifts of honey, ghee, and cornflowers, but Asmaa refused to take them from her, accept them, or let them into her house. Until she sent a message to Aisha to ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about this, so she told him, “So he ordered her to accept her gifts.” And you shall admit her to her abode.” Then God Almighty revealed: “God does not forbid you from those who do not fight you on account of religion, nor expel you from your homes. “Be righteous of them.” [Al-Mumtahina: 8] until the last two verses: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3804 - True"
"3805","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Sulaiman al-Faqih in Baghdad told us, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, and Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, my brother told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Fatima bint Utbah bin Rabi’ah bin Abd Shams, that Abu Hudhayfah bin Utbah, may God be pleased with him, He brought her and Hind, the daughter of Utbah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she pledged allegiance to him. She said: He took it upon us and stipulated on us. She said: I said to him: Oh. Cousin, have you learned of any of these infirmities or infirmities among your people? Abu Hudhayfah said: Yes, then pledge allegiance to him, for this is what he pledges allegiance to and this is what he stipulates. Hind said: I do not pledge allegiance to you for stealing. I steal from My husband’s money, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, restrained his hand, and she restrained her hand until he sent for Abu Sufyan, who made her permission for her. Abu Sufyan said: As for wet, it is a blessing, and as for dry, it is no and not a blessing. She said: So we pledged allegiance to him, then Fatima said: There is no dome more hateful to me than your dome, nor would I like for God to make it permissible and whatever is in it, by God. There is no dome more beloved to me for God to populate and bless than your dome. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Also, by God, none of you truly believes until I am more beloved to him than his son and father.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3805 - True"
"3806","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid told me, my father told me, Al-Awza’i told me, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, Abu Salamah told me, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salam, may God be pleased with him, he said: We gathered and discussed each other and said: Which of you will the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, come to ask him which deed is most beloved to God? Then we dispersed. We granted that one of us might come to him, so he sent to us the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he gathered us together and started gesticulating to one another, “and he recited to us.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. All that is in the heavens and all that is in the earth glorified God. And He is the Mighty, the All-Wise. O you who have believed, why do you say something not? You will do until the end of the surah. Abu Salamah said: So Abdullah bin Salam recited it to us from the beginning to the end. Yahya said: So he recited it to us Abu Salamah from the beginning to the end. Al-Awza’i said: So Yahya bin Abi Kathir recited it to us from the beginning to the end Ishaq Al-Fazari, and Al-Awza’i read it to us from beginning to end. Muawiyah bin Amr said, and Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari read it to us from the beginning. He recited it to us from the beginning to the end, said Abu Bakr ibn Balawayh, and Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr read it to us from beginning to end. Al-Hakim said: “And I say: He read it to us. Abu Bakr bin Balawayh, from beginning to end: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"3807","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told me, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told me, Ishaq told us, Jarir told me, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “Jesus, peace and blessings be upon him, promised his companions Twelve men in a house, and he came out to them from another side of the house, shaking his head, and mentioned a hadith, and said at the end of it, and God Almighty revealed: {So We supported those who believed against their enemy, so they became victorious} [As-Saff: 14] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3807 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3808","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr al-Muzaki told us about Marwa, Abdul Aziz bin Hatim told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah al-Muqri told us, we told him Amr ibn Abi Qais, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Maysara, “This verse is written in the Torah as seven hundred verses {Glory be to God. In the heavens and all that is on earth, the King, the Holy, the Mighty, the Wise.} The beginning of Surat Al-Jumu’ah.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3808 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3809","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, Ali bin Issa told me, and the word for it, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told me, Abu Hisham Al-Rifai told us, Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad Al-Muharbi told us, On the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: Abu Jahl passed by the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. While he was praying, he said: “Am I not tired of you praying, O Muhammad? I have learned that no one is more persistent in it than me.” So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rebuked him. And peace be upon him. Gabriel said: peace be upon him, {so let him call his caller, and we will leave the rabbis.} [Al-Alq: 18] By God, if he had called his caller, a rabbis would have taken him. “The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3809 - True"
"3810","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Wahhab told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, Ismail bin Abi told us Khaled, on the authority of Qais ibn Abi Hazim, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Long this prayer, and shorten this prayer.” “The sermon, meaning the Friday prayer.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3810 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3811","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marwa, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl al-Balkhi told us, Yaqoub bin Muhammad al-Zuhri told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Usayd ibn Abi Usayd, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever abandons Friday prayer three times without necessity, God will set a seal on his heart.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3811 - Ya’qub bin Muhammad Al-Zuhri. Wah"
"3812","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, about Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Azdi, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, may God be pleased with him, who said: We invaded with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and there were people with us. Of the Bedouins, we used to rush for water, and the Bedouins preceded us, so the Bedouin preceded its companions, filling the basin, and putting water around it. stones, and he would be beaten until his companions came. Then a man from the Ansar Bedouins came and let his camel loose the reins so she could drink, but she refused. To let him go, he took out a stone and it gushed out, so the Bedouin raised a stick and struck the Ansari’s head with it, causing him to be injured. Then Abdullah bin Ubayy brought the head of The hypocrites, so he told him, and he was one of his companions, so Abdullah bin Ubayy became angry, then he said: Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of God, may God bless him. And he greeted until they dispersed from around him, meaning the Bedouins, and they were talking to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at mealtime, so Abdullah said To his companions: When they disperse from Muhammad and bring food to Muhammad, let him and those with him eat. Then he said to his companions: When you return To Medina, and let the more honorable expel from it the meaner. Zaid said: And I am my uncle’s buttocks.So I heard Abdullah, and we were his uncles, so I told my uncle, so he went off and informed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent for him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He swore, denied, and apologized. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, believed him and lied to me. Then he came to my uncle and said: I did not want to hate you. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Muslims lied to you. Then a grief fell upon me that had never fallen upon anyone, while I was traveling with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and my head throbbed from Concern, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me and “licked my ears and laughed in my face.” He did not make me happy that I had eternity or this world, then Abu Bakr caught up with me and said: What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say to you? I said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not say anything to me except that he “licked my ears and laughed in my face” and said: “Rejoice.”Then Omar caught up with me and said: What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, tell you? So I said to him the same as I said to Abu Bakr. When we became “the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited Surah Al-Munafiqun” {When the hypocrites come to you They said: We bear witness that you are the Messenger of God.} [Al-Munafiqun: 1] until it reached: He conveyed, “In order that they may bring out the more honorable from among them the meaner” [Al-Munafiqun: 8] “The two sheikhs have agreed to extract a few letters from this hadith from the hadith of Abu Ishaq al-Subai’i, on the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam. Al-Bukhari, following Abu Ishaq, reported from the hadith of Shu’bah on the authority of al-Hikam, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ka’b. Al-Qurazi, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, but they did not narrate it in its length, and the chain of transmission is authentic.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3812 - Sahih and two extracts from it"
"3813","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Kunasa, saying: I heard Sufyan Al-Thawri, He was asked about the saying of God Almighty: {It is He who created you, so among you is a disbeliever and among you is a believer} [At-Taghabun: 2] and he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, On the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Every servant will be resurrected as he died.” Muslim narrated the hadith of Al-A’mash He did not bring it out in this context.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3813 - According to Muslim’s condition and extracted from it"
"3814","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Amr bin Muhammad told us Al-Anqazi, told us about Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “This verse was revealed {Indeed, of Your wives and your children are enemies to you, so beware of them” [Al-Taghabun: 14] Concerning a people of Mecca who converted to Islam and wanted to come to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted them, but their wives and children refused to invite them, so they came to Medina, and when they came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, they saw them. They understood and understood to punish them, so God Almighty revealed {And if they pardon and forgive} [Al-Taghabun: 14] the verse: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3814 - True"
"3815","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Jami’ bin Shaddad, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, He said: “A man came to Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, and asked him about this verse: {And whoever is saved from the miserliness of himself, those are they.” Al-Muflihun} [Al-Hashr: 9], and indeed I am a man who cannot do anything, and nothing comes out of my hands, and I feared that this verse might have befallen me, so Abd said God: “You mentioned miserliness, and an evil thing is miserliness. As for what God mentioned in the Qur’an, it is not as you said. That is when you take someone else’s money. “Or your brother’s wealth and you may eat it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3815 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3816","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Muhammad bin Maslamah told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, about Al-Alaa bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God Almighty says I asked for a loan from my servant, but he refused to lend to me, and my servant cursed me, not knowing, saying: “And I forbade him and he forbade him, and I am eternity.” Then Abu Hurairah recited God Almighty says: “If you lend to God a good loan, He will multiply it for you” [Al-Tagahabun: 17] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3816 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3817","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Sana’ani informed us of Mecca, Ali bin Al-Mubarak Al-Sana’ani told us, Yazid bin Al-Mubarak told us, Muhammad bin Thawr, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi’, the client of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: Abd Yazid divorced Abu Rukana, Umm Rukana, then he married a woman from Muzainah, and she came to the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. She said: O Messenger of God, nothing can help me except what this hair can help a hair that I took from her head. So she took The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was excited at that, so he called Rukana and his brothers, then said to those sitting with him: “Do you see such-and-such from such-and-such?” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abd Yazid: “Divorce her.” He did so, and he said to Abu Rukanah: “Take her back.” He said: O Messenger of God, I I divorced her. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I know that, so take her back.” Then it was revealed: “O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them.” Because of their waiting period} [At-Talaq: 1] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3817 - Muhammad bin Ubaidullah bin Abi Rafi’ is weak"
"3818","Professor Abu Al-Walid told me, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told me, Kamil bin Talha told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Musa bin Uqba told us, on the authority of Nafi’, On the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, {unless they commit a clear indecency} [An-Nisa: 19] He said: “Her leaving her house is a clear indecency.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”"
"3819","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumayl told us, Khams bin Al-Hasan Al-Tamimi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Saleel Dharib bin Nuqayr Al-Qaisi, who said: Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made He recited this verse, “And whoever fears God, He will make for him a way out and provide for him from where he does not expect.” [At-Talaq: 3] He said: So he started repeating it. Until I fell asleep, and he said: “O Abu Dharr, if the people had taken it, it would have been sufficient for them.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3819 - True"
"3820","Abu Al-Qasim Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Uqba bin Khalid Al-Sakouni told me about Kufa, Ubaid bin Kathir Al-Amiri told us, Abbad told us Bin Yaqoub, Yahya bin Adam told us, Israel told us, Ammar bin Abi Muawiya told us, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him God said about them, he said: This verse was revealed {And whoever fears God - He will make for him a way out and provide for him from where he does not expect} [At-Talaq: 3] about a man. Whoever is most courageous is poor and light-handed and has many dependents. He came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him, and he said to him: “Fear God and be patient,” so he returned. To his companions, they said: What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, give you? He said: He did not give me anything and said to me: “Fear God and be patient.” He did not stay for a while until a son of his brought a sheep of his that had been attacked by the enemy. Then he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about it and told him about it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “All of it,” so it was revealed: “And whoever He fears God. He will make for him a way out and provide for him from where he does not expect.} [At-Talaq: 2] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3820 - Rather, it is objectionable"
"3821","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Jarir informed us, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Tarif, on the authority of Amr bin Salem, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, said: “When the verse in Surat Al-Baqarah was revealed to a number of women, they said: There remained a number of women who were not mentioned, the young and the old, nor those who had stopped menstruating, and those who were pregnant, so God Almighty revealed The verse in Surat An-Nisa {And those of your women who have given up menstruating, if you are in doubt, then their period of waiting shall be three months; and those who have not menstruated. And the pregnant women, their term is that they give birth to their burden.} [At-Talaq: 4] “The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not take it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3821 - True"
"3822","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Ubaid bin Ghannam Al-Nakhai told us, Ali bin Hakim informed us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he said: {It is God who created seven heavens and of the earth the like of them} [At-Talaq: 12] He said: Seven In every land there is a prophet like your prophet, and Adam like Adam, and Noah like Noah, and Abraham like Abraham, and Jesus like Jesus. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and no He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3822 - True"
"3823","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: “{Seven heavens and of the earth the like of them} [At-Talaq: 12] He said: In every earth On the authority of Ibrahim, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3823 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3824","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told me, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Zakaria Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Bukayr al-Hadrami, Sulayman bin al-Mughirah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had A nation he traversed, and Aisha and Hafsa did not stop with him until he made it forbidden to himself, so God revealed this verse {O Prophet, why You prohibit what God has made lawful for you, seeking the pleasure of your wives.} [Prohibition: 1] until the end of the verse: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3824 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3825","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Mahran told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salem Al-Aftas, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: A man came to him and said: I have made my wife forbidden to me, and he said: “You lied, she is not your duty.” With what is forbidden, then he recited this verse {O Prophet, why do you forbid what God has made lawful for you, seeking?} [Prohibition: 1] The verse: “This is an authentic hadith according to the condition Al-Bukhari and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3825 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3826","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, on the authority of Al-Thawri, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying: “Protect yourselves and your families from the Fire” [Al-Tahrim: 6] He said: “Teach yourselves and your families good.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3826 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3827","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl informed us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab informed us, Ja’far bin Aoun informed us, Mas’ar informed us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik Bin Umair, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Bin Sabit, on the authority of Amr Bin Maimun, on the authority of Abdullah Bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The stones Which God called in the Qur’an {whose fuel are people and stones} [Al-Tahrim: 6] stones of sulphur, which God created with Himself as He willed or as He willed. This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3827 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3828","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Hamza told me Al-Bukhari, my father told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, I am Muhammad bin Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Hazim, I think it is on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, that a young man from The Ansar entered him out of fear of the fire, and he used to cry at the mention of the fire until that kept him in the house, so he mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and came to him in the house. When he entered it, the boy embraced him and fell down dead. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Prepare your companion, for the difference is over.” “His liver” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3828 - The report is almost fabricated"
"3829","Abu Abdullah told us, after him, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told me, and Abu Bakr told us Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya dictated, Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Ahmad bin Mansour told me, on the authority of Mansour Ibn Ammar said: “I performed Hajj and went down one of the tracks of Kufa and went out on a dark night, when I saw a screamer screaming in the middle of the night.” And he says: My God, by Your glory and Your majesty, by disobeying You, I did not intend to disobey You, and I disobeyed You when I disobeyed You, and I am not ignorant of that, but It is a sin that you helped me with because of my misery, and I was deceived by your relaxed protection of me, and I disobeyed you because of my ignorance and disagreed with you because of my ignorance, so now from your torment. Who will rescue me and whose rope will I cling to if you cut off your rope from me? And his youth and his youth. So when he finished saying it, I recited a verse from The Book of God {Protect yourselves and your families from a fire whose fuel is people and stones, over which are harsh and severe angels} [Al-Tahrim: 6] verse. So I heard a strong movement, then I did not hear anything after that, so I went on, and when it was the next day, I returned to my hall, and I saw a funeral taking place. And behold, an old old woman, and I asked her about the matter of the dead person, but she did not know me, so she said: A man passed here, and God will not reward him except his reward for my son. “Yesterday, as he was standing praying, he recited a verse from the Book of God, and when my son heard it, his gallbladder broke and he fell dead.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3829 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3830","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Al-Nu’man. Ibn Bashir, on the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, “{Repent to God in sincere repentance} [Al-Tahrim: 8] He said: That a servant commits a sin and then repents and does not It is returned with “authentic chain of transmission” and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3830 - True"
"3831","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abaya Al-Asadi, he said: Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said, “Sincere repentance expiates every sin while it is in the Qur’an, then He recited {O you who have believed, repent to God in sincere repentance, perhaps your Lord will atone for you your evil deeds} [Al-Tahrim: 8] the verse “This is a hadith It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"3832","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Yahya Al-Hamani told us, Utbah bin Yaqzan told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the words of God Almighty: {A day when God will not disgrace the Prophet and those who believe with him, their light will before them and with their oaths, they say, “Our Lord, perfect for us our light.” [Al-Tahrim: 8] He said: “There is not one of the monotheists who will not be given light on the Day of Resurrection. As for the hypocrite, he extinguishes his light, and the believer is apprehensive about what he saw of the extinguishing of the hypocrite’s light, for he says: {Our Lord, perfect for us our light} [Al-Tahrim: 8] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3832 - Wah threshold"
"3833","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, On the authority of Suleiman bin Qattah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {so they betrayed them} [Al-Tahrim: 10] He said: “They did not commit adultery, but Noah’s wife used to say: To the people, he is crazy, and as for Lot’s wife, she was pointing out to the guest, that is their betrayal.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3833 - True"
"3834","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Suleiman Al-Taymi told us, about Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, may God be pleased with him, said: “Pharaoh’s wife was being tortured by the sun, and when they turned away from her, the angels shaded her.” “With her wings, she could see her home in Paradise.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3834 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3835","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Ata bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When I was taken on my journey, she passed by me.” It smells good, so I said: What is this smell? “So they said: This is the scent of the comb. Pharaoh’s daughter and her sons were combing it, and the comb fell from her hand, and she said: In the name of God. Then his daughter said: My father? She said: No, but rather my Lord, your Lord, and the Lord of your father. She said: I will tell that to my father. She said: Yes. So she informed him, so he called for her and her child, and she said: I have a need for you. He said: What is it? She said: You will collect my bones and my son’s bones and bury them all. He said: You have a right over us. So he brought her children and dropped them, one by one, until it was her last child, and he was a breastfeeding boy. Then he said: Be patient, mother, for you are upon the truth. Then she was thrown with her son. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Four spoke when they were young: this one, Joseph, the companion of Gregory, and Jesus, who witnessed.” Ibn Maryam, peace be upon him, said: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3835 - True"
"3836","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya, they said: Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, Dawud bin Abi Al-Furat told us, on the authority of Alba bin Ahmar Al-Yashkari, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote four lines, then he said: “Do you know what “This?” They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “Indeed, the best of the women of the people of Paradise are Khadija bint Khuwaylid, Fatima bint Muhammad, and Maryam bint Imran. And Asiya bint Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh, in addition to what God told us of her news in the Qur’an {she said, “My Lord, build for me a house with you in Paradise and save me from Pharaoh and his work, and save me from the wrongdoing people} [Al-Tahrim: 11] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it with this wording.” Rather, they agreed on The hadith which:\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3836 - True"
"3837","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Sadaqa bin Muhammad told us, Suleiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, and Muhammad bin Abdullah told me Bin Quraysh, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Ibn Numayr told us, and Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ja’far bin Abi Talib, on the authority of his uncle Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “The best of her women is Maryam bint Imran, and the best of her women is Khadija.” Narrated by Al-Bukhari in Al-Sahih on the authority of Sadaqa bin Muhammad, and narrated by Muslim On the authority of Abu Khaythamah and Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah with this context\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3837 - They took it out, so why did you include it?"
"3838","Abu Al-Walid Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Imran Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abbas Al-Jashmi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A surah from the Book of God Almighty is only thirty verses. “She interceded for a man and took him out of Hell and admitted him to Paradise.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not take him out, and it happened to me when I heard this. Al-Harf, which is Surat Al-Mulk.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3838 - True"
"3839","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Sufyan informed, about... Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: “A man will be brought into his grave, and his feet will be brought, and his feet will say: You have no right to do so.” There is a way before me. He used to stand and recite Surah Al-Mulk with me, then he would come from his chest or he said his stomach, and he would say: You have no way before me. He used to recite Surat Al-Mulk with me, then his head would be brought and he would say: You have no way before me. Surat Al-Mulk used to be recited with me, he said: So it is. The deterrent prevents one from the torment of the grave, and it is in the Torah Surat Al-Mulk, and whoever recites it in a night will indeed say more and more frequently. “This is an authentic hadith.” The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3839 - True"
"3840","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, about Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “The first thing God created was the pen, and He said to it: Write, and He said: And what should I write? He said: Destiny, and it will flow from that day as it is until the Hour comes. He said: His throne was on the water, so the vapor of the water rose. Then the heavens parted from it, then Nun was created, and the earth was spread over it, and the earth was on Nun’s back, so Nun was disturbed, and the earth moved, and it remained firm. By the mountains, for the mountains are proud of the earth. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3840 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3841","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih in Baghdad informed us, Hilal bin al-Alaa al-Raqi told us, Ubayy told us, Ubayd Allah bin Amr al-Raqi told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Abi Unaisa, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, {By the pen and what they write} [Al-Qalam: 1] He said: “And what they write.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3841 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3842","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani informed us in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abdul Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, about Qatada, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, on the authority of Saad ibn Hisham ibn Amir, regarding the words of God Almighty {And indeed, you are the master of a great creation} [Al-Qalam: 4] He said: I asked Aisha, may God be pleased with her: O Mother of the Believers, inform me about the character of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: “Do you recite the Qur’an?” So I said: Yes, and she said: “The creation of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is the Qur’an.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3842 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3843","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {After that I will be taken down a hill} [Al-Qalam: 13] He said: “It is known by its evil just as a sheep is known by its sheep.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3843 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3844","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abdullah bin Rabah told us, Musa bin Ali told us, he said: I heard my father speaking, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, that he recited this verse {Manna'} [Al-Qalam: 13] for good is an aggressor, a sinner, who after that was burdened with a burden and said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, says: “The people of Hell are all arrogant, arrogant, and unruly people, and the people of Paradise are weak and defeated.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that Muslim, and he did not narrate it in this context. “They narrated it from the hadith of Shu’bah and Al-Thawri, on the authority of Ma’bad ibn Khalid, on the authority of Harithah ibn Wahb.” On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, briefly.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3844 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3845","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told us, Saeed bin Yahya Al-Umawi told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he reported Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, that he was asked about the Almighty’s saying: {The Day when a shin will be uncovered} [Al-Qalam: 42] He said: “If anything of the Qur’an is hidden from you, seek it in poetry, for it is the collection of the Arabs.” Did you not hear what the poet said:\n [The sea of rage]\n Be patient with Anak, for it is an everlasting evil... Your people have enacted beheadings.\n And the war broke out among us\n Ibn Abbas said: This is a day of distress and distress. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and is better than a hadith narrated on the authority of Ibn Masoud with a chain of narration. It is true that I did not fully narrate his narration in this place.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3845 - True"
"3846","Abu Bakr al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying: “He imposed it on them for seven nights and eight days as a decisive decision” [Al-Haqqah: 7]. He said: “Continued stories.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3846 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3847","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, Muhammad bin Musa Al-Bashani told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin informed us Waqid, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, in His Almighty saying: {And the earth bore And the mountains were crushed with one crush.} [Al-Haqqah: 14] He said: “They will become dust on the faces of the disbelievers, not on the faces of the believers. That is the saying of the Almighty. And Glorious is He: {Faces that Day will be covered with dust, exhausted by time} [Abs: 41] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3847 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3848","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ali Al-Maydani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told me, Abu Ghassan Al-Nahdi told me, Sharik told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amira, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf bin Qais, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib, may God be pleased with him, in His Almighty saying: {And He carries The throne of your Lord will be above them that day, eight.} [Al-Haqqah: 17] He said: “Eight angels in the likeness of moving creatures, between their hooves to their knees. A journey of sixty-three years. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it. This hadith was attributed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him. Shuaib bin Khaled Al-Razi, Al-Walid bin Abi Thawr, and Amr bin Thabit bin Abi Al-Muqaddam conceded, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, and there was no evidence The two sheikhs with one of them. I mentioned the hadith of Shuaib bin Khalid, as it is the closest to being used as evidence.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3848 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3849","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Yahya bin Al-Ala told us, on the authority of his uncle Shuaib bin Khalid said: Samak bin Harb told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amira, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf bin Qays, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib. May God be pleased with him. He said: We were sitting with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in Batha’ when a cloud passed by and he looked at it and said to them: “Is it Do you know what this is called? They said: Yes, these are the clouds. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And the Muzn.” They said: And the Muzn. He said: “By An-Anana,” then he said: “Do you know what is between the sky and the earth?” They said: No. He said: “The distance between them is either one, two, or seventy-three years, and the heaven above it is like that, and God is not above that. Nothing is hidden from him of the deeds of the children of Adam. And in the seventh heaven are eight beasts, and between their hooves and their knees is like the distance between one sky to another.”"
"3850","Abdullah bin Omar Al-Jawhari told me about Marw, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Ubi told us, Harun bin Marouf told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Wahb, Amr Ibn Al-Harith informed me, on the authority of Abu Al-Samh, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “With water like mud” [Al-Kahf: 29] He said: “Like turbid oil, so when it is brought to him, the scalp of his face will fall off, even if it is a bucket of two washes.” “It is spilled in this world because you stink of the people of the world.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3850 - True"
"3851","Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {Then We would have severed from him the two jaws} [Al-Haqqah: 46] He said: “The beating of the heart.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it was not “He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3851 - True"
"3852","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told me, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Warqa’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {Then We certainly severed from him the two jaws} [Al-Haqqah: 46]. He said: “It is a rope “The heart that is in the back” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3852 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3853","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hassan bin Ayyub informed us, Ali bin Abdul-Aziz informed us, Abu Ubaid informed us, Ibn Adiy told us, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad Al-Dili, and Yahya ibn Yamar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, he said: “What are sinners? It is only the sinners. What is soap? “It is the Sabians.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3853 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3854","Muhammad bin Ali al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim al-Ghifari told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Sa'id bin Jubayr, {A questioner asked about a torment that will befall the disbelievers that has no recourse from God, the Possessor of Ascents} [Al-Ma'arij: 2] Dhu Al-Darajat {He asked Questioner} [Al-Ma’arij: 1] He said: He is Al-Nadr bin Al-Harith bin Kalada. He said: “O God, if this is the truth from You, then rain down stones upon us.” “From the sky.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3854 - according to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"3855","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sayegh told us in Ashkelon, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Jarir bin Uthman told us, Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Maysarah, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Busr bin Jahash Al-Qurashi, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited this verse {Then what about those who disbelieved before you, divided on the right, and strong on the left? Does every one of them aspire to enter a garden of bliss? Nay, indeed, We created them. Of what they know} Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spit on his palm and said: “God says: O son of Adam, how can you help me when I created you from Like this, until when I made you straight and straightened you, you walked between two pieces of sand, and the earth had a groan from you, meaning a complaint, so you were gathered together and prevented, until when you reached Al-Taraqi “You said: ‘Shall you give in charity? When is the time for charity?’ This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3855 - True"
"3856","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {And He made the moon among them a light} [Nuh: 16] He said: “His face is to the throne and his back is to the earth.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3856 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3857","Mukarram bin Ahmad al-Qadi told us, in Baghdad, Abd al-Malik bin Muhammad al-Raqqashi told us, Yahya bin Hammad told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abi Bishr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, neither read anything about the jinn nor saw them.” But he set out with a group of his companions, heading to the market of Ukaz, and he was separated between the devils and the news of heaven, and meteors were sent down upon them. So they returned to their people and said: What is the matter with you? They said: There has been a barrier between us and the news of the sky, and meteors have been sent down upon us. They said: This is nothing but something that has happened, so strike the east of the earth. And its west, look at this that has happened. So they set out to strike the east and west of the earth, seeking what has happened. Between them and the news of heaven, there when they returned to their people, they said: {Indeed, we have heard a wondrous Qur’an that guides to right path} [Al-Jinn: 2] so we believed in it. And we will not associate anyone with our Lord, so God Almighty revealed: “It has been revealed to me that a group of the jinn listened, but it was only revealed to him the saying of the jinn: ‘This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context. Rather, Muslim alone narrated the hadith of Dawud bin Abi Hind on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, in length without these words, and Al-Bukhari narrated the hadith of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim said: I asked Alqamah whether Abdullah was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the night of the jinn, and he mentioned a few letters. “A hadith was narrated. Trustworthy imams narrated it on the authority of an unknown man, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, that he witnessed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the night of the jinn.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3857 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3858","Abu Al-Hussein Ubayd Allah bin Muhammad Al-Balkhi told us from the origin of his book, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Abu Salih told us Abdullah bin Salih, Al-Layth bin Saad told me, Yunus bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Uthman bin Sunnah told me Al-Khuza’i, who was a man from the Levant, said that he heard Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He said to his companions while he was in Mecca: “Whoever among you would like to attend the command of the jinn tonight should do so.” But none of them attended except me. So we set off until we were at the top of Mecca. He drew a line for me with his foot, then ordered me to sit in it. Then he set off until he stood up and opened the Qur’an. Then a lot of black clouds covered him, blocking me from him until I could not hear his voice. Then they took off and began to go away like pieces of cloud. Until a group of them remained, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished with the dawn and set off and emerged, then he came to me and said: “What did the group do?” So I said: They are those, O Messenger of God. So he took a bone and dung and gave it to them as provisions. Then he forbade anyone from enjoying a bone or dung. With dung\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3858 - It is authentic according to a group"
"3859","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told me, Muhammad bin Sabiq told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {And whoever turns away from the remembrance of his Lord - He will cause him to undergo an ascending torment} [Al-Jinn: 17] He said: “A mountain in Hell” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3859 - True"
"3860","Abu Ahmed Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told me, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz told me, my grandfather Ahmed bin Mani’ told me, he told me Hushaym, Mughirah told me, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {They almost They will be upon him.} [Al-Jinn: 19] He said: “They would bow as he bowed and prostrate as he prostrated,” meaning the jinn. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it was not “He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3860 - True"
"3861","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Al-Hasan bin Bishr Al-Hamdani told us, Al-Hakam bin Abdul-Malik told us. Al-Qurashi, Qatada narrated to us, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, who said: I said to Aisha, may God be pleased with her: Tell me about the reading The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, she said: “When it was revealed to him {O, O Muzzammil, rise up through the night except for a little while} [Al-Muzzammil: 2], they stayed awake for a year until the night fell. Their feet, so God Almighty revealed: {So recite what is possible of the Qur’an, knowing that there will be sick among you.} “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3861 - Al-Hakam bin Abdul Malik is weak"
"3862","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Muawiyah told me Ibn Salih, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Jubayr ibn Nufayr, who said: I performed Hajj and went to Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and asked her about performing Hajj. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: “Aren’t you reading, O Muzzammil?” I said: Yes, she said: “It is his rising.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3862 - True"
"3863","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub and Ibrahim bin Asma told us, saying: Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Wahib told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {O, Muzzammil} [Al-Muzzammil: 1] He said: “You have decided this matter, so do it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3863 - True"
"3864","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hassan bin Ayyub told us, Abdullah bin Zakaria told us in Mecca, Khallad bin Yahya bin Ayyub told us, Mas’ar told us, on the authority of Samak. Al-Hanafi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “When the beginning of Al-Muzzammil was revealed, they were standing in a manner similar to how they had stood in the month of Ramadan until The last of it was revealed, and he said: There was about a year between the first and the last of it: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3864 - True"
"3865","Muhammad bin Ali al-Sana’ani told me about Mecca, Ali bin al-Mubarak al-Sana’ani told me, Zaid bin al-Mubarak told us, Muhammad bin Thawr told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when it was revealed to him while he was on His she-camel lost her calf and was unable to move, and she recited the words of God Almighty: {Indeed, We will cast upon you a heavy word} [Al-Muzzammil: 5] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3865 - True"
"3866","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Hamid bin Abi Hamid Al-Muqri told us, Ishaq bin Suleiman Al-Razi told us, Abu Ghassan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Sharhabeel, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, {Indeed, the rising of the night} [Al-Muzzammil: 6] said: “It is In Ethiopian, “the night prayer.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3866 - True"
"3867","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Handali told me in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Shabib bin Shaybah, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {food with bitterness} [Al-Muzzammil: 13] He said: “A thorn that takes hold of the throat and neither enters nor comes out.” And in the Almighty’s saying, “A dense, deserted hill” [Al-Muzzammil: 14], He said: “The deserted hill from which, if you take a part of it, the rest of it follows you, and the deserted hill is made of sand.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3867 - Shabib bin Shaybah is weak"
"3868","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub and Ibrahim bin Asma told us, saying: Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Wahib told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {O you, the Muddaththir} [Al-Muddaththir: 1] He said: “You have scattered this “The command, then do it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3868 - True"
"3869","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Barti told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “And your clothes, so purify them” [Al-Muddaththir: 4] He said: “From sin.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3869 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3870","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yazid bin Harun Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Aslam Al-Ijli, on the authority of Bishr ibn Shaghaf, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them both, said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: What are the pictures? He said: “A horn into which a blow will be blown.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3870 - True"
"3871","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Ghayath bin Al-Muthanna told us, Bahz bin told me. Hakim, who said: “Zurarah ibn Awfa led us in the mosque of Banu Qusayr and he recited al-Muddathathir, and when he reached this verse {So when he recited in al-Naqur} [Al-Muddaththir: 8] He fell down dead. He said with amusement: “So I was among those who carried it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3871 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3872","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani informed us in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abdul Razzaq informed us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub Al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that Al-Walid ibn Al-Mughirah came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and recited The Qur’an was written on him, and it was as if he had been deigned to do so. This reached Abu Jahl, so he came to him and said: O uncle, your people want to collect money for you. He said: Why? He said: To give it to you, for you came to Muhammad to present what came before him. He said: The Quraysh have learned that I am one of the richest of them. He said: Then say something about him that will convey to your people that you reject him or that you hate him. He said: What should I say? “By God, there is not a more knowledgeable man among you.” By poetry of my own, and I do not know of a verse of my own, nor of a poem of my own, nor of the poetry of the jinn. By God, there is no resemblance to the one who says any of this. By God, indeed Because of his saying that he says sweetness, and indeed there is sweetness upon him, and indeed he is fruitful above and watering below, and indeed he is exalted and what is exalted, and indeed he To destroy what is under it. He said: Your people will not be satisfied with you until you say something about it. He said: So let me think, and when he thought, he said: “This is magic that is more effective than anything else.” So “Leave me and whom I created alone” was revealed [Al-Muddaththir: 11] “This is A hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3872 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"3873","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran narrated to me, my grandfather narrated to me, Abu Ubayd Allah Al-Wahbi narrated to me, my uncle narrated to me, about Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Al-Samh, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Woe is a valley in Hell into which the disbeliever falls for forty falls before he reaches its bottom, and the ascent is a mountain in Hell, and he ascends therein for seventy Autumn, then it falls, and it is like that. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3873 - True"
"3874","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmed bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Harthi told us, Ali bin Qadim told us, Sufyan told us Al-Thawri, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Imran Al-Qattan, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, in His Almighty saying: {Every soul for what it has earned hostage, except those of the right hand.} [Al-Muddaththir: 39] He said: “They are the children of the Muslims.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3874 - True"
"3875","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz informed us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid informed us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Dhibyan, on the authority of Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying: {She fled from the tyrants} [Al-Muddaththir: 51] He said: The tyrants are the archers. “Sniping” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3875 - True"
"3876","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Surayj bin Al-Numan told us, Suhail bin Abi Hazm told us, Thabit told us Al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recite: {And you do not will except that He wills. God is the people of piety and the people of forgiveness} He said: Your Lord Almighty says: I am worthy to fear that He will place with me another god, and I It is worthy for the one who fears God to appoint with me another god that I may forgive him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3876 - True"
"3877","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, On the authority of Tamim Al-Dhabi, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: I went to Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, for a year. I did not speak to him, and he did not know me, so I heard Saeed bin Jubair says: Ibn Abbas said to me: “Who is the man?” I said: From the people of Iraq. He said: “From which one?” I said: From Banu Asad. He said: “From their Hurriyah or from whom God has bestowed blessings?” I said: Of those upon whom God has bestowed blessings. He said: Ask. I said: \"\"{I do not swear by the Day of Resurrection} [Resurrection: 1] \"\" He said: Your Lord swears by whatever He wills of His creation. I said: \"\" {And I do not swear by the blameworthy soul} [Resurrection: 2] “He said: From the blameworthy soul. I said: “Does man think that We will gather together his bones? Yes, We are able to level his building.” [Resurrection: 4] “He said: If He had willed, He could have made him a shoe or a hoof. I said: “{So settled and stored} [Al-An'am: 98]” He said: “So settled in the womb and stored in the loins” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3877 - True"
"3878","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Muhammad bin Sabiq told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {Rather, man desires to commit wickedness before Him} [Al-Qiyamah: 5] He says: “I will repent {Ayaan will be asked on the day Resurrection} [Resurrection: 6] “And it will become clear to him when the sight flashes.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3878 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3879","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, On the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, in the Almighty’s saying: “The day some of the signs of your Lord come, no soul will benefit from its belief if it does not believe in it.” Before} [Al-An'am: 158] he said: “The rising of the sun from the west,” then he recited this verse: “And the sun and the moon are brought together. Man will say on that day, ‘Where Al-Mafar} [Resurrection: 10] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3879 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3880","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Abdul-Malik bin Abjar told us, on the authority of Thuwayr bin Abi Fakhta, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The lowest status among the people of Paradise is a man.” He will look at his two-thousand-year kingdom. He will see its maximum as he sees its lowest. He will look at his wives, his servants, and his companions. And the best of the people of Paradise are “It is a status for one who looks at the face of God Almighty twice every day,” followed by Israel bin Yunus, on the authority of Thuwayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with him. About them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The lowest status of the people of Paradise is the one who sees in his kingdom two thousand years, and that The best of them is in status as he who looks at the face of God Almighty twice every day, then he recited {faces that Day will be radiant} [Al-Qiyamah: 22] He said: “Whiteness and purity” {a looker to her Lord} [Resurrection: 23] He said: “He looks every day on the face of God Almighty.” This hadith is explained in response to The innovator, and Thuwayr bin Abi Fakhta, and if they did not expel him, then nothing would be taken against him other than converting to Shiism.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3880 - Rather, it is a weak hadith, meaning Thawair bin Abi Fakhta"
"3881","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to me, Arim narrated to me, Abu Awanah narrated to me, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: I told Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both: “{Deserved for you, so more worthy} [Al-Qiyamah: 34] “Something said by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, or something that God revealed? He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said it, then God revealed it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3881 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3882","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi informed us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Yazid bin Iyad informed us, about Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Abu Al-Yasa’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that whenever the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited {Is not that Able to give life to the dead.} [Al-Qiyamah: 40] He said: “Yes,” and when he recited {Is not Allah the most wise of all judges} [Al-Tin: 8] he said: “Yes.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3882 - True"
"3883","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Duhaim informed us, Ahmad ibn Hazim al-Ghafari informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abraham Ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Muwarriq al-Ijli, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: Has a time come upon man? For a long time, nothing had been mentioned until He sealed it, then said: “I see what you do not see and I hear what you do not hear. Nothing in it has the space of four fingers, except for an angel with his forehead prostrated to God. By God, if you knew what I know, you would laugh a little. And you wept much and did not enjoy yourself with women on beds, and you would go out into the ascents, daring to God Almighty. By God, I wish I were a tree. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3883 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3884","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Sulaiman bin Al-Harith told us, Abu Ghassan told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Al-Bara’ ibn Azib, may God be pleased with him, in His Almighty’s saying: {And its harvests were humbled in a great humiliation} [Al-Insan: 14]. He said: “It was humbled for them.” “And they may eat from it however they wish.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3884 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3885","Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Sayrifi told me about Marw, Abd al-Samad ibn al-Fadl told me, Hafs ibn Umar al-Adni told me, al-Hakam ibn Aban told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “He mentioned the chariots of the people of Paradise, then he recited {And when you saw, then you saw bliss and dominion Great} [Al-Insan: 20] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3885 - Hafs bin Omar Al-Adni, wah"
"3886","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, Muhammad bin Musa Al-Bashani told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, On the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, in His saying, the Almighty, the Majestic: {And the mursalat by custom} [Al-Mursalat: 1] He said: “They are “The angels were sent in a reasonable manner.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3886 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3887","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, Samak bin Harb told us, On the authority of Khaled bin Arara, he said: A man stood up to Ali, may God be pleased with him, and said: What are storms? He said: “The winds.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3887 - True"
"3888","Abu Bakr al-Shafi’i told me, Ishaq bin al-Hasan told me, Abu Hudhayfah told me, Sufyan told me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abbas, I heard Ibn Abbas May God be pleased with them, and he was asked about this verse: {Indeed, it casts evil like castles} [Al-Mursalat: 32]. He said: “In the pre-Islamic era, we used to cut wood. Two or three cubits, so we raise it in the winter and call it Al-Qasr.” He said: I heard Ibn Abbas, when he was asked about {Jamalat Safar} [Al-Mursalat: 33] he said: “The ropes of ships are joined together until they are like the ropes of a traveller.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3888 - True"
"3889","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Hamid bin Abi Hamid Al-Muqri told us, Ishaq bin Sulayman told us, Talha bin Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “When God wanted to create creation, He sent the wind, and it drew the water until It opened from the tip of the Kaaba, and it is the one that is under the Kaaba. Then He extended the earth until it reached whatever God willed in length and width. He said: And it was This is how it extends, and Ibn Abbas showed me with his hand like this and like this. He said: “So God made the mountains as anchorages and pegs.” So Abu Qubays was one of the first A mountain placed on the earth “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3889 - Talha bin Amr weak"
"3890","Abu Balaj narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, in the Almighty’s saying: {We will abide therein for generations} [Al-Naba’: 23] He said: “The eras “Eighty years.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3890 - True"
"3891","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us, Abu Abdullah Al-Bushangi told us, Abu Abdullah Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Hushaym told us, he reported Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {A devastating cup} [Al-Naba’: 34] He said: “It is the one that follows “Full.” He said: Perhaps I heard Al-Abbas say: Give us water and give us water. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3891 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"3892","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Sulaiman al-Wasiti told us, Muhammad bin Yazid bin Khunais told us, he said: We were with Sufyan. We returned the revolutionary, and Saeed bin Hassan Al-Makhzoumi, who was our group’s storyteller, entered and visited us during the month of Ramadan. Sufyan said to him: How is the hadith you told me about Umm Salih? He said: Umm Salih told me, on the authority of Safiyya bint Shaybah, on the authority of Umm Habibah, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The words of the son of Adam against him have no meaning except enjoining what is right, or forbidding what is wrong, or mentioning God.” Muhammad bin Yazid said: I said: How severe This, then Sufyan said: How severe is this hadith? It was brought by a woman on the authority of a woman. This is in the Book of God Almighty, with whom He sent it. Your Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited {The Day when the Spirit and the angels will stand in array. They will not speak except to whom the Most Gracious has permitted and who will speak the truth} [Al-Naba’: 38], and he said: {By the era, indeed, mankind is in loss, except those who believe and do righteous deeds and enjoin each other to truth and each other to patience} [Al-Asr: 2] And he said: {There is no good in much of their private whispering, except in one who enjoins charity, or kindness, or reconciliation between people} [An-Nisa: 114] The verse\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3892 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3893","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Warqa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, {and women who drown by drowning and women who rise to life} [Al-Nazi’at: 2] He said: “Death” is valid on one condition. The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3893 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3894","Abu An-Nadr al-Faqih told us, Muadh bin Najda al-Qurashi told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad Ibn Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Tufayl Ibn Ubayy Ibn Ka’b, on the authority of Ubayy Ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was A quarter of the night passed, and he said: “O people, remember the blessing of God. O people, remember. The tremor has come, followed by the next. Death has come.” “Including what is in it.” Then Ubayy ibn Ka’b said: O Messenger of God, I pray for you often, so how many of my prayers should I devote to you? He said: “Whatever you want.” The hadith: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3894 - True"
"3895","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Bishr bin Musa Al-Asadi told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha Radi On her behalf, she said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was being asked about the Hour until it was revealed to him. From its remembrance to your Lord its end” [Al-Nazi’at: 43] “He said: “So it ended.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, for Ibn Uyaynah used to send it with his last.”"
"3896","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Saeed bin Yahya bin Saeed Al-Umawi told us, Ubayy told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The word “‘abas wa tawala” was revealed regarding the blind man of Ibn Umm Maktum, and she said: He came to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he began to say: Guide me. She said: And with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one of the great polytheists. She said: So he made The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away from one of them and turned to the other and said: “Do you think there is harm in what I am saying?” Then he said: “No.” For this was revealed. He frowned and said, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They did not narrate it. Some people sent it on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3896 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3897","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Abdul Tamimi told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, Abu Abdullah told us, my father told me, Ishaq told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, my father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, told him that he heard Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, say: {So We made therein grow grain and grapes. And trees, and olive trees, and palm trees, and gardens of trees, and fruit, and a father.} [Abs: 28] He said: We know all of this, but what is the father? Then he broke a stick that was in His hand and said: “This is the burden of God’s life. Follow what has become clear to you of this Book.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3897 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3898","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih in Baghdad told us, Ismail bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, my father told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ayyash, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Sawda, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The people will be resurrected barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised, covered with sweat, reaching the earlobe.” She said: I said: O Messenger of God, how bad you made him look at each other. To some, he said: “The people were distracted from that,” and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: “The day a man will flee from his brother, his mother, and his father.” And his companion and his children. On that day every man of them will have a matter that will enrich him.} [Abs: 35] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.” With this wording,” and they agreed on the hadith of Hatim bin Abi Saghira, on the authority of Abu Mulaika, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, in brief.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3898 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3899","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, in His Almighty saying: {And the earth bore And the mountains were crushed with one crush.} [Al-Haqqah: 14] He said: “They will become dust on the faces of the disbelievers, not on the faces of the believers.” That is the saying of the Almighty. And Glorious is He: {Faces that Day will be covered with dust, exhausted by time} [Abs: 41] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3899 - True"
"3900","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ibrahim bin Musa Al-Farra told us, Hisham bin Yusuf Al-San’ani told us, Abdullah bin Buhair al-San’ani told me, Abdul Rahman bin Yazid told me that he heard Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, saying: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever loves to look at the Day of Resurrection, let him read when the sun is swirled.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3900 - True"
"3901","Muhammad ibn al-Khalil al-Asbahani informed us, Musa ibn Ishaq al-Khutami informed us, Ubayy told us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam told us, Husayn informed us, about Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the words of God Almighty: {And when the beasts were gathered together} [Al-Takwir: 5] He said: “The gathering of the animals Its death and all things will be gathered together with death except jinn and mankind.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3901 - True"
"3902","Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, On the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, in His Almighty’s saying: {And when the souls were married} [Al-Takwir: 7] He said: “These are two men who do the work. By it they will enter Paradise and Hell, the ungodly with the ungodly, and the righteous with the righteous.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3902 - True"
"3903","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told us about Mecca, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Badal bin Al-Muhabbir told us, Zakaria bin Abu Zaida, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Maysara, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, saying in His saying, the Almighty: {So I do not swear by the unclean, the genitive, the sweeping} [Al-Takwir: 16] He said: “They are the cows of the wild beast.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3903 - True"
"3904","Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Karazi told us, Ali bin Abdul-Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Khaled bin Arara said: “When Othman, may God be pleased with him, was killed, that scared me greatly, so I went to Ali, may God be pleased with him, and we were together.” With him, when a man asked him what {the surroundings and the sweeping} [Al-Takwir: 16] he said: The planets. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3904 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3905","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abu Ghassan Sharik told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd Khair, on the authority of Abu Husayn, On the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, both of them on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, that he went out when dawn broke and said: “What an excellent hour this is the Witr prayer,” then he recited {And the night when it is hard, and the morning when it is warmed} [Al-Takwir: 18] “It is valid according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not produce it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3905 - Sahih according to Muslim’s conditions"
"3906","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed us, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, Hisham bin Hassan informed us, about Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah, on the authority of Hudhayfah ibn Al-Yaman, may God be pleased with him, said: A questioner rose during the time of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said hello and asked, but the people remained silent. Then a man gave it to him and the people gave it to him. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever does good, do good, it will be for him.” His reward, and like the rewards of those who followed him, not diminished in the slightest from their rewards. And whoever He followed him without diminishing anything from their burdens.” He said: And Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman recited, “A soul knows what it has put forward and what it puts back.” [Al-Infitar: 5] “This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, they agreed on the hadith of Jarir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him: “Whoever introduces Islam.” Just\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3906 - True"
"3907","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Hamid bin Abi Hamid told us, Ishaq bin Sulayman told us, he said: I heard Ibrahim bin Yazid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, said: I saw Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, reciting Woe to the Ones who turn away while he was crying. He said: “He is the man He hires the man or the measurer, knowing that he is negligent in his measure, so the burden is on him.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3907 - Ibrahim bin Yazid Wah"
"3908","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah, the judge in Egypt, told us, Safwan bin Issa told us, Muhammad bin Ajlan told us, about Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The believer, when He committed a sin and there was a black spot in his heart, so if he repents and repents and seeks forgiveness, his heart will be cleansed of it, and if he increases it, it increases until he is attached to it. His heart, that is the ransom which God mentioned in His Book: {No, but what they used to earn ransom over their hearts} [Al-Muttaffifin: 14] “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that A Muslim, and they did not produce it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3908 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3909","Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’atha, on the authority of Zaid bin Muawiyah, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Qays, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: {Its ending is musk} [Al-Muttaffin: 26] He said: “It is mixed and not “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3909 - True"
"3910","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Warqa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {When the sky split open and gave permission to its Lord and came true} [Al-Inshiqaq: 2] He said: I heard {And when the earth was stretched out} [Al-Inshiqaq: 3] He said: “On the Day of Resurrection” {And it will throw up what is in it and become empty} [Al-Inshiqaq: 4] He said: “It will bring forth what is in it of “The dead.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3910 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3911","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with him, said: The House existed before the earth by two thousand years. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3911 - True"
"3912","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Saeed bin Sulayman told us, Sulayman bin Daoud told us Al-Yamami, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Three: Whoever is among them, God will give him an easy reckoning and admit him into Paradise by His mercy.” They said: To whom, O Messenger of God? He said: “You give to those who deprived you, you forgive those who wronged you, and you maintain ties with those who cut ties with you.” He said: If I do that, what do I have, O Messenger of God? He said: “That you may be held accountable with an easy account, and God will admit you to Paradise by His mercy.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3912 - Suleiman bin Daoud Al-Yamami is weak"
"3913","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad Al-Qurashi told us in Kufa, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Al-Hasan bin Atiya told us, on the authority of Hamza Ibn Habib, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, in His Almighty saying: {You will ride on a plate On the authority of Tabq [Al-Inshiqaq: 19] he said: “The heaven.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3913 - They did not produce anything for Al-Hasan and there is weakness in him"
"3914","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Hushaym told us, Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, in the Almighty’s saying: {You will ride one level after another} [Al-Inshiqaq: 19] He said: meaning your Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He says: “At once after another.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it."
"3915","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad, who is Ibn Ja’far told us, On the authority of Shu`bah, he said: I heard Ali bin Zaid and Yunus bin Ubaid speaking on the authority of Ammar, the client of Banu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him. As for Ali, he raised him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and as for Yunus, he was not considered Abu Hurairah in this verse {and a witness and a witness} [Al-Buruj: 3] He said: “What is witnessed is the Day of Arafat and Friday, and what is witnessed is the one who is promised on the Day of Resurrection.” The hadith of Shu’bah on the authority of Yunus ibn Ubaid is authentic on the authority of The condition of the two sheikhs and they did not include it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3915 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3916","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Arfaja, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: {And the sky full of constellations} [Al-Buruj: 1] {Indeed, the oppression of your Lord is severe} [Al-Buruj: 12] to The last one. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3916 - True"
"3917","Ali bin Issa Al-Hiri told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told me, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza Al-Thumali, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “Indeed, among the things God has created are a preserved tablet of white pearls, two covers of red ruby, his pen.” Light, and His Book is a light that is seen every day three hundred and sixty glances, or once, and at each time it creates and provides, and gives life and causes death. And He exalts and humiliates, and does whatever He pleases. That is His saying: “Every day is about a matter” [Al-Rahman: 29] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. Hamza Al-Thumali was only criticized for extremism in his doctrine.”"
"3918","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to me, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Baghawi narrated to me, my grandfather Ahmad bin Mani’ narrated to me, Abu Yusuf narrated to me. Al-Qadi, Mutarrif bin Tarif told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Abi Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in his saying, Glory be to And Glorious is He: {He emerges from between the backbone and the ribs} [Al-Tariq: 7] He said: \"\"{The steel} [Al-Tariq: 7] is the solid, {and the ribs} [Al-Tariq: 7] are four ribs of Every side of the lower ribs “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3918 - True"
"3919","Ibrahim bin Hatim Al-Zahid told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-San’ani told me, Muhammad bin Jatham told me, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Khusayf, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {and the sky that has a return} [Al-Tariq: 11] He said: “rain” {and the earth that has cracks} [Al-Tariq: 12] He said: “That of plants.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3919 - True"
"3920","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told me, Yahya bin Othman bin Saleh al-Sahmi told me, my father and Amr bin al-Rabi` bin Tariq told us, And Saeed bin Abi Maryam, they said: Yahya bin Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her. On her authority, she said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite in the Witr prayer in the first rak’ah: “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,” and in the second: “Say, O O disbelievers, and in the third time, “Say, ‘He is Allah, One,’ and say, ‘I seek refuge in the Lord of creation,’ and say, ‘I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.’” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two Sheikhs did not narrate it like this. Rather, Al-Bukhari narrated it alone on the authority of Ibn Abi Maryam. This addition is only known from the hadith Yahya bin Ayyub only, and it was narrated with another authentic chain of narration.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3920 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3921","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Jazari told us, Khusayf told us, On the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Jarir, he said: We asked Aisha: What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recite in Witr? She said: “In the first rak’ah he used to recite, ‘Glorify the name of your Lord Most High,’ and in the second, ‘O you disbelievers,’ and in the third, ‘O you disbelievers.’” He is God, one and the two exorcists.” The Imam of the people of Egypt, in the hadith and narration, Saeed bin Katheer bin Ufayr, on the authority of Yahya bin Ayyub “I looked for it at the time I was dictating the book of Witr, but I did not find it, and I have found it again.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3921 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3922","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to perform the two rak’ahs in which he prayed Witr.” After them, “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,” and say, “O you disbelievers,” and reciting in the Witr prayer, “Say, ‘He is Allah, the One,’ and say, ‘I seek refuge in the Lord of creation.’” And say, “I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.”"
"3923","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told us, Al-Haytham bin Khalaf told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim, and Shurayh bin Yunus told us, they said: Hushaym told us, Abu Bishr told us, On the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, that whenever he recited {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} [Al-A'la: 1], he would say: “Glory be to “My Lord is the Most High, He who created and created Himself.” He said: This is the reading of Ubayy ibn Ka’b. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3923 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3924","Abu Al-Walid told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, Hushaym told us, Ali bin Ata told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim Ibn Rabi’ah, he said: Saad Ibn Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him, whenever he recited “Glorify the name of your Lord Most High,” he would say: “{We will make you recite, so you will not forget} He said: “He remembers the Qur’an for fear that it will forget.” He said: And I heard Sa’d reciting: “We do not abrogate any verse or cause it to be forgotten” [Al-Baqarah: 106]. I said: For indeed Saeed bin Al-Musayyab recites: Or should we forget it? Sa’d said: “The Qur’an was not revealed to Al-Musayyab, nor to the family of Al-Musayyab. God Almighty said: {We will make you read, so you do not forget} And He said: {And remember your Lord when you forget} [Al-Kahf: 24] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3924 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3925","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Khidr bin Aban Al-Hashimi told us, Sayyar bin Hatim told us, Ja’far bin Suleiman told us, he said: I heard Aba Imran al-Juni, says: Omar ibn al-Khattab passed by the monastery of a monk and called out to him: Oh monk, oh monk. He said: So he looked over him and made Omar look at him and cry. He said: Then he was told: O Commander of the Faithful, what makes you cry about this? He said: “I mentioned the words of God Almighty in His Book: {A working, constant worker who makes a hot fire watered by a well-filled spring} [Al-Ghashiya: 4] So that is the one who It made me cry, “This is a timely story, for Abu Imran al-Juni did not know the time of Omar.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3925 - Al-Juni did not realize Omar, but it is a relevant story"
"3926","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abu Dawud Omar bin Saad Al-Hafari told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but God. So when they say it, their blood and their property are protected from me except according to what is due therein and their reckoning is with God.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: “ {You have no control over them, except for him who turns back and disbelieves, then God will punish him with the greatest punishment} [Al-Ghashiya: 23] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3926 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3927","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Bishr bin Musa told me, Khallad bin Yahya told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Aghar, on the authority of Khalifa bin Husayn bin Qais, on the authority of Abu Nasr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {and the dawn} [Al-Fajr: 1] He said: “The dawn of the day” {and ten nights} [Al-Fajr: 2] He said: “The ten days of sacrifice.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. This Abu Nasr is Al-Aswad bin Hilal.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3927 - True"
"3928","Ahmad bin Kamil al-Qadi told us, Abu Qalabah told us, Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith told us, Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Imran bin Issam, A sheikh from the people of Basra, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about “Shaf’ and Witr” [Al-Fajr: 3] He said: “It is prayer, part of it is Shafa’a, and part of it is Witr.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3928 - True"
"3929","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ali bin Bakr Al-Adl told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Saeed bin Mansour Al-Makki told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar reported, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, in His saying, the Almighty, The pegs who transgressed in the land} [Al-Fajr: 11] He said: “Pharaoh set four pegs for his wife, then he placed a great millstone on her back. Until she died.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3929 - True"
"3930","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, Ibrahim bin Hilal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Abu Hamza told us, about Al-A'mash, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja'd, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, {By Al-Fajr} [Al-Fajr: 1] He said: “He swore {Indeed, your Lord is watching} [Al-Fajr: 14] The passage of the path has three bridges: a bridge over which is trustworthiness, a bridge over which is kinship, and a bridge over which is the Lord Almighty. “This is an authentic hadith.” The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3930 - True"
"3931","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, about Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {I do not swear by this country while you are settled in this Al-Balad} [Al-Balad: 2] He said: “It is permissible for him to do in it whatever he wants.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3931 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3932","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hussein al-Qadi in Hamadan told us, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Warqa’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty saying: {And a father and what he begot} [Al-Balad: 3] He said: “He means by the father “Adam and what he begot his son.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3932 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3933","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ataa, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {We created man in a liver} [Al-Balad: 4] He said: “In the distress of creation in his birth and growth. “His teeth, his hair, his livelihood, and his circumcision.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3933 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3934","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar Al-Ataridi told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, Asim told us, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, {And We guided him to the two ways of help} [Al-Balad: 10] He said: “Good and evil.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3934 - True"
"3935","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Hamid bin Abi Hamid Al-Muqri told us, Ishaq bin Suleiman Al-Razi told us, he said: I heard Talha bin Amr, and he was asked about the words of God Almighty: {or food on a day of hunger} [Al-Balad: 14] and he said: Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir told us, On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Among the necessities of forgiveness is feeding the Muslim.” Al-Saghban: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3935 - True"
"3936","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Yazid bin Al-Haytham told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Layth told us, Al-Ashja’i told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {or a poor person living in dusty land} [Al-Balad: 16] He said: “The one who is cast out and has no home.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3936 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3937","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Ibn Fudayl told us, Husayn told us, about Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {or a poor person living in dust} [Al-Balad: 16] He said: “The dust that does not Nothing protects him from dust.”"
"3938","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Warqa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {And the sun and its brightness} [Al-Shams: 1] He said: “its light” {and the moon when He followed it. [Al-Shams: 2] {And the earth and what flattened it} [Al-Shams: 6] He said: “He spread it out.” He said: {And the soul and what flattened it and inspired in it its immorality and piety} [Al-Shams: 8] He said: “He knew Its misery and its happiness. “He who purified it has succeeded, and he who trampled upon it has been disappointed.” [Al-Shams: 9] He said: “He misled her.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3938 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3939","Ali bin Issa told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Umar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hanzalah, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, in the Almighty’s saying: {So he inspired her with her immorality and her piety} [Al-Shams: 8] He said: “He adhered to her her immorality and her piety.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3939 - True"
"3940","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Wahb Al-Hafiz narrated, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Yusuf narrated Al-Faryabi, my father told me, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Mawhib, he said: I heard Ali bin Al-Hussein, He spoke on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Six whom I have cursed, and may God curse them and every prophet.” The one who exaggerates in the Book of God, the one who denies God’s decree, the one who rules with tyranny in order to humiliate whom God honors and exalts him whom God has humiliated, and the one who abandons the Book of God will be answered. For my Sunnah, and the one from my family who makes lawful what God has forbidden, and the one who makes lawful what God has forbidden.” Sufyan said: Recite a surah by the night when it covers, {as for those who “Whoever gives and is pious and is sincere in the good, We will make it easy for the hardship.” [Al-Lail: 6] “This is what Abu Ali told us, and it has an authentic chain of narration. I am afraid I mentioned it in the past.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3940 - Al-Dhahabi was silent about it in his summary in this place"
"3941","It was narrated to us by Abdullah bin Jaafar bin Darastuwaih Al-Farisi, Ya’qub bin Sufyan told us, Ishaq bin Muhammad Al-Farwi told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Al-Rijal, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Mawhib, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Six have been cursed and God has cursed, and every prophet is answered; The one who overdid the Book of God Almighty, the one who denies the decrees of God, and the one who rules with tyranny in order to humiliate whomever God honors and honor whomever God humiliates. And the one who deems permissible what God has forbidden, and the one from my family who deems permissible what God has forbidden, and the one who abandons my Sunnah.” Imam Al-Bukhari cited Ishaq bin Muhammad as evidence. Al-Farawi and Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Rijal in al-Jami’ al-Sahih, and this is more correct than the first chain of transmission.”"
"3942","Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, Saeed bin Yahya Al-Umawi told us, my uncle Abdul told me Allah bin Saeed, on the authority of Ziyadah bin Abdullah al-Bakai, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Atiq told me, On the authority of Amer bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, he said: Abu Quhafa said to Abu Bakr: I see you freeing weak necks. So you did what you did, you set free men who would prevent you and stand up against you. Abu Bakr said: “O my father, I only want what I want, when these verses were revealed about it. So We will make it easy for ease} [Al-Lail: 6] to the Almighty’s saying: “And no one has with Him any blessing that can be rewarded except for seeking the face of his Lord, the Most High.” And He will be satisfied.} [Al-Layl: 19] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3942 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3943","Abu Amr Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Asqalani told me, Issam bin Rawad bin Al-Jarrah told me, my father told me, Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubaid Allah, he said: Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas told me, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “I see The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was pleased with what would be opened to his nation after him, so he was pleased with that. So God Almighty revealed the forenoon and the night when it fell to His saying: “And your Lord will give you, and you will be satisfied.” [Al-Duha: 5] He said: “So He gave him a thousand palaces in Paradise of pearls of dust, musk in every palace thereof.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3943 - Issam bin Rawad narrated it alone on the authority of his father, and it has been weak"
"3944","Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Muzaki told us with dictation, Ahmad bin Salamah told us, Abdullah bin Al-Jarrah told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I asked God a question. I wish I had not asked him. I mentioned the messengers of my Lord and said: O Lord, You subjected the wind to Solomon, and spoke to Moses, and the Blessed and Most High said: Did not I found you an orphan and took you in, a lost person and I guided you, a needy person and I enriched you? He said: I said: Yes. I wished I had not asked him, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3944 - True"
"3945","Ishaq bin Muhammad al-Hashimi told us about Kufa, Muhammad bin Ali bin Affan al-Amiri told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he informed us Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam, may God be pleased with him, who said: When Abu Lahab’s hands came down, he repented, and he and his wife repented. A carrier of firewood in her sack.} [Al-Masad: 5] A rope from Masad. He said: Then it was said to the wife of Abu Lahab: Indeed, Muhammad has provoked you, so she came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him while he was sitting in public. She said: Oh Muhammad, why are you spelling me? He said: So he said: “By God, I have not satirized you. No one has satirized you except God.” He said: She said: Have you seen me carrying firewood or have you seen a rope of wood on my neck? Obstructed? Then she set off, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stayed for several days without visiting him. She came to him and said: O Muhammad, I have never seen your friend say good-bye to you. And he told you. So God Almighty revealed: “And by the forenoon and the night when it settles” [Al-Duha: 1] “Your Lord has not left you nor has He said.” This is an authentic hadith, just as we narrated this. The Sheikh, but I found a problem with him.”"
"3946","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran Al-Asbahani told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Yazid bin Zaid, he said: When Abu Lahab’s hands came down, he repented, so he mentioned a hadith like it, word for word, and the words of God Almighty {And as for By the grace of your Lord, speak.} [Al-Duha: 11] I did not find a single letter in it with any chain of transmission nor a saying of the Companions, so I mentioned two letters in it for the Followers.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3945 - Al-Hakim said its chain of transmission is authentic, except that I found a defect in it."
"3947","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Al-Hasan bin Ahmad bin Al-Layth told us, Ali bin Hashim Al-Razi told us, Humaid bin Abd told us Al-Rahman Al-Rawasi, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, said: Abu Ishaq said: “O young people, take advantage of the fact that rarely a night goes by without me reciting an Alif. Verily, I recite Al-Baqarah in one rak’ah, and I fast during the sacred months and three days of every month, Mondays and Thursdays, then he recited “And as for the grace of your Lord, speak.” [Al-Duha: 11]\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3947 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3948","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Al-Hasan bin Ahmad bin Al-Layth told us, Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, Hushaym told us, Abu Balg, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: “A man would meet one of his brothers and say: God provided me with such and such prayer yesterday and provided for someone.” Goodness is such and such. “May God have mercy on Amr bin Ubayd Allah al-Subai’i and Amr bin Maymun al-Awdi, for he alerted her to what encourages young people to worship.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3948 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3949","It was narrated to us by Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Abu Muslim narrated to us, and Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Qazzaz told us, they said: Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, Thabit Al-Bunani reported, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Gabriel came to him while he was playing with The two boys, so he took him and struck him, so he tore open his heart and extracted a clot from it, and said: This is the share of Satan from you. He said: So he washed him in a basin. Of gold with Zamzam water, then to his mother, then he returned it to its place. He said: And the young men came seeking his mother, meaning his back, and they said: Indeed Muhammad had been killed, so his back came looking for him, so he faced her while returning, and he was discolored. Anas said: We used to see the traces of the thread in His chest is “authentic in its chain of transmission, but they did not narrate it.” “The narration has been authenticated on the authority of Omar ibn al-Khattab and Ali ibn Abi Talib: “No hardship will prevail over two ease.” It was narrated with a narrated chain of transmission on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3949 - Sahih according to Muslim’s conditions"
"3950","Muhammad ibn Ali al-San’ani informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-San’ani informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of al-Hasan. In the words of God Almighty: {Indeed, with hardship comes ease} [Explanation: 6] He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out one day rejoicing and laughing, and he was He says: “No hardship can overcome two ease {For with hardship there is ease, indeed with hardship there is ease} [Al-Sharh: 6].”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3950 - Sent"
"3951","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Warqa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {By the fig and the olive} [Al-Tin: 1] He said: “The fruit that he eats.” Al-Nas” {and Mount Sinin} [Al-Tin: 2] he said: “Al-Tur” [Al-Baqarah: 63] the mountain, and {Sinin} [Al-Tin: 2] he said: “The Blessed.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3951 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3952","Ali bin Issa told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Umar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “Whoever recites the Qur’an will not be returned to the most miserable life, lest he should know anything after knowing it. That is the saying of the Almighty.” “Then We returned it to the lowest of the low, except those who believe.” [Al-Tin: 6] He said: “Except those who have read the Qur’an.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3952 - True"
"3953","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Sinan Al-Ramli told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha May God be pleased with her, she said: “The first surah revealed from the Qur’an: Recite in the name of your Lord who created.” And behold, Ibn Uyaynah did not hear it from Al-Zuhri.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3953 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3954","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh informed us, saying: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, she said: “The first surah to be revealed from the Qur’an: Read in the name of your Lord.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”"
"3955","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Salem Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Hammad told us, Abd Al-Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Amr bin A dinar, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He was in Hira when the king brought him a pattern of brocade on which was written: Read In the name of your Lord who created until {what He does not know} [Al-Al`alq: 5] “Then I heard Abu Ali al-Hafiz say: The mention of Jabir in its chain of transmission is an illusion.”"
"3956","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Zangwayh informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, He told me, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in Hira and mentioned it. The first continuous hadith has all of its narrators trustworthy. I based this book on the idea that an increase in confidence is acceptable. As for the prostration in {Read in the name of your Lord} [Al-Al-Alq: 1], it was narrated by Muslim, on the authority of Abu Al-Tahir, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Amr ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Jaafar, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3955 - Its authenticity is mursal"
"3957","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Harun bin Sulaiman told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zar, On the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, he said: “The commandments for prostration in the Qur’an are the revelation of Lam, and the revelation of prostration, and the star, and recite in the name of your Lord who created.” And I am amazed at someone who spoke to me who does not prostrate in the joint.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3957 - True"
"3958","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Jarir informed us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {Indeed, We sent it down on the Night of Decree} [Al-Qadr: 1] He said: “It was sent down “The Qur’an on the Night of Decree was one sentence to the heaven of the world, at the position of the stars.” So God used to reveal it to His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. One after the other, the Almighty said: {And those who disbelieve say, “If only the Qur’an had not been revealed to him in one sentence; thus, that We might thereby strengthen your heart.” And We recited it with a chant} [Al-Furqan: 32] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3958 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3959","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Issa Al-Wasiti told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hakim bin Jubayr, On the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The Qur’an was sent down on the Night of Decree from the highest heaven to the lowest heaven.” One sentence, then he separated in the years, saying: And he recited this verse {I do not swear by the positions of the stars, and indeed it is a great oath, if only you knew} [Al-Waqi’ah: 76] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3959 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3960","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Abu Amir Al-Aqdi informed us, Ikrimah bin Ammar told us Al-Yamami, on the authority of Abu Zamil Samak Al-Hanafi, he said: Malik bin Marthad told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I said to Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him: Did Did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mention the Night of Decree? He said: Yes, I said: O Messenger of God, tell me about Laylat Al-Qadr, is it during Ramadan, or during a month other than Ramadan? He said: “Rather, in Ramadan.” I said: Tell me, O Messenger of God, is it with the prophets as they were? When the prophets are taken away, it is raised, or is it to On the Day of Resurrection? He said: “No, but until the Day of Resurrection.” I said: O Messenger of God, tell me which Ramadan it is? He said: “In the last ten days, do not ask me about anything after that.” So I said: I swore to you by my right upon you, O Messenger of God. What ten days is it? He said: He became very angry with me, as he has never been angry with me before or after, and he said: “If God had willed, He would have made it known to you. Search for it on the seventh day.” “The last days, do not ask me about anything after that.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3960 - True"
"3961",""
"3962","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Abu Dawud told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zar, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, said that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited to him something that had not happened, and he recited in it: “Indeed, the essence of religion in the eyes of God is Hanifism.” Judaism, Christianity, or Magianism, and whoever does good, it will not be declared an unbelief for him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3962 - True"
"3963","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I heard Al-Fudayl bin Amr, He said to Abu Wael Shaqiq bin Salamah: Did you hear Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, say: “Whoever says I am a believer, let him say I am in Paradise” and he said: Yes, then Al-Mughirah said: Abu Wa’il Shaqiq ibn Salamah read: Those who disbelieved were not among the People of the Book until it was conveyed {and they were not commanded. Except that they should worship God, sincere in religion to Him.} [Al-Baynah: 5] until the Almighty’s saying: {And that is the religion of value.} [Al-Baynah: 5] He read it while he was exposing With the Murji’ah, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3963 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3964","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani and Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub told us, saying: Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Saeed told us. Ibn Abi Ayyub, Ayyash Ibn Abbas Al-Qatbani told us, on the authority of Issa Ibn Hilal Al-Sadfi, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, may God be pleased with them both, he said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Recite to me, O Messenger of God. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Read three of the Dhawat Ra’, and the man said: I have grown in age, my heart has hardened, and my tongue has become harsh. He said: “Recite three Dhawat Ra’” and he said the same as his first article. So he said: “Recite three of the Rosaries.” He said the same as he had said. The man said: O Messenger of God, recite to me a comprehensive surah. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it to him: “When there is an earthquake” [Al-Zalzalah: 1] until he finished it, and the man said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not add anything more."
"3965","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani and Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub told us, saying: Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Saeed told us. Ibn Abi Ayyub, Yahya Ibn Abi Sulaiman told me, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited May God bless him and grant him peace. This verse {On that day will its news be revealed} [Al-Zalzalah: 4] He said: “Do you know what its news is? They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “Then its news is that it bears witness against every male and female slave of what was done on its back, to say: He did such-and-such, or such-and-such on such-and-such day. And so and so are her narrations: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3965 - This Yahya is a denier of hadith, said Al-Bukhari"
"3966","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, and Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told us, saying: Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Wasiti told us, Yazid bin Harun, Sufyan bin Husayn reported, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu Asma al-Rahbi, he said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with us On his authority, he ate lunch with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when this verse was revealed: {So whoever does an atom’s weight of good will see it, and whoever does a weight of good A speck of evil that he will see} [Al-Zalzalah: 8] Then Abu Bakr seized him and said: O Messenger of God, have we seen all of the evil that we have done? He said: “Whatever you see of what you dislike, that is what you will be rewarded for. Good will be delayed for its people in the Hereafter.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3966 - Sent"
"3967","Muhammad bin Ahmad al-Mahboubi told us about Marw, Sa`id bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, Abdul Karim told me Al-Jazari, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the Almighty’s saying: {And the enemy animals are slaughtered} [Al-Adiyat: 1] He said: “They are horses.” {Then the murrayat are a cup} [Al-Adiyat: 2] He said: “When a man is exposed to his elbow.” {Then the murrayat are a spot} [Al-Adiyat: 3] Horses become an enemy {so they soaked with it} [Al-Adiyat: 4] He said: “The dust” {So they put together a crowd therewith} [Al-Adiyat: 5] The enemy {Indeed, man is in hiding before his Lord} [Al-Adiyat: 6] He said: “The unbelievers”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3967 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3968","Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi Hamadan told us, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein bin Dizil told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Al-Mubarak bin Faddalah, on the authority of Al-Hasan, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a believing servant dies, his soul will receive the souls of The believers say to him: What did so-and-so do? So when he said: He died, they said: He was taken to his mother, the abyss, so wretched was the mother and miserable was the nurse. This is an authentic mursal hadith. The chain of transmission, because I did not find an explanation for this Surah according to the conditions of the book, so I took it out, as I did not find it permissible to exclude it from a hadith.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3968 - Sent"
"3969","Abu Amr Othman bin Abdullah bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Harithi told us, Muadh bin Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah bin Ash-Shakhir, that his father told him, saying: I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello while reciting {Your distraction is multiplication} [At-Takhara: 1] and he said: “The son of Adam says: My wealth is my wealth, and do you have any of your wealth except what you have eaten?” So did you wear it, or did you wear it and it did not work out, or did you give in charity and did so? “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and is not stipulated by the two sheikhs, and Abdullah bin Al-Shakheer does not have a narrator other than his son who is a mutarrif. We looked, and a Muslim had He took it from the hadith of Shu’bah on the authority of Qatada in brief.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3969 - Narrated by Muslim in brief"
"3970","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Muhammad bin Bakr Al-Barsani told us, Ja’far bin Burqan told us, he said: I heard Yazid bin Al-Assam, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I do not fear poverty for you, but I “I fear for you to multiply, and I do not fear for you to make a mistake, but I fear for you to do it intentionally.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but he did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3970 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3971","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr Dhi Murr, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, that he “recited: By the era and the calamities of time, indeed man is in loss.” This hadith The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3971 - True"
"3972","Abu Hafs Ahmad bin Ahad Al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, Harun bin Saeed Al-Aili told us, Abdullah bin Wahb, Amr bin Al-Harith informed me, on the authority of Darraj Abu Al-Samh, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, {Woe for every smite} [Al-Hamza: 1] He said: “Woe is the valley in Hell into which the infidel will fall for forty autumns before he finishes. “The Account of the People” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3972 - True"
"3973","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Qurashi told us in Kufa, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Hamza al-Zayat, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim ibn Damra, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, that he “mentioned the Fire, and magnified its command, and remembered of it.” God willed that he mention it, then he said: It is fixed upon them in extended pillars. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3973 - True"
"3974","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Qaboos bin Abi Dhabyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, who said: The companions of the elephant approached, until when they approached Mecca, Abd met them. Al-Muttalib said to their king: What has brought you to us? What has bothered you, O our Lord? Have you not been sent and we may bring you everything you wanted? “He said: I was told about this house that no one enters unless he is safe, so I came to frighten its people. He said: “We will bring you everything you want, so return.” He refused but to let him in and set off to walk towards it. Abdul Muttalib lagged behind, so he stood on a mountain. He said: “I do not witness the destruction of this house and its people.” Then he said:\n [full sea]\n\n Oh God, every god has...permissible, so prevent your permissible\n They never overcome their problems...never yours.\n Oh God, if you do... then do what you want.\n Then they came like a cloud from towards the sea until they were shaded by the birds of Ababil, which God Almighty said: {You shall cast upon them stones made of shale}. [Al-Fil: 4] He said: Then he made the elephant roar, and made them like edible chaff. [Al-Fil: 5] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3974 - True"
"3975","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi told us, Ahmad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Narsi told us, Yaqoub bin Muhammad Al-Zuhri told us, Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Thabit bin Shurahbil, Othman bin Abdullah bin Abi Atiq told me, on the authority of Saeed bin Amr bin Ja’dah bin Hubayra, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandmother, Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God favored the Quraysh with seven virtues; Indeed, I am among them, and that prophecy is among them, and that veiling is among them, and that watering is among them, and that God gave them victory over the elephant, and that they worshiped God ten times. “For years, no one else would worship Him, and that God revealed to them a chapter of the Qur’an.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it, “In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.” {To make the Quraysh accustomed to the journey of winter and summer, so let them worship the Lord of this House, who has fed them against hunger and made them safe from fear} [Quraysh: 2] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3975 - Jacob is weak and Ibrahim is the author of evil deeds. This man denied them."
"3976","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “The bare vessels” is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3976 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3977","Ali bin Issa told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ali Radi God said, “And they withhold the aid” [Al-Ma’un: 7]. He said: “It is the obligatory zakat. They show off their prayers and withhold their zakat.” This is an authentic chain of narration. “Sent, for Mujahid did not hear from Ali.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3977 - Interrupted"
"3978","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi, and Amr bin Muhammad bin Al-Hasan told us, they said: Omar bin Hafs Al-Sadusi told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Abu Uwais told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of his brother Abdullah bin Muslim bin Shihab, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about Al-Kawthar and he said: “It is a river that God gave me in Paradise, its soil.” Musk, whiter than milk and sweeter than honey, is brought back by birds whose necks are like the necks of carrots.” Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, said: Oh Messenger of God, it is gentle. He said: “Its food is more delicious than it.” Muslim narrated this hadith from the hadith of Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, on the authority of al-Mukhtar ibn Falaful, on the authority of Anas “When it was revealed {Indeed, We have given you Al-Kawthar} [Al-Kawthar: 1] it was more complete and longer than it, but I included it in the individuals of Asim bin Ali, for Abu Uwais is trustworthy, but he did not memorize a hadith from his brother Abdullah on the authority of his brother Abdullah with a chain of transmission, and this is the well-known hadith from Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Muslim, On the authority of his father\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3978 - Narrated by Muslim"
"3979","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim Al-Adl informed me, my father informed me, Yahya bin Yahya informed me, Hushaym informed me, Abu Bishr informed me, about Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {Indeed, We have given you Al-Kawthar} [Al-Kawthar: 1] He said: “Al-Kawthar is the great goodness that He gave you.” May God bless him. Abu Bishr said: I said to Saeed: Some people claim that it is a river in Paradise. He said: “And the river is of abundant goodness.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. As for His saying, the Almighty, the Majestic, “so pray for your Lord.” And slaughter} [Al-Kawthar: 2] The Companions differed in their interpretation, and the best of them is what was narrated on the authority of the Commander of the Faithful, Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him. In two narrations, the first of which\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3979 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3980","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali, and Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, they said: Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim Al-Jahdari, on the authority of Uqba bin Sahban, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, {Pray to your Lord and sacrifice} [Al-Kawthar: 2] He said: “It is placing your right hand on Your left hand in prayer” and the second narration\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3980 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3981","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us in Hamdan, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris al-Razi told us, Wahb bin Abi Marhum told us, we told him Israel bin Hatim, on the authority of Muqatil bin Hayyan, on the authority of Al-Asbagh bin Nabatah, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, he said: When it was revealed This verse is about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: {Indeed, We have given you Al-Kawthar, so pray to your Lord and sacrifice} [Al-Kawthar: 2] The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Gabriel, what is this lake that my Lord commanded me to do?” He said: It is not a lake, but he orders you, when you deprive yourself for prayer, to raise your hands when you say “Allahu Akbar,” and when you bow, and when you raise Your head from bowing, for it is our prayer and the prayer of the angels who are in the seven heavens. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The raising of hands out of the submissiveness that God Almighty said: {But they did not submit to their Lord nor did they supplicate} [Al-Mu’minun: 76] \"\"\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3981 - Israel is an unreliable author of miracles and the most reliable Shiite is abandoned by Al-Nasa’i."
"3982","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Abu Ja’far Al-Hadrami told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Farwa bin Nawfal Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of his father, that he said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Tell me something to say, and he said: “When you go to Your bed, so recite {Say, O you disbelievers} [Al-Kafirun: 1] until its conclusion, for it is an acquittal from polytheism. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it has not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3982 - True"
"3983","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, Shu’bah told us, Abu Ishaq, I heard Abu Ubaidah, speaking on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to often say: “Glory be to You, our Lord, and with Your praise,” and when it descended, when God’s victory and conquest came, he said: “Glory be to You, our Lord, and with Your praise. O God, forgive me. You are the Most Merciful. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3983 - True"
"3984","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr Al-Muzaki told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Ansari told us, Al-Aswad told us Ibn Shayban, on the authority of Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab, on the authority of his father, said: Lahab ibn Abi Lahab used to curse the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Prophet said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Oh God, give your dog power over him.” So he went out in a caravan, heading to the Levant, and he stayed one house, and said: I fear the call of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he greeted him. They said to him: No, so they put their belongings around him and sat guarding him. Then the lion came and snatched it and took it away. “The chain of narration is authentic, but it was not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3984 - True"
"3985","And Muhammad bin Al-Mu’mal bin Al-Hasan told me, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad told us, Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, he said: It was recited to Sufyan bin Uyaynah and I. Al-Zuhri witnessed, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {His wealth did not avail him, nor did he earn} [Al-Masad: 2] He said: “His earning His son.” Ahmad ibn Hanbal said: Ibn Uyaynah did not mention to us what he heard about it, then I was informed that he heard it from Omar ibn Habib\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3985 - Amr bin Habib Wah"
"3986","Then Muhammad ibn al-Mu’ammil informed me, Al-Fadl told us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal told me, Abd al-Razzaq told me, Muammar told me, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Abu Al-Tufayl, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas one day when the Banu Abi Lahab came to him and were disputing among themselves about something, so he stood up to reconcile between them, so he pushed him away. Some of them fell on the bed, and Ibn Abbas got angry and said: “Remove from me the evil gain - meaning his son - {His wealth does not avail him and what He earned} [Al-Masad: 2] \"\"\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3986 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"3987","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz, and Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Ali told us, saying: Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Muhammad bin Previously, Abu Ja`far al-Razi narrated to us, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, “The polytheists said: O Muhammad, attribute your Lord to us. Then God Almighty revealed: {Say: He is God, one, God, the Eternal} [Al-Ikhlas: 2] He said: Al-Samad: the one who did not beget, {And he was not begotten, and there is no one equal to Him} [Al-Ikhlas: 3] because there is no Nothing is born except that it will die, and nothing dies except that it will be inherited. Indeed, God does not die nor bequeath any inheritance. {And there is no one equal to Him} [Al-Ikhlas: 4]. He has no counterpart, and there is nothing like him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3987 - True"
"3988","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, my father told us, I heard Yahya bin Ayyub, narrating On the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Aslam Abi Imran al-Tajibi, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, may God be pleased with him, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, He recited from Surah Yusuf and Surat Hud. He said: “O Uqba, recite, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation, for you will never recite a surah more beloved to God. “And inform him of it, and if you are able not to miss it, do so.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3988 - True"
"3989","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid ibn Ibrahim al-Hafiz narrated to us Hamdan, Ibrahim ibn al-Hussein narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, Ibn Abi narrated to us Dhi’ib, on the authority of his uncle Al-Harith bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He took her hand and pointed her to the moon and said: “Seek refuge in God from the evil of this, for it is dark when it sets.” The chain of transmission is authentic and it is not “He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3989 - True"
"3990","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah Al-Bakri told us, Al-Qasim bin Al-Hakam told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ziyad bin Thuwayb, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to greet me and said: “Shall I not perform ruqyah to you as Gabriel ruqyah did to me? Peace be upon him? I said: Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for it. He said: “In the name of God, I perform ruqyah for you, and God will heal you from every disease in you, from the evil of blowing on the knot, and from the evil of the envier when he is envious.” So he performed ruqyah with her three times.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3990 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3991","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sana’ani informed us of Mecca, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abbad informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Sufyan al-Thawri informed us, about Hakim bin Jubayr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “There is no newborn without obsessive thoughts in his heart. If he mentions God, he deceives, and if he is negligent, he whispers, which is the Almighty’s saying: “The deceitful whisperer” [Al-Nas: 4] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.” And they did not bring it out.” The last book of interpretation. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds, and may God’s blessings be upon our master Muhammad, his family, and all his companions. Book Dates of the predecessors of the prophets and messengers. Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us dictation in the month of Rabi’ The last, in the year four hundred and one: a book of the histories of the earlier prophets and messengers, and a mention of their virtues and news, along with Nations on the tongue of our Master the Chosen One, may God bless him and grant him peace and all of them, for Imam Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ismail narrated it in This place is from the authentic mosque before the beginning of Sharia law, and the Companions mentioned it, so I followed it. Mention of what was narrated with authentic chains of transmission from the mention of Adam, the father of mankind, may God’s prayers be upon him, and his wife Eve, peace be upon her, when they were descended to The earth, which was not mentioned by the two sheikhs, mentioned Adam, peace be upon him.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3991 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
